window.SECTOR_NARR={"xlk":{"now":"Tech is the undisputed #1 sector (RS rank 1, +24.3% vs SPY +6.3%) and cycle position ~84/100. The tape is goldilocks/reflation risk-on, led by semis (SMH +67.9%) and high-beta (+20.7% vs low-vol), which kept defensives lagging (+6.9% vs cyclicals +11.2%) — but importantly this is NOT a narrow melt-up: equal-weight quietly beat cap-weight by +2.9%, so participation has broadened underneath the leaders. The leg is TOPPING: Broadcom's early-June refusal to raise its AI outlook triggered a $1T+ semis wipeout, the classic distribution signature of a maturing, mega-cap-led melt-up now broadening into late-cycle.","legs":{"2021-12-27":{"title":"Rate-shock duration de-rating","body":"As the Fed pivoted hawkish into a 9% CPI print, a rate-regime selloff (TLT -11.3%, yields surging) crushed long-duration tech, where rich multiples hung on far-future earnings. XLK finished dead last (rank 10/11, -20.0%) as a strong dollar (+3.1% DXY) and the Russia-Ukraine invasion added a stagflationary risk-off bid; only Energy (+32.9%) escaped the duration unwind.","drivers":["rate regime","duration de-rating","stretched valuations","strong dollar"],"title_zh":"利率冲击下的久期重定价","body_zh":"美联储在9%的CPI数据中转向鹰派，利率象限的抛售（TLT -11.3%、收益率飙升）重创长久期科技股——其高估值依赖于遥远的未来盈利。XLK垫底（排名10/11，-20.0%），强美元（+3.1% DXY）和俄乌战争叠加出滞胀式的避险买盘；只有能源（+32.9%）逃过了这场久期重定价。","drivers_zh":["利率象限","久期重定价","估值过高","强美元"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Oversold relief bounce","body":"A sharp tech/semis-led risk-on rip (SMH +18.8%, growth>value +8.7, VIX 32→19) as the market digested the first Fed hike and an oversold growth complex snapped back. Tech ranked #2/11 in a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (equal-weight lagged by -2.4%) — but nothing in the inflation or rates picture had actually turned.","drivers":["oversold bounce","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","short cover"],"title_zh":"超卖后的反弹","body_zh":"一波由科技/半导体引领的风险偏好急涨（SMH +18.8%、成长跑赢价值 +8.7、VIX 32→19），市场消化了首次加息、超卖的成长板块强力反弹。在狭窄、大盘股主导的盘面中（等权落后 -2.4%）科技排名第2/11——但通胀和利率的格局实际上并未转向。","drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","空头回补"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Hiking-cycle bear leg","body":"The Fed accelerated to 50-75bp hikes and QT as inflation stayed near 9%, a rate-regime move (TLT -14.1%, +5.3% DXY) that re-crushed long-duration tech to dead last (rank 9, -24.5%). This was a genuine flight-to-safety — defensives (-11.2%) far outperformed cyclicals (-18.2%) with VIX 19→33 — as semis broke down (SMH -28.1%) into the June bear low.","drivers":["aggressive hikes","rate regime","flight-to-safety","strong dollar"],"title_zh":"加息周期的熊市腿","body_zh":"通胀维持在9%附近，美联储加速至50-75个基点加息并缩表，这一利率象限的move（TLT -14.1%、+5.3% DXY）将长久期科技股再度打到垫底（排名9，-24.5%）。这是真正的避险——防御板块（-11.2%）远超周期板块（-18.2%），VIX 19→33——半导体崩溃（SMH -28.1%），跌向6月熊市低点。","drivers_zh":["激进加息","利率象限","避险","强美元"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-inflation hope rally","body":"Tech ripped ~23% on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +20.8%, growth>value +9.2, VIX 33→20) as the market bet inflation had peaked and the Fed would soon pivot. Falling yields lifted rate-sensitive growth and money edged out of safety — Tech ranked #2/11 in a goldilocks tape — before Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole killed it.","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","tech-led risk-on","pivot bet","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"通胀见顶预期下的反弹","body_zh":"科技急涨约23%，源于科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +20.8%、成长跑赢价值 +9.2、VIX 33→20），市场押注通胀已见顶、美联储即将转向。收益率回落提振了对利率敏感的成长股，资金撤出防御——在金发姑娘式盘面中科技排名第2/11——直到鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派讲话终结了这轮反弹。","drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","科技引领风险偏好","转向押注","金发姑娘象限"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Jackson Hole hawkish reset","body":"Powell's Jackson Hole vow to hold rates 'higher for longer' was a rate-regime move (TLT -12.7%, +6.4% DXY pushing the dollar to new highs) that slammed long-duration tech to near the bottom (rank 10, -22.9%). A hot September CPI sealed the deflation-scare selloff and the SMH -28.8% breakdown into the October bear-market low.","drivers":["Jackson Hole","rate regime","strong dollar","deflation-scare quad"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置","body_zh":"鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔誓言将利率维持\"更高更久\"，这是一记利率象限的move（TLT -12.7%、+6.4% DXY将美元推至新高），把长久期科技股打到接近垫底（排名10，-22.9%）。火热的9月CPI坐实了通缩恐慌式抛售，以及SMH -28.8%的崩溃，跌向10月熊市低点。","drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔","利率象限","强美元","通缩恐慌象限"]},"2022-10-12":{"title":"The genAI bull run","body":"A softer October CPI marked the rate-peak inflection, and ChatGPT's launch ignited a generative-AI super-cycle that made the semis the dominant theme (SMH +226.2%) in a goldilocks risk-on melt-up (growth>value +52.9, VIX 34→13, -7.3% DXY tailwind). XLK ranked #1/11 and more than doubled (+107%) — but this was the narrowest of tapes, with equal-weight lagging cap-weight by a staggering -28.7%.","drivers":["genAI super-cycle","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"生成式AI牛市","body_zh":"更温和的10月CPI标志着利率见顶拐点，ChatGPT的发布点燃了生成式AI超级周期，使半导体成为主导主题（SMH +226.2%），处于金发姑娘式的风险偏好飙升中（成长跑赢价值 +52.9、VIX 34→13、-7.3% DXY 顺风）。XLK排名第1/11并翻倍有余（+107%）——但这是极度狭窄的盘面，等权指数落后市值加权高达 -28.7%。","drivers_zh":["生成式AI超级周期","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","金发姑娘象限"]},"2024-07-10":{"title":"Yen-carry air-pocket","body":"A BoJ rate hike and a weak US jobs report violently unwound the yen-carry trade, hitting the most crowded AI longs hardest — Tech air-pocketed ~17% (dead last, rank 11) as semis cratered (SMH -24.8%). This was a flight-to-safety: defensives (+2.2%) led cyclicals (-5.5%) with VIX 13→28, a fast technical deleveraging, not a fundamental break.","drivers":["yen-carry unwind","flight-to-safety","crowded momentum","growth-scare jobs print"],"title_zh":"日元套息交易的瞬间真空","body_zh":"日本央行加息与疲软的美国就业报告剧烈瓦解了日元套息交易，对最拥挤的AI多头打击最重——科技瞬间真空约17%（垫底，排名11），半导体暴跌（SMH -24.8%）。这是一次避险：防御板块（+2.2%）领先周期板块（-5.5%），VIX 13→28，属于快速的技术性去杠杆，而非基本面破裂。","drivers_zh":["日元套息瓦解","避险","拥挤动量","增长恐慌就业数据"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Soft-landing AI recovery","body":"Tech rebounded +23% as the carry-unwind panic faded into a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +22.2%, growth>value +12.1, VIX 28→15), with the Fed's September cut and post-election deregulation bets fueling Nvidia-led AI enthusiasm. Leadership stayed narrow and mega-cap (equal-weight lagged by -6.2%), even as a rate-regime backup (TLT -6.1%) and strong dollar (+3.8% DXY) built underneath.","drivers":["Fed cuts begin","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","rate regime"],"title_zh":"软着陆下的AI复苏","body_zh":"随着套息瓦解的恐慌消退，科技反弹 +23%，演变为科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +22.2%、成长跑赢价值 +12.1、VIX 28→15），美联储9月降息与大选后放松监管的押注助燃了英伟达领涨的AI热情。领涨保持狭窄且集中于大盘股（等权落后 -6.2%），尽管底层正酝酿利率象限回升（TLT -6.1%）与强美元（+3.8% DXY）。","drivers_zh":["美联储开启降息","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","利率象限"]},"2025-02-19":{"title":"DeepSeek + tariff shock","body":"The late-January DeepSeek cheap-AI scare cracked the capex thesis (Nvidia's record one-day value loss), and April's 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariffs detonated a broad crash that sent Tech dead last (rank 11, -25.7%, SMH -30.1%). This was a violent flight-to-safety — defensives (-7.7%) far outran cyclicals (-18.7%) as VIX exploded 15→52 — bottoming around April 8.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","reciprocal tariffs","flight-to-safety","capex-thesis doubt"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek叠加关税冲击","body_zh":"1月底DeepSeek廉价AI恐慌击碎了资本开支逻辑（英伟达创纪录的单日市值蒸发），4月\"解放日\"对等关税引爆了一场全面崩盘，将科技打到垫底（排名11，-25.7%，SMH -30.1%）。这是一次剧烈的避险——防御板块（-7.7%）远超周期板块（-18.7%），VIX 暴涨 15→52——在4月8日附近见底。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","对等关税","避险","资本开支逻辑动摇"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Tariff-pause AI melt-up","body":"Trump's tariff pause and device exemptions detonated a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +104.8%, growth>value +29.9, VIX 52→17, -3.6% DXY tailwind) with hyperscaler spend estimates past $400B. XLK ranked #1/11 (+69.7%) on Nvidia/Broadcom records, but it was the textbook narrow tape — equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -15.1% as money concentrated in a handful of AI names.","drivers":["tariff de-escalation","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","AI-capex melt-up"],"title_zh":"关税暂停下的AI飙升","body_zh":"特朗普暂停关税并豁免设备，引爆了科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +104.8%、成长跑赢价值 +29.9、VIX 52→17、-3.6% DXY 顺风），云厂商资本开支预期突破4000亿美元。XLK排名第1/11（+69.7%），由英伟达/博通创纪录推动，但这是教科书式的狭窄盘面——资金集中于少数几只AI龙头，等权落后市值加权 -15.1%。","drivers_zh":["关税降级","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","AI资本开支飙升"]},"2025-10-29":{"title":"Hawkish valuation reset","body":"A hawkish Fed turn repriced borrowing costs just as hyperscalers committed to the most expensive build-out in a generation, sparking an AI-complex valuation reset that sent Tech dead last (rank 11, -15.9%). Unusually, this wasn't a risk-off panic — defensives and cyclicals fell roughly in line — it was a stagflation-ish rotation OUT of crowded megacap growth (growth-value -19.5) into Energy (+42.9%, oil +70.1%), with equal-weight beating cap-weight by +8.2% as breadth finally broadened.","drivers":["hawkish Fed","AI valuation reset","rotation out of megacap","broadening breadth"],"title_zh":"鹰派下的估值重置","body_zh":"美联储转鹰重新定价了借贷成本，恰逢云厂商承诺一代人以来最昂贵的建设，引发AI板块的估值重置，将科技打到垫底（排名11，-15.9%）。不同寻常的是，这并非避险恐慌——防御与周期板块跌幅大体相当——而是一次滞胀式轮动，资金撤出拥挤的大盘成长（成长-价值 -19.5），转入能源（+42.9%，油价 +70.1%），等权跑赢市值加权 +8.2%，市场广度终于扩散。","drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派","AI估值重置","撤出大盘股","市场广度扩散"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Oil-fade AI rip","body":"Tech ripped ~55% (rank #1) as the Iran-war oil tail faded toward the mid-June ceasefire and the AI-capex trade roared back in a reflation/risk-on melt-up (SMH +74.4%, growth>value +10.9, VIX 31→16). It was again narrow and mega-cap-led (equal-weight lagged by -8.6%); the leg crested into early June as Broadcom's refusal to raise its full-year AI outlook detonated a $1T+ semis wipeout — the late-cycle top.","drivers":["oil-tail unwind","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","AVGO outlook top"],"title_zh":"油价消退下的AI急涨","body_zh":"随着伊朗战争的油价尾部风险消退、临近6月中停火，AI资本开支交易强势回归，科技在再通胀/风险偏好的飙升中急涨约55%（排名第1，SMH +74.4%、成长跑赢价值 +10.9、VIX 31→16）。盘面再度狭窄并由大盘股主导（等权落后 -8.6%）；该上涨腿在6月初见顶，博通拒绝上调全年AI展望引爆超过1万亿美元的半导体市值蒸发——这就是周期晚期的顶部。","drivers_zh":["油价尾部风险消退","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","博通展望见顶"]}},"now_zh":"科技是无可争议的第一板块（相对强度排名第1，+24.3% 对 SPY +6.3%），周期位置约84/100。盘面处于金发姑娘/再通胀的风险偏好状态，由半导体（SMH +67.9%）和高贝塔（+20.7% 对低波）引领，使得防御板块落后（+6.9% 对周期 +11.2%）——但重要的是，这并非狭窄的飙升：等权指数已悄然跑赢市值加权 +2.9%，领涨之下参与度正在扩散。该上涨腿正在筑顶：6月初博通拒绝上调其AI展望，引发超过1万亿美元的半导体市值蒸发——这是成熟、由大盘股主导的飙升行情典型的派发信号，如今正向周期晚期扩散。"},"xle":{"now":"Energy is rolling over as of mid-2026 — RS rank #11, the weakest sector — even though it still sits #2 over the trailing window (+21.5%). The 2026 tape is a tech/semis melt-up (SMH +67.9%, high-beta over low-vol +20.7), and money is rotating into AI growth, not the post-ceasefire oil-tail unwind that is draining the Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz war premium out of crude. The one nuance: oil itself is +20.9% and copper−gold +18.0 with reflation cyclicals (+11.2%) leading defensives (+6.9%) — a reflation-quad backdrop that could re-bid Energy if the AI trade narrows further. For now a strong dollar (+3.4% DXY) is a headwind and XLE is a value-quality income play out of favor in a growth-led tape.","legs":{"2020-10-28":{"title":"Vaccine reflation, energy leads the reopening","body":"XLE roared off pandemic lows as the November 2020 vaccine news ignited the reopening/reflation trade in the most beaten-down sector — Energy ranked #1/11 (+107.7%) in a reflation quad with cyclicals (+48.7%) trouncing defensives (+14.9%), oil +92.9% and copper−gold +43.1. A weaker dollar (−3.1% DXY) was a tailwind and broad participation (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +12.3%) confirmed the rotation. WTI climbed from the low-$30s past $70 by June 2021 on rebounding travel, OPEC+ supply discipline, and the February 2021 Texas freeze that shut in production.","drivers":["reflation quad","risk-on leadership","weak dollar tailwind","OPEC+ discipline"],"title_zh":"疫苗再通胀，能源领涨复工","body_zh":"随着2020年11月疫苗消息在跌幅最深的板块点燃复工/再通胀交易，XLE从疫情低点强劲反弹——能源在再通胀象限中排名第1/11（+107.7%），周期板块（+48.7%）大幅跑赢防御板块（+14.9%），原油+92.9%、铜金比+43.1。美元走弱（−3.1% DXY）形成顺风，市场广度宽阔（等权跑赢市值加权+12.3%）印证了这轮轮动。WTI在出行回升、OPEC+供应纪律以及2021年2月得州寒潮停产推动下，到2021年6月从30美元出头攀升至70美元上方。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","风险偏好领涨","弱美元顺风","OPEC+供应纪律"]},"2021-06-15":{"title":"Delta scare, OPEC+ hike — Energy worst as defensives bid","body":"Crude reversed as OPEC+ agreed in July 2021 to add back 400,000 b/d per month while the Delta variant sparked demand fears, dragging WTI from the mid-$70s toward the high-$60s and making Energy the worst sector (−17.7%, #11). This was a flight-to-safety wobble — defensives (+5.7%) led cyclicals (−1.4%) with VIX 17→22 and yields falling (TLT +6.9%) — plus a strong-dollar headwind (+3.3% DXY); a sentiment repricing, not a fundamental glut, with U.S. inventories still drawing.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","rate regime (yields fell)","strong dollar","OPEC+ output increase"],"title_zh":"Delta惊吓与OPEC+增产——防御被买入，能源垫底","body_zh":"OPEC+于2021年7月同意每月增产40万桶/日，叠加Delta变异株引发需求担忧，原油转跌，WTI从75美元中段跌向60美元后段，能源成为最弱板块（−17.7%，第11）。这是一次避险式震荡——防御板块（+5.7%）跑赢周期板块（−1.4%），VIX 17→22、收益率回落（TLT +6.9%）——叠加强美元逆风（+3.3% DXY）；属情绪重新定价，而非基本面过剩，美国库存仍在去化。","drivers_zh":["避险","利率环境（收益率回落）","强美元","OPEC+增产"]},"2021-08-19":{"title":"Energy crisis + Russia spike — Energy alone vs a rate-regime selloff","body":"A global energy crunch and then Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent Brent above $120 and WTI to ~$127, making Energy the sole leader (+108.6%, #1) while the broad tape was a rate-regime selloff (TLT −23.1% as yields surged) and a strong-dollar (+9.6% DXY) headwind crushed everything else — Tech −8.4%, Comm −26.2%. Sanctions risk, record LNG exports and chronic shale discipline starved the market; XLE was the top sector of 2022 precisely because it inversely benefited from the inflation/rate shock punishing growth.","drivers":["rate regime (yields surged)","Russia-Ukraine invasion","strong dollar","capex discipline + buybacks"],"title_zh":"能源危机+俄油飙升——能源独涨，对抗利率环境抛售","body_zh":"全球能源紧缺，继而2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰，使布伦特升破120美元、WTI升至约127美元，能源成为唯一领涨者（+108.6%，第1）；而大盘是一轮利率环境抛售（收益率飙升，TLT −23.1%），强美元（+9.6% DXY）逆风压垮其他一切——科技−8.4%、通信−26.2%。制裁风险、创纪录LNG出口和长期页岩气供应纪律使市场供应紧张；XLE恰因从惩罚成长的通胀/利率冲击中反向受益，而成为2022年最强板块。","drivers_zh":["利率环境（收益率飙升）","俄乌战争","强美元","资本开支纪律+回购"]},"2022-06-08":{"title":"Recession scare crushes the oil peak","body":"From the June 8 peak crude rolled over hard as aggressive Fed hikes and the largest-ever SPR releases stoked recession and demand-destruction fears, knocking ~$30/bbl off WTI and making Energy the worst sector (−26.0%, #11). This was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad — cyclicals (−13.0%) and Energy itself led the decline while defensives held up far better (−2.3%) in a flight-to-safety — compounded by a strong-dollar (+5.9% DXY) headwind, even as physical fundamentals stayed tight.","drivers":["deflation-scare quad","flight-to-safety","strong dollar","Fed hikes + SPR releases"],"title_zh":"衰退恐慌压垮油价顶部","body_zh":"从6月8日高点起，美联储激进加息与史上最大规模释放战略石油储备加剧衰退和需求破坏担忧，原油大幅回落，WTI下跌约30美元/桶，能源成为最弱板块（−26.0%，第11）。这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限——周期板块（−13.0%）与能源自身领跌，而防御板块在避险中表现稳健得多（−2.3%）——叠加强美元（+5.9% DXY）逆风，即便实物基本面仍紧张。","drivers_zh":["通缩恐慌象限","避险","强美元","美联储加息+释放储备"]},"2022-07-14":{"title":"Tight supply sparks a reflation-quad rebound","body":"Energy bounced back to #1 (+24.6%) as the market refocused on tight supply: OPEC+ delivered only a token 100,000 b/d September hike and Russia throttled then shut Nord Stream gas. The rebound came in a clean reflation/growth-up quad — cyclicals (+11.9%) led defensives (+3.6%), copper−gold +11.1 — with the dollar flat and no flight-to-safety, so Energy led on its own merits rather than as a hedge. Resilient cash flows and buybacks supported XLE even as crude stayed choppy below its June highs.","drivers":["reflation quad","sector-led (not hedge)","tight supply","Nord Stream cuts"],"title_zh":"供应紧张引发再通胀象限反弹","body_zh":"市场重新聚焦供应紧张，能源反弹回到第1（+24.6%）：OPEC+仅象征性宣布9月增产10万桶/日，俄罗斯先限气后切断北溪天然气。这轮反弹处于干净的再通胀/增长上行象限——周期板块（+11.9%）跑赢防御板块（+3.6%），铜金比+11.1——美元持平、无避险情绪，因此能源是凭自身基本面领涨，而非作为对冲。稳健的现金流和回购支撑XLE，即便原油在6月高点下方震荡。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","板块自身领涨（非对冲）","供应紧张","北溪减供"]},"2022-08-29":{"title":"Strong dollar + rate regime hit oil","body":"Energy gave back gains as oil slid on a soaring dollar (+4.8% DXY), the most aggressive Fed tightening in decades (TLT −7.8% as yields surged), and recession fears that overwhelmed tight supply — Energy was worst (−17.4%, #11). It was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with a flight-to-safety tilt: defensives (−5.5%) held up far better than cyclicals (−11.4%) and Energy. Continued SPR releases and softening Chinese demand under COVID lockdowns added pressure, pulling WTI toward the mid-$70s.","drivers":["rate regime (yields surged)","strong dollar","flight-to-safety","Fed hikes + SPR releases"],"title_zh":"强美元+利率环境打压油价","body_zh":"在美元飙升（+4.8% DXY）、数十年来最激进的美联储紧缩（收益率飙升，TLT −7.8%）以及压倒供应紧张的衰退担忧下，油价下滑，能源回吐涨幅并垫底（−17.4%，第11）。这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限并带避险倾向：防御板块（−5.5%）远比周期板块（−11.4%）和能源稳健。持续释放战略石油储备以及中国新冠封控下需求走软增添了压力，将WTI拉向70美元中段。","drivers_zh":["利率环境（收益率飙升）","强美元","避险","美联储加息+释放储备"]},"2022-09-26":{"title":"OPEC+ 2mb/d cut, weak dollar power a reflation bounce","body":"Energy rallied back to #1 (+36.8%) after OPEC+ announced its biggest cut since 2020 — a headline 2 million b/d reduction — to defend prices. The setup was textbook for the sector: a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +16.6% over defensives +4.2%), a weakening dollar (−6.7% DXY) tailwind, and broadening participation (equal-weight beat cap-weight +4.0%). China-reopening hopes added fuel, lifting WTI and powering a sharp XLE recovery into mid-November.","drivers":["reflation quad","weak dollar tailwind","broadening breadth","OPEC+ 2mb/d cut"],"title_zh":"OPEC+减产200万桶、弱美元推动再通胀反弹","body_zh":"OPEC+宣布2020年以来最大幅度减产——名义上削减200万桶/日以捍卫价格，能源反弹回到第1（+36.8%）。这一组合对该板块堪称教科书：再通胀/增长上行象限（周期+16.6%跑赢防御+4.2%）、美元走弱（−6.7% DXY）的顺风，以及市场广度扩张（等权跑赢市值加权+4.0%）。中国重启预期火上浇油，推升WTI，推动XLE在11月中旬前强劲复苏。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","弱美元顺风","市场广度扩张","OPEC+减产200万桶"]},"2022-11-15":{"title":"Demand worry, SVB shock, rate regime flips","body":"Energy faded into early 2023 as weak-demand worries capped crude, then crashed in mid-March when the SVB collapse and Credit Suisse turmoil routed risk assets — WTI tumbled ~12% to near $66, its lowest since December 2021, leaving Energy worst (−17.3%, #11). The rate regime flipped: yields fell hard (TLT +8.7%) on a flight to Treasuries, which rotated money toward duration-sensitive growth (Tech +7.7%, Comm +9.1%) and away from value-cyclical Energy. A credit-instability shock, not a supply story, drove the move.","drivers":["credit shock / risk-off","rate regime (yields fell)","growth over value rotation","SVB banking crisis"],"title_zh":"需求担忧、硅谷银行冲击、利率环境反转","body_zh":"需求疲软担忧压制原油，能源进入2023年初回落，随后在3月中旬硅谷银行倒闭和瑞信动荡冲击风险资产时崩盘——WTI暴跌约12%至接近66美元，为2021年12月以来最低，能源垫底（−17.3%，第11）。利率环境反转：避险买入国债使收益率大幅回落（TLT +8.7%），资金随之轮动进入对久期敏感的成长板块（科技+7.7%、通信+9.1%），离开价值-周期的能源。驱动此轮的是信用不稳定冲击，而非供应因素。","drivers_zh":["信用冲击/风险规避","利率环境（收益率回落）","成长跑赢价值轮动","硅谷银行危机"]},"2023-03-17":{"title":"Range-bound crude lags the AI melt-up","body":"Energy ground higher only +34.2% (#6) over a long stretch — a laggard not because it was broken but because it was starved: this was the tech/semis-led AI melt-up (SMH +96.6%, growth over value +30.3) where Comm +79.3%, Financials +68.8% and Tech +65.1% soaked up the flows, and the dollar firmed (+3.6% DXY) against Energy. OPEC+ Saudi voluntary cuts defended a ~$70-90 Brent band while majors returned record cash (~$114bn in 2023), but a flat oil tape simply couldn't compete with AI for capital.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","starved (out of favor)","strong dollar headwind","OPEC+ Saudi cuts + record buybacks"],"title_zh":"区间震荡的原油跑输AI逼空上涨","body_zh":"能源在漫长阶段中仅缓涨+34.2%（第6）——跑输不是因为它坏了，而是被冷落：这是科技/半导体主导的AI逼空上涨（SMH +96.6%，成长跑赢价值+30.3），通信+79.3%、金融+68.8%、科技+65.1%吸走了资金，美元走强（+3.6% DXY）也对能源不利。沙特自愿减产领衔的OPEC+捍卫约70-90美元布伦特区间，巨头返还创纪录现金（2023年约1140亿美元），但横盘的油价根本无法在资本争夺中与AI抗衡。","drivers_zh":["科技主导的风险偏好","被冷落（失宠）","强美元逆风","OPEC+沙特减产+创纪录回购"]},"2024-11-22":{"title":"Soft oil, OPEC+ delay — narrow mega-cap tape leaves Energy behind","body":"Crude drifted in a narrow ~$73 Brent range as weak Chinese demand and a looming non-OPEC surplus capped prices and OPEC+ delayed unwinding cuts again, leaving Energy worst (−14.3%, #11). The broad tape was narrow and mega-cap-led (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by −4.5%) with growth over value (+9.2), so even as the index barely moved (SPY −1.6%), unloved value-cyclical Energy was left behind. A hawkish December Fed cut added to the overhang.","drivers":["narrow breadth","growth over value","weak demand / OPEC+ delay","hawkish Fed"],"title_zh":"油价疲软、OPEC+推迟——巨头主导的窄幅盘面把能源甩在后面","body_zh":"中国需求疲软和迫近的非OPEC过剩压制价格、OPEC+再度推迟解除减产，原油在约73美元布伦特窄幅区间徘徊，能源垫底（−14.3%，第11）。大盘狭窄且由巨头主导（等权跑输市值加权−4.5%），成长跑赢价值（+9.2），因此即便指数几乎未动（SPY −1.6%），不受待见的价值-周期能源仍被甩在后面。12月美联储鹰派降息加重了隐忧。","drivers_zh":["市场广度狭窄","成长跑赢价值","需求疲软/OPEC+推迟","鹰派美联储"]},"2024-12-19":{"title":"New-year crude rally — Energy leads as growth wobbles","body":"Oil rallied to start 2025, Brent jumping toward a five-month high above $80 on cold-weather demand, fresh Russia sanctions, China-stimulus hopes and inventory draws, and Energy led at #1 (+14.8%) even as SPY fell −3.1%. The rotation favored value: defensives (+5.9%) and Energy beat cyclicals (+1.0%) while growth cracked (semis −10.0%, growth−value −12.5), aided by a falling dollar (−4.2% DXY) tailwind. Producer discipline kept the firmer tape supporting XLE's dividends and buybacks into early April.","drivers":["value over growth rotation","weak dollar tailwind","broadening breadth","winter demand + Russia sanctions"],"title_zh":"新年原油上涨——成长摇摆，能源领涨","body_zh":"2025年开年油价上涨，布伦特在寒冷天气需求、新一轮对俄制裁、中国刺激预期和库存去化推动下跳升至80美元上方的五个月高点；即便SPY下跌−3.1%，能源仍以第1领涨（+14.8%）。轮动偏向价值：防御板块（+5.9%）和能源跑赢周期板块（+1.0%），而成长走弱（半导体−10.0%、成长减价值−12.5），美元下行（−4.2% DXY）形成顺风。生产商纪律使坚挺的盘面支撑XLE的分红和回购直至4月初。","drivers_zh":["价值跑赢成长轮动","弱美元顺风","市场广度扩张","冬季需求+对俄制裁"]},"2025-04-02":{"title":"Liberation Day tariff crash — Energy worst in a panic","body":"Trump's April 2 'reciprocal tariff' shock triggered a global growth and demand scare that slammed crude, with WTI plunging toward $57-60 by April 8 and Energy worst (−18.8%, #11). It was a violent flight-to-safety: VIX spiked 22→52 and defensives (−7.4%) sharply outperformed cyclicals (−14.3%) and Energy as everything sold off. The rout was amplified when OPEC+ stunned the market by tripling its planned May output hike, piling supply onto collapsing demand expectations.","drivers":["flight-to-safety (VIX 22→52)","deflation-scare quad","tariff demand shock","OPEC+ accelerated unwind"],"title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘——恐慌中能源垫底","body_zh":"特朗普4月2日的“对等关税”冲击引发全球增长和需求恐慌，猛烈打压原油，到4月8日WTI暴跌至57-60美元，能源垫底（−18.8%，第11）。这是一次剧烈的避险：VIX飙升22→52，普跌之中防御板块（−7.4%）大幅跑赢周期板块（−14.3%）和能源。当OPEC+出人意料地将其计划中的5月增产幅度增至三倍、向崩塌的需求预期叠加供应时，这轮暴跌被进一步放大。","drivers_zh":["避险（VIX 22→52）","通缩恐慌象限","关税需求冲击","OPEC+加速解除减产"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Iran-Hormuz supershock — Energy leads its own war rally","body":"From the tariff low, crude recovered through 2025 and then exploded in early 2026 when the Iran-Israel war erupted: Brent rocketed from ~$72 toward ~$120 by mid-March 2026 as a Strait-of-Hormuz threat to ~20% of world oil flows handed Energy the #1 spot (+68.9%). This was the rare leg where Energy led not as a hedge but as the catalyst — a reflation quad (oil +67.2%) with a weak-dollar (−2.7% DXY) tailwind, even as semis (+108.6%) and a narrow mega-cap tape ran alongside. War-risk windfall cash flows powered XLE's massive rally into late March (2026 = house view).","drivers":["reflation quad / sector catalyst","weak dollar tailwind","Iran war + Hormuz risk premium","windfall cash flows"],"title_zh":"伊朗-霍尔木兹超级冲击——能源主导自己的战争行情","body_zh":"从关税低点起，原油在2025年逐步复苏，随后在2026年初伊朗-以色列战争爆发时暴涨：霍尔木兹海峡威胁到全球约20%的石油流动，使布伦特到2026年3月中旬从约72美元飙升至约120美元，能源因此登上第1（+68.9%）。这是少见的一段——能源不是作为对冲、而是作为催化剂领涨——处于再通胀象限（原油+67.2%）并伴随弱美元（−2.7% DXY）顺风，尽管同期半导体（+108.6%）与狭窄的巨头盘面并行。战争风险带来的超额现金流推动XLE在3月底前大幅上涨（2026年为本站观点）。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限/板块催化","弱美元顺风","伊朗战争+霍尔木兹风险溢价","超额现金流"]},"2026-03-27":{"title":"Ceasefire unwinds the oil premium as semis melt up","body":"Energy rolled over to worst (−14.7%, #11) as the war-risk premium drained out of crude — a mid-June 2026 ceasefire and Hormuz-reopening hopes sent oil tumbling (oil −23.1%) and WTI back below ~$70. The pain was doubled by where the money went: a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +76.3%, Tech +47.2%) in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight lagged by −6.8%) pulled flows into AI growth and out of value-cyclical Energy. With the 'oil tail' priced out and Middle East supply returning, XLE gave back its war-driven gains (house view).","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","starved (out of favor)","narrow breadth","ceasefire / risk-premium drain"],"title_zh":"停火解除油价溢价，半导体逼空上涨","body_zh":"随着战争风险溢价从原油中抽干，能源见顶垫底（−14.7%，第11）——2026年6月中旬的停火以及霍尔木兹重新开放预期使油价大跌（原油−23.1%），WTI回落至约70美元下方。资金去向令痛苦加倍：科技/半导体主导的风险偏好逼空上涨（SMH +76.3%、科技+47.2%）发生在狭窄的巨头盘面中（等权跑输−6.8%），将资金拉入AI成长、抽离价值-周期的能源。在“油价尾部风险”被定价剔除、中东供应回归的情况下，XLE回吐了战争驱动的涨幅（本站观点）。","drivers_zh":["科技主导的风险偏好","被冷落（失宠）","市场广度狭窄","停火/风险溢价抽干"]}},"now_zh":"截至2026年年中，能源板块正在见顶回落——相对强度排名第11，为最弱板块——尽管在过去窗口仍排名第2（+21.5%）。2026年的盘面是科技/半导体的逼空式上涨（SMH +67.9%，高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7），资金正轮动进入AI成长，而非源于停火后油价尾部风险解除、正从原油中抽干伊朗/霍尔木兹海峡战争溢价。一个细微之处：原油本身+20.9%、铜金比+18.0，再通胀型周期板块（+11.2%）跑赢防御板块（+6.9%）——这是一个再通胀象限的背景，若AI交易进一步收窄、市场广度变窄，可能重新青睐能源。眼下强美元（+3.4% DXY）构成逆风，在成长主导的盘面里，XLE是被冷落的价值-质量型分红资产。"},"xlf":{"now":"Trending, RS#5 (pos~51) but a near-term laggard at -2.7% (rank 9/11) — the leadership is a narrow, semis-led tape (SMH +67.9%) where capital flows into Tech/Energy/Industrials and leave cyclical-value banks behind. The macro is constructive underneath: a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, copper-gold +18.0, oil +20.9%), broadening participation (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight) and growth-minus-value -15.2% — a value-friendly backdrop banks usually lead in. Deregulation, the M&A/capital-markets revival and stable NIM are the bull case; a 2026 hiking bias, a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) and credit-cost watch cap the upside. XLF isn't broken — it's out of favor in a mega-cap melt-up, and a rotation back to value/breadth is the turn to watch.","legs":{"2020-06-26":{"title":"Reflation rally — banks lead the cycle","body":"Financials rode the post-COVID reopening to the #1 spot of all 11 sectors (+88.7%) in a textbook reflation/growth-up quad — cyclicals +73.8% vs defensives +38.3%, oil +114.7%, copper-gold +67.7. A steepening curve and surging long yields (TLT -11.5%) widened net interest margins while reserve releases and buybacks lifted EPS; a weak dollar (-2.6% DXY) and broad participation (equal-weight +8.5% over cap-weight, VIX 35→18) confirmed banks were leading risk-on, not riding it.","drivers":["reflation quad","risk-on leader #1","steepening curve / NIM","broad participation"],"title_zh":"再通胀上涨——银行领跑周期","body_zh":"金融板块乘着疫情后复工东风，在标准的再通胀/增长上行象限中登上全部11个板块的第1名（+88.7%）——周期股+73.8% vs 防御股+38.3%，油价+114.7%，铜金比+67.7。曲线变陡和长端收益率飙升（TLT -11.5%）扩大了净息差，准备金释放和回购提振每股收益；弱势美元（-2.6% DXY）和广泛参与（等权重领先市值加权+8.5%，VIX 35→18）印证了银行在领涨风险偏好，而非被动跟涨。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","风险偏好领涨第1","曲线变陡/净息差","广泛参与"]},"2022-01-12":{"title":"Hawkish pivot — flight-to-safety hits banks","body":"As the Fed pivoted hawkish into 9% CPI, the tape flipped to flight-to-safety (defensives -8.9% vs cyclicals -16.1%, VIX 18→33) inside a stagflation-ish quad. Banks fell -25.3% but only ranked #8/11 — geared to growth and credit, they held up far better than Tech (-26.7%) and Discretionary (-33.1%). A violent rate-regime move (TLT -21.3%) and a +9.1% DXY spike were the macro drivers; investors looked past higher NIM to peaking margins and a frozen IPO/IB-fee pipeline.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","rate regime (TLT -21%)","strong dollar","IB fee drought"],"title_zh":"鹰派转向——避险情绪打击银行","body_zh":"随着美联储在9% CPI下转向鹰派，行情切换为避险（防御股-8.9% vs 周期股-16.1%，VIX 18→33），处于偏滞胀象限。银行下跌-25.3%，但仅排名11档中第8——与增长和信用挂钩的它们远比科技（-26.7%）和可选消费（-33.1%）抗跌。剧烈的利率象限切换（TLT -21.3%）和美元跳升+9.1%是宏观驱动；投资者越过更高的净息差，看到息差见顶和冻结的IPO/投行手续费管道。","drivers_zh":["避险","利率象限切换(TLT -21%)","强势美元","投行手续费枯竭"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Tech-led bounce — banks a follower","body":"Banks rebounded +16.7% with the broad market as a softer inflation print sparked a summer relief rally, but this was a tech/semis-led risk-on move (SMH +19.5%, growth>value +8.8, VIX 33→20) and XLF only ranked #6/11 — a follower, not a leader. Long yields actually eased back over the leg (TLT +4.2%), so the move was a growth-led rebound, not a rate-driven NIM story; a +2.8% DXY and the goldilocks/disinflation flavor favored growth names over value banks. It was a bear-market bounce, not a credit all-clear.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","relief rally","yields eased (TLT +4%)","follower not leader"],"title_zh":"科技领涨反弹——银行跟随","body_zh":"随着偏软的通胀数据点燃夏季纾解上涨，银行随大盘反弹+16.7%，但这是由科技/半导体主导的风险偏好行情（SMH +19.5%，成长>价值+8.8，VIX 33→20），XLF仅排名11档中第6——是跟随者而非领涨者。这一段长端收益率实际回落（TLT +4.2%），因此这是成长主导的反弹，而非利率驱动的净息差行情；+2.8% DXY和金发姑娘/去通胀的味道更利好成长股而非价值类银行。这是熊市反弹，而非信用风险解除。","drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好","纾解反弹","收益率回落(TLT +4%)","跟随非领涨"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole reset — rate-regime selloff","body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole message ended the summer bounce and reignited a rate-regime selloff: long yields surged again (TLT -13.0%) and the dollar ripped +6.4% inside a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 20→34). Banks fell -15.0% but ranked #4/11 — recession and credit-cost fears returned as provisions climbed, yet financials held up better than rate-sensitive names like Real Estate (-24.7%) and Tech (-22.7%).","drivers":["rate regime (TLT -13%)","strong dollar","deflation-scare quad","rising provisions"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重置——利率象限抛售","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔信息终结了夏季反弹，重新点燃利率象限抛售：长端收益率再度飙升（TLT -13.0%），美元在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中飙升+6.4%（VIX 20→34）。银行下跌-15.0%，但排名11档中第4——随着计提攀升，衰退和信用成本担忧卷土重来，但金融板块比房地产（-24.7%）、科技（-22.7%）等利率敏感板块更抗跌。","drivers_zh":["利率象限(TLT -13%)","强势美元","通缩恐慌象限","计提上升"]},"2022-10-12":{"title":"Peak-rate rally — value-friendly reflation","body":"Banks rallied +22.9% off the October low to rank #3/11 as cooling CPI and peak-Fed hopes lifted risk assets in a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +18.6% vs defensives +10.2%). A sharply weaker dollar (-8.7% DXY) and broad participation (equal-weight +3.3%, VIX 34→19) made this a value-friendly turn financials could lead, with resilient NIM and better-than-feared Q3/Q4 earnings adding fuel.","drivers":["reflation quad","weak dollar tailwind","broad participation","earnings beats"],"title_zh":"利率见顶上涨——利好价值的再通胀","body_zh":"随着降温的CPI和美联储见顶预期在再通胀/增长上行象限中提振风险资产（周期股+18.6% vs 防御股+10.2%），银行从10月低点反弹+22.9%，排名11档中第3。大幅走弱的美元（-8.7% DXY）和广泛参与（等权重+3.3%，VIX 34→19）让这成为银行能够领涨的利好价值拐点，稳健的净息差和好于担忧的三/四季度业绩添柴加薪。","drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","弱势美元顺风","广泛参与","业绩超预期"]},"2023-02-07":{"title":"SVB crisis — XLF the lone casualty","body":"The collapse of Silicon Valley Bank and Signature triggered the worst bank panic since 2008. This was idiosyncratic, not a macro de-risk: XLF fell -16.3% and ranked dead last #11/11 while Tech was essentially flat (-0.1%) and the broad selloff was mild (SPY -5.7%). Defensives outperformed (-3.0% vs cyclicals -8.6%) and breadth narrowed (-4.3%) as deposit flight, unrealized bond losses and funding stress crushed regionals — until the Fed's BTFP and rescues stemmed the run.","drivers":["sector-specific shock","worst sector #11","deposit flight / unrealized losses","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"硅谷银行危机——XLF独自受灾","body_zh":"硅谷银行和签名银行的倒闭引发2008年以来最严重的银行恐慌。这是特异性事件而非宏观去风险：XLF下跌-16.3%，垫底排名11档中第11，而科技基本持平（-0.1%），大盘抛售温和（SPY -5.7%）。防御股跑赢（-3.0% vs 周期股-8.6%），市场广度收窄（-4.3%），存款外流、未实现债券损失和融资压力压垮区域银行——直到美联储的BTFP工具和救助遏制挤兑。","drivers_zh":["板块特异冲击","最差板块第11","存款外流/未实现损失","市场广度收窄"]},"2023-03-17":{"title":"Crisis fades — deregulation trade, banks #2","body":"Once contagion was contained, financials embarked on a +74.4% rally to rank #2/11 even inside a narrow, mega-cap melt-up (semis +107.8%, equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -24.1%). Banks rode a rate-regime tailwind — long yields surged (TLT -11.2%), supporting NIM — alongside a stronger dollar (+3.3% DXY) and the reflation quad. The 2024 soft landing, the Fed's September cut and the Trump-election deregulation/M&A 'bank trade' powered the move into early 2025.","drivers":["risk-on leader #2","rate regime (TLT -11%)","Trump deregulation / M&A","narrow breadth backdrop"],"title_zh":"危机消退——放松监管交易，银行排名第2","body_zh":"在传染得到遏制后，金融板块开启+74.4%的上涨，即便在狭窄的大型股熔涨中（半导体+107.8%，等权重落后市值加权-24.1%）仍排名11档中第2。银行借力利率象限顺风——长端收益率飙升（TLT -11.2%）支撑净息差——以及更强的美元（+3.3% DXY）和再通胀象限。2024年的软着陆、美联储9月降息以及特朗普当选的放松监管/并购\"银行交易\"，推动行情直至2025年初。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好领涨第2","利率象限(TLT -11%)","特朗普放松监管/并购","狭窄广度背景"]},"2025-02-19":{"title":"Tariff-crash risk-off — banks hold up","body":"Financials slid -15.5% into the April reciprocal-tariff crash, a sharp flight-to-safety event (defensives -7.7% vs cyclicals -18.7%, VIX spiking 15→52) inside a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Yet XLF ranked #5/11 — geared to growth and credit, banks held up better than Tech (-25.7%) as breadth actually broadened (+2.8%) and the dollar weakened (-3.9% DXY), before the April-8/9 tariff-pause low.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","VIX 15→52","deflation-scare quad","relative resilience #5"],"title_zh":"关税崩盘风险规避——银行抗跌","body_zh":"金融板块下滑-15.5%，滑入4月的对等关税崩盘，这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限中的剧烈避险事件（防御股-7.7% vs 周期股-18.7%，VIX从15飙升至52）。但XLF排名11档中第5——与增长和信用挂钩的银行比科技（-25.7%）更抗跌，期间市场广度实际扩张（+2.8%），美元走弱（-3.9% DXY），直至4月8/9日关税暂缓低点。","drivers_zh":["避险","VIX 15→52","通缩恐慌象限","相对抗跌第5"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery — but starved by the semis melt-up","body":"Off the tariff-pause low banks rallied +29.7% on deregulation, a capital-markets revival and a wave of megadeal M&A that revived IB fees — yet XLF ranked only #6/11. This was a narrow, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +116.1%, equal-weight lagged by -10.1%, growth>value +17.3) in a goldilocks/disinflation quad: value banks weren't broken, they were starved as flows chased Tech (+63.9%). A weaker dollar (-4.3% DXY) rounded out the backdrop.","drivers":["starved by semis melt-up","narrow breadth","deregulation / M&A","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"复苏——但被半导体熔涨冷落","body_zh":"从关税暂缓低点起，银行凭借放松监管、资本市场复兴以及重振投行手续费的一波巨型并购浪潮上涨+29.7%——但XLF仅排名11档中第6。这是金发姑娘/去通胀象限中由半导体主导的狭窄风险偏好熔涨（SMH +116.1%，等权重落后-10.1%，成长>价值+17.3）：价值类银行并未走坏，只是在资金追逐科技（+63.9%）时被冷落。走弱的美元（-4.3% DXY）补全了背景。","drivers_zh":["被半导体熔涨冷落","市场广度狭窄","放松监管/并购","金发姑娘象限"]},"2026-01-06":{"title":"Oil shock — stagflation hits banks hardest","body":"The Iran/Hormuz oil shock pushed CPI to ~4.2% and flipped the Fed to a hiking bias, lifting the dollar (+1.6% DXY) into a stagflation-ish quad (oil +74.4%). XLF fell -14.8% and ranked dead last #11/11 — even as breadth broadened (+4.2%) toward Energy (+38.0%) and defensives, growth-geared banks bore the brunt of renewed recession/credit-cost fears despite healthy NIM, with deregulation and deal flow only cushioning the pullback.","drivers":["stagflation quad / oil shock","worst sector #11","Fed hiking bias","credit caution"],"title_zh":"油价冲击——滞胀对银行打击最重","body_zh":"伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击将CPI推升至约4.2%，使美联储转向加息倾向，在偏滞胀象限中推升美元（+1.6% DXY，油价+74.4%）。XLF下跌-14.8%，垫底排名11档中第11——即便市场广度向能源（+38.0%）和防御股扩张（+4.2%），尽管净息差健康，与增长挂钩的银行仍首当其冲承受重燃的衰退/信用成本担忧，放松监管和交易流仅缓冲了回调。","drivers_zh":["滞胀象限/油价冲击","最差板块第11","美联储加息倾向","信用谨慎"]}},"now_zh":"处于趋势阶段，相对强度排名第5（位置约51），但短期落后，回报-2.7%（排名11档中第9）——当前领涨是由半导体主导的狭窄行情（SMH +67.9%），资金涌入科技/能源/工业，把周期性价值类的银行甩在后面。底层宏观其实是建设性的：再通胀/增长上行象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，铜金比+18.0，油价+20.9%）、市场广度扩张（等权重领先市值加权+2.9%）、成长减价值为-15.2%——这通常是银行领跑的利好价值环境。放松监管、并购/资本市场复兴和稳定的净息差是多头逻辑；2026年的加息倾向、走强的美元（+3.4% DXY）和信用成本警示限制上行空间。XLF并未走坏——只是在大型股熔涨中被冷落，重回价值/广度的板块轮动是值得关注的拐点。"},"xlre":{"now":"Topping, RS#5 (pos~81) — REITs are +12.1% YTD but middle-of-the-pack as money chases the semis melt-up (SMH +67.9%, high-beta beat low-vol by +21pts), starving the low-vol duration trade. The 2026 oil-shock inflation, a Fed hiking bias and a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) cap the bond proxy, though firmer breadth (equal-weight +2.9% vs cap-weight) hints the late-cycle rotation could broaden back toward yield plays if long rates roll over.","legs":{"2021-12-31":{"title":"Rate-shock derating leads the tape down","body":"The Fed's hawkish turn against 9% CPI sent the 10Y surging (TLT −7.6%), and as the textbook rate-regime move it hammered the long-duration bond proxy first — REITs fell −15.1%, the worst defensive. This was a rate selloff, not a flight-to-safety: defensives actually lagged cyclicals (−7.4% vs −5.4%) with VIX 17→31, because rising discount rates compressed property valuations and made REIT yields uncompetitive versus Treasuries.","drivers":["rate regime","duration hit","valuation compression","reflation quad"],"title_zh":"利率冲击下修领跌大盘","body_zh":"美联储在9% CPI下转向鹰派使10年期收益率飙升（TLT −7.6%），作为典型的利率象限走势，它首当其冲地重创了长久期债券替代品——REIT下跌−15.1%，是表现最差的防御板块。这是一轮利率抛售，而非避险：防御股实际跑输周期股（−7.4% vs −5.4%），VIX由17升至31，因上升的贴现率压缩了房产估值，并使REIT收益率相对国债失去竞争力。","drivers_zh":["利率象限","久期受挫","估值压缩","再通胀象限"]},"2022-02-23":{"title":"Defensive rate-pause bounce, #3 sector","body":"With yields briefly stabilizing and inflation fears pausing, buyers rotated into beaten-down real assets — REITs bounced +15.7% (rank #3), behind only Energy and Utilities as defensives led cyclicals (+12.7% vs +7.9%) and semis stayed in the doghouse (SMH −4.2%). This was a value-over-growth, stagflation-quad relief move, but the bigger picture stayed bearish: the dollar firmed (+4.4% DXY) and the 10Y kept climbing (TLT −10.7%), capping the counter-trend rebound.","drivers":["defensive rotation","relief rally","rate pause","stagflation quad"],"title_zh":"防御性利率暂停反弹，板块第3","body_zh":"随着收益率短暂企稳、通胀担忧暂歇，买盘轮入被打压的实物资产——REIT反弹+15.7%（排名第3），仅次于能源和公用事业，防御股领先周期股（+12.7% vs +7.9%），半导体仍遭冷落（SMH −4.2%）。这是一轮价值跑赢成长的滞胀象限纾解走势，但大格局仍偏空：美元走强（DXY +4.4%）、10年期收益率续升（TLT −10.7%），封住了这轮逆势回升。","drivers_zh":["板块轮动","纾解反弹","利率暂停","滞胀象限"]},"2022-04-20":{"title":"Fastest hiking crushes the duration trade","body":"As the Fed accelerated hikes and the 10Y surged (TLT −7.8%), the long-duration bond proxy sold off −23.2% into the June low — rank #10, worse even than other defensives (−14.5% avg). Higher cap rates compressed property values, a strong dollar (+3.2% DXY) added a stagflation-quad headwind, and recession fears deepened the de-rating as VIX climbed 20→33.","drivers":["rate regime","cap-rate rise","strong dollar","stagflation quad"],"title_zh":"最快加息压垮久期交易","body_zh":"随着美联储加速加息、10年期收益率飙升（TLT −7.8%），长久期债券替代品抛售−23.2%至6月低点——排名第10，甚至弱于其他防御板块（平均−14.5%）。更高的资本化率压缩了房产价值，强势美元（DXY +3.2%）叠加滞胀象限逆风，衰退担忧随VIX由20升至33而加深了估值下修。","drivers_zh":["利率象限","资本化率上升","强势美元","滞胀象限"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-Fed relief in a semis-led bounce","body":"REITs rallied +18.7% (rank #4) as rates pulled back from the June peak (TLT +3.7%) on softer-inflation hopes. But the leadership belonged to the risk-on melt-up — semis +20.8%, growth>value, VIX 33→20 — so the bond proxy rode a goldilocks-quad relief rather than leading; falling yields, not sector strength, lifted rate-sensitive real estate off its lows.","drivers":["yield pullback","tech-led risk-on","duration relief","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"美联储见顶纾解，半导体领涨的反弹","body_zh":"随着利率因偏软的通胀预期从6月高点回落（TLT +3.7%），REIT上涨+18.7%（排名第4）。但领涨权属于风险偏好熔涨——半导体+20.8%、成长跑赢价值、VIX由33降至20——因此债券替代品是搭上了金发女孩象限的纾解,而非领涨;是收益率回落而非板块自身强势，将利率敏感的房地产从低点托起。","drivers_zh":["收益率回落","科技领涨风险偏好","久期缓解","金发女孩象限"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Jackson Hole yield surge, worst sector","body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole and a renewed climb in Treasury yields (TLT −14.2%) drove the bond proxy to fresh lows — REITs fell −25.5%, the single worst sector (#11). A surging dollar (+6.3% DXY) deepened the slowdown/deflation-scare quad, and the near one-for-one inverse link between REITs and the 10Y carried the drawdown into October even as VIX rose 20→32.","drivers":["hawkish Powell","rate regime","strong dollar","rate sensitivity"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔收益率飙升，最差板块","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔讲话和美债收益率的新一轮攀升（TLT −14.2%），将债券替代品推向新低——REIT下跌−25.5%，是唯一最差板块（第11）。飙升的美元（DXY +6.3%）加深了放缓/通缩恐慌象限，REIT与10年期之间近乎一对一的反向关联将回撤延续至10月，其间VIX由20升至32。","drivers_zh":["鹰派鲍威尔","利率象限","强势美元","利率敏感性"]},"2022-10-14":{"title":"Disinflation pivot snaps the duration trade higher","body":"Cooling CPI sparked peak-rate hopes and yields fell hard (TLT +11.0%), so the duration-sensitive bond proxy roared back +25.3% (rank #2). A collapsing dollar (−10.2% DXY) and broadening tape (equal-weight +4.3%) drove a goldilocks-quad recovery, and discount-rate fears eased as VIX fell 32→19 into early 2023.","drivers":["disinflation hopes","rate regime","broadening breadth","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"去通胀转向带动久期交易飙升","body_zh":"降温的CPI点燃利率见顶预期、收益率大幅回落（TLT +11.0%），久期敏感的债券替代品强势反弹+25.3%（排名第2）。崩塌的美元（DXY −10.2%）与扩张的市场广度（等权重 +4.3%）驱动了金发女孩象限的复苏，贴现率担忧随VIX由32降至19而缓解，直至2023年初。","drivers_zh":["去通胀预期","利率象限","市场广度扩张","金发女孩象限"]},"2023-02-02":{"title":"Yields grind higher, the lone laggard","body":"As the 10Y ground toward its October-2023 peak (TLT −21.3%), the bond proxy slid −21.1% — dead-last (#11) while SPY was flat and semis rose, a textbook rate-regime divergence. A narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight lagged by −12.7%) and a firmer dollar (+4.7% DXY) starved real estate of flows, and office-distress/work-from-home headlines weighed on sentiment even as office was a small index slice; the sector bottomed in late October.","drivers":["rate regime","narrow breadth","office distress","duration drag"],"title_zh":"收益率磨升，唯一的落后者","body_zh":"随着10年期向2023年10月峰值缓步磨升（TLT −21.3%），债券替代品下滑−21.1%——垫底（第11），其间SPY持平、半导体上涨，是典型的利率象限背离。狭窄的大型股行情（等权重落后−12.7%）和走强的美元（DXY +4.7%）使房地产资金枯竭，办公楼困境与居家办公的头条拖累情绪——即便办公楼只是指数中的一小部分；该板块在10月底触底。","drivers_zh":["利率象限","市场广度狭窄","办公楼困境","久期拖累"]},"2023-10-25":{"title":"Rate-cut pivot revives the bond proxy","body":"Disinflation and the Fed's 2024 pivot lowered yields (TLT +16.3%), reviving the duration trade and lifting REITs +45.4% off the yield peak. The rally trailed the semis-led melt-up (SMH +72.8%) in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight −5.1%), but AI-datacenter demand and resilient industrial/healthcare names led the sector, with the September-2024 cut and election-year optimism extending a goldilocks-quad recovery as VIX fell 20→14.","drivers":["rate-cut pivot","rate regime","AI datacenters","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"降息转向重振债券替代品","body_zh":"去通胀和美联储2024年的政策转向压低收益率（TLT +16.3%），重振久期交易，使REIT从收益率峰值反弹+45.4%。在狭窄的大型股行情（等权重 −5.1%）中，这轮上涨落后于半导体领涨的熔涨（SMH +72.8%），但AI数据中心需求和坚韧的工业/医疗标的领涨板块，2024年9月的降息和大选年乐观情绪延续了金发女孩象限的复苏，VIX由20降至14。","drivers_zh":["降息转向","利率象限","AI数据中心","金发女孩象限"]},"2024-11-27":{"title":"Yields rebound, then tariff flight-to-safety","body":"Post-election yields backed up and the 10Y returned toward mid-2024 highs (TLT −3.3%), undoing the duration tailwind. The April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash then dragged the sector to its April-8 low — but as a defensive REITs cushioned the blow (−16.6%, rank #6), with defensives down only −8.6% versus cyclicals −18.7% in a true flight-to-safety as VIX exploded 14→52.","drivers":["yields rebound","duration headwind","flight-to-safety","tariff crash"],"title_zh":"收益率回升，继而关税避险","body_zh":"大选后收益率回升、10年期重回2024年年中高位（TLT −3.3%），抵消了久期顺风。随后2025年4月的对等关税崩盘将板块拖向4月8日低点——但作为防御资产，REIT缓冲了冲击（−16.6%，排名第6），在真正的避险中防御股仅跌−8.6%、周期股跌−18.7%，其间VIX由14爆升至52。","drivers_zh":["收益率回升","久期逆风","避险","关税崩盘"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery starved by the semis melt-up","body":"REITs recovered +26.2% off the tariff-pause low on easing rates and durable AI-datacenter/industrial demand — but it was a middling rank #7, badly lagging the risk-on melt-up: semis ripped +240.9% and high-beta beat low-vol by +111pts, draining flows from the low-vol bond proxy. By 2026 the Iran/Hormuz oil shock, ~4.2% CPI and a Fed hiking bias capped the rally in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight −8.7%), leaving the rate-sensitive sector topping.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","defensives starved","oil-shock inflation","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"复苏被半导体熔涨冷落","body_zh":"REIT凭借利率缓解和持久的AI数据中心/工业需求，从关税暂缓低点复苏+26.2%——但仅排名第7，大幅落后于风险偏好熔涨：半导体狂飙+240.9%、高贝塔跑赢低波动+111个百分点，抽走了低波动债券替代品的资金。到2026年，伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击、约4.2%的CPI和美联储加息倾向在狭窄的大型股行情（等权重 −8.7%）中封住了涨势，使这个利率敏感的板块筑顶。","drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好","防御股被冷落","油价冲击通胀","市场广度狭窄"]}},"now_zh":"正在筑顶，相对强度排名第5（位置约81）——REIT年初至今+12.1%，但表现居中，因资金追逐半导体熔涨（SMH +67.9%，高贝塔跑赢低波动+21个百分点），冷落了低波动的久期交易。2026年的油价冲击通胀、美联储加息倾向和走强的美元（DXY +3.4%）封住了这个债券替代品，不过市场广度回暖（等权重 +2.9% 跑赢市值加权）暗示，若长端利率回落，周期晚期的板块轮动可能重新转向收益类资产。"},"xli":{"now":"Trending up (RS#2 leader) — reshoring, defense, and AI-power/datacenter electrification capex keep XLI a genuine #2 leader (+15.8%) even as the 2026 tape is the narrowest in the cycle: high-beta has crushed low-vol by +20.7% and growth lags value by −15.2%, so this is broad-cyclical leadership, not a mega-cap melt-up — equal-weight is actually beating cap-weight (+2.9%). The reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals 11.2% vs defensives 6.9%, oil +20.9%, copper−gold +18.0) and a +3.4% DXY favor domestic industrial demand over multinationals; watch ISM and whether the semis bid (+67.9%) keeps capex flowing.","legs":{"2022-01-04":{"title":"Fed liftoff: rate-regime de-rate, money flees to safety","body":"Industrials de-rated hard (−19.8%) as the Fed pivoted to aggressive hiking — a rate-regime shock that crushed long-duration assets (TLT −21.4%) and a strong dollar (+8.7% DXY) that hit the multinational revenue base. This was a flight-to-safety rotation, not sector strength: defensives (−10.4%) outran cyclicals (−16.3%) as VIX ran 17→31. Caterpillar warned in late April that China COVID lockdowns would crimp demand, ISM rolled over, and Russia-Ukraine spiked input/energy costs into a stagflation quad (oil +42.3%).","drivers":["rate regime","flight-to-safety","strong dollar","China lockdowns / stagflation quad"],"title_zh":"美联储启动加息：利率体制杀估值，资金避险","body_zh":"随着美联储转向激进加息，工业股大幅杀估值（−19.8%）——这是一次利率体制冲击，重创长久期资产（TLT −21.4%），强势美元（+8.7% DXY）则打击跨国企业的营收基础。这是一次避险轮动而非板块走强：防御股（−10.4%）跑赢周期股（−16.3%），VIX由17升至31。卡特彼勒在4月底警告中国新冠封控将抑制需求，ISM见顶回落，俄乌冲突在滞胀象限中推高投入与能源成本（油价+42.3%）。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","避险轮动","强势美元","中国封控/滞胀象限"]},"2022-06-17":{"title":"Peak-inflation bounce in a semis-led risk-on tape","body":"Industrials rallied +18.0% off the June low on 'peak inflation' optimism and Fed-pivot hopes, but they were a passenger (rank #4), not the engine: this was a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +18.5%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 31→20) that pulled flows into high-beta, with discretionary and tech out front. July industrial production rose and ISM held in expansion, while aerospace/defense added support as Boeing deliveries recovered and the Ukraine war underpinned a multi-year defense tailwind — a goldilocks quad as oil rolled over (−21.0%).","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","peak-inflation hope / Fed pivot bets","resilient production","defense tailwind / goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"半导体领涨风险偏好行情中的“通胀见顶”反弹","body_zh":"工业股在6月低点反弹+18.0%，受益于“通胀见顶”乐观情绪与美联储转向预期，但它只是搭车者（排名第4）而非引擎：这是一次半导体领涨的风险偏好融涨（SMH +18.5%、成长跑赢价值+7.2、VIX由31降至20），资金涌入高贝塔，可选消费与科技领跑。7月工业生产回升、ISM维持扩张，航空航天/国防形成支撑——波音交付量回升，乌克兰战争奠定多年期国防顺风——油价回落（−21.0%）构成金发姑娘象限。","drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好","通胀见顶预期/美联储转向押注","生产韧性","国防顺风/金发姑娘象限"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole, FedEx warning, rate-regime selloff","body":"The bounce reversed (−17.2%) as Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole killed pivot hopes and a hot CPI drove another 75bp hike — a rate-regime selloff (TLT −11.4%) with a strong dollar (+5.3% DXY) headwind in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil −8.1%, VIX 20→32). The sector-specific gut-punch was FedEx pulling guidance and warning of a 'worldwide recession' — a ~21% one-day crash that hammered transports and signaled collapsing global freight, sinking XLI even as the broad selloff was indiscriminate (defensives −12.4% barely beat cyclicals −15.3%).","drivers":["rate regime","Jackson Hole hawkish / hot CPI","FedEx recession warning","strong dollar / slowdown quad"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔、联邦快递预警、利率体制抛售","body_zh":"反弹随后逆转（−17.2%）：鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派表态浇灭转向预期，高企的CPI促使美联储再加息75个基点——这是一次利率体制抛售（TLT −11.4%），强势美元（+5.3% DXY）在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中构成逆风（油价−8.1%，VIX由20升至32）。板块层面的重击来自联邦快递撤回指引并警告“全球衰退”——单日暴跌约21%，重创运输股、预示全球货运崩塌，拖累XLI；不过此次广泛抛售几乎无差别（防御股−12.4%仅略胜周期股−15.3%）。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","杰克逊霍尔鹰派/CPI高企","联邦快递衰退预警","强势美元/放缓象限"]},"2022-09-30":{"title":"Soft landing + AI capex: cyclicals lead, but breadth narrows","body":"XLI rode a soft-landing macro and a capex super-cycle to +79.5%, the #3 sector, in a tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +166.2%, growth>value +38.9, VIX 32→14) with a weaker dollar (−5.7% DXY) tailwind — though leadership narrowed sharply (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by −21.2%). Aerospace recovered hard (GE Aerospace, RTX) on record backlogs and rising defense budgets, while reshoring tailwinds from CHIPS/IIJA lifted machinery (Caterpillar, Deere) and electrical-equipment names tied to early AI/datacenter electrification. The Fed's first cuts (Sep 2024) plus the Nov election sparked a cyclical 'Trump trade' into a goldilocks quad.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on / narrow breadth","aerospace/defense backlogs","reshoring + CHIPS/IIJA capex","Fed cuts + Trump-trade rotation"],"title_zh":"软着陆+AI资本开支：周期股领涨，但广度收窄","body_zh":"工业股乘着软着陆宏观与资本开支超级周期上行+79.5%，位列第3，处于半导体领涨的风险偏好体制（SMH +166.2%、成长跑赢价值+38.9、VIX由32降至14），并享美元走弱（−5.7% DXY）的顺风——但领涨明显收窄（等权落后市值加权−21.2%）。航空航天强劲复苏（GE航空航天、RTX）受订单积压创纪录与国防预算上升驱动，CHIPS法案/IIJA的回流顺风提振机械（卡特彼勒、迪尔）及与早期AI/数据中心电气化挂钩的电气设备公司。美联储首次降息（2024年9月）叠加11月大选，在金发姑娘象限中点燃周期性“特朗普交易”。","drivers_zh":["科技领涨/市场广度狭窄","航空航天/国防订单积压","回流+CHIPS/IIJA资本开支","美联储降息+特朗普交易轮动"]},"2024-11-29":{"title":"Reciprocal tariffs gut supply chains, money flees to safety","body":"Trump's April 2025 'reciprocal' tariffs cratered industrials −18.5% into an April 8 low, with big China-exporting cyclicals leading the Dow down — Boeing fell ~9% and Caterpillar ~6% in two days. This was a flight-to-safety rotation as VIX spiked 14→52: defensives (−8.9%) sharply outran cyclicals (−19.2%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil −12.4%). Industrials' globalized supply chains and machinery/aerospace input costs made the sector a clear casualty even as a weaker dollar (−2.6% DXY) offered no offset.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","April reciprocal tariffs","Boeing/Caterpillar supply-chain hit","growth fears / slowdown quad"],"title_zh":"对等关税冲击供应链，资金涌向避险","body_zh":"特朗普2025年4月的“对等”关税将工业股打入4月8日低点（−18.5%），对华出口占比高的大型周期股领跌道指——波音两日内跌约9%、卡特彼勒跌约6%。这是一次避险轮动，VIX由14飙升至52：在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中，防御股（−8.9%）大幅跑赢周期股（−19.2%，油价−12.4%）。工业板块全球化的供应链以及机械/航空航天的投入成本使其成为明显的受害者，即便美元走弱（−2.6% DXY）也未能提供缓冲。","drivers_zh":["避险轮动","4月对等关税","波音/卡特彼勒供应链受挫","增长担忧/放缓象限"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Industrials lead the rebound — a true #2, not just a passenger","body":"Off the April low industrials surged +60.3% as a genuine #2 leader, powered by aerospace/defense (GE Aerospace, RTX) and the AI-power/datacenter electrification capex boom — GE Vernova and Eaton riding a transformer/switchgear shortage — alongside bonus-depreciation reigniting machinery orders and reshoring. In a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +20.4%, oil +20.7%) this was risk-on leadership, though the tape stayed narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by −8.8%) under a roaring semis bid (SMH +255%). The late-cycle leg held up through the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock on durable defense and AI-infrastructure demand.","drivers":["risk-on leadership / reflation quad","aerospace/defense + AI-power electrification capex","reshoring","narrow breadth / resilient through Hormuz shock"],"title_zh":"工业股领涨反弹——真正的第二领头，而非搭车者","body_zh":"自4月低点起，工业股作为名副其实的第二领头飙升+60.3%，受航空航天/国防（GE航空航天、RTX）及AI电力/数据中心电气化资本开支热潮驱动——GE Vernova与伊顿乘着变压器/开关设备短缺上行，叠加加成折旧重新点燃机械订单与制造业回流。在再通胀/增长向上的象限中（周期股+51.4% vs 防御股+20.4%、油价+20.7%），这是风险偏好领涨；尽管在半导体强劲买盘下（SMH +255%）市场广度仍偏窄（等权落后市值加权−8.8%）。这一晚周期阶段在2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击中依靠稳健的国防与AI基础设施需求得以挺住。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好领涨/再通胀象限","航空航天/国防+AI电力电气化资本开支","制造业回流","市场广度狭窄/挺过霍尔木兹冲击"]}},"now_zh":"趋势向上（RS排名第2，行业领头）——制造业回流、国防开支以及AI电力/数据中心电气化的资本开支，使工业板块（+15.8%）稳居名副其实的第二领头位置；即便2026年市场广度为本轮周期最窄（高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7%、成长落后价值−15.2%），这仍是广泛的周期股领涨而非大盘股独涨——等权指数实际上跑赢市值加权+2.9%。再通胀/增长向上的象限（周期股11.2% vs 防御股6.9%、油价+20.9%、铜-金+18.0）叠加美元走强+3.4%，更利好本土工业需求而非跨国企业；关注ISM以及半导体的买盘（+67.9%）能否持续带动资本开支。"},"xlb":{"now":"Rolling over (RS#7) — XLB is mid-pack (+13.3%, #4) but it's a quiet detente, not leadership: a +3.4% DXY (the Hormuz oil shock firming the dollar) is a direct headwind for dollar-priced metals, and copper-over-gold is actually firm (+18.0) on structural tightness. The tape has broadened (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +2.9%) and oil ripped +20.9% into a reflation/growth-up quad — a backdrop that should help cyclicals — but soft China demand and the strong dollar keep capping the industrial-metals bid.","legs":{"2022-04-20":{"title":"Copper crash meets recession risk-off","body":"Materials got hammered (−21.1%, #10) as copper logged its biggest quarterly decline since 2011, slumping below $7,000/tonne on China's COVID lockdowns, an +8.1% DXY surge that made metals dearer, and Fed-hiking recession fears. This wasn't sector-specific — it was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where cyclicals (−17.5%) were dumped far harder than defensives (−8.9%), and copper-over-gold cratered −18.3 — but the strong-dollar headwind made miners (Freeport) and chemicals (Dow, LyondellBasell) the worst of the cyclical bunch.","drivers":["copper crash","China lockdowns","strong dollar (+8.1% DXY)","slowdown quad"],"title_zh":"铜价崩跌叠加衰退避险","body_zh":"材料板块遭重创（−21.1%，第10），铜价创2011年以来最大季度跌幅，跌破每吨7,000美元，背后是中国新冠封控、美元飙升+8.1%抬高金属价格以及美联储加息引发的衰退担忧。这并非板块独有——而是增长放缓/通缩恐慌象限，周期股（−17.5%）被抛售远甚于防御股（−8.9%），铜金比暴跌−18.3——但强势美元逆风使矿企（自由港）与化工股（陶氏、利安德巴塞尔）成为周期板块中最差的一类。","drivers_zh":["铜价崩跌","中国封控","强势美元（+8.1% DXY）","放缓象限"]},"2022-07-14":{"title":"Peak-inflation bounce, dollar relents","body":"Materials snapped back +14.9% as a softer inflation read and Fed-pivot hopes pushed the dollar off its highs (−1.9% DXY), letting copper and beaten-down metals rebound with a tech/semis-led risk-on summer rally (SMH +16.3%). It was a reflation/growth-up quad — cyclicals (+16.7%) led defensives (+7.6%) and copper-over-gold turned up +9.2 — but XLB only ranked #5: deeply oversold miners and chemicals bounced on the easing-recession narrative and a weaker greenback that relieves dollar-priced commodities, lagging the higher-beta discretionary/industrials leaders.","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","dollar pullback (−1.9% DXY)","tech-led risk-on","reflation quad"],"title_zh":"通胀见顶反弹，美元退潮","body_zh":"材料板块反弹+14.9%，温和的通胀数据与美联储转向预期将美元拉离高位（−1.9% DXY），使铜和遭抛售的金属随科技/半导体引领的风险偏好夏季行情回升（SMH +16.3%）。这是再通胀/增长向上象限——周期股（+16.7%）领先防御股（+7.6%），铜金比转正+9.2——但XLB仅排名第5：深度超卖的矿业与化工股在衰退缓和叙事和走软美元（利好以美元计价的大宗商品）下反弹，落后于高贝塔的可选消费/工业领涨股。","drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","美元回落（−1.9% DXY）","科技引领风险偏好","再通胀象限"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole reignites the dollar wrecking-ball","body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole sent the dollar surging toward a 20-year high (+7.1% DXY) and yields ripping (TLT −10.4%), a double rate-regime-and-FX wrecking-ball that pushed copper back down and dragged gold below $1,700, crushing Freeport and Newmont. The −17.0% (#8) drop came in a slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety — defensives (−9.1%) held up better than cyclicals (−15.1%), VIX 20→32 — so XLB fell as the dollar-sensitive cyclical caught in a higher-for-longer regime, not on a Materials-specific catalyst.","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish","dollar 20-year high (+7.1% DXY)","rate regime (TLT −10.4%)","flight-to-safety"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重启美元破坏力","body_zh":"鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派表态将美元推向20年高位（+7.1% DXY），收益率飙升（TLT −10.4%），形成利率体制与汇率的双重打击，使铜价重新下行、黄金跌破1,700美元，重创自由港与纽蒙特。这−17.0%（第8）的下跌发生在增长放缓/通缩恐慌的避险中——防御股（−9.1%）比周期股（−15.1%）更抗跌，VIX由20升至32——因此XLB是作为陷入“更高更久”体制的美元敏感型周期股而下跌，并非材料板块独有的催化剂。","drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派","美元20年高位（+7.1% DXY）","利率体制（TLT −10.4%）","避险"]},"2022-09-26":{"title":"Soft landing + weak dollar lift metals, but mega-caps lead","body":"XLB rallied +51.0% over two years as a soft-landing economy and a collapsing dollar (−9.3% DXY) powered copper toward record highs and gold to all-time highs; the Fed's jumbo 50bp cut in Sept 2024 plus China's ~$560B stimulus supercharged industrial-metals demand. But this was a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +169.2%, growth>value +33.4) with narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by −18.9%), so Materials (#5) trailed the mega-cap leaders — strong as a cyclical in a goldilocks quad, but not where the index leadership lived.","drivers":["Fed cuts begin","weak dollar (−9.3% DXY) tailwind","China stimulus","narrow mega-cap breadth"],"title_zh":"软着陆+弱美元提振金属，但巨头领涨","body_zh":"材料板块两年内上涨+51.0%，软着陆经济与崩跌的美元（−9.3% DXY）推动铜价逼近历史高位、黄金创历史新高；美联储2024年9月一次性降息50个基点叠加中国约5,600亿美元刺激，大幅提振工业金属需求。但这是科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +169.2%，成长>价值+33.4），市场广度狭窄（等权重落后市值加权−18.9%），因此材料（第5）落后于巨头领涨股——作为金发女孩象限中的周期股表现强劲，但并非指数领涨所在。","drivers_zh":["美联储开启降息","弱美元（−9.3% DXY）顺风","中国刺激","狭窄的巨头市场广度"]},"2024-10-18":{"title":"Tariff shock + flight-to-safety crush the cyclical","body":"XLB cratered −23.2% (dead last, #11) as Trump's November win, 25% steel/aluminum duties in March 2025, and the April reciprocal tariffs triggered a crash bottoming around April 8 — Materials sat squarely in the tariff bullseye. The macro was a slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety (VIX 18→52) where defensives (−9.3%) sharply outperformed cyclicals (−15.5%), and XLB was the most-punished cyclical of all. The dollar barely moved (−0.5% DXY), so this was a tariff-and-de-risking story, not an FX squeeze — global-cyclical chemicals and miners absorbed the worst of the trade-war de-risk.","drivers":["Trump tariff shock","steel/aluminum duties","flight-to-safety","slowdown quad"],"title_zh":"关税冲击+避险打压周期股","body_zh":"材料板块暴跌−23.2%（垫底，第11），特朗普11月胜选、2025年3月落地的25%钢铝关税以及4月对等关税引发崩跌并在4月8日前后见底——材料正处于关税靶心。宏观背景是增长放缓/通缩恐慌的避险（VIX由18升至52），防御股（−9.3%）大幅跑赢周期股（−15.5%），而XLB是所有周期股中受打击最重的。美元几乎未动（−0.5% DXY），因此这是关税与去风险的故事，而非汇率挤压——全球周期型化工与矿业股承受了贸易战去风险的最重一击。","drivers_zh":["特朗普关税冲击","钢铝关税","避险","放缓象限"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Metals roar back on weak dollar, then roll over","body":"XLB rebounded +46.6% off the tariff-crash low as a weakening dollar (−6.0% DXY) and AI/datacenter demand ran copper ~40% higher into record territory and gold surged to a late-January-2026 peak. It rode a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +131.2%, VIX 52→18) in a reflation/growth-up quad, but only ranked #4 with narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged −5.9%). By early 2026 it rolled over: the Iran/Hormuz oil shock firmed the dollar again and softening Chinese demand sapped the industrial-metals bid even as structural copper tightness lingered.","drivers":["weak dollar (−6.0% DXY) tailwind","copper/gold record highs","tech-led risk-on","Hormuz strong-dollar rollover"],"title_zh":"金属借弱美元强势回归后回落","body_zh":"材料板块自关税崩跌低点反弹+46.6%，走弱的美元（−6.0% DXY）与AI/数据中心需求推动铜价上涨约40%进入创纪录区间，黄金飙升并在2026年1月底见顶。它搭乘了科技/半导体引领的风险偏好逼空行情（SMH +131.2%，VIX由52降至18），处于再通胀/增长向上象限，但仅排名第4，市场广度狭窄（等权重落后−5.9%）。进入2026年初板块见顶回落：伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击再度推升美元，中国需求走软削弱工业金属买盘，尽管结构性的铜供应紧张仍然存在。","drivers_zh":["弱美元（−6.0% DXY）顺风","铜/金创历史新高","科技引领风险偏好","霍尔木兹强美元回落"]}},"now_zh":"见顶回落（RS第7）——XLB位居中游（+13.3%，第4），但这是平静的休战而非领涨：美元走强+3.4%（霍尔木兹油价冲击推升美元）对以美元计价的金属构成直接逆风，而铜金比实际上仍坚挺（+18.0），受结构性供应紧张支撑。市场广度已扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%），油价飙升+20.9%进入再通胀/增长向上象限——本应利好周期股的背景——但中国需求疲软与强势美元持续压制工业金属买盘。"},"xlv":{"now":"EXPANDING (RS #4) — XLV is being starved by the 2026 semis/memory melt-up (SMH +68%, high-beta over low-vol +21%) yet quietly turning: it's +3.3% and ranks #8/11, but with VIX calm (14→18), value beating growth (growth−value −15.2) and broadening participation (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight), money is leaking out of the narrow mega-cap tech tape toward cheap quality defensives. Health care is bid as tech tops, though drug-pricing (MFN/RFK Jr.) and pharma-tariff policy remain overhangs.","legs":{"2022-04-08":{"title":"Rate-regime de-rating hits biotech","body":"A rate-regime selloff: the Fed's aggressive 2022 hiking cycle and the June 9.1% CPI shock sent yields surging (TLT −10.1%) and the dollar +4.9% (DXY), crushing long-duration health care — biotech (XBI) sank to multi-year lows as rising real rates discounted distant cash flows. In a stagflation-ish quad, large-cap pharma/devices cushioned XLV (−16% vs cyclicals −16.3%, ranking #6/11), but quality couldn't fully offset the duration hit.","drivers":["rate regime","Fed rate hikes","9.1% CPI shock","biotech de-rating"],"title_zh":"利率体制杀估值冲击生物科技","body_zh":"一轮利率体制驱动的抛售：美联储2022年激进的加息周期与6月9.1%的CPI冲击推动收益率飙升（TLT −10.1%）、美元+4.9%（DXY），重创长久期医疗保健——生物科技（XBI）跌至多年低位，因实际利率上升对远期现金流贴现折让。在偏滞胀的象限中，大型制药/器械相对缓冲了XLV（−16%，对比周期股 −16.3%，排名第6/11），但优质属性仍无法完全抵消久期冲击。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","美联储加息","9.1% CPI冲击","生物科技杀估值"]},"2022-06-17":{"title":"Defensive bid, then starved by the AI melt-up","body":"Off the June 2022 low, health care first caught a defensive safe-haven bid (VIX 31→17) and re-rated on the GLP-1/obesity-drug super-cycle — Eli Lilly (tirzepatide) and Novo Nordisk drove leadership. But as the tech/semis melt-up took over (SMH +131%, growth−value +36, narrow mega-cap breadth −18.7%), XLV was starved: nothing broke, money simply rotated to tech in a goldilocks quad, leaving it +36% but only #6/11.","drivers":["defensives starved","tech-led risk-on","GLP-1 obesity drugs","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"防御买盘，随后被AI逼空式上涨冷落","body_zh":"自2022年6月低点起，医疗保健先获得防御避险买盘（VIX 31→17），随后凭借GLP-1/减肥药超级周期重估——礼来（替尔泊肽）与诺和诺德引领涨势。但当科技/半导体的逼空式上涨接管行情后（SMH +131%、成长减价值 +36、狭窄大盘广度 −18.7%），XLV遭冷落：板块本身并未出问题，只是在金发女孩象限中资金转向科技，令其虽涨约36%却仅排名第6/11。","drivers_zh":["防御被冷落","科技主导风险偏好","GLP-1减肥药","市场广度狭窄"]},"2024-09-16":{"title":"Policy hit while the tape rallied without it","body":"This wasn't a market selloff — SPY rose +5.4% and cyclicals +6.1% — XLV alone got hit, ending the single worst sector (−17%, #11/11) as election/policy risk crystallized: RFK Jr. at HHS, the May 2025 Most-Favored-Nation drug-pricing order, and threatened pharma tariffs pushed pharma valuations to historic lows. With yields surging (TLT −13.4%) and a narrow goldilocks tape rotating into Comm/Financials/Discretionary leaders, GLP-1 enthusiasm cooled on pricing/competition fears.","drivers":["idiosyncratic selloff","MFN drug pricing","RFK Jr. / MAHA","rate regime"],"title_zh":"政策独立打击，而大盘无此板块照样上涨","body_zh":"这并非大盘抛售——SPY上涨+5.4%、周期股+6.1%——唯独XLV遭重创，成为表现最差板块（−17%，第11/11），因选举/政策风险落地：小罗伯特·肯尼迪执掌HHS、2025年5月的最惠国(MFN)药品定价行政令以及医药关税威胁，将制药估值压至历史低位。在收益率飙升（TLT −13.4%）、狭窄的金发女孩行情转向通信/金融/可选消费龙头之际，GLP-1热情在定价/竞争担忧下降温。","drivers_zh":["个股独立抛售","MFN药品定价","小罗伯特·肯尼迪/MAHA","利率体制"]},"2025-05-14":{"title":"Rate tailwind + cheap-quality rerating","body":"From the post-tariff washout, XLV rallied ~27% to #4/11 — but not on a flight-to-safety: this was a risk-ON, cyclical-led reflation tape (cyclicals +25.6% vs defensives +18.7%, high-beta over low-vol +60, semis +147%). Health care's own tailwinds carried it: yields FELL (TLT +7.5%), a boost for the bond-proxy quality defensive, while cheap post-selloff valuations and value beating growth (growth−value −12.2) rewarded the rotation into cheap quality, and clarity on drug-pricing deals stripped out some tail risk. It led even as breadth stayed narrow (equal-weight −4.4%).","drivers":["rate tailwind","cheap-quality rerating","value over growth","pricing-deal clarity"],"title_zh":"利率顺风＋低估值优质资产重估","body_zh":"自关税后的洗盘中，XLV反弹约27%至第4/11——但这并非避险买盘：当时是风险偏好、周期股领涨的再通胀行情（周期股 +25.6% 对比防御股 +18.7%、高贝塔减低波动 +60、半导体 +147%）。推动它的是医疗保健自身的顺风：收益率下行（TLT +7.5%），利好这一债券替代品类优质防御资产，同时关税抛售后的低估值、价值跑赢成长（成长减价值 −12.2）奖励了向低估值优质资产的轮动，药品定价协议的明朗化也消除了部分尾部风险。即便市场广度依旧狭窄（等权重 −4.4%），它仍领先。","drivers_zh":["利率顺风","低估值优质资产重估","价值跑赢成长","定价协议明朗"]}},"now_zh":"扩张中（RS第4）——XLV正被2026年半导体/存储的逼空式上涨所冷落（SMH +68%，高贝塔减低波动 +21%），但已悄然转向：板块+3.3%、排名第8/11，然而在VIX平静（14→18）、价值跑赢成长（成长减价值 −15.2）以及市场广度扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%）的背景下，资金正从狭窄的大盘科技行情中渗出，流向低估值的优质防御资产。科技见顶之际医疗保健获得买盘，尽管药品定价（最惠国MFN/小罗伯特·肯尼迪）与医药关税政策仍是悬而未决的隐忧。"},"xlp":{"now":"ROLLING OVER (RS #8) — staples are being starved, not broken: XLP is up ~8.8% (rank #6) but the tape is a tech-led melt-up (semis +67.9%, high-beta over low-vol +20.7), so flows keep rotating out of low-vol defensives. The 2025 flight-to-safety bid is fading at the margin even as XLP stays a recession hedge, and value-over-growth (growth−value −15.2) hints the rotation could broaden if the mega-cap leadership cracks.","legs":{"2022-04-20":{"title":"Rate-driven de-rating, even the defensive couldn't hide","body":"This wasn't a clean flight-to-safety: with the 10Y surging (TLT −16.0%) and the dollar ripping +12.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, the rate-regime de-rating hit everything, and even staples fell ~16.3% as 9% CPI input-cost inflation compressed margins before pricing caught up. XLP only ranked #5/11 because the whole tape was red — defensives (−14.6%) barely edged cyclicals (−15.5%) — so its 'outperformance' was relative cushioning, not strength, into the October 2022 low.","drivers":["rate regime","strong dollar","input-cost inflation","margin pressure"],"title_zh":"利率驱动的杀估值，连防御板块也无处藏身","body_zh":"这并非干净的避险行情：在10年期收益率飙升（TLT −16.0%）、美元在放缓/通缩担忧象限中暴涨+12.4%的背景下，利率体制的杀估值冲击了一切，连必需消费品也下跌约16.3%——9%的CPI投入成本通胀在提价跟上之前先挤压了利润率。XLP仅排名第5/11，只因整个市场一片惨绿——防御板块（−14.6%）勉强好于周期板块（−15.5%）——所以它的'跑赢'只是相对缓冲而非真正的强势，直至2022年10月低点。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","强势美元","投入成本通胀","利润率承压"]},"2022-10-07":{"title":"Starved by the AI melt-up — up 48%, but the laggard","body":"Off the October 2022 low staples did everything right — pricing power, steady demand and reliable dividends drew a flight-to-safety bid into early 2026 as tariff and oil-shock uncertainty flared, lifting XLP ~48% to its February 2026 peak. But it still ranked #9/11: nothing was wrong with the defensive, money simply rotated to tech in a narrow, mega-cap-led melt-up (SMH +341.8%, growth over value +42.4, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by −31.3%). A weak dollar (−13.5% DXY) and goldilocks quad turbo-charged the risk-on leaders, leaving low-vol staples to win on an absolute basis while badly lagging on a relative one.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","defensives starved","flight-to-safety"],"title_zh":"被AI逼空行情冷落——上涨48%，却是落后者","body_zh":"自2022年10月低点起必需消费品样样做对——定价权、稳定需求与可靠股息，在2026年初关税与油价冲击的不确定性升温时吸引了避险买盘，将XLP推升约48%至2026年2月峰值。但它仍仅排名第9/11：防御板块本身并无问题，资金只是在狭窄的、大型股主导的逼空行情中轮动至科技（半导体+341.8%，成长跑赢价值+42.4，等权重落后市值加权达−31.3%）。疲软的美元（−13.5% DXY）与金发女孩象限为风险偏好的领涨者火上浇油，令低波动的必需消费品在绝对收益上获胜，却在相对表现上严重落后。","drivers_zh":["科技主导风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","防御板块被冷落","避险"]}},"now_zh":"见顶回落（RS第8）——必需消费品是被冷落而非走坏：XLP上涨约8.8%（排名第6），但当前是科技主导的逼空行情（半导体+67.9%，高贝塔减低波动+20.7），资金持续从低波动防御板块轮动流出。2025年的避险买盘在边际上正在消退，尽管XLP仍是衰退对冲工具；而价值跑赢成长（成长减价值−15.2）暗示，若大型科技股的领导地位破裂，板块轮动可能扩散。"},"xlu":{"now":"BOTTOMING (RS #9) — Utilities isn't broken, it's being starved: a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +68%, high-beta over low-vol +21%) is pulling flows out of low-vol defensives even as XLU still grinds +8.5%. A strong dollar (+3.4% DXY) and a 2026 rate-hike bias keep a lid on the bond proxy, and last year defensives actually lagged cyclicals (6.9% vs 11.2% with VIX only 14→18) — but broadening breadth (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight) plus the structural AI-datacenter electricity-demand thesis underpin a base if leadership rotates off the narrow mega-cap tape.","legs":{"2022-04-08":{"title":"Rate-regime selloff hits the bond proxy","body":"Utilities are classic bond proxies, so the Fed's hiking campaign and surging Treasury yields (TLT −10.1%) repriced the rate-sensitive sector's multiples in the spring 2022 stagflation drawdown — a strong dollar (+4.9% DXY) compounded the macro pressure. XLU still cushioned the broad rout (−16% vs SPY −18%), but it slightly underperformed the defensive cohort (−15.7% vs defensives −14.8%) as VIX ran 21→31, since rising bond yields stripped the income proxy of its dividend edge into the mid-June low.","drivers":["rate regime","bond-proxy","strong dollar","stagflation quad"],"title_zh":"利率体制抛售冲击债券替代品","body_zh":"公用事业是经典的债券替代品，因此美联储加息与飙升的美债收益率（TLT −10.1%）在2022年春季滞胀回调中重新定价了这一利率敏感板块的估值倍数——强美元（+4.9% DXY）加剧了宏观压力。XLU仍缓冲了大盘抛售（−16% vs SPY −18%），但略逊于整体防御板块（−15.7% vs 防御板块 −14.8%），在VIX走高21→31之际，上行的债券收益率剥夺了这一收益替代品的股息优势，直至6月中旬低点。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","债券替代品","强美元","滞胀象限"]},"2022-06-17":{"title":"Defensive safe-haven rally as growth scare bites","body":"As recession fears mounted in summer 2022, defensives edged out cyclicals (+13.4% vs +13.1%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, and utilities rallied ~21% (#2 of 11) on steady cash flows and dividends. With oil collapsing −19.9% and VIX easing 31→24, the flight-to-safety bid plus a brief lull in yields lifted the bond proxy into its mid-September peak — defensive demand, not a yield tailwind (TLT still −3.6%).","drivers":["flight-to-safety","defensive safe-haven","growth scare quad","yield lull"],"title_zh":"增长恐慌中的防御避险反弹","body_zh":"随着2022年夏季衰退担忧升温，在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中防御板块微幅跑赢周期股（+13.4% vs +13.1%），公用事业凭借稳定现金流与股息上涨约21%（11个板块中排名第2）。油价暴跌 −19.9%、VIX回落31→24，避险买盘叠加收益率短暂回落，将债券替代品推升至9月中旬峰值——靠的是防御需求，而非收益率顺风（TLT仍 −3.6%）。","drivers_zh":["避险","防御避险","增长恐慌象限","收益率回落"]},"2022-09-12":{"title":"Yield spike past 4% crushes the bond proxy","body":"A sharp rate-regime surge in Treasury yields past 4% into early October (TLT −6.4%) repriced the bond proxy violently — with safe bond yields topping utility dividend yields and a strong dollar (+4.6% DXY) tightening conditions, income investors rotated away. XLU fell ~21% in a month (#10 of 11), a deeper loss than even broad defensives (−12%), in a textbook rate-sensitive selloff as VIX spiked 24→34.","drivers":["rate regime","10Y yield >4%","bond-proxy repricing","strong dollar"],"title_zh":"收益率破4%飙升重创债券替代品","body_zh":"美债收益率在10月初前急升突破4%（TLT −6.4%）的利率体制冲击，对债券替代品进行了剧烈重新定价——当无风险债券收益率超过公用事业股息收益率、强美元（+4.6% DXY）收紧条件，收益型投资者纷纷转向。XLU一个月内下跌约21%（11个板块中排名第10），跌幅甚至超过整体防御板块（−12%），在VIX飙升24→34之际上演教科书式的利率敏感型抛售。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","10年期收益率>4%","债券替代品重定价","强美元"]},"2022-10-12":{"title":"Rate-relief bounce on falling yields and weaker dollar","body":"When yields reversed lower off their October peak (TLT +7.8%) and the dollar rolled over (−8.2% DXY), the bond proxy bounced ~18% (#3 of 11) off the 2022 low. Defensives led cyclicals (+15.4% vs +13.4%) with broadening breadth (equal-weight +2.2% over cap-weight) and VIX collapsing 34→23 — the move tracked the inverse path of the 10-year yield, confirming the sector's rate-driven character.","drivers":["rate regime","yield pullback","weaker dollar","broadening breadth"],"title_zh":"收益率回落、美元走弱下的利率缓和反弹","body_zh":"当收益率从10月峰值反转下行（TLT +7.8%）、美元走软（−8.2% DXY）时，债券替代品自2022年低点反弹约18%（11个板块中排名第3）。防御板块领先周期股（+15.4% vs +13.4%），市场广度走宽（等权重跑赢市值加权 +2.2%），VIX骤降34→23——走势与10年期收益率呈反向路径，印证了该板块的利率驱动属性。","drivers_zh":["利率体制","收益率回落","美元走弱","市场广度走宽"]},"2022-12-13":{"title":"Starved by the 2023 AI risk-on, not broken","body":"Utilities wasn't broken through 2023 — it was starved as a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +29.9%, growth over value +19.9, VIX 23→18) rotated money out of low-vol defensives, even as 'higher-for-longer' rates (TLT −17.1%) and a stronger dollar piled on. With breadth narrow (equal-weight lagging cap-weight by −11.1%) and cash/bonds offering competitive yields, XLU drifted down ~20% (worst of 11) to a bottom in early October 2023 as yields peaked near cycle highs.","drivers":["starved (tech-led risk-on)","narrow breadth","higher-for-longer rates","bond competition"],"title_zh":"被2023年AI风险偏好冷落，而非走坏","body_zh":"整个2023年公用事业并未走坏——而是在科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +29.9%、成长跑赢价值 +19.9、VIX 23→18）将资金从低波动防御板块抽离时被冷落，叠加“更高更久”的利率（TLT −17.1%）与走强的美元雪上加霜。市场广度狭窄（等权重落后市值加权 −11.1%），现金和债券提供有竞争力的收益率，XLU震荡下行约20%（11个板块中最差），在2023年10月初收益率逼近周期高点时见底。","drivers_zh":["被冷落（科技引领风险偏好）","市场广度狭窄","更高更久利率","债券竞争"]},"2023-10-02":{"title":"AI-datacenter power super-cycle re-rating","body":"From the October 2023 low, utilities staged a historic re-rating (#3 of 11, ~82%) as the AI-datacenter electricity-demand super-cycle reframed the sector from sleepy bond proxy to a structural growth story — power names (Vistra, Constellation, NextEra) led as hyperscaler load forecasts surged after years of flat demand. A goldilocks quad with falling yields (TLT +15.2%) and a weaker dollar (−8.7% DXY) gave the bond proxy a tailwind, letting defensives nearly keep pace with cyclicals (50.5% vs 57.1%) even as a narrow, semis-led tape (SMH +181.7%, equal-weight −13.4% behind cap-weight) dominated the index into the February 2026 peak.","drivers":["AI-datacenter power demand","electricity super-cycle","rate tailwind / weaker dollar","Vistra/Constellation/NextEra"],"title_zh":"AI数据中心电力超级周期重估","body_zh":"自2023年10月低点起，公用事业上演历史性重估（11个板块中排名第3，约 +82%），AI数据中心电力需求超级周期将板块从沉闷的债券替代品重塑为结构性增长故事——电力公司（Vistra、Constellation、NextEra）领涨，超大规模厂商在多年需求平淡后负荷预测大幅上调。金发女孩象限下收益率回落（TLT +15.2%）、美元走弱（−8.7% DXY）为债券替代品提供顺风，使防御板块几乎追平周期股（50.5% vs 57.1%），尽管狭窄的、半导体引领的行情（SMH +181.7%、等权重落后市值加权 −13.4%）主导着指数，直至2026年2月峰值。","drivers_zh":["AI数据中心电力需求","电力超级周期","利率顺风/美元走弱","Vistra/Constellation/NextEra"]}},"now_zh":"筑底中（RS第9）——公用事业并非走坏，而是被冷落：科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +68%、高贝塔跑赢低波动 +21%）把资金从低波动防御板块抽离，即便XLU仍小幅上行 +8.5%。强美元（+3.4% DXY）与2026年加息倾向压制着这一债券替代品，去年防御板块其实落后周期股（6.9% vs 11.2%，VIX仅14→18）——但市场广度走宽（等权重跑赢市值加权 +2.9%）叠加AI数据中心电力需求的结构性逻辑，一旦领导权脱离狭窄的大盘股行情，便为其奠定底部。"},"xlc":{"now":"BOTTOMING (RS #10, deeply washed out) — XLC is the tape's worst sector at -9.6% (rank 11/11) while Tech (+24.3%) and a +67.9% semis melt-up (SMH) lead a high-beta-over-low-vol risk-on regime (+20.7%). But growth is LAGGING value (-15.2%), so this isn't a clean tech bid carrying Meta/Alphabet — the AI-capex/ad-cycle wobble has the basket starved as money rotates into semis and energy, not the mega-cap ad names. Breadth is broadening (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight) and VIX stays calm (14->18), so the washout looks more like neglect than panic, leaving XLC positioned to turn off a beaten base if the growth-over-value flip rotates flows back to its Meta/Alphabet core.","legs":{"2021-09-01":{"title":"Ad recession meets rate de-rating","body":"XLC was 2022's worst-hit S&P sector (-46.7%, rank 11/11) as a digital ad recession gutted Meta and Alphabet and Netflix cratered ~36% in a day on its first subscriber loss. The pain was amplified by a brutal rate-regime move — the 10Y surged with TLT -34.1% and the dollar ripped +22.2% (DXY) — which crushed the long-duration, growth-heavy streaming/mega-cap basket while Energy (+100.4%) ran. It fell ~47% into the November 2022 low.","drivers":["ad recession","Meta/Netflix collapse","rate regime","strong dollar"],"title_zh":"广告衰退叠加利率杀估值","body_zh":"XLC是2022年标普中受打击最严重的板块（-46.7%，11个中垫底），数字广告衰退掏空了Meta和Alphabet，奈飞因首次订户流失单日暴跌约36%。痛苦被剧烈的利率象限切换放大——10年期收益率飙升（TLT -34.1%）、美元暴涨+22.2%（DXY）——重创了这个长久期、偏成长的流媒体/大型科技股篮子，而能源（+100.4%）大涨。该板块下跌约47%至2022年11月低点。","drivers_zh":["广告衰退","Meta/奈飞崩跌","利率象限","美元走强"]},"2022-11-03":{"title":"AI mega-cap melt-up, narrow tape","body":"Off the 2022 low XLC ripped +137.2% to lead all sectors (rank 1/11) as the ad market healed and the genAI boom lifted its Meta/Alphabet-dominated basket — Netflix +~83% on ad-tier growth, Meta +~65% on AI ad targeting. This was a textbook tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +182.3%, growth>value +62.4, VIX 25->15, dollar -5.6%), and a hyper-narrow one — equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -31.3%, so the mega-cap concentration that crushed XLC in 2022 became its rocket fuel into the February 2025 high.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","AI/genAI boom","narrow breadth","Meta/Alphabet/Netflix"],"title_zh":"AI大型科技股暴涨，窄幅行情","body_zh":"自2022年低点起，XLC暴涨+137.2%、领涨所有板块（11个中第1），广告市场回暖、生成式AI热潮提振了以Meta/Alphabet为主的篮子——奈飞因广告版增长上涨约83%、Meta因AI广告定向上涨约65%。这是教科书式的科技/半导体主导的风险偏好暴涨（SMH +182.3%、成长跑赢价值+62.4、VIX 25->15、美元-5.6%），且极度狭窄——等权重跑输市值加权-31.3%，于是2022年压垮XLC的大型科技股集中度，反而成了它冲向2025年2月高位的燃料。","drivers_zh":["科技主导风险偏好","AI/生成式AI热潮","市场广度狭窄","Meta/Alphabet/奈飞"]},"2025-02-14":{"title":"DeepSeek and the tariff flight-to-safety","body":"The late-January DeepSeek scare questioned AI-capex ROI and April's reciprocal-tariff crash detonated a flight-to-safety — VIX spiked 15->52, defensives held (-6.5%) while cyclicals were hammered (-18.1%) and SMH fell -28.8%. XLC's Meta/Alphabet concentration left it on the wrong side of that rotation, down ~18% (rank 9/11) into the April 8 low even as the selloff broadened (equal-weight +3.2% over cap-weight).","drivers":["flight-to-safety","DeepSeek AI scare","April tariff crash","mega-cap concentration"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税引发的避险","body_zh":"1月底的DeepSeek恐慌质疑了AI资本开支的投资回报率，4月的对等关税崩跌引爆了避险情绪——VIX飙升15->52，防御板块抗跌（-6.5%）而周期股遭重创（-18.1%）、SMH下跌-28.8%。XLC对Meta/Alphabet的集中持仓使其站在了这次轮动的错误一侧，下跌约18%（11个中第9）至4月8日低点，尽管抛售在扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+3.2%）。","drivers_zh":["避险","DeepSeek AI恐慌","4月关税崩跌","大型科技股集中度"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Post-tariff AI rebound on a narrow tape","body":"From the April low XLC rebounded +40.7% (rank 3/11) as the tariff pause sparked a sharp relief rally and a tech/semis-led risk-on regime reasserted — SMH +124.9%, growth>value +12.2, VIX collapsed 52->17, dollar -5.8%. Alphabet re-rated on TPU/AI monetization and Meta on ad strength, but the advance ran on narrow, mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight -9.5% under cap-weight) and faded into the late-January 2026 high as the 2026 oil shock and AI-capex doubts triggered a tech-led pullback.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","tariff-pause relief","narrow breadth","AI monetization"],"title_zh":"关税后AI反弹，窄幅行情","body_zh":"自4月低点起，XLC反弹+40.7%（11个中第3），关税暂停引发强劲缓和行情，科技/半导体主导的风险偏好象限重新占上风——SMH +124.9%、成长跑赢价值+12.2、VIX崩塌52->17、美元-5.8%。Alphabet因TPU/AI变现重估、Meta因广告强劲而走高，但这轮上涨依赖狭窄的大型科技股主导广度（等权重跑输市值加权-9.5%），并在2026年1月底高位消退，因2026年油价冲击与AI资本开支疑虑引发科技主导的回调。","drivers_zh":["科技主导风险偏好","关税暂停缓和","市场广度狭窄","AI变现"]}},"now_zh":"筑底中（RS第10，深度超卖）——XLC是当前盘面最差的板块，-9.6%（11个板块中垫底），而科技（+24.3%）与+67.9%的半导体（SMH）暴涨引领着高贝塔跑赢低波动的风险偏好象限（+20.7%）。但成长正在跑输价值（-15.2%），所以这并非干净的科技买盘在带动Meta/Alphabet——AI资本开支/广告周期的动摇使该篮子被冷落，资金转向半导体和能源，而非大型广告股。市场广度在扩张（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%），VIX保持平静（14->18），因此这次washout更像被忽视而非恐慌，若成长跑赢价值的拐点把资金轮动回其Meta/Alphabet核心，XLC具备从重创底部反转的条件。"},"xly":{"now":"XLY is bottoming (RS rank #6, cycle position ~31, below its 200-day) but for once it isn't being saved by the rotation tape — it's being starved by it. The 2026 melt-up is narrow and tech-led (Tech +24.3%, semis/SMH +67.9%, high-beta beating low-vol by +20.7%), yet discretionary sits #10 of 11 at -5.2% because the consumer is squeezed by oil-driven inflation (CPI 4.2%, gasoline surging on the Iran/Hormuz shock) and a hawkish Fed. With Amazon and Tesla ~a third of the ETF, XLY is a leveraged bet on those two re-joining the risk-on leaders once pump prices and rates relent; the breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%), which is the first crack of a turn.","legs":{"2021-11-19":{"title":"Fed-hike shock de-rates Amazon, Tesla as money flees to safety","body":"With CPI heading toward 9% and the Fed pivoting to aggressive hikes, the long-duration growth names that dominate XLY de-rated hard, led by Amazon and Tesla, and discretionary finished dead-last (#11 of 11, -22.7%). This was a flight-to-safety rotation, not just sector weakness: defensives held +3.3% against cyclicals -3.4% as VIX ripped 18→36, while the end of stimulus and rising mortgage rates squeezed real wages, big-ticket demand and homebuilders.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Fed hikes / inflation squeeze","Amazon/Tesla de-rate","stagflation quad (oil +57%)"],"title_zh":"加息冲击重估亚马逊特斯拉，资金避险出逃","body_zh":"随着CPI迈向9%、美联储转向激进加息，主导XLY的长久期成长股大幅估值下修，以亚马逊和特斯拉为首，可选消费垫底（11个板块中第11位，-22.7%）。这是一轮避险轮动，而不只是板块走弱：在VIX从18飙升至36之际，防御板块守住+3.3%、周期板块为-3.4%，与此同时刺激政策退出和抵押贷款利率上升挤压了实际工资、大额需求和房屋建筑商。","drivers_zh":["避险","美联储加息/通胀挤压","亚马逊/特斯拉估值下修","滞胀象限（油价+57%）"]},"2022-03-07":{"title":"Bear-market bounce: discretionary leads a risk-on snap","body":"After the Nasdaq's March 14 low, beaten-down discretionary mega-caps like Amazon and Tesla snapped back to lead the tape (#1 of 11, +17.5%) as the Fed's first hike removed near-term uncertainty and money rotated back into high-beta growth — semis +16.9%, growth beating value +7.2, VIX collapsing 36→19. The relief was narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight -2.0%) and rate-sensitive rather than a fundamental improvement in the consumer.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","Fed clarity / short covering","Amazon/Tesla bounce","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"熊市反弹：可选消费引领risk-on弹升","body_zh":"在纳指3月14日见底后，亚马逊、特斯拉等被打压的可选消费大型股强劲反弹并领涨大盘（11个板块中第1位，+17.5%），因美联储首次加息消除了近期不确定性，资金重新轮动回高贝塔成长股——半导体+16.9%，成长跑赢价值+7.2，VIX从36回落至19。这轮纾解狭窄（等权落后市值权重-2.0%）且对利率敏感，而非消费者基本面的真正改善。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","美联储明朗化/空头回补","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Retail margin shock and a flight-to-safety leg down","body":"Walmart and Target delivered rare earnings misses in May as freight, payroll and inventory costs crushed margins and shoppers pulled back on big-ticket goods, dropping discretionary to dead-last (#11, -28.0%). The selloff was a defensive rotation — defensives -2.8% vs cyclicals -11.9% with VIX 19→29 — compounded by a rate-regime move (TLT -8.8%) and a stronger dollar (+3.5% DXY) that hammered Amazon and the homebuilders.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Walmart/Target miss","rate regime (TLT -8.8%)","strong dollar"],"title_zh":"零售利润率冲击，叠加避险下挫","body_zh":"沃尔玛和塔吉特在5月罕见地业绩不及预期，因运费、薪资和库存成本压垮了利润率，消费者在大额商品上收紧开支，使可选消费跌至垫底（第11位，-28.0%）。这轮抛售是防御性轮动——防御板块-2.8%对周期板块-11.9%，VIX从19升至29——并叠加利率体制走高（TLT -8.8%）和走强的美元（DXY +3.5%），重创了亚马逊和房屋建筑商。","drivers_zh":["避险","沃尔玛/塔吉特不及预期","利率体制（TLT -8.8%）","美元走强"]},"2022-05-24":{"title":"Oversold relief: discretionary tops the leaderboard","body":"After a historic losing streak, deeply oversold discretionary names bounced to #1 of 11 (+14.4%) as retailers' results were reframed as execution problems rather than a broken consumer. This was a risk-on snap led by cyclicals (+7.0% vs defensives +0.9%, reflation quad) with Amazon and beaten-down retail rebounding — a technical relief, not a fundamental turn.","drivers":["risk-on leadership","oversold bounce","execution-not-consumer narrative","reflation quad"],"title_zh":"超卖纾解：可选消费登顶榜首","body_zh":"在历史性的连跌之后，深度超卖的可选消费股反弹至11个板块中第1位（+14.4%），因零售商的业绩被重新解读为执行问题而非消费者崩塌。这是一轮由周期股引领的risk-on弹升（周期+7.0%对防御+0.9%，再通胀象限），亚马逊和被打压的零售股回升——属于技术性纾解，而非基本面扭转。","drivers_zh":["risk-on领涨","超卖反弹","执行问题而非消费者叙事","再通胀象限"]},"2022-06-02":{"title":"Hot CPI, 75bp hike trigger a broad risk-off flush","body":"A scorching 8.6% CPI print and the Fed's first 75bp hike since 1994 sent rate-sensitive discretionary names to dead-last (#11, -14.6%) into the mid-June bottom. This was an everything-down flush — defensives also bled (-9.5%) as VIX climbed 25→33 — with Amazon, Tesla and the homebuilders leading the slide as recession odds and mortgage rates spiked.","drivers":["broad risk-off","hot CPI / 75bp hike","recession fear","deflation-scare quad"],"title_zh":"高CPI，75个基点加息触发全面risk-off抛售","body_zh":"炙热的8.6% CPI数据和美联储自1994年以来首次75个基点加息，使利率敏感的可选消费股跌至垫底（第11位，-14.6%），直至6月中旬触底。这是一轮无差别下跌——VIX从25升至33之际防御板块也失血（-9.5%）——随着衰退概率和抵押贷款利率飙升，亚马逊、特斯拉和房屋建筑商领跌。","drivers_zh":["全面risk-off","高CPI/加息75个基点","衰退担忧","通缩恐慌象限"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-inflation summer rally, discretionary leads","body":"From the June low, hopes that inflation had peaked and the Fed might soon pivot made discretionary the strongest sector (#1 of 11, +28.8%) as money rotated into high-beta growth — semis +19.5%, growth beating value +8.8, VIX 33→20. Amazon and Tesla led rate-sensitive cyclicals higher on Amazon's Q2 report and cooling July CPI, before Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole ended it.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","peak-inflation / Fed-pivot bets","Amazon rebound","goldilocks quad"],"title_zh":"通胀见顶夏季上涨，可选消费领涨","body_zh":"从6月低点起，对通胀已见顶、美联储可能很快转向的预期，使可选消费成为表现最强的板块（11个板块中第1位，+28.8%），资金轮动进入高贝塔成长股——半导体+19.5%，成长跑赢价值+8.8，VIX从33回落至20。亚马逊和特斯拉凭借亚马逊二季度业绩和7月CPI降温引领利率敏感的周期股走高，直至鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔讲话终结了行情。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","通胀见顶/押注美联储转向","亚马逊回升","金发女孩象限"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole and Tesla collapse drive a flight-to-safety","body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole killed the pivot trade and a rate-regime move (TLT -13.1%) kept yields climbing, but the bigger drag was Tesla's record collapse into year-end as Musk dumped billions in shares for Twitter, demand softened and Tesla cut prices. The rotation was defensive (defensives -2.7% vs cyclicals -7.0%) as Amazon's slowing retail and a strained consumer carried XLY to dead-last (#11, -26.7%) at its December low.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Jackson Hole hawkish","Tesla collapse / Musk sales","rate regime (TLT -13.1%)"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔与特斯拉崩盘引发避险","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔讲话终结了政策转向交易，利率体制走高（TLT -13.1%）使收益率持续攀升，但更大的拖累是特斯拉在年底前的历史性崩盘——马斯克为收购推特抛售了数十亿美元股票，需求走软，特斯拉降价。轮动偏向防御（防御板块-2.7%对周期板块-7.0%），亚马逊放缓的零售和承压的消费者将XLY拖至垫底（第11位，-26.7%）的12月低点。","drivers_zh":["避险","杰克逊霍尔鹰派","特斯拉崩盘/马斯克抛售","利率体制（TLT -13.1%）"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"Amazon, Tesla lead a narrow, tech-led recovery","body":"Disinflation, a resilient consumer and the AI-driven mega-cap rebound powered a ~41% rally led by Amazon and Tesla, the two names that drive the ETF (#3 of 11). This was a classic narrow, tech-led melt-up — semis +60.8%, growth beating value +27.7, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -10.2%, VIX 22→14 — that pulled flows back into high-beta discretionary into the July 2023 peak.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","Amazon/Tesla recovery","disinflation / resilient consumer","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"亚马逊、特斯拉引领狭窄、科技主导的复苏","body_zh":"去通胀、坚韧的消费者和AI驱动的大型股反弹，推动了一轮约41%的上涨，由驱动该ETF的两只股票——亚马逊和特斯拉领涨（11个板块中第3位）。这是一轮典型的狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨——半导体+60.8%，成长跑赢价值+27.7，等权落后市值权重-10.2%，VIX从22降至14——将资金重新拉回高贝塔可选消费，直至2023年7月见顶。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","亚马逊/特斯拉复苏","去通胀/坚韧消费者","市场广度狭窄"]},"2023-07-19":{"title":"Yield spike to 5% de-rates duration-heavy discretionary","body":"The 10-year Treasury surging toward 5%, its highest since 2007, on stronger data and deficit worries was a pure rate-regime move (TLT -17.0%) that crushed XLY's long-duration valuations to dead-last (#11, -16.2%). A stronger dollar (+6.3% DXY) and higher borrowing costs hit Amazon, Tesla and rate-sensitive homebuilders, threatening auto and big-ticket spending.","drivers":["rate regime (TLT -17.0%)","10-year toward 5% / higher-for-longer","strong dollar","Amazon/Tesla pressure"],"title_zh":"收益率升至5%重估久期偏重的可选消费","body_zh":"受强劲数据和赤字担忧推动，10年期美债收益率飙升至接近5%——为2007年以来最高，这是一次纯粹的利率体制走高（TLT -17.0%），将XLY的长久期估值压至垫底（第11位，-16.2%）。走强的美元（DXY +6.3%）和上升的借贷成本打击了亚马逊、特斯拉和利率敏感的房屋建筑商，威胁汽车和大额消费。","drivers_zh":["利率体制（TLT -17.0%）","10年期接近5%/更高更久","美元走强","亚马逊/特斯拉承压"]},"2023-10-26":{"title":"Rate cuts and a narrow, tech-led melt-up; Tesla rockets","body":"Falling yields (TLT +12.0%), the Fed's September 2024 cut and a remarkably resilient consumer drove a ~63% melt-up that put discretionary back at #1 of 11 on record holiday spending. It was a narrow, tech-led tape — semis +82.9%, growth beating value +30.7, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -13.1% — with Tesla exploding higher after Trump's November win and Amazon's strength carrying XLY to its December 17, 2024 record peak.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","rate cuts (TLT +12%)","Tesla post-election surge","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"降息与狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨；特斯拉飙升","body_zh":"回落的收益率（TLT +12.0%）、美联储2024年9月降息和异常坚韧的消费者，推动了约63%的飙升，凭借创纪录的假日消费使可选消费重回11个板块中第1位。这是一轮狭窄、科技主导的行情——半导体+82.9%，成长跑赢价值+30.7，等权落后市值权重-13.1%——特斯拉在特朗普11月获胜后暴涨，亚马逊的强势将XLY推向2024年12月17日的纪录高点。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","降息（TLT +12%）","特斯拉大选后飙升","市场广度狭窄"]},"2024-12-17":{"title":"DeepSeek then tariff crash trigger a flight-to-safety","body":"The peak unwound as January's DeepSeek shock hit AI/mega-cap sentiment and Amazon, then April's reciprocal-tariff announcement crushed import-heavy retail and slapped 25% levies on autos and parts, sending discretionary to dead-last (#11, -26.0%). It was a flight-to-safety rout — defensives -4.0% vs cyclicals -16.6% as VIX exploded 16→52 — with Tesla collapsing from its post-election high into the April 8 low.","drivers":["flight-to-safety","DeepSeek shock","reciprocal / auto tariffs","Tesla/Amazon decline"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek继而关税崩盘触发避险","body_zh":"随着1月的DeepSeek冲击打击AI/大型股情绪和亚马逊，继而4月的对等关税公告重创进口依赖型零售并对汽车及零部件征收25%关税，顶部随之瓦解，可选消费跌至垫底（第11位，-26.0%）。这是一轮避险溃败——VIX从16暴涨至52之际，防御板块-4.0%对周期板块-16.6%——特斯拉从大选后高点崩跌至4月8日低点。","drivers_zh":["避险","DeepSeek冲击","对等/汽车关税","特斯拉/亚马逊下跌"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Tariff-pause recovery rides the narrow, tech-led tape","body":"Trump's 90-day tariff pause sparked a furious rebound, and a still-resilient consumer plus AI euphoria drove discretionary to #2 of 11 (+42.1%) through 2025 into early 2026. It was a narrow, tech-led, weak-dollar melt-up — semis +117.8%, growth beating value +17.1, equal-weight lagging cap-weight -10.3%, VIX 52→15 — as Amazon and Tesla recovered and big-ticket demand held despite lingering tariff costs.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","tariff pause / resilient consumer","Amazon/Tesla rebound","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"关税暂缓复苏，搭乘狭窄、科技主导的行情","body_zh":"特朗普90天的关税暂缓引发了一轮迅猛反弹，仍然坚韧的消费者叠加AI热潮，推动可选消费升至11个板块中第2位（+42.1%），贯穿2025年直至2026年初。这是一轮狭窄、科技主导、弱美元的逼空上涨——半导体+117.8%，成长跑赢价值+17.1，等权落后市值权重-10.3%，VIX从52降至15——亚马逊和特斯拉复苏，大额需求在残留的关税成本下保持稳健。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","关税暂缓/坚韧消费者","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"]},"2026-01-12":{"title":"Oil shock and hawkish Fed leave discretionary stranded","body":"The Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz oil shock sent gas prices and CPI toward 4.2% (oil +72.9%, a stagflation quad), squeezing real wages and discretionary spending just as a hawkish Fed leaned toward hikes, dropping XLY to dead-last (#11, -15.0%). Notably it wasn't a clean flight-to-safety — breadth actually broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.3%) — but energy-led inflation and higher rates hit the big-ticket, rate-sensitive parts of XLY and pressured Amazon and Tesla.","drivers":["stagflation quad (oil +73%)","oil shock / gas squeeze","hawkish Fed","broadening breadth"],"title_zh":"油价冲击与鹰派美联储令可选消费搁浅","body_zh":"伊朗/霍尔木兹海峡油价冲击使汽油价格和CPI升向4.2%（油价+72.9%，滞胀象限），在鹰派美联储倾向加息之际挤压实际工资和可选消费支出，使XLY跌至垫底（第11位，-15.0%）。值得注意的是这并非干净的避险——市场广度反而扩大（RSP跑赢SPY +4.3%）——但能源驱动的通胀和更高的利率打击了XLY中利率敏感的大额消费部分，并施压亚马逊和特斯拉。","drivers_zh":["滞胀象限（油价+73%）","油价冲击/汽油挤压","鹰派美联储","市场广度扩大"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Ceasefire relief, but discretionary trails the tech-led tape","body":"A mid-June Iran ceasefire and reopening of the Strait of Hormuz pulled oil back toward $70, easing the pump-price squeeze and sparking a relief bounce in Amazon and Tesla. But XLY (+15.3%) trailed a narrow, tech-led melt-up (Tech +46.4%, semis +65.5%, equal-weight lagging cap-weight -8.8%, VIX 31→16) — discretionary is rejoining risk-on, not leading it, with a hawkish Fed and below-trend positioning keeping the recovery tentative.","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","Iran ceasefire / oil relief","Amazon/Tesla bounce","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"停火纾解，但可选消费落后于科技主导的行情","body_zh":"6月中旬的伊朗停火和霍尔木兹海峡重新开放，使油价回落至约70美元，缓解了汽油价格挤压，并在亚马逊和特斯拉中引发了纾解反弹。但XLY（+15.3%）落后于一轮狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨（Tech +46.4%，半导体+65.5%，等权落后市值权重-8.8%，VIX从31降至16）——可选消费是在重新加入risk-on而非领涨，仍然鹰派的美联储和低于趋势的持仓使复苏保持谨慎。","drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","伊朗停火/油价纾解","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"]}},"now_zh":"XLY正在筑底（相对强度排名第6，周期位置约31，位于200日均线下方），但这一次轮动行情并没有救它——而是把它\"冷落\"了。2026年的逼空上涨狭窄且由科技引领（Tech +24.3%，半导体/SMH +67.9%，高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7%），可选消费却以-5.2%排在11个板块中的第10位，因为消费者受油价驱动的通胀（CPI 4.2%，汽油因伊朗/霍尔木兹冲击飙升）和鹰派美联储挤压。由于亚马逊和特斯拉约占该ETF三分之一，XLY是对这两只股票在油价与利率松动后重新加入risk-on领涨阵营的杠杆化押注；市场广度正在扩大（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%），这是转向的第一道裂缝。"},"b-ai_infra":{"now":"AI infrastructure is topping after a 465% run off the April 2025 low that rode a textbook risk-on melt-up (SMH +271%, VIX collapsing 45->17). The early-June Broadcom AI-outlook miss cracked the leadership just as the regime turned hawkish: DXY +3.4%, a reflation/growth-up quad with Tech and Energy leading, and breadth quietly broadening (RSP +2.9% vs SPY). As a high-beta buildout play, the basket now amplifies any wobble in this dollar-stronger, post-Hormuz tape, trading on whether hyperscaler capex can keep funding compute.","now_zh":"AI基础设施在自2025年4月低点上涨465%后正在筑顶，这轮上涨乘的是教科书式的风险偏好(risk-on)熔涨(半导体SMH +271%、VIX从45崩至17)。6月初博通(Broadcom)未上调AI展望恰好在市场转鹰之际击穿了龙头：美元DXY +3.4%、再通胀/增长向上象限(quad)下科技与能源领涨、市场广度悄然转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)。作为高贝塔的建设主题，该篮子如今放大了这一美元走强、霍尔木兹海峡冲击后行情的任何动摇，交易核心是超大规模云厂商资本开支能否继续为算力提供资金。","legs":{"2021-12-27":{"title":"Rate-shock de-rating in a flight-to-safety","body":"The 2022 Fed-hiking cycle hammered long-duration compute as yields surged (TLT -21.4%) and the dollar ripped +9.4% in a stagflation-ish quad. This was a rate-regime-and-risk-off flush, not a sector event: defensives led (-1.9%) while cyclicals fell -12.8% with VIX 18->27, and as a high-multiple, high-beta group the buildout names amplified the de-rating (SMH -38.1% vs SPY -19.5%). With no AI catalyst yet, there was nothing to offset the brutal repricing.","drivers":["Fed hiking / yields up (TLT -21.4%)","duration de-rating","flight-to-safety (VIX 18->27)","Russia-Ukraine"],"title_zh":"避险中的利率冲击估值重置","body_zh":"2022年美联储加息周期重创了长久期算力，收益率飙升(TLT -21.4%)、美元在类滞胀象限暴涨+9.4%。这是一次利率体制叠加避险(risk-off)的冲洗，而非板块事件：防御股领先(-1.9%)、周期股下跌-12.8%、VIX从18升至27；作为高估值、高贝塔群体，建设股放大了估值下修(SMH -38.1% vs SPY -19.5%)。当时尚无AI催化剂，无从对冲这场残酷的重定价。","drivers_zh":["美联储加息/收益率上行(TLT -21.4%)","久期估值下修","避险(VIX 18->27)","俄乌冲突"]},"2022-07-01":{"title":"Peak-inflation bounce on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A summer relief rally fired on hopes inflation had peaked and the Fed would pivot, and the tape went risk-on: SMH +25.8%, growth beat value (+7.1), VIX cooled 27->20 and oil fell -17.5% in a goldilocks quad. As a high-beta corner, the buildout amplified the melt-up that pulled flows out of defensives, but it was a positioning bounce, not a fundamental turn in AI capex.","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","Fed-pivot bet","risk-on melt-up (SMH +25.8%, VIX 27->20)","oversold bounce"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中的通胀见顶反弹","body_zh":"夏季缓解性反弹源于通胀见顶、美联储转向的预期，行情转向风险偏好(risk-on)：半导体SMH +25.8%、成长跑赢价值(+7.1)、VIX从27降至20、油价在金发女孩象限下跌-17.5%。作为高贝塔领域，建设股放大了这场把资金从防御股抽出的熔涨，但这只是仓位反弹，并非AI资本开支的基本面转折。","drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","押注美联储转向","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +25.8%, VIX 27->20)","超卖反弹"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Hawkish Jackson Hole resets rates","body":"Powell's hard-line Jackson Hole killed the pivot trade and sent yields back up (TLT -14.2%) with the dollar +6.3% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. VIX spiked 20->32 and the move was broad-and-rate-driven (cyclicals -13.4%, defensives -12.5%), but as the most rate-sensitive corner of tech the long-duration buildout led the laggards (SMH -29.8% vs SPY -16.3%).","drivers":["hawkish Powell","rate-regime move (TLT -14.2%)","stronger dollar (+6.3%)","VIX 20->32"],"title_zh":"鹰派杰克逊霍尔会议重置利率","body_zh":"鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的强硬表态终结了转向交易，收益率重新上行(TLT -14.2%)、美元在放缓/通缩恐慌象限走强+6.3%。VIX飙升20->32，这是一次广泛且由利率驱动的下跌(周期股-13.4%、防御股-12.5%)，但作为科技板块对利率最敏感的领域，长久期建设股领跌(SMH -29.8% vs SPY -16.3%)。","drivers_zh":["鲍威尔鹰派","利率体制移动(TLT -14.2%)","美元走强(+6.3%)","VIX 20->32"]},"2022-10-14":{"title":"ChatGPT ignites the supercycle into a narrow melt-up","body":"From the October 2022 low, ChatGPT's late-November launch detonated a generative-AI capex supercycle, with Nvidia and the datacenter/networking stack the prime beneficiaries. The macro could not have been more supportive: a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +230.6%, growth>value +55.3, VIX 32->13, DXY -7.3%) in a goldilocks quad, but it was a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY by -28.4%). Hyperscaler GPU orders plus the first Fed cuts in September 2024 powered a 261% run.","drivers":["ChatGPT / genAI","Nvidia datacenter","narrow risk-on melt-up (SMH +231%, RSP -28.4% vs SPY)","Fed cuts begin"],"title_zh":"ChatGPT在窄幅熔涨中点燃超级周期","body_zh":"从2022年10月低点起，ChatGPT于11月底发布引爆了生成式AI资本开支超级周期，英伟达(Nvidia)与数据中心/网络产业链是主要受益者。宏观环境再支持不过：金发女孩象限下科技/半导体引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +230.6%、成长跑赢价值+55.3、VIX 32->13、DXY -7.3%)，但这是窄幅的大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -28.4%)。超大规模云厂商GPU订单加上2024年9月首次降息，推动篮子上涨261%。","drivers_zh":["ChatGPT/生成式AI","英伟达数据中心","窄幅风险偏好熔涨(SMH +231%, RSP跑输SPY -28.4%)","美联储开启降息"]},"2024-07-10":{"title":"Yen-carry unwind air-pocket","body":"An August 2024 yen-carry unwind hit crowded AI-compute longs hardest in a sudden flight-to-safety: VIX exploded 13->28, defensives led (+2.2%) while cyclicals fell -5.5%, and breadth broadened (RSP +6.6% vs SPY) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The fundamental buildout was untouched, but as a high-beta, over-owned leveraged long the basket took an outsized -24.8% SMH hit versus SPY's -7.6%.","drivers":["yen-carry unwind","flight-to-safety (VIX 13->28)","deleveraging","crowded high-beta longs"],"title_zh":"日元套息平仓的空气陷阱","body_zh":"2024年8月的日元套息平仓在突然的避险中对拥挤的AI算力多头打击最重：VIX从13暴涨至28、防御股领先(+2.2%)、周期股下跌-5.5%、市场广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%)，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。建设基本面未受影响，但作为高贝塔、过度持仓的杠杆多头，该篮子遭受超额下跌(SMH -24.8% vs SPY -7.6%)。","drivers_zh":["日元套息平仓","避险(VIX 13->28)","去杠杆","拥挤的高贝塔多头"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Capex melt-up resumes in a narrow risk-on tape","body":"Once the carry shock cleared, hyperscaler capex guidance and relentless GPU demand drove a 50% recovery into late January 2025, riding a tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +26.9%, growth>value +13.9, VIX 28->15) in a goldilocks quad. It was a narrow mega-cap leadership tape (RSP -5.7% vs SPY) even as yields rose (TLT -7.2%) and the dollar firmed +4.8% — the buildout reclaimed leadership as the capex narrative re-accelerated.","drivers":["hyperscaler capex","GPU demand","narrow risk-on (SMH +26.9%, VIX 28->15, RSP -5.7%)","leadership reclaimed"],"title_zh":"资本开支熔涨在窄幅风险偏好行情中重启","body_zh":"套息冲击消退后，超大规模云厂商资本开支指引与持续的GPU需求推动篮子在2025年1月底前回升50%，乘的是科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +26.9%、成长跑赢价值+13.9、VIX 28->15)，处于金发女孩象限。这是窄幅大盘股领导行情(RSP跑输SPY -5.7%)，尽管收益率上行(TLT -7.2%)、美元走强+4.8%——随着资本开支叙事再加速，建设股夺回领导地位。","drivers_zh":["超大规模云厂商资本开支","GPU需求","窄幅风险偏好(SMH +26.9%, VIX 28->15, RSP -5.7%)","夺回领导地位"]},"2025-01-22":{"title":"DeepSeek scare flushes high-beta into a VIX spike","body":"DeepSeek's late-January cheap-model claim triggered a violent re-rating of the compute thesis, with Nvidia logging a record single-day market-cap loss. It hit during a flight-to-safety flush — VIX rocketed 15->45, defensives held (-2.2%) while cyclicals collapsed -16.3%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -27.1) — that deepened into April's Liberation Day tariff crash. As the leveraged long of the AI complex the basket led the wreck (SMH -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%), bottoming around April 8.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","capex-efficiency fear","risk-off flush (VIX 15->45, high-beta -27.1)","Liberation Day tariffs"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌在VIX飙升中冲洗高贝塔","body_zh":"DeepSeek在1月底声称的廉价模型引发了算力逻辑的剧烈重定价，英伟达录得史上最大单日市值损失。它在一次避险冲洗中发生——VIX从15飙至45、防御股守住(-2.2%)而周期股崩跌-16.3%、高贝塔被重创(SPHB-SPLV -27.1)——并延续至4月“解放日”关税崩盘。作为AI板块的杠杆多头，篮子领跌(SMH -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%)，在4月8日前后见底。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","资本开支效率担忧","避险冲洗(VIX 15->45, 高贝塔-27.1)","“解放日”对等关税"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"465% melt-up off the tariff low","body":"Off the April 2025 tariff low the buildout exploded 465% on resurgent hyperscaler capex, riding the most violent risk-on reset of the cycle: VIX collapsed 45->17 and high-beta dominated (SPHB-SPLV +124.5) in a reflation/growth-up quad with Tech +111.9% leading. As the high-beta proxy for the entire compute trade the basket maximally amplified the melt-up (SMH +271.1% vs SPY +49.0%), in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -13.4% vs SPY).","drivers":["hyperscaler capex","violent risk-on reset (VIX 45->17, high-beta +124.5)","narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -13.4%)","reflation quad"],"title_zh":"自关税低点的465%熔涨","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点，建设股在重燃的超大规模云厂商资本开支推动下暴涨465%，乘的是本周期最猛烈的风险偏好重置：VIX从45崩至17、高贝塔主导(SPHB-SPLV +124.5)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限、科技+111.9%领涨。作为整个算力交易的高贝塔代理，篮子最大化放大了熔涨(SMH +271.1% vs SPY +49.0%)，处于窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -13.4%)。","drivers_zh":["超大规模云厂商资本开支","猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX 45->17, 高贝塔+124.5)","窄幅大盘股行情(RSP -13.4%)","再通胀象限"]}}},"b-ai_software":{"now":"AI software is trending but mid-pack on relative strength, having given back 22% since June 2026 as the semis-led wipeout spread up the stack. The backdrop has turned hawkish: DXY +3.4%, a reflation/growth-up quad where Tech and Energy lead but breadth is broadening (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) and growth lags value (-15.2). As a long-duration high-beta group the application layer feels every dollar-stronger, higher-rate twist, now hanging on whether enterprise AI monetization (Microsoft Copilot, Palantir) can justify multiples.","now_zh":"AI软件处于趋势中但相对强度居中，自2026年6月以来回吐22%，因半导体引领的暴跌沿产业链向上蔓延。背景已转鹰：美元DXY +3.4%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限(quad)、科技与能源领涨但市场广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、成长跑输价值(-15.2)。作为长久期高贝塔群体，应用层感受着每一次美元走强、利率上行的转折，如今取决于企业AI变现(微软Copilot、Palantir)能否支撑估值倍数。","legs":{"2021-11-16":{"title":"SaaS de-rating leads a flight-to-safety","body":"High-multiple application and platform software led the 2021-22 growth wreck as yields surged (TLT -8.7%) and the dollar firmed +3.3% in a stagflation-ish quad. It was a risk-off rotation — defensives held (+0.8%) vs cyclicals -5.1% with VIX 16->32 — and as the longest-duration corner of tech, SaaS amplified it (Tech -16.1%, SMH -21.2% vs SPY -10.8%). With AI monetization years away, the group had no earnings story to defend its multiples.","drivers":["rates up (TLT -8.7%)","SaaS de-rating","flight-to-safety (VIX 16->32)","growth unwind"],"title_zh":"SaaS估值下修领跌避险行情","body_zh":"高估值的应用与平台软件领跌2021-22年的成长股崩塌，收益率飙升(TLT -8.7%)、美元在类滞胀象限走强+3.3%。这是一次避险(risk-off)轮动——防御股守住(+0.8%) vs 周期股-5.1%、VIX从16升至32——作为科技中久期最长的领域，SaaS放大了跌幅(科技-16.1%、SMH -21.2% vs SPY -10.8%)。当时AI变现尚需数年，该板块没有盈利故事来捍卫估值倍数。","drivers_zh":["利率上行(TLT -8.7%)","SaaS估值下修","避险(VIX 16->32)","成长股平仓"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Oversold relief in a narrow risk-on bounce","body":"A sharp but brief bounce off oversold levels lifted software as VIX collapsed 32->19 and growth beat value (+9.5) in a reflation/growth-up quad. It was a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP -3.0% vs SPY) and pure positioning — the relief faded fast as the hiking path steepened.","drivers":["oversold bounce","risk-on snapback (VIX 32->19)","narrow breadth (RSP -3.0%)","rate-fear pause"],"title_zh":"窄幅风险偏好反弹中的超卖修复","body_zh":"软件股从超卖水平出现短暂而剧烈的反弹，VIX从32崩至19、成长跑赢价值(+9.5)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。这是窄幅大盘股领导行情(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)、纯仓位驱动——随着加息路径变陡，这波修复很快消退。","drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","风险偏好回升(VIX 32->19)","窄幅广度(RSP -3.0%)","利率担忧暂缓"]},"2022-04-04":{"title":"Real-yield repricing in a stagflation flush","body":"Software resumed its slide as the Fed signaled a faster, steeper path and real yields surged (TLT -14.7%), with the dollar +4.7% in a stagflation-ish quad. The flight-to-safety was deep (defensives -11.5% vs cyclicals -17.1%, VIX 19->33), and profitless application names with no near-term earnings were repriced hardest (Tech -23.5% vs SPY -19.7%).","drivers":["faster hikes / real yields up (TLT -14.7%)","stagflation flush (VIX 19->33)","stronger dollar (+4.7%)","profitability fear"],"title_zh":"类滞胀冲洗中的实际收益率重定价","body_zh":"随着美联储释放更快、更陡峭路径信号、实际收益率飙升(TLT -14.7%)、美元在类滞胀象限走强+4.7%，软件股恢复下跌。避险很深(防御股-11.5% vs 周期股-17.1%、VIX 19->33)，缺乏近期盈利的应用层个股被重定价得最重(科技-23.5% vs SPY -19.7%)。","drivers_zh":["加息加速/实际收益率上行(TLT -14.7%)","类滞胀冲洗(VIX 19->33)","美元走强(+4.7%)","盈利能力担忧"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-rate-fear bounce on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A summer rally on hopes the worst of tightening was priced lifted software off its June low, as the tape went risk-on: SMH +20.8%, growth>value (+9.2), VIX cooled 33->20 and oil crashed -24.0% in a goldilocks quad. The move was sentiment-driven and high-beta amplified, with no earnings support, and it unwound into the autumn.","drivers":["peak-rate hope","risk-on melt-up (SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","disinflation (oil -24%)","no earnings support"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中的利率恐慌见顶反弹","body_zh":"夏季反弹源于市场预期最糟紧缩已被消化，将软件股托离6月低点，行情转向风险偏好：SMH +20.8%、成长跑赢价值(+9.2)、VIX从33降至20、油价在金发女孩象限崩跌-24.0%。这波走势由情绪驱动、被高贝塔放大、缺乏盈利支撑，并在秋季回落。","drivers_zh":["利率见顶预期","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","去通胀(油价-24%)","无盈利支撑"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Final tightening leg, rate-driven low","body":"Hawkish Fed messaging and surging yields (TLT -9.5%) drove software to its cycle low into early January 2023 in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. It was a broad, rate-led drawdown (breadth broadened, RSP +4.9% vs SPY) rather than a panic, and the long-duration group bottomed (Tech -19.6% vs SPY -10.8%) just before the AI narrative arrived.","drivers":["hawkish Fed","rate-regime move (TLT -9.5%)","broadening (RSP +4.9%)","cycle low"],"title_zh":"紧缩末段、利率驱动的低点","body_zh":"鹰派的美联储表态与飙升的收益率(TLT -9.5%)将软件股推至2023年初的周期低点，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。这是广泛、由利率驱动的回撤(广度转宽，RSP跑赢SPY +4.9%)而非恐慌，长久期板块见底(科技-19.6% vs SPY -10.8%)恰好在AI叙事到来前。","drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派","利率体制移动(TLT -9.5%)","广度转宽(RSP +4.9%)","周期低点"]},"2023-01-05":{"title":"AI platform supercycle in a narrow goldilocks melt-up","body":"From the January 2023 low, generative AI turned software platforms into the prime monetization vehicle, with Microsoft Copilot and Palantir leading a 268% run. The macro was a textbook tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +155.3%, growth>value +67.1, VIX 22->15) in a goldilocks quad, but extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -32.7%) — a mega-cap tape — even as yields rose (TLT -7.8%). Fed cuts from September 2024 and an AI land-grab compounded the move despite the SVB scare and yen-carry air-pocket.","drivers":["genAI platforms","Microsoft / Palantir","narrow risk-on melt-up (SMH +155%, RSP -32.7% vs SPY)","Fed cuts"],"title_zh":"窄幅金发女孩熔涨中的AI平台超级周期","body_zh":"从2023年1月低点起，生成式AI使软件平台成为首要变现载体，微软Copilot与Palantir领涨，涨幅268%。宏观是教科书式科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +155.3%、成长跑赢价值+67.1、VIX 22->15)，处于金发女孩象限，但极度窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -32.7%)——大盘股行情——尽管收益率上行(TLT -7.8%)。2024年9月起的美联储降息与AI跑马圈地放大了行情，尽管经历硅谷银行恐慌与日元套息空气陷阱。","drivers_zh":["生成式AI平台","微软/Palantir","窄幅风险偏好熔涨(SMH +155%, RSP跑输SPY -32.7%)","美联储降息"]},"2025-02-18":{"title":"DeepSeek and tariff crash flush high-beta","body":"DeepSeek's cheap-AI scare bled into software on fears cheaper models would commoditize the application layer, then deepened in April's Liberation Day tariff crash. It was a flight-to-safety flush — VIX rocketed 15->45, defensives held (-4.8%) vs cyclicals -16.7%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -25.0) — and as a long-duration high-beta group software led the laggards (Tech -24.6% vs SPY -17.1%), bottoming near April 4 with the broad market.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","commoditization fear","risk-off flush (VIX 15->45, high-beta -25.0)","Liberation Day tariffs"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税崩盘冲洗高贝塔","body_zh":"DeepSeek廉价AI恐慌蔓延至软件，市场担忧更便宜的模型会使应用层商品化，随后在4月“解放日”关税崩盘中加深。这是一次避险冲洗——VIX从15飙至45、防御股守住(-4.8%) vs 周期股-16.7%、高贝塔被重创(SPHB-SPLV -25.0)——作为长久期高贝塔群体，软件领跌(科技-24.6% vs SPY -17.1%)，在4月4日前后随大盘见底。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","商品化担忧","避险冲洗(VIX 15->45, 高贝塔-25.0)","“解放日”对等关税"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Monetization-proof recovery on a risk-on reset","body":"The tariff pause and stronger enterprise AI bookings drove a 67% recovery as Copilot-style seat monetization proved real, riding a violent risk-on reset (VIX collapsed 45->16, high-beta dominated SPHB-SPLV +65.5, DXY -4.1%) in a goldilocks quad with Tech +64.4% leading. It was a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -13.1% vs SPY); the rally stalled in late October into a hawkish valuation reset.","drivers":["tariff pause","enterprise AI bookings","risk-on reset (VIX 45->16, high-beta +65.5)","narrow breadth (RSP -13.1%)"],"title_zh":"风险偏好重置下的变现验证复苏","body_zh":"关税暂停与更强劲的企业AI订单推动67%的复苏，因Copilot式席位变现被证明真实可行，乘的是猛烈的风险偏好重置(VIX从45崩至16、高贝塔主导SPHB-SPLV +65.5、DXY -4.1%)，处于金发女孩象限、科技+64.4%领涨。这是窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -13.1%)；反弹在10月底因鹰派估值重置而停滞。","drivers_zh":["关税暂停","企业AI订单","风险偏好重置(VIX 45->16, 高贝塔+65.5)","窄幅广度(RSP -13.1%)"]},"2025-10-27":{"title":"Hawkish valuation reset, rate-driven","body":"A late-2025 hawkish repricing compressed the richest software multiples, then the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock (oil +57.5%) pushed CPI to ~4.2% and a Fed hiking bias deepened the drawdown in a reflation/growth-up quad. The pain was rate-driven and rotation-led — Energy +30.9% led while growth lagged value (-15.7) and breadth broadened (RSP +3.5% vs SPY) — and long-duration software bore the brunt of higher discount rates (Tech -4.3% even as SMH held +21.8%) into April 2026.","drivers":["valuation reset","Hormuz oil shock (oil +57.5%)","CPI ~4.2% / Fed hiking bias","growth-lags-value rotation (-15.7)"],"title_zh":"利率驱动的鹰派估值重置","body_zh":"2025年末的鹰派重定价压缩了估值最高的软件倍数，随后2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+57.5%)将CPI推升至约4.2%、美联储转向加息倾向，在再通胀/增长向上象限加深回撤。痛苦由利率驱动、板块轮动主导——能源+30.9%领涨、成长跑输价值(-15.7)、广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +3.5%)——长久期软件在更高贴现率下首当其冲(科技-4.3%，尽管SMH守住+21.8%)，延续至2026年4月。","drivers_zh":["估值重置","霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+57.5%)","CPI约4.2%/美联储加息倾向","成长跑输价值轮动(-15.7)"]},"2026-04-10":{"title":"Ceasefire risk-on bounce","body":"Software rebounded 53% as the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire eased the oil-and-rates overhang (oil -4.6%) and risk appetite returned: SMH +39.1%, growth>value (+8.6), VIX cooled 19->16 in a reflation/growth-up quad. As a high-beta group it amplified the snapback (Tech +37.1% led, SMH +39.1% vs SPY +11.4%) in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -5.4% vs SPY) before breadth narrowed again.","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire","risk-on (SMH +39.1%, VIX 19->16)","rates relief (oil -4.6%)","narrow breadth (RSP -5.4%)"],"title_zh":"停火后的风险偏好反弹","body_zh":"随着6月中旬霍尔木兹海峡停火缓解油价与利率压制(油价-4.6%)、风险偏好回归，软件股反弹53%：SMH +39.1%、成长跑赢价值(+8.6)、VIX从19降至16，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。作为高贝塔群体，它放大了这波回升(科技+37.1%领涨、SMH +39.1% vs SPY +11.4%)，处于窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -5.4%)，随后市场广度再度收窄。","drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火","风险偏好(SMH +39.1%, VIX 19->16)","利率压力缓解(油价-4.6%)","窄幅广度(RSP -5.4%)"]},"2026-06-01":{"title":"Semis wipeout spreads up into a flight-to-safety","body":"Broadcom's early-June refusal to raise its AI outlook triggered a semis wipeout that spread up the stack into software as the tape went risk-off: defensives led (+5.3%) vs cyclicals -0.1%, VIX rose 16->19, oil crashed -22.0% and growth lagged value (-11.5) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Breadth broadened (RSP +4.6% vs SPY) as the application layer gave back 22% (Tech -5.6%, Comm -8.4%) and the market questioned whether AI spend would keep funding software multiples.","drivers":["Broadcom miss","flight-to-safety (VIX 16->19, defensives led)","growth-lags-value (-11.5)","AI-spend doubt"],"title_zh":"半导体暴跌在避险中向上蔓延","body_zh":"博通在6月初拒绝上调AI展望，引发半导体暴跌，并沿产业链向上蔓延至软件，行情转向避险：防御股领先(+5.3%) vs 周期股-0.1%、VIX升至16->19、油价崩跌-22.0%、成长跑输价值(-11.5)，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +4.6%)，应用层回吐22%(科技-5.6%、通讯-8.4%)，市场质疑AI支出能否继续支撑软件估值。","drivers_zh":["博通不及预期","避险(VIX 16->19, 防御股领先)","成长跑输价值(-11.5)","AI支出存疑"]}}},"b-ai_agents":{"now":"The agentic AI layer is at prime entry after a 49% drawdown into April 2026, the deepest in the AI complex given its speculative, application-native profile — exactly what a long-duration high-beta basket does when the regime turns. The tape is now reflation/growth-up with DXY +3.4%, broadening breadth (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) and growth lagging value (-15.2), a mixed setup for the longest-duration, least-profitable AI names. Recovery hinges on whether agent platforms convert pilots into recurring revenue while higher rates punish profitless growth.","now_zh":"AI智能体层在2026年4月前经历49%回撤后处于理想入场点，因其投机性、应用原生属性，这是整个AI板块中最深的回撤——正是长久期高贝塔篮子在体制转向时的表现。当前行情为再通胀/增长向上、美元DXY +3.4%、广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、成长跑输价值(-15.2)，对久期最长、盈利最差的AI个股是喜忧参半的格局。复苏取决于智能体平台能否将试点转化为经常性收入，而更高的利率正在惩罚无盈利成长。","legs":{"2021-02-09":{"title":"Growth-froth top as rates twitch","body":"Speculative application software topped early as the 2021 growth froth peaked and the first yield twitch began rotation out of long-duration tech (TLT -8.4%, growth lagged value -13.2). In a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (RSP +5.4% vs SPY, Financials/Energy/Materials led) the most unprofitable, highest-beta corner led the decline even as SPY rose +5.5% — high-beta cracking before the index.","drivers":["growth froth","early rate rotation (TLT -8.4%, growth-val -13.2)","broadening (RSP +5.4%)","high-beta top"],"title_zh":"利率初动下的成长泡沫见顶","body_zh":"投机性应用软件提早见顶，因2021年成长泡沫触顶、收益率首次抽动开启资金轮出长久期科技(TLT -8.4%、成长跑输价值-13.2)。在转宽的再通胀/增长向上行情中(RSP跑赢SPY +5.4%、金融/能源/材料领涨)，最不盈利、高贝塔的领域领跌，尽管SPY上涨+5.5%——高贝塔先于指数破位。","drivers_zh":["成长泡沫","早期利率轮动(TLT -8.4%, 成长-价值-13.2)","广度转宽(RSP +5.4%)","高贝塔见顶"]},"2021-05-13":{"title":"Liquidity-fueled final melt-up","body":"Abundant liquidity powered a final 45% melt-up in speculative app software into the November 2021 peak, riding a tech-led risk-on tape (SMH +30.1%, growth>value +18.3, VIX 23->15) in a reflation/growth-up quad with falling yields (TLT +9.2%). It was a narrow mega-cap melt-up (RSP -5.7% vs SPY) — the last hurrah before the rate cycle turned.","drivers":["easy liquidity / falling yields (TLT +9.2%)","risk-on melt-up (SMH +30.1%, VIX 23->15)","narrow breadth (RSP -5.7%)","final melt-up"],"title_zh":"流动性驱动的最后熔涨","body_zh":"充裕流动性推动投机性应用软件在2021年11月见顶前完成最后45%熔涨，乘的是科技引领的风险偏好行情(SMH +30.1%、成长跑赢价值+18.3、VIX 23->15)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限、收益率回落(TLT +9.2%)。这是窄幅大盘股熔涨(RSP跑输SPY -5.7%)——利率周期转向前的最后狂欢。","drivers_zh":["宽松流动性/收益率回落(TLT +9.2%)","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +30.1%, VIX 23->15)","窄幅广度(RSP -5.7%)","最后熔涨"]},"2021-11-04":{"title":"Rate-cycle de-rating in a flight-to-safety","body":"The Fed's hawkish pivot crushed the highest-multiple, lowest-profit software hardest, a 49% collapse into March 2022 as yields surged (TLT -10.0%) and the dollar firmed +5.0% in a stagflation-ish quad. The flight-to-safety (defensives +1.0% vs cyclicals -4.1%, VIX 15->32) left long-duration cash-burners nowhere to hide (Tech -14.8%, Comm -21.3%), with the basket amplifying the index drop.","drivers":["hawkish pivot","rate-regime move (TLT -10.0%)","flight-to-safety (VIX 15->32)","cash-burn fear"],"title_zh":"避险中的利率周期估值下修","body_zh":"美联储鹰派转向对估值最高、盈利最差的软件打击最重，在2022年3月前暴跌49%，收益率飙升(TLT -10.0%)、美元在类滞胀象限走强+5.0%。避险(防御股+1.0% vs 周期股-4.1%、VIX 15->32)让长久期烧钱股无处可藏(科技-14.8%、通讯-21.3%)，篮子放大了指数跌幅。","drivers_zh":["鹰派转向","利率体制移动(TLT -10.0%)","避险(VIX 15->32)","烧钱担忧"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Oversold snapback on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A violent 28% two-week bounce off deeply oversold levels reflected positioning, not a turn, as VIX collapsed 32->19 and the tape went risk-on (SMH +18.8%, growth>value +8.7) in a reflation/growth-up quad. It was a narrow mega-cap melt-up (RSP -2.4% vs SPY) and reversed almost immediately.","drivers":["oversold snapback","risk-on melt-up (SMH +18.8%, VIX 32->19)","narrow breadth (RSP -2.4%)","positioning"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中的超卖反弹","body_zh":"深度超卖后两周内剧烈反弹28%，反映仓位调整而非转折，VIX从32崩至19、行情转向风险偏好(SMH +18.8%、成长跑赢价值+8.7)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。这是窄幅大盘股熔涨(RSP跑输SPY -2.4%)，几乎立即逆转。","drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +18.8%, VIX 32->19)","窄幅广度(RSP -2.4%)","仓位调整"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Resumed rate selloff, flight-to-safety","body":"Surging real yields (TLT -9.5%) and a stronger dollar (+5.5%) drove speculative software down another 39% into May in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The flight-to-safety was sharp (defensives -4.2% vs cyclicals -13.1%, VIX 19->33), and profitless growth remained the most punished factor (Tech -18.7%, Discretionary -24.0% vs SPY -14.9%).","drivers":["real yields up (TLT -9.5%)","flight-to-safety (VIX 19->33)","stronger dollar (+5.5%)","profitless growth"],"title_zh":"避险中的利率抛售重启","body_zh":"实际收益率飙升(TLT -9.5%)与美元走强(+5.5%)推动投机性软件在5月前再跌39%，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。避险剧烈(防御股-4.2% vs 周期股-13.1%、VIX 19->33)，无盈利成长仍是受惩罚最重的因子(科技-18.7%、可选消费-24.0% vs SPY -14.9%)。","drivers_zh":["实际收益率上行(TLT -9.5%)","避险(VIX 19->33)","美元走强(+5.5%)","无盈利成长"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Bear-market relief bounce","body":"A 33% bear-market rally fired on peak-inflation hopes and short-covering in the most beaten-down names, as VIX eased 33->25 in a reflation/growth-up quad (oil +10.6%, Energy led). The high-beta basket amplified the bounce (SMH +13.4% vs SPY +6.3%), but with no earnings support it faded.","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","short-covering (VIX 33->25)","high-beta amplification (SMH +13.4%)","no earnings support"],"title_zh":"熊市修复反弹","body_zh":"33%的熊市反弹源于通胀见顶预期与跌幅最深个股的空头回补，VIX在再通胀/增长向上象限缓和33->25(油价+10.6%、能源领涨)。高贝塔篮子放大了反弹(SMH +13.4% vs SPY +6.3%)，但缺乏盈利支撑随后消退。","drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","空头回补(VIX 33->25)","高贝塔放大(SMH +13.4%)","无盈利支撑"]},"2022-06-02":{"title":"Capitulation to the cycle low","body":"Relentless hiking and liquidity withdrawal drove a 48% capitulation into late December 2022, the cycle bottom, as yields surged (TLT -13.0%) and oil collapsed -32.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Defensives held (+1.0%) vs cyclicals -7.2% in a broadening tape (RSP +2.8% vs SPY); the highest-beta group was left for dead (Comm -22.9%) just as generative AI was about to arrive.","drivers":["liquidity withdrawal / yields up (TLT -13.0%)","slowdown quad (oil -32.4%)","broadening (RSP +2.8%)","cycle bottom"],"title_zh":"投降式下跌至周期低点","body_zh":"持续加息与流动性收紧推动该板块在2022年12月底投降式下跌48%，触及周期底部，收益率飙升(TLT -13.0%)、油价在放缓/通缩恐慌象限崩跌-32.4%。防御股守住(+1.0%) vs 周期股-7.2%，处于转宽行情(RSP跑赢SPY +2.8%)；这个最高贝塔群体被弃如敝屣(通讯-22.9%)，就在生成式AI即将到来之际。","drivers_zh":["流动性收紧/收益率上行(TLT -13.0%)","放缓象限(油价-32.4%)","广度转宽(RSP +2.8%)","周期底部"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"AI-application supercycle, the highest-beta winner","body":"From the December 2022 low the agentic/AI-application thesis drove an extraordinary 934% run as ChatGPT created a new monetization layer and Fed cuts began September 2024. The macro was a textbook tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +158.0%, growth>value +65.0, VIX 22->15) in a goldilocks quad, but extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -32.0%) — a mega-cap tape. As the highest-beta corner of AI the basket maximally amplified every up-leg of the buildout.","drivers":["AI applications / ChatGPT","narrow risk-on melt-up (SMH +158%, RSP -32.0% vs SPY)","Fed cuts","highest beta"],"title_zh":"AI应用超级周期，最高贝塔的赢家","body_zh":"从2022年12月低点起，智能体/AI应用逻辑推动了惊人的934%涨幅，因ChatGPT创造全新变现层、美联储于2024年9月开启降息。宏观是教科书式科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +158.0%、成长跑赢价值+65.0、VIX 22->15)，处于金发女孩象限，但极度窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -32.0%)——大盘股行情。作为AI中贝塔最高的领域，篮子最大化放大了建设主题的每一段上涨。","drivers_zh":["AI应用/ChatGPT","窄幅风险偏好熔涨(SMH +158%, RSP跑输SPY -32.0%)","美联储降息","最高贝塔"]},"2025-02-13":{"title":"DeepSeek hits app layer in a VIX panic","body":"DeepSeek's cheap-model scare hit the agent layer hardest on fears commoditized models would gut application economics, then deepened in the Liberation Day tariff crash. It was a flight-to-safety panic — VIX exploded 15->52, defensives held (-7.3%) vs cyclicals -18.0%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -20.9) — and as the highest-beta basket it led the wreck (Tech -24.7% vs SPY -18.3%), falling 38% to its April 8 bottom.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","model commoditization","flight-to-safety panic (VIX 15->52, high-beta -20.9)","Liberation Day tariffs"],"title_zh":"VIX恐慌中DeepSeek冲击应用层","body_zh":"DeepSeek廉价模型恐慌对智能体层打击最重，市场担忧商品化模型会侵蚀应用经济效益，随后在“解放日”关税崩盘中加深。这是一次避险恐慌——VIX从15暴涨至52、防御股守住(-7.3%) vs 周期股-18.0%、高贝塔被重创(SPHB-SPLV -20.9)——作为贝塔最高的篮子，它领跌(科技-24.7% vs SPY -18.3%)，下跌38%至4月8日底部。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","模型商品化","避险恐慌(VIX 15->52, 高贝塔-20.9)","“解放日”对等关税"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Agent-hype recovery on a violent risk-on reset","body":"The tariff pause and surging interest in agentic platforms drove a 93% snapback as enterprises piloted AI agents at scale, riding a violent risk-on reset (VIX collapsed 52->16, high-beta dominated SPHB-SPLV +61.1, DXY -3.3%) in a goldilocks quad with Tech +61.9% leading. As the highest-beta AI corner in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -11.1% vs SPY), it led the rebound before topping in October 2025.","drivers":["tariff pause","agent hype","violent risk-on reset (VIX 52->16, high-beta +61.1)","narrow breadth (RSP -11.1%)"],"title_zh":"猛烈风险偏好重置中的智能体热潮复苏","body_zh":"关税暂停与对智能体平台的兴趣激增推动93%的回升，因企业大规模试点AI智能体，乘的是猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX从52崩至16、高贝塔主导SPHB-SPLV +61.1、DXY -3.3%)，处于金发女孩象限、科技+61.9%领涨。作为贝塔最高的AI领域，在窄幅大盘股行情中(RSP跑输SPY -11.1%)领涨这波反弹，随后在2025年10月见顶。","drivers_zh":["关税暂停","智能体热潮","猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX 52->16, 高贝塔+61.1)","窄幅广度(RSP -11.1%)"]},"2025-10-09":{"title":"Deepest AI drawdown, rate-and-rotation driven","body":"A hawkish valuation reset plus the 2026 Hormuz oil shock (oil +57.0%) and Fed hiking bias drove a 49% collapse, the deepest in the AI complex given the basket's speculative profile. In a reflation/growth-up quad the rotation was punishing — Energy +31.7% led, growth lagged value (-15.6), breadth broadened (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) — and higher discount rates fell hardest on the longest-duration, least-profitable agent names (Tech -1.4% even as SMH held +26.9%).","drivers":["valuation reset","Hormuz oil shock (oil +57.0%)","Fed hiking bias / growth-lags-value (-15.6)","duration pain"],"title_zh":"利率与轮动驱动的AI最深回撤","body_zh":"鹰派估值重置叠加2026年霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+57.0%)与美联储加息倾向，推动篮子暴跌49%，鉴于其投机属性，这是整个AI板块最深的回撤。在再通胀/增长向上象限，轮动颇为残酷——能源+31.7%领涨、成长跑输价值(-15.6)、广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)——更高贴现率对久期最长、盈利最差的智能体个股打击最重(科技-1.4%，尽管SMH守住+26.9%)。","drivers_zh":["估值重置","霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+57.0%)","美联储加息倾向/成长跑输价值(-15.6)","久期承压"]},"2026-04-10":{"title":"Ceasefire high-beta snapback","body":"The mid-June Hormuz ceasefire and easing oil-and-rates pressure (oil -4.6%) drove a 40% high-beta bounce off the April low, with VIX cooling 19->16 and growth beating value (+8.6) in a reflation/growth-up quad. As the highest-beta AI corner it amplified the snapback (Tech +37.1% led, SMH +39.1% vs SPY +11.4%) in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -5.4% vs SPY); whether it holds depends on agent platforms converting pilots into durable recurring revenue.","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire","rates relief (oil -4.6%)","high-beta risk-on bounce (SMH +39.1%, VIX 19->16)","narrow breadth (RSP -5.4%)"],"title_zh":"停火后的高贝塔反弹","body_zh":"6月中旬霍尔木兹海峡停火与油价、利率压力缓解(油价-4.6%)，推动这个高贝塔篮子自4月低点反弹40%，VIX降至19->16、成长跑赢价值(+8.6)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。作为贝塔最高的AI领域，它放大了回升(科技+37.1%领涨、SMH +39.1% vs SPY +11.4%)，处于窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -5.4%)；能否持续取决于智能体平台能否将试点转化为持久的经常性收入。","drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火","利率压力缓解(油价-4.6%)","高贝塔风险偏好反弹(SMH +39.1%, VIX 19->16)","窄幅广度(RSP -5.4%)"]}}},"b-ai_neoclouds":{"now":"GPU-cloud hosting is trending and ranks #2 on relative strength after a 570% run off the April 2025 low that rode a violent risk-on melt-up (SMH +268%, VIX 52->16, high-beta dominant). Its high-beta, capital-intensive profile makes it the sharpest amplifier of the regime — it now meets a hawkish turn (DXY +3.4%, reflation/growth-up quad, broadening breadth RSP +2.9% vs SPY) where the early-June Broadcom outlook miss is the first real test of whether GPU-leasing economics hold as the buildout matures.","now_zh":"GPU云托管处于趋势中，在自2025年4月低点上涨570%后相对强度排名第2，这轮上涨乘的是猛烈的风险偏好(risk-on)熔涨(半导体SMH +268%、VIX 52->16、高贝塔主导)。其高贝塔、重资本属性使其成为体制最锋利的放大器——如今遭遇转鹰(美元DXY +3.4%、再通胀/增长向上象限、广度转宽RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)，6月初博通未上调展望是对GPU租赁经济效益能否在建设成熟期保持稳健的首次真正考验。","legs":{"2021-11-12":{"title":"Pre-pivot leverage wipeout in a dollar surge","body":"These capital-intensive, high-beta names (many ex-bitcoin miners) collapsed 84% as the rate cycle turned, yields surged (TLT -21.2%) and the dollar exploded +10.0% in a stagflation-ish quad. It was a flight-to-safety (defensives +1.8% vs cyclicals -13.7%, VIX 16->29) and crypto/leverage unwind, and as the highest-beta corner with no AI-compute story the group massively amplified the index drop (SMH -32.0% vs SPY -18.4%).","drivers":["rates up (TLT -21.2%) / dollar +10.0%","flight-to-safety (VIX 16->29)","crypto-leverage unwind","leverage wipeout"],"title_zh":"美元飙升中转向前的杠杆崩塌","body_zh":"这些重资本、高贝塔个股(许多是前比特币矿企)暴跌84%，因利率周期转向、收益率飙升(TLT -21.2%)、美元在类滞胀象限暴涨+10.0%。这是避险(防御股+1.8% vs 周期股-13.7%、VIX 16->29)与加密/杠杆平仓，作为没有AI算力故事的最高贝塔领域，该板块巨幅放大了指数跌幅(SMH -32.0% vs SPY -18.4%)。","drivers_zh":["利率上行(TLT -21.2%)/美元+10.0%","避险(VIX 16->29)","加密杠杆平仓","杠杆崩塌"]},"2022-06-30":{"title":"Violent oversold bounce on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A 103% rip off washed-out levels reflected the basket's extreme high-beta character, firing on peak-inflation hopes as the tape went risk-on (SMH +21.0%, growth>value +7.0, VIX 29->20) in a goldilocks quad with oil falling -15.5%. The bounce was pure positioning — the highest-beta group ripped hardest off the low — and reversed sharply.","drivers":["oversold bounce","risk-on melt-up (SMH +21.0%, VIX 29->20)","peak-inflation hope","extreme high beta"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中的剧烈超卖反弹","body_zh":"从超卖水平暴涨103%，反映该篮子极高的贝塔属性，由通胀见顶预期点燃，行情转向风险偏好(SMH +21.0%、成长跑赢价值+7.0、VIX 29->20)，处于金发女孩象限、油价下跌-15.5%。这波反弹纯属仓位驱动——最高贝塔群体在低点暴涨最猛——随后急剧逆转。","drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +21.0%, VIX 29->20)","通胀见顶预期","极高贝塔"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Hawkish reset and crypto-winter new lows","body":"Powell's Jackson Hole hawkishness and crypto-winter contagion drove a 64% collapse to new lows into late December as yields surged (TLT -12.8%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Defensives held (-2.3%) vs cyclicals -6.7% in a broadening tape (RSP +3.9% vs SPY); the pre-AI cohort was among the most distressed in the market (SMH -19.0% vs SPY -11.4%).","drivers":["hawkish Powell / yields up (TLT -12.8%)","crypto winter","broadening (RSP +3.9%)","new lows"],"title_zh":"鹰派重置与加密寒冬再创新低","body_zh":"鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派表态与加密寒冬传染推动篮子暴跌64%，在12月底创新低，收益率飙升(TLT -12.8%)，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。防御股守住(-2.3%) vs 周期股-6.7%，处于转宽行情(RSP跑赢SPY +3.9%)；AI前时代的这批个股是市场中最困顿的群体之一(SMH -19.0% vs SPY -11.4%)。","drivers_zh":["鲍威尔鹰派/收益率上行(TLT -12.8%)","加密寒冬","广度转宽(RSP +3.9%)","再创新低"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"GPU-cloud thesis born in a risk-on melt-up","body":"From the December 2022 low, generative AI created the GPU-cloud leasing thesis, and these high-beta hosts exploded 560% as compute scarcity made leased capacity precious. The macro was a tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +60.4%, growth>value +25.8, VIX 22->14, DXY -4.5%) in a goldilocks quad, narrow at the top (RSP -9.5% vs SPY). The ChatGPT catalyst turned distressed miners into AI-infrastructure plays.","drivers":["genAI / ChatGPT","GPU-cloud thesis","risk-on melt-up (SMH +60.4%, VIX 22->14)","narrow breadth (RSP -9.5%)"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中GPU云逻辑诞生","body_zh":"从2022年12月低点起，生成式AI催生了GPU云租赁逻辑，这些高贝塔托管商暴涨560%，因算力稀缺使租赁产能变得珍贵。宏观是科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +60.4%、成长跑赢价值+25.8、VIX 22->14、DXY -4.5%)，处于金发女孩象限、顶部窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -9.5%)。ChatGPT催化剂将困顿矿企转变为AI基础设施标的。","drivers_zh":["生成式AI/ChatGPT","GPU云逻辑","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +60.4%, VIX 22->14)","窄幅广度(RSP -9.5%)"]},"2023-07-13":{"title":"Rate-driven summer pullback","body":"A 57% pullback hit as long yields surged through autumn 2023 (TLT -17.6%) and the dollar firmed +6.4% in a reflation/growth-up quad, with the AI rally pausing. VIX rose 14->22 and breadth narrowed (RSP -4.1% vs SPY); the basket's high-beta, capital-intensive profile amplified the rate-driven drawdown (SMH -10.2% vs SPY -6.0%).","drivers":["yields surge (TLT -17.6%)","stronger dollar (+6.4%)","rate-driven pullback (VIX 14->22)","high beta"],"title_zh":"利率驱动的夏季回调","body_zh":"随着长端收益率在2023年秋季飙升(TLT -17.6%)、美元在再通胀/增长向上象限走强+6.4%、AI上涨暂歇，篮子回调57%。VIX升至14->22、广度收窄(RSP跑输SPY -4.1%)；其高贝塔、重资本属性放大了利率驱动的回撤(SMH -10.2% vs SPY -6.0%)。","drivers_zh":["收益率飙升(TLT -17.6%)","美元走强(+6.4%)","利率驱动回调(VIX 14->22)","高贝塔"]},"2023-10-20":{"title":"Yield-peak GPU rip on a risk-on turn","body":"As long yields peaked in late October 2023 and reversed hard (TLT +21.9%), these GPU hosts ripped 180% into year-end on insatiable AI-compute demand, riding a risk-on turn (SMH +24.5%, VIX 22->12, DXY -4.9%) in a reflation/growth-up quad with breadth broadening (RSP +2.2% vs SPY). Falling rates plus scarcity supercharged the high-beta move.","drivers":["yield peak / reversal (TLT +21.9%)","risk-on turn (SMH +24.5%, VIX 22->12)","GPU demand","capacity buildout"],"title_zh":"风险偏好转向中收益率见顶后的GPU暴涨","body_zh":"随着长端收益率在2023年10月底见顶并急剧反转(TLT +21.9%)，这些GPU托管商在年底前暴涨180%，受益于难以满足的AI算力需求，乘的是风险偏好转向(SMH +24.5%、VIX 22->12、DXY -4.9%)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限、广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.2%)。利率回落叠加稀缺性极大强化了这波高贝塔走势。","drivers_zh":["收益率见顶/反转(TLT +21.9%)","风险偏好转向(SMH +24.5%, VIX 22->12)","GPU需求","产能扩建"]},"2023-12-27":{"title":"Overbought high-beta flush","body":"A 51% flush in January 2024 unwound an overbought, over-owned position in the highest-beta AI corner, with yields ticking up (TLT -7.1%) in a calm-VIX slowdown quad and breadth narrow (RSP -3.2% vs SPY). It was a positioning reset, not a demand change — the high-beta basket simply gave back the overshoot.","drivers":["overbought flush","rate tick-up (TLT -7.1%)","narrow breadth (RSP -3.2%)","high-beta positioning reset"],"title_zh":"超买高贝塔回吐","body_zh":"2024年1月的51%回吐平掉了AI最高贝塔领域中超买、过度持仓的头寸，收益率小幅上行(TLT -7.1%)，处于VIX平静的放缓象限、广度窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -3.2%)。这是仓位重置而非需求变化——高贝塔篮子只是回吐了超涨。","drivers_zh":["超买回吐","利率小幅上行(TLT -7.1%)","窄幅广度(RSP -3.2%)","高贝塔仓位重置"]},"2024-01-24":{"title":"CoreWeave-era buildout in a narrow goldilocks tape","body":"A 272% run powered by massive GPU-cloud capacity deals and AI-compute demand carried the basket into December 2024, with Fed cuts from September adding fuel. The tape was a tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +29.2%, growth>value +10.4, ultra-calm VIX 13->13) in a goldilocks quad, narrow at the top (RSP -6.2% vs SPY) even as the dollar firmed +2.6%. Leased GPU economics looked structurally scarce and richly priced.","drivers":["GPU-cloud deals","AI compute demand","narrow risk-on melt-up (SMH +29.2%, RSP -6.2%)","Fed cuts"],"title_zh":"窄幅金发女孩行情中CoreWeave时代的建设","body_zh":"由大规模GPU云产能交易与AI算力需求驱动的272%上涨将篮子带入2024年12月，9月起的美联储降息添了一把火。行情是科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +29.2%、成长跑赢价值+10.4、VIX超低13->13)，处于金发女孩象限、顶部窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -6.2%)，尽管美元走强+2.6%。租赁GPU经济效益看上去结构性稀缺且估值丰厚。","drivers_zh":["GPU云交易","AI算力需求","窄幅风险偏好熔涨(SMH +29.2%, RSP -6.2%)","美联储降息"]},"2024-12-06":{"title":"DeepSeek and tariff plunge in a VIX panic","body":"DeepSeek's cheap-AI scare hit the capital-intensive hosts hard on fears efficient models would slash GPU demand, then deepened in the Liberation Day tariff crash. It was a flight-to-safety panic — VIX exploded 13->52, defensives held (-6.7%) vs cyclicals -18.5%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -22.7) — and the high-beta basket led the wreck (SMH -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%), falling 57% to its April 8 bottom.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","GPU-demand fear","flight-to-safety panic (VIX 13->52, high-beta -22.7)","Liberation Day tariffs"],"title_zh":"VIX恐慌中DeepSeek与关税暴跌","body_zh":"DeepSeek廉价AI恐慌对重资本托管商打击沉重，市场担忧高效模型会大幅削减GPU需求，随后在“解放日”关税崩盘中加深。这是一次避险恐慌——VIX从13暴涨至52、防御股守住(-6.7%) vs 周期股-18.5%、高贝塔被重创(SPHB-SPLV -22.7)——高贝塔篮子领跌(SMH -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%)，下跌57%至4月8日底部。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","GPU需求担忧","避险恐慌(VIX 13->52, 高贝塔-22.7)","“解放日”对等关税"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Compute-scarcity melt-up, strongest in the complex","body":"The tariff pause and proof that AI-compute demand only accelerated drove a 570% melt-up, the strongest in the AI complex, as GPU-leasing backlogs swelled. It rode the most violent risk-on reset of the cycle (VIX collapsed 52->16, high-beta dominated SPHB-SPLV +122.0) in a reflation/growth-up quad with Tech +114.0% leading, narrow at the top (RSP -13.1% vs SPY). The run survived the late-2025 valuation reset and the Hormuz shock, with the early-June Broadcom miss its first real test.","drivers":["tariff pause","GPU-leasing backlog","violent risk-on reset (VIX 52->16, high-beta +122.0)","Broadcom test"],"title_zh":"算力稀缺熔涨，板块最强","body_zh":"关税暂停加上AI算力需求只增不减的验证，推动篮子熔涨570%，为AI板块最强，因GPU租赁订单积压膨胀。它乘的是本周期最猛烈的风险偏好重置(VIX从52崩至16、高贝塔主导SPHB-SPLV +122.0)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限、科技+114.0%领涨、顶部窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -13.1%)。这轮上涨挺过了2025年末估值重置与霍尔木兹冲击，6月初博通不及预期是其首次真正考验。","drivers_zh":["关税暂停","GPU租赁积压","猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX 52->16, 高贝塔+122.0)","博通考验"]}}},"b-mag7":{"now":"The Magnificent Seven are rolling over, lagging on relative strength as the early-June Broadcom-led semis wipeout and a regime turn eroded mega-cap leadership. The tape is reflation/growth-up but hawkish underneath — DXY +3.4%, growth lagging value (-15.2), and crucially breadth is broadening (RSP +2.9% vs SPY), the opposite of the narrow mega-cap melt-ups that carried the seven. With NVDA and the AI-capex names under pressure and rates biased higher, the cohort that led the market is now the source of its drag.","now_zh":"七巨头(Magnificent Seven)正在见顶回落，相对强度落后，因6月初博通引领的半导体暴跌与体制转向侵蚀了大盘股领导地位。行情为再通胀/增长向上但底层偏鹰——美元DXY +3.4%、成长跑输价值(-15.2)，关键是市场广度正在转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)，与曾扛起七巨头的窄幅大盘股熔涨相反。在英伟达(NVDA)及AI资本开支个股承压、利率偏向上行之际，曾领涨大盘的这一群体如今成了拖累来源。","legs":{"2021-11-19":{"title":"Mega-cap rate de-rating, quality cushions","body":"The 2022 Fed-hiking cycle de-rated even the mega-cap leaders as yields surged (TLT -10.7%) and the dollar firmed +3.1% in a stagflation-ish quad, with the Russia-Ukraine shock hitting sentiment. It was a flight-to-safety (defensives +1.2% vs cyclicals -3.4%, VIX 18->32) in a broadening tape (RSP +4.3% vs SPY); the quality of the seven cushioned the fall relative to speculative tech (SMH -23.1% vs the cohort's -25.3%).","drivers":["Fed hiking / yields up (TLT -10.7%)","flight-to-safety (VIX 18->32)","broadening (RSP +4.3%)","Russia-Ukraine"],"title_zh":"大盘股利率估值下修，质地缓冲","body_zh":"2022年美联储加息周期甚至下修了大盘龙头估值，收益率飙升(TLT -10.7%)、美元在类滞胀象限走强+3.1%，俄乌冲击打击情绪。这是避险(防御股+1.2% vs 周期股-3.4%、VIX 18->32)，处于转宽行情(RSP跑赢SPY +4.3%)；七巨头的质地相对投机性科技股缓冲了跌幅(SMH -23.1%，篮子-25.3%)。","drivers_zh":["美联储加息/收益率上行(TLT -10.7%)","避险(VIX 18->32)","广度转宽(RSP +4.3%)","俄乌冲突"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Quality-led relief on a risk-on bounce","body":"A 24% bounce off oversold levels saw the highest-quality mega-caps lead as VIX collapsed 32->19 and growth beat value (+9.5) in a reflation/growth-up quad. It was a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP -3.0% vs SPY) — exactly where the seven shine — and the relief faded as the hiking path steepened.","drivers":["oversold bounce","risk-on snapback (VIX 32->19)","narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -3.0%)","quality bid"],"title_zh":"风险偏好反弹中质地驱动的修复","body_zh":"从超卖水平反弹24%，最高质地的大盘股领涨，VIX从32崩至19、成长跑赢价值(+9.5)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。这是窄幅大盘股领导行情(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)——正是七巨头闪光之处——随着加息路径变陡，这波修复消退。","drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","风险偏好回升(VIX 32->19)","窄幅大盘股行情(RSP -3.0%)","质地买盘"]},"2022-04-04":{"title":"Real-yield repricing in a stagflation flush","body":"Surging real yields (TLT -14.7%), a faster hiking path and a stronger dollar (+4.7%) drove the seven down 33% into June in a stagflation-ish quad. The flight-to-safety was deep (defensives -11.5% vs cyclicals -17.1%, VIX 19->33); even high-quality mega-cap multiples could not escape the rate repricing (Tech -23.5% vs SPY -19.7%).","drivers":["real yields up (TLT -14.7%)","stagflation flush (VIX 19->33)","stronger dollar (+4.7%)","multiple compression"],"title_zh":"类滞胀冲洗中的实际收益率重定价","body_zh":"实际收益率飙升(TLT -14.7%)、更快加息路径与美元走强(+4.7%)推动七巨头在6月前下跌33%，处于类滞胀象限。避险很深(防御股-11.5% vs 周期股-17.1%、VIX 19->33)；即便高质地大盘股估值也无法逃脱利率重定价(科技-23.5% vs SPY -19.7%)。","drivers_zh":["实际收益率上行(TLT -14.7%)","类滞胀冲洗(VIX 19->33)","美元走强(+4.7%)","估值倍数压缩"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-rate-hope rally on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A 27% summer rally fired on hopes the worst of tightening was priced, with mega-caps leading as the tape went risk-on (SMH +20.8%, growth>value +9.2, VIX 33->20) in a goldilocks quad with oil crashing -24.0%. The move was sentiment-driven and unwound into autumn.","drivers":["peak-rate hope","risk-on melt-up (SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","disinflation (oil -24%)","mega-cap bid"],"title_zh":"风险偏好熔涨中的利率见顶预期反弹","body_zh":"27%的夏季反弹源于市场预期最糟紧缩已被消化，大盘股领涨，行情转向风险偏好(SMH +20.8%、成长跑赢价值+9.2、VIX 33->20)，处于金发女孩象限、油价崩跌-24.0%。这波由情绪驱动的走势在秋季回落。","drivers_zh":["利率见顶预期","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","去通胀(油价-24%)","大盘股买盘"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Final tightening leg, rate-driven low","body":"Hawkish Fed messaging and surging yields (TLT -12.8%) drove a 36% slide to the late-December 2022 cycle low in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. It was a broad, rate-led drawdown (defensives -2.3% vs cyclicals -6.7%, breadth broadened RSP +3.9% vs SPY); the seven bottomed (Tech -19.5% vs SPY -11.4%) just before the AI narrative reignited mega-cap leadership.","drivers":["hawkish Fed / yields up (TLT -12.8%)","slowdown quad","broadening (RSP +3.9%)","cycle low"],"title_zh":"紧缩末段、利率驱动的低点","body_zh":"鹰派的美联储表态与飙升的收益率(TLT -12.8%)推动七巨头下跌36%，至2022年12月底的周期低点，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。这是广泛、由利率驱动的回撤(防御股-2.3% vs 周期股-6.7%、广度转宽RSP跑赢SPY +3.9%)；七巨头见底(科技-19.5% vs SPY -11.4%)恰好在AI叙事重燃大盘股领导地位前。","drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派/收益率上行(TLT -12.8%)","放缓象限","广度转宽(RSP +3.9%)","周期低点"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"AI mega-cap supremacy in a narrow melt-up","body":"From the December 2022 low, the generative-AI boom concentrated gains in the seven, a 270% run as NVDA, MSFT and the cohort captured the AI capex and monetization wave. The macro was a tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +157.5%, growth>value +70.5, VIX 22->14) in a goldilocks quad, and crucially extremely narrow — equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -32.4% — the mega-cap-led tape the seven define. Fed cuts from September 2024 extended the dominance despite the yen-carry air-pocket.","drivers":["genAI boom / NVDA / MSFT","narrow mega-cap melt-up (SMH +157%, RSP -32.4% vs SPY)","AI capex","Fed cuts"],"title_zh":"窄幅熔涨中的AI大盘股霸权","body_zh":"从2022年12月低点起，生成式AI热潮将涨幅集中于七巨头，上涨270%，因英伟达、微软等捕获了AI资本开支与变现浪潮。宏观是科技引领的风险偏好熔涨(SMH +157.5%、成长跑赢价值+70.5、VIX 22->14)，处于金发女孩象限，且关键是极度窄幅——等权跑输市值权重-32.4%——正是七巨头定义的大盘股行情。2024年9月起的美联储降息延续了主导地位，尽管经历日元套息空气陷阱。","drivers_zh":["生成式AI热潮/英伟达/微软","窄幅大盘股熔涨(SMH +157%, RSP跑输SPY -32.4%)","AI资本开支","美联储降息"]},"2024-12-24":{"title":"DeepSeek and tariff drawdown in a VIX panic","body":"The DeepSeek cheap-AI scare and April's Liberation Day tariff crash drove a 29% drawdown, with NVDA and the AI-levered names leading the decline. It was a flight-to-safety panic — VIX exploded 14->52, defensives held (-3.8%) vs cyclicals -15.7%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -23.2) — in a broadening tape (RSP +3.7% vs SPY); the cohort bottomed (Tech -25.1% vs SPY -17.2%) around April 8 with the broad market.","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","Liberation Day tariffs","flight-to-safety panic (VIX 14->52, high-beta -23.2)","NVDA-led decline"],"title_zh":"VIX恐慌中DeepSeek与关税回撤","body_zh":"DeepSeek廉价AI恐慌与4月“解放日”关税崩盘推动七巨头回撤29%，英伟达及AI高敞口个股领跌。这是一次避险恐慌——VIX从14暴涨至52、防御股守住(-3.8%) vs 周期股-15.7%、高贝塔被重创(SPHB-SPLV -23.2)——处于转宽行情(RSP跑赢SPY +3.7%)；该群体在4月8日前后随大盘见底(科技-25.1% vs SPY -17.2%)。","drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","“解放日”对等关税","避险恐慌(VIX 14->52, 高贝塔-23.2)","英伟达领跌"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"AI-capex leadership returns on a risk-on reset","body":"The tariff pause and a resurgent AI-capex melt-up drove a 73% recovery as mega-cap earnings power reasserted itself, riding a violent risk-on reset (VIX collapsed 52->17, high-beta dominated SPHB-SPLV +68.1, DXY -3.6%) in a goldilocks quad with Tech +69.7% leading. It was a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -15.1% vs SPY) — the seven reclaimed leadership before topping in late October 2025.","drivers":["tariff pause","AI-capex melt-up","risk-on reset (VIX 52->17, high-beta +68.1)","narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -15.1%)"],"title_zh":"风险偏好重置中AI资本开支领导地位回归","body_zh":"关税暂停与重燃的AI资本开支熔涨推动七巨头复苏73%，大盘股盈利能力重新确立，乘的是猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX从52崩至17、高贝塔主导SPHB-SPLV +68.1、DXY -3.6%)，处于金发女孩象限、科技+69.7%领涨。这是窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -15.1%)——七巨头夺回领导地位，随后在2025年10月底见顶。","drivers_zh":["关税暂停","AI资本开支熔涨","风险偏好重置(VIX 52->17, 高贝塔+68.1)","窄幅大盘股行情(RSP -15.1%)"]},"2025-10-29":{"title":"Valuation reset and oil shock, broadening tape","body":"A late-2025 hawkish valuation reset, then the 2026 Hormuz oil shock (oil +70.1%) lifting CPI to ~4.2% and a Fed hiking bias drove an 18% pullback in a stagflation-ish quad. Crucially the tape broadened hard against the seven — equal-weight beat cap-weight by +8.2% as Energy +42.9% led and growth lagged value (-19.5) — though the cohort's quality limited the damage (SMH only -1.3% vs Tech -15.9%).","drivers":["valuation reset","Hormuz oil shock (oil +70.1%)","Fed hiking bias / broadening (RSP +8.2%)","growth-lags-value (-19.5)"],"title_zh":"估值重置与石油冲击，行情转宽","body_zh":"2025年末的鹰派估值重置，随后2026年霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+70.1%)将CPI推升至约4.2%、美联储转向加息倾向，推动七巨头在类滞胀象限回撤18%。关键是行情对七巨头大幅转宽——等权跑赢市值权重+8.2%，能源+42.9%领涨、成长跑输价值(-19.5)——尽管其质地限制了损失(SMH仅-1.3% vs 科技-15.9%)。","drivers_zh":["估值重置","霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+70.1%)","美联储加息倾向/广度转宽(RSP +8.2%)","成长跑输价值(-19.5)"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Ceasefire bounce, then roll-over as breadth broadens","body":"The mid-June Hormuz ceasefire fueled a 29% bounce, riding a tech-led risk-on snapback (SMH +65.5%, growth>value +10.3, VIX 31->16) in a reflation/growth-up quad, narrow at the top (RSP -8.8% vs SPY). But the rally stalled as the early-June Broadcom-led semis wipeout and broadening breadth (RSP now +2.9% vs SPY) eroded mega-cap leadership — the cohort is rolling over with NVDA and AI-capex names leading the market lower.","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire","risk-on snapback (SMH +65.5%, VIX 31->16)","Broadcom semis wipeout","broadening breadth"],"title_zh":"停火反弹，随后随广度转宽见顶回落","body_zh":"6月中旬霍尔木兹海峡停火推动29%反弹，乘的是科技引领的风险偏好回升(SMH +65.5%、成长跑赢价值+10.3、VIX 31->16)，处于再通胀/增长向上象限、顶部窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -8.8%)。但随着6月初博通引领的半导体暴跌与市场广度转宽(RSP现跑赢SPY +2.9%)侵蚀大盘股领导地位，反弹停滞——该群体正在见顶回落，英伟达与AI资本开支个股领跌大盘。","drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火","风险偏好回升(SMH +65.5%, VIX 31->16)","博通半导体暴跌","广度转宽"]}}},"b-ai_semiconductors":{"now":"Rolling over from an 87th-percentile high. After a +119% spring-2026 melt-up the AI-chip leaders (Nvidia/AMD/Broadcom/TSMC) are fading as breadth broadens away from mega-cap (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and a post-Hormuz hawkish Fed with a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) caps long-duration multiples. SMH is still up 67.9% but this high-beta basket (SPHB-SPLV +20.7) had amplified the risk-on tape on the way up and is now first to give back leadership.","now_zh":"从87百分位高位回落。在2026年春季+119%飙升之后,AI芯片龙头(英伟达/AMD/博通/台积电)动能减弱,市场广度从大盘股扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%),霍尔木兹冲击后偏鹰的美联储叠加走强的美元(DXY +3.4%)压制长久期估值。SMH仍上涨67.9%,但这只高贝塔篮子(SPHB-SPLV +20.7)上行时放大了风险偏好行情,如今率先交出领导力。","legs":{"2021-12-27":{"title":"Fed-hiking bear crushes high-beta chips","body":"AI-chip names fell 35% as the Fed pivoted to aggressive hikes — yields surged (TLT -21.4%) and the dollar ripped +9.4%, a textbook rate shock for long-duration tech. The regime was a risk-off flight-to-safety (VIX 18->27, high-beta lagged low-vol by -19.5%) into a stagflation-ish quad, and this high-beta basket amplified it: SMH -38.1% versus SPY -19.5%. Real-yield compression plus digestion of the pandemic semis over-order hit the richest GPU/accelerator multiples hardest.","drivers":["risk-off rate shock","Fed hiking","multiple compression","semis inventory"],"title_zh":"美联储加息熊市重创高贝塔芯片","body_zh":"AI芯片股下跌35%,因美联储转向激进加息——收益率飙升(TLT -21.4%)、美元大涨+9.4%,是典型的长久期科技股利率冲击。当时处于避险的资金奔向安全资产(VIX 18->27,高贝塔跑输低波-19.5%)的类滞胀象限,这只高贝塔篮子放大了行情:SMH -38.1% 对 SPY -19.5%。实际收益率压缩叠加疫情期间芯片超额订单消化,对估值最高的GPU/加速器名字打击最重。","drivers_zh":["避险利率冲击","美联储加息","估值压缩","半导体库存"]},"2022-07-01":{"title":"Semis-led bear bounce on peak-inflation hope","body":"A sharp +38% bear-market rally as peak-inflation hopes eased VIX 27->20 (bonds roughly flat, TLT -0.6%) — a tech/semis-led risk-on burst (semis +23.4% vs SPY +12.2%, growth>value +6.7) in a goldilocks-flavored quad. As a high-beta basket it led the squeeze higher, but the move was positioning, not a fundamental turn, with semis still facing demand cuts.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","peak-inflation hope","short squeeze","high-beta lead"],"title_zh":"半导体领涨的熊市反弹,押注通胀见顶","body_zh":"通胀见顶预期令VIX回落27->20(债券基本持平,TLT -0.6%),带来+38%急剧熊市反弹——这是一轮科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好爆发(半导体+23.4% 对 SPY +12.2%,成长跑赢价值+6.7)的类金发姑娘象限。作为高贝塔篮子,它领涨这波挤压,但此乃仓位驱动而非基本面转向,芯片需求仍面临下修。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","通胀见顶预期","空头回补","高贝塔领涨"]},"2022-08-18":{"title":"Jackson Hole hawkish leg down","body":"Chips fell another 32% into the October low as Powell's Jackson Hole speech killed the pivot trade — yields surged again (TLT -13.8%) and the dollar pushed +5.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 20->32). The macro de-rating compounded a theme-specific blow: the first US export-control rules on advanced Nvidia/AMD data-center GPUs to China amplified the high-beta drawdown (SMH -28.4% vs SPY -16.1%).","drivers":["rate-driven risk-off","Jackson Hole","export controls","dollar up"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派下跌","body_zh":"鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的讲话击碎转向交易,芯片再跌32%至10月低点——收益率再度飙升(TLT -13.8%)、美元推升+5.4%,处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限(VIX 20->32)。宏观估值下杀叠加主题利空:美国首次对华先进英伟达/AMD数据中心GPU出口管制,放大了高贝塔回撤(SMH -28.4% 对 SPY -16.1%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动避险","杰克逊霍尔","出口管制","美元走强"]},"2022-10-14":{"title":"The genAI supercycle melt-up","body":"A monster +381% run off the October-2022 low, ignited by ChatGPT and Nvidia's blowout 2023 data-center guidance and supercharged by a goldilocks risk-on regime: VIX collapsed 32->13, growth crushed value by +55.3, the dollar fell -7.3% and breadth narrowed hard (RSP lagged SPY -28.4%) — a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket led from the front (SMH +230.6% vs SPY +61.1%). AI accelerator demand became the dominant market narrative through the 2024 Fed-cut tape.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","ChatGPT/genAI","Nvidia datacenter","AI capex"],"title_zh":"生成式AI超级周期飙升","body_zh":"从2022年10月低点起涨+381%,由ChatGPT和英伟达2023年爆表的数据中心指引点燃,并被金发姑娘式风险偏好行情助燃:VIX崩落32->13,成长大幅跑赢价值+55.3,美元下跌-7.3%,市场广度急剧收窄(RSP跑输SPY -28.4%)——这只高贝塔篮子在大盘股主导的行情中一马当先(SMH +230.6% 对 SPY +61.1%)。AI加速器需求成为市场主导叙事,贯穿2024年美联储降息行情。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","ChatGPT/生成式AI","英伟达数据中心","AI资本开支"]},"2024-07-10":{"title":"Yen-carry unwind shakeout","body":"A swift -27% drop as the August yen-carry unwind forced deleveraging across crowded AI longs — VIX spiked 13->28 in a flight-to-safety where defensives (+2.2%) beat cyclicals (-5.5%) and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +6.6%). The slowdown-scare risk-off hit this leveraged high-beta basket disproportionately (SMH -24.8% vs SPY -7.6%) before chips quickly stabilized.","drivers":["risk-off deleveraging","yen-carry unwind","rotation","high-beta amplifies"],"title_zh":"日元套息平仓震荡","body_zh":"8月日元套息平仓迫使拥挤的AI多头去杠杆,快速下跌27%——VIX飙升13->28,避险行情中防御板块(+2.2%)跑赢周期股(-5.5%),市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%)。放缓恐慌的避险对这只带杠杆的高贝塔篮子打击格外严重(SMH -24.8% 对 SPY -7.6%),芯片随后迅速企稳。","drivers_zh":["避险去杠杆","日元套息平仓","轮动","高贝塔放大"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Cut-cycle relief rally, mega-cap-led","body":"A +66% recovery into January 2025 as the Fed's September cut and election-driven risk appetite revived AI-capex enthusiasm — a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (VIX 28->15, growth>value +13.9) even as yields rose (TLT -7.2%) and the dollar firmed +4.8%. Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -5.7%), and Blackwell anticipation plus hyperscaler orders carried this high-beta basket (SMH +26.9%) to new highs.","drivers":["risk-on melt-up","Fed cut Sep","Blackwell","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"降息周期反弹,大盘股主导","body_zh":"美联储9月降息和大选后风险偏好重燃AI资本开支热情,回升+66%至2025年1月——这是一轮科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升(VIX 28->15,成长跑赢价值+13.9),尽管收益率上行(TLT -7.2%)、美元走强+4.8%。市场广度保持狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -5.7%),对Blackwell的预期和云厂订单推动这只高贝塔篮子(SMH +26.9%)创新高。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好飙升","美联储9月降息","Blackwell","窄幅广度"]},"2025-01-22":{"title":"DeepSeek scare into the tariff crash","body":"Chips fell 42% as the late-January DeepSeek shock questioned whether AI could be trained far cheaper, then April's reciprocal-tariff crash deepened the rout — a violent risk-off flush with VIX exploding 15->45 and high-beta cratering vs low-vol by -27.1%. Defensives (-2.2%) beat cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad, and this leveraged basket amplified the move (SMH -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%); notably yields fell (TLT +7.2%) and the dollar weakened, so it was a growth-scare, not a rate, selloff.","drivers":["risk-off flush","DeepSeek","reciprocal tariffs","capex-efficiency fear"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌叠加关税崩盘","body_zh":"1月底DeepSeek冲击引发对AI训练可大幅降本的质疑,芯片下跌42%,随后4月对等关税崩盘加深跌势——这是一场剧烈的避险抛售,VIX暴涨15->45,高贝塔相对低波重挫-27.1%。在放缓恐慌象限中防御板块(-2.2%)跑赢周期股(-16.3%),这只带杠杆篮子放大了跌幅(SMH -32.3% 对 SPY -16.4%);值得注意的是收益率下行(TLT +7.2%)、美元走弱,所以这是成长恐慌而非利率主导的抛售。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","DeepSeek","对等关税","资本效率担忧"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Post-tariff AI melt-up, V-shaped","body":"A +153% surge off the April low as tariff fears faded and a goldilocks risk-on regime roared back — VIX collapsed 45->17, high-beta beat low-vol by a massive +67.5, growth>value +28.3, and a weaker dollar (-3.1%) added fuel. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -15.2%), a mega-cap melt-up this high-beta basket led (SMH +100.8% vs SPY +35.8%); Nvidia, Broadcom's custom-ASIC wins and TSMC pricing power drove the leaders to fresh records.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","AI capex re-accel","custom ASIC","tariff relief"],"title_zh":"关税后AI飙升,V型反转","body_zh":"关税担忧消退、金发姑娘式风险偏好行情卷土重来,从4月低点飙升+153%——VIX崩落45->17,高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+67.5,成长跑赢价值+28.3,走弱的美元(-3.1%)添柴。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -15.2%),这是一轮由这只高贝塔篮子领涨的大盘股飙升(SMH +100.8% 对 SPY +35.8%);英伟达、博通的定制ASIC订单和台积电定价权推动龙头创新高。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","AI资本开支再加速","定制ASIC","关税缓解"]},"2025-10-31":{"title":"Late-2025 hawkish reset, leadership broadens out","body":"A -27% pullback as a hawkish Fed reset and circular AI-financing worries pressured the richest multiples. Tellingly, this was a leadership rotation rather than a market crash: SPY only fell -6.8% and breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY +7.7%) in a stagflation-ish quad, so capital left over-owned high-beta AI chips (SMH flat at +0.2%) for the rest of the tape. Vendor-financing-loop and concentration fears took the froth out of the leaders.","drivers":["leadership rotation","hawkish reset","AI financing fears","valuation"],"title_zh":"2025年末鹰派重置,领导力扩散","body_zh":"鹰派的美联储重置和对AI循环融资的担忧压制最高估值,回调27%。值得注意的是,这是领导力轮动而非市场崩盘:SPY仅下跌-6.8%,市场广度急剧扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +7.7%),处于类滞胀象限,资金从被过度持有的高贝塔AI芯片(SMH持平+0.2%)流向其余板块。对供应商融资闭环和集中度风险的担忧挤出了龙头泡沫。","drivers_zh":["领导力轮动","鹰派重置","AI融资担忧","估值"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Hormuz-shock rebound, then top","body":"A +119% rebound from the spring low survived the Iran/Hormuz oil shock and CPI spike, riding a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (VIX 31->16, growth>value +10.9) into the mid-June ceasefire. The advance stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -8.6%), a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket amplified (SMH +74.4% vs SPY +19.9%). By early June Broadcom's results flagged narrowing breadth, leaving the group rolling over from extreme highs.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","Hormuz ceasefire","Broadcom breadth","narrowing leadership"],"title_zh":"霍尔木兹冲击后反弹再见顶","body_zh":"从春季低点反弹+119%,熬过伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击和CPI跳升,搭乘科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升(VIX 31->16,成长跑赢价值+10.9),在6月中旬停火前后见顶。这波上涨广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -8.6%),是被这只高贝塔篮子放大的大盘股行情(SMH +74.4% 对 SPY +19.9%)。6月初博通业绩暴露市场广度收窄,该板块从极端高位开始回落。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","霍尔木兹停火","博通广度","领导力收窄"]}}},"b-memory_storage":{"now":"Topping at the 95th percentile and the No.1 relative-strength basket. A 2025-26 DRAM/HBM/NAND undersupply super-cycle drove an extraordinary run in Micron/SK Hynix, but with SMH +67.9%, breadth now broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) in a reflation/growth-up quad, the parabola looks exhausted. As the highest-beta semis sub-theme (it amplified the SPHB-SPLV +20.7 risk-on tape on the way up) it is the most exposed if the regime cools.","now_zh":"在95百分位见顶,是相对强度第一的篮子。2025-26年DRAM/HBM/NAND供不应求的超级周期推动美光/SK海力士飙升,但SMH +67.9%、市场广度开始扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、美元走强(DXY +3.4%)处于再通胀/增长向上象限,抛物线显疲态。作为贝塔最高的半导体子主题(上行时放大了SPHB-SPLV +20.7的风险偏好行情),若行情降温它最为脆弱。","legs":{"2022-01-04":{"title":"Memory glut meets the rate-shock bear","body":"Memory fell 48% through 2022 as a brutal DRAM/NAND oversupply collided with a rate-shock bear: yields surged (TLT -29.1%, one of the worst bond years on record) and the dollar ripped +8.5% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with risk-off rotation into defensives (+0.4% vs cyclicals -8.6%). The high-beta drawdown (SMH -36.4% vs SPY -19.8%) compounded falling bit prices and bloated PC/handset inventories in a classic memory down-cycle.","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","DRAM oversupply","bit-price collapse","Fed hiking"],"title_zh":"内存供过于求遭遇利率冲击熊市","body_zh":"2022年内存下跌48%,严重的DRAM/NAND供过于求叠加利率冲击熊市:收益率飙升(TLT -29.1%,创纪录最差债券年之一),美元大涨+8.5%,处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限,资金避险转向防御板块(+0.4% 对 周期股-8.6%)。高贝塔回撤(SMH -36.4% 对 SPY -19.8%)叠加位价下跌、PC/手机库存高企,构成典型内存下行周期。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","DRAM供过于求","位价崩跌","美联储加息"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"Cycle trough to HBM dawn, on a narrow melt-up","body":"A +163% rally as memory makers slashed capex and capacity, tightening the cycle into 2024 — and the backdrop was a textbook tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up: VIX fell 22->12, growth crushed value by +56.6, but breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -27.1%), a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket led (SMH +182.2% vs SPY +48.3%). The genAI boom seeded the HBM story, making high-bandwidth memory the key bottleneck for AI accelerators.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","capex cuts","supply discipline","HBM demand"],"title_zh":"周期触底到HBM黎明,搭乘窄幅飙升","body_zh":"内存厂商大砍资本开支和产能,周期收紧至2024年,反弹+163%——背景是教科书式的科技/半导体领涨风险偏好飙升:VIX回落22->12,成长大幅跑赢价值+56.6,但市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -27.1%),是被这只高贝塔篮子领涨的大盘股行情(SMH +182.2% 对 SPY +48.3%)。生成式AI热潮孕育HBM故事,使高带宽内存成为AI加速器的关键瓶颈。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","削减资本开支","供给纪律","HBM需求"]},"2024-06-18":{"title":"Carry-unwind correction","body":"A -25% pullback as the August yen-carry unwind and profit-taking hit the year's biggest winners — a flight-to-safety where VIX spiked 12->28 and defensives (+2.9%) beat cyclicals (-3.8%) in a slowdown-scare quad. This high-beta basket amplified the deleveraging (SMH -23.6% vs SPY -5.1%), but the dip was positioning-driven with the underlying HBM demand thesis intact.","drivers":["risk-off deleveraging","yen-carry unwind","profit-taking","high-beta amplifies"],"title_zh":"套息平仓回调","body_zh":"8月日元套息平仓和获利了结冲击全年最大赢家,回调25%——避险行情中VIX飙升12->28,防御板块(+2.9%)跑赢周期股(-3.8%),处于放缓恐慌象限。这只高贝塔篮子放大了去杠杆(SMH -23.6% 对 SPY -5.1%),但此跌由仓位驱动,底层HBM需求逻辑未变。","drivers_zh":["避险去杠杆","日元套息平仓","获利了结","高贝塔放大"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"HBM-led recovery on a risk-on tape","body":"A +25% recovery into February 2025 as Fed cuts and AI-server demand re-firmed HBM pricing — a tech/semis-led risk-on rebound (VIX 28->16, growth>value +11.9) even as the dollar firmed +3.0% and yields rose (TLT -5.7%). Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -6.0%) as SK Hynix and Micron qualified next-gen HBM for the leading accelerators, supporting the bid.","drivers":["risk-on rebound","Fed cut","HBM pricing","narrow breadth"],"title_zh":"HBM主导复苏,搭乘风险偏好行情","body_zh":"美联储降息和AI服务器需求重新巩固HBM价格,回升+25%至2025年2月——这是科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好反弹(VIX 28->16,成长跑赢价值+11.9),尽管美元走强+3.0%、收益率上行(TLT -5.7%)。市场广度保持狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -6.0%),SK海力士和美光为领先加速器认证次世代HBM,支撑买盘。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","美联储降息","HBM定价","窄幅广度"]},"2025-02-20":{"title":"DeepSeek & tariff risk-off drawdown","body":"Memory fell 37% as the DeepSeek scare and April's reciprocal-tariff crash hit AI hardware in a violent risk-off flush — VIX exploded 16->45, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -23.6%, and defensives (-5.7%) beat cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad. This leveraged basket amplified the move (SMH -29.9% vs SPY -17.0%); a weaker dollar and falling yields confirm it was a growth-scare, not a rate, selloff that briefly clouded the memory super-cycle thesis.","drivers":["risk-off flush","DeepSeek","reciprocal tariffs","demand fear"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险回撤","body_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌和4月对等关税崩盘在剧烈避险抛售中冲击AI硬件,内存下跌37%——VIX暴涨16->45,高贝塔相对低波重挫-23.6%,放缓恐慌象限中防御板块(-5.7%)跑赢周期股(-16.3%)。这只带杠杆篮子放大了跌幅(SMH -29.9% 对 SPY -17.0%);美元走弱、收益率下行印证这是成长恐慌而非利率主导的抛售,一度遮蔽内存超级周期逻辑。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","DeepSeek","对等关税","需求担忧"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Memory super-cycle melt-up to the top","body":"An extraordinary +1,754% run as a genuine 2025-26 undersupply super-cycle took hold across DRAM, HBM and NAND, riding a roaring risk-on regime: VIX collapsed 45->17 and high-beta beat low-vol by an enormous +124.5 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -13.4%), a mega-cap-led melt-up this highest-beta semis basket led from the front (SMH +271.1% vs SPY +49.0%). Spot and contract prices spiked as AI memory content per server soared while makers stayed capacity-disciplined into the mid-2026 top.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","undersupply super-cycle","HBM/DRAM pricing","supply discipline"],"title_zh":"内存超级周期飙升至顶","body_zh":"2025-26年真实的供不应求超级周期席卷DRAM、HBM和NAND,惊人上涨+1,754%,搭乘狂热的风险偏好行情:VIX崩落45->17,高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+124.5,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -13.4%),这只贝塔最高的半导体篮子在大盘股飙升中一马当先(SMH +271.1% 对 SPY +49.0%)。AI服务器单机内存用量激增、厂商保持产能纪律,现货与合约价格飙升,直至2026年中见顶。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","供不应求超级周期","HBM/DRAM定价","供给纪律"]}}},"b-semicap_equipment":{"now":"Topping at the 97th percentile. Wafer-fab equipment (ASML/AMAT/LRCX/KLAC) rode the AI-capex pick-and-shovel trade to extreme highs, but with SMH +67.9%, breadth broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY, a headwind for these export-heavy multinationals) in a reflation/growth-up quad, the China export-control overhang and a stretched high-beta leg (SPHB-SPLV +20.7) now argue for digestion.","now_zh":"在97百分位见顶。晶圆厂设备(ASML/AMAT/LRCX/KLAC)搭乘AI资本开支的卖铲逻辑冲至极端高位,但SMH +67.9%、市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、美元走强(DXY +3.4%,对这些以出口为主的跨国公司构成逆风)处于再通胀/增长向上象限,中国出口管制阴影和过度拉伸的高贝塔涨势(SPHB-SPLV +20.7)如今指向消化。","legs":{"2022-01-03":{"title":"WFE down-cycle meets the rate-shock bear","body":"Equipment fell 41% as a memory/logic capex pause met a rate-shock bear: yields surged (TLT -19.0%) and the dollar ripped +9.2% in a stagflation-ish quad, with risk-off rotation into defensives (-2.4% vs cyclicals -13.5%, VIX 17->27). The high-beta drawdown (SMH -37.9% vs SPY -19.6%) was amplified by recession fears that compressed the cyclical WFE names as fab spend slowed.","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","Fed hiking","capex pause","WFE de-rating"],"title_zh":"晶圆厂设备下行周期遭遇利率冲击熊市","body_zh":"内存/逻辑资本开支暂停叠加利率冲击熊市,设备下跌41%:收益率飙升(TLT -19.0%),美元大涨+9.2%,处于类滞胀象限,资金避险转向防御板块(-2.4% 对 周期股-13.5%,VIX 17->27)。高贝塔回撤(SMH -37.9% 对 SPY -19.6%)被衰退担忧放大,晶圆厂支出放缓压缩了周期性的WFE名字。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","美联储加息","资本开支暂停","WFE估值下杀"]},"2022-07-01":{"title":"Bear-rally bounce on peak-inflation hope","body":"A +32% bounce on peak-inflation hopes and a brief yield reprieve (TLT +3.2%) as VIX eased 27->21 in a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +8.6% vs defensives +2.4%). This high-beta basket led the relief (SMH +25.2% vs SPY +8.6%), but the rally was short-lived as the broader semis capex outlook stayed cautious.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","peak-inflation hope","high-beta lead"],"title_zh":"熊市反弹,押注通胀见顶","body_zh":"受通胀见顶预期和收益率短暂回落(TLT +3.2%)提振,反弹+32%,VIX回落27->21,处于类金发姑娘象限(周期股+8.6% 对 防御板块+2.4%)。这只高贝塔篮子领涨这波缓解(SMH +25.2% 对 SPY +8.6%),但由于半导体资本开支前景仍谨慎,反弹未能持续。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","通胀见顶预期","高贝塔领涨"]},"2022-08-04":{"title":"October export-control shock, rate-driven","body":"WFE fell 31% into October as Jackson Hole hawkishness re-ignited the rate regime — yields surged again (TLT -17.0%) and the dollar pushed +7.2% (VIX 21->32). On top of the macro de-rating, sweeping US export controls on advanced chipmaking tools to China landed: the October 2022 rules directly threatened AMAT/LRCX/KLAC China revenue, deepening the high-beta drawdown (SMH -29.4% vs SPY -13.3%).","drivers":["rate-driven risk-off","export controls","Jackson Hole","China revenue"],"title_zh":"10月出口管制冲击,利率驱动","body_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重新点燃利率行情,WFE跌至10月,下挫31%——收益率再度飙升(TLT -17.0%),美元推升+7.2%(VIX 21->32)。在宏观估值下杀之上,美国对华先进芯片制造工具的全面出口管制落地:2022年10月的规则直接威胁AMAT/LRCX/KLAC的中国收入,加深高贝塔回撤(SMH -29.4% 对 SPY -13.3%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动避险","出口管制","杰克逊霍尔","中国收入"]},"2022-10-14":{"title":"AI-capex pick-and-shovel melt-up","body":"A +170% run as the genAI buildout drove leading-edge and advanced-packaging tool orders, supercharged by a goldilocks risk-on regime: VIX collapsed 32->13, growth crushed value +47.6 and the dollar fell -8.0% (a tailwind for these multinationals). Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -24.1%), a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket led (SMH +221.7% vs SPY +62.1%). ASML's EUV backlog and TSMC's capacity expansion made WFE a core way to play the AI-capex wave through 2024.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","AI capex","EUV/advanced packaging","TSMC capacity"],"title_zh":"AI资本开支卖铲飙升","body_zh":"生成式AI建设潮推动先进制程和先进封装设备订单,上涨+170%,并被金发姑娘式风险偏好行情助燃:VIX崩落32->13,成长大幅跑赢价值+47.6,美元下跌-8.0%(对这些跨国公司构成顺风)。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -24.1%),是被这只高贝塔篮子领涨的大盘股行情(SMH +221.7% 对 SPY +62.1%)。ASML的EUV订单积压和台积电产能扩张,使WFE成为2024年间布局AI资本开支浪潮的核心方式。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","AI资本开支","EUV/先进封装","台积电产能"]},"2024-07-16":{"title":"Tightened-curbs risk-off drawdown","body":"A deep -53% slide as the yen-carry unwind, DeepSeek scare and tightened China-tool export rules compounded across two flushes — VIX exploded 13->52 in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where defensives (-1.2%) beat cyclicals (-11.8%). This high-beta basket was hit hardest (SMH -34.0% vs SPY -11.3%) as threats of broader equipment restrictions and a softer mainstream-node outlook layered onto the risk-off into the April-2025 low.","drivers":["risk-off flush","export-rule tightening","DeepSeek","carry unwind"],"title_zh":"管制收紧避险回撤","body_zh":"日元套息平仓、DeepSeek恐慌和对华设备出口规则收紧在两轮抛售中叠加,深跌53%——VIX暴涨13->52,处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限,防御板块(-1.2%)跑赢周期股(-11.8%)。这只高贝塔篮子受创最重(SMH -34.0% 对 SPY -11.3%),更广泛设备限制的威胁和主流制程前景转弱叠加于避险之上,直至2025年4月低点。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","出口规则收紧","DeepSeek","套息平仓"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"AI-capex super-rally to the top","body":"A +424% surge off the April low as record fab investment and HBM/leading-edge capacity additions drove tool demand, riding a roaring risk-on regime: VIX collapsed 52->17 and high-beta beat low-vol by a huge +124.5 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -12.3%), a mega-cap-led melt-up this high-beta basket amplified (SMH +272.9% vs SPY +51.7%). ASML, AMAT, LRCX and KLAC printed all-time highs into mid-2026, with the memory super-cycle adding a second leg of equipment orders before the top.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","record fab capex","HBM capacity","memory cycle"],"title_zh":"AI资本开支超级反弹至顶","body_zh":"创纪录的晶圆厂投资和HBM/先进制程产能扩张推动设备需求,从4月低点飙升+424%,搭乘狂热的风险偏好行情:VIX崩落52->17,高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+124.5,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -12.3%),这是被这只高贝塔篮子放大的大盘股飙升(SMH +272.9% 对 SPY +51.7%)。ASML、AMAT、LRCX和KLAC在2026年中前创历史新高,内存超级周期为设备订单增添第二条腿,随后见顶。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","创纪录晶圆厂资本开支","HBM产能","内存周期"]}}},"b-non_ai_tech":{"now":"Topping at the 89th percentile. Legacy and diversified tech hardware, networking and non-AI analog/MCU semis got swept up in the broad 2025-26 tech melt-up (SMH +67.9%), but with breadth now broadening away from mega-cap (RSP beat SPY +2.9%), a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY, a headwind for these multinational hardware names) and a still-stretched high-beta tape (SPHB-SPLV +20.7), the move looks extended versus its non-AI fundamentals.","now_zh":"在89百分位见顶。传统及多元化科技硬件、网络设备和非AI模拟/MCU芯片被2025-26年广泛的科技飙升裹挟(SMH +67.9%),但市场广度开始从大盘股扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、美元走强(DXY +3.4%,对这些跨国硬件名字构成逆风),高贝塔行情仍过度拉伸(SPHB-SPLV +20.7),相对其非AI基本面,涨势显得过度拉伸。","legs":{"2022-01-04":{"title":"Rate-shock hardware reset","body":"Non-AI tech fell 25% as a rate-shock bear hit hardware multiples and demand: yields surged (TLT -18.0%) and the dollar ripped +10.6% in a stagflation-ish quad, with risk-off rotation into defensives (-3.7% vs cyclicals -15.8%, VIX 17->28). Cooling PC, handset and analog/MCU end-markets met a sharp valuation reset, and the basket's high beta amplified the drawdown (SMH -37.2% vs SPY -19.4%).","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","Fed hiking","hardware demand","multiple reset"],"title_zh":"利率冲击硬件重置","body_zh":"利率冲击熊市冲击硬件估值和需求,非AI科技下跌25%:收益率飙升(TLT -18.0%)、美元大涨+10.6%,处于类滞胀象限,资金避险转向防御板块(-3.7% 对 周期股-15.8%,VIX 17->28)。降温的PC、手机和模拟/MCU终端市场遭遇急剧估值重置,篮子的高贝塔放大了回撤(SMH -37.2% 对 SPY -19.4%)。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","美联储加息","硬件需求","估值重置"]},"2022-07-05":{"title":"Summer semis-led bear bounce","body":"A +22% rebound on a brief peak-inflation narrative — a tech/semis-led risk-on burst (semis +22.7%, growth>value +4.6, VIX 28->20) in a reflation/growth-up quad. The bounce faded as recession and inventory worries persisted across legacy hardware, with the move tracking the broader high-beta squeeze rather than any non-AI fundamental turn.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","peak-inflation hope","semis-led"],"title_zh":"夏季半导体领涨熊市反弹","body_zh":"受通胀见顶叙事短暂提振,反弹+22%——这是科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好爆发(半导体+22.7%,成长跑赢价值+4.6,VIX 28->20)的再通胀/增长向上象限。由于传统硬件的衰退和库存担忧持续,反弹逐渐消退,此波跟随更广泛的高贝塔挤压而非任何非AI基本面转向。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","通胀见顶预期","半导体领涨"]},"2022-08-18":{"title":"Hawkish, rate-driven leg into the low","body":"A 20% drop into October as Jackson Hole reset rate expectations higher — yields surged (TLT -12.3%) and the dollar pushed +5.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 20->34). Soft consumer-electronics demand and inventory corrections compounded the rate-driven de-rating (SMH -27.4% vs SPY -16.3%).","drivers":["rate-driven risk-off","Jackson Hole","inventory correction","yields up"],"title_zh":"鹰派利率驱动下探至低点","body_zh":"杰克逊霍尔将利率预期上调,跌至10月,下挫20%——收益率飙升(TLT -12.3%)、美元推升+5.4%,处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限(VIX 20->34)。疲软的消费电子需求和库存调整叠加于利率驱动的估值下杀之上(SMH -27.4% 对 SPY -16.3%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动避险","杰克逊霍尔","库存调整","收益率上升"]},"2022-10-12":{"title":"Steady recovery on a narrow tech melt-up","body":"A +83% recovery as the Fed-cut path and stabilizing hardware demand lifted the group, carried by a goldilocks risk-on melt-up: VIX collapsed 34->13, growth crushed value +45.2, the dollar fell -8.0% and breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -24.4%), a mega-cap-led tape (SMH +217.4%). The rally was milder than AI-levered peers, reflecting maturer end-markets and the 2024 inventory normalization.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","Fed cuts","demand stabilization","inventory normalization"],"title_zh":"搭乘窄幅科技飙升稳步复苏","body_zh":"美联储降息路径和企稳的硬件需求提振该板块,回升+83%,被金发姑娘式风险偏好飙升带动:VIX崩落34->13,成长大幅跑赢价值+45.2,美元下跌-8.0%,市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -24.4%),是大盘股主导的行情(SMH +217.4%)。涨幅较AI杠杆较高的同业温和,反映更成熟的终端市场和2024年的库存正常化。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","美联储降息","需求企稳","库存正常化"]},"2024-07-16":{"title":"Carry-unwind air pocket","body":"A -18% dip during the August yen-carry unwind — a flight-to-safety where VIX spiked 13->28, defensives (+0.9%) beat cyclicals (-8.1%) and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +3.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad. Lower-beta non-AI tech held up better than the crowded AI trade, though it still amplified the broad risk-off (SMH -22.7% vs SPY -8.2%).","drivers":["risk-off deleveraging","yen-carry unwind","lower-beta cushion"],"title_zh":"套息平仓气穴","body_zh":"8月日元套息平仓期间下跌18%——避险行情中VIX飙升13->28,防御板块(+0.9%)跑赢周期股(-8.1%),市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +3.3%),处于放缓恐慌象限。低贝塔的非AI科技比拥挤的AI交易更抗跌,但仍放大了广泛避险(SMH -22.7% 对 SPY -8.2%)。","drivers_zh":["避险去杠杆","日元套息平仓","低贝塔缓冲"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Modest cut-driven lift, mega-cap-led","body":"A +19% rise into February 2025 on the Fed's September cut and a firmer hardware cycle — a tech/semis-led risk-on tape (VIX 28->16, growth>value +11.9) though the dollar firmed +3.0% and yields rose (TLT -5.7%). Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -6.0%) and gains were restrained as the AI narrative siphoned leadership away from non-AI tech.","drivers":["risk-on tape","Fed cut Sep","narrow breadth","hardware cycle"],"title_zh":"降息温和提振,大盘股主导","body_zh":"美联储9月降息和更稳固的硬件周期推动,回升+19%至2025年2月——这是科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好行情(VIX 28->16,成长跑赢价值+11.9),尽管美元走强+3.0%、收益率上行(TLT -5.7%)。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -6.0%),由于AI叙事将领导力从非AI科技吸走,涨幅受限。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好行情","美联储9月降息","窄幅广度","硬件周期"]},"2025-02-20":{"title":"DeepSeek & tariff risk-off slide","body":"A 31% drop through the DeepSeek scare and April's reciprocal-tariff crash, in a violent risk-off flush: VIX exploded 16->52, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -22.0%, and defensives (-7.7%) beat cyclicals (-18.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad. Hardware names with China exposure and consumer cyclicality were hit by tariff and demand fears, with the basket amplifying the de-risking (SMH -30.2% vs SPY -18.4%).","drivers":["risk-off flush","DeepSeek","reciprocal tariffs","China exposure"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险下滑","body_zh":"经历DeepSeek恐慌和4月对等关税崩盘,在剧烈避险抛售中下跌31%:VIX暴涨16->52,高贝塔相对低波重挫-22.0%,放缓恐慌象限中防御板块(-7.7%)跑赢周期股(-18.3%)。具中国敞口和消费周期性的硬件名字受关税和需求担忧打击,篮子放大了去风险(SMH -30.2% 对 SPY -18.4%)。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","DeepSeek","对等关税","中国敞口"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Broad tech melt-up sweep","body":"A +203% surge off the April low as a roaring risk-on regime lifted the entire tech complex: VIX collapsed 52->16, high-beta beat low-vol by a huge +121.4, the dollar fell -3.6% and growth>value +15.1 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -15.2%); the AI-capex melt-up and memory super-cycle spilled into networking silicon, analog/MCU and legacy hardware (SMH +252.4%), re-rating the whole group into the mid-2026 top.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","AI spillover","networking/analog demand","re-rating"],"title_zh":"广泛科技飙升裹挟","body_zh":"狂热的风险偏好行情提振整个科技板块,从4月低点飙升+203%:VIX崩落52->16,高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+121.4,美元下跌-3.6%,成长跑赢价值+15.1,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度保持狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -15.2%);AI资本开支飙升和内存超级周期外溢至网络芯片、模拟/MCU和传统硬件(SMH +252.4%),令整个板块估值重估,直至2026年中见顶。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","AI外溢","网络/模拟需求","估值重估"]}}},"b-non_ai_software":{"now":"Trending but mid-pack on relative strength. As long-duration, rate-sensitive enterprise SaaS this basket is the most exposed to the rate leg of any regime: it lagged the AI leaders and just pulled back ~27% into late June as the post-Hormuz hawkish Fed bias and a firming dollar (+3.4% DXY) re-pressured software multiples, even as breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) in a reflation/growth-up quad.","now_zh":"处于上升趋势但相对强度居中。作为长久期、利率敏感的企业SaaS,这只篮子对任何行情的利率部分最为敏感:它落后于AI龙头,6月底刚回调约27%,因霍尔木兹冲击后偏鹰的美联储倾向和走强的美元(DXY +3.4%)再度压制软件估值,尽管市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%),处于再通胀/增长向上象限。","legs":{"2021-11-09":{"title":"Duration-software de-rating in a rate-shock bear","body":"Non-AI software fell 47% as the Fed pivot hammered the longest-duration, profitless-growth SaaS names: yields surged (TLT -12.3%) and the dollar firmed +5.4% in a stagflation-ish, risk-off regime (VIX 18->32, defensives +1.3% vs cyclicals -5.1%). Rising discount rates and a hard valuation reset hit the high-multiple software complex hardest, with the basket's long duration amplifying the rate move (SMH -20.6% vs SPY -10.5%).","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","Fed hiking","duration sell-off","SaaS valuation"],"title_zh":"久期软件估值下杀,处于利率冲击熊市","body_zh":"美联储转向重击久期最长、尚未盈利的成长型SaaS名字,非AI软件下跌47%:收益率飙升(TLT -12.3%)、美元走强+5.4%,处于类滞胀、避险行情(VIX 18->32,防御板块+1.3% 对 周期股-5.1%)。贴现率上升和硬性估值重置对高估值软件板块打击最重,篮子的长久期放大了利率冲击(SMH -20.6% 对 SPY -10.5%)。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","美联储加息","久期抛售","SaaS估值"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Brief oversold bounce","body":"A +32% bounce off oversold conditions as rate volatility briefly eased (VIX 32->19) in a reflation/growth-up quad, with breadth narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.0%). The relief faded fast with the hiking cycle still accelerating, a duration-sensitivity reflex rather than a regime turn.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","oversold rebound","rate pause"],"title_zh":"短暂超卖反弹","body_zh":"利率波动短暂缓和(VIX 32->19),从超卖状态反弹+32%,处于再通胀/增长向上象限,市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)。加息周期仍在加速,缓解迅速消退,此乃久期敏感性的反射而非行情转向。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","超卖反弹","利率暂停"]},"2022-04-04":{"title":"Rate-driven new lows","body":"A 38% slide to mid-June lows as real yields surged (TLT -14.7%) and the dollar rose +4.7% in a stagflation-ish flight-to-safety (VIX 19->33, defensives -11.5% vs cyclicals -17.1%). Software multiples kept compressing and slowing software-spend guidance compounded the macro pressure; the long-duration basket undercut the index (SMH -24.4% vs SPY -19.7%).","drivers":["rate-driven risk-off","real yields","spend slowdown","multiple compression"],"title_zh":"利率驱动新低","body_zh":"实际收益率飙升(TLT -14.7%)、美元上涨+4.7%,处于类滞胀的避险行情(VIX 19->33,防御板块-11.5% 对 周期股-17.1%),下滑38%至6月中旬低点。软件估值持续压缩,软件支出指引放缓加剧宏观压力;长久期篮子跑输指数(SMH -24.4% 对 SPY -19.7%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动避险","实际收益率","支出放缓","估值压缩"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Peak-inflation relief rally","body":"A +41% rally on peak-inflation hopes and a yield pullback (TLT +5.2%) as VIX eased 33->20 in a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +12.7% vs defensives +12.3%). The bounce was a duration-sensitivity reflex tracking the broad risk-on squeeze, not a fundamental inflection.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","peak-inflation hope","duration reflex"],"title_zh":"通胀见顶反弹","body_zh":"受通胀见顶预期和收益率回落(TLT +5.2%)提振,VIX回落33->20,处于类金发姑娘象限(周期股+12.7% 对 防御板块+12.3%),反弹+41%。此弹升是久期敏感性的反射,跟随广泛的风险偏好挤压,而非基本面拐点。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","通胀见顶预期","久期反射"]},"2022-08-10":{"title":"Hawkish, rate-driven reset leg down","body":"A 37% drop into November as Jackson Hole and persistent inflation pushed yields sharply higher (TLT -18.7%) and the dollar +5.1%, with breadth broadening (RSP beat SPY +3.4%). The renewed rate-driven de-rating fell hardest on profitless software (SMH -18.7% vs SPY -10.6%).","drivers":["rate-driven risk-off","Jackson Hole","yields up","de-rating"],"title_zh":"鹰派利率驱动重置下跌","body_zh":"杰克逊霍尔和顽固通胀大幅推高收益率(TLT -18.7%)、美元+5.1%,市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +3.4%),跌至11月,下挫37%。新一轮利率驱动的估值下杀对未盈利软件打击最重(SMH -18.7% 对 SPY -10.6%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动避险","杰克逊霍尔","收益率上升","估值下杀"]},"2022-11-09":{"title":"Disinflation re-rating on a narrow melt-up","body":"A +114% recovery as cooling CPI and the eventual 2024 Fed cuts revived risk appetite — a goldilocks risk-on melt-up where the dollar fell -5.9%, growth crushed value +42.2 and breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -18.4%), a mega-cap-led tape. Falling discount rates re-rated this long-duration basket (SMH +113.9% vs SPY +36.6%), with margin-improvement stories and durable subscription revenue rebuilding the bid through early 2024.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","disinflation","Fed cuts","margin improvement"],"title_zh":"去通胀估值重估,搭乘窄幅飙升","body_zh":"CPI降温和最终2024年的美联储降息重燃风险偏好——金发姑娘式风险偏好飙升,美元下跌-5.9%,成长大幅跑赢价值+42.2,市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -18.4%),是大盘股主导的行情,回升+114%。贴现率下行令这只长久期篮子估值重估(SMH +113.9% 对 SPY +36.6%),利润率改善故事和稳健的订阅收入在2024年初前重建买盘。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","去通胀","美联储降息","利润率改善"]},"2024-02-09":{"title":"Capex-anxiety risk-off pullback","body":"A -27% pullback as AI-capex fears questioned whether software budgets would be diverted to compute, with the yen-carry unwind adding pressure. The regime was a flight-to-safety: VIX spiked 13->39, yields fell (TLT +7.4%) and defensives (+10.8%) crushed cyclicals (+2.1%) in a slowdown-scare quad, so capital rotated out of high-beta software (SMH +4.6% only) into safety despite soft net-retention prints.","drivers":["risk-off rotation","AI-capex crowding","net retention","carry unwind"],"title_zh":"资本开支焦虑避险回调","body_zh":"AI资本开支担忧引发软件预算是否被算力挤占的质疑,日元套息平仓增添压力,回调27%。当时是避险行情:VIX飙升13->39,收益率下行(TLT +7.4%),防御板块(+10.8%)大幅跑赢周期股(+2.1%),处于放缓恐慌象限,资金从高贝塔软件(SMH仅+4.6%)轮动至安全资产,叠加疲软的净留存数据。","drivers_zh":["避险轮动","AI资本开支挤占","净留存","套息平仓"]},"2024-08-05":{"title":"Cut-cycle software rebound","body":"A +56% recovery as the Fed's September cut lifted rate-sensitive software — a tech/semis-led risk-on tape (VIX 39->13, growth>value +11.3) even as the dollar firmed +3.2% and yields rose (TLT -3.2%). Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.7%); improving budgets and a soft-landing narrative carried the group into December 2024.","drivers":["risk-on tape","Fed cut Sep","soft landing","budget recovery"],"title_zh":"降息周期软件反弹","body_zh":"美联储9月降息提振利率敏感的软件,回升+56%——这是科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好行情(VIX 39->13,成长跑赢价值+11.3),尽管美元走强+3.2%、收益率上行(TLT -3.2%)。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -3.7%);改善的预算和软着陆叙事推动该板块至2024年12月。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好行情","美联储9月降息","软着陆","预算复苏"]},"2024-12-06":{"title":"DeepSeek & tariff risk-off drawdown","body":"A 34% drop through the DeepSeek scare and April's reciprocal-tariff crash, in a violent flight-to-safety: VIX exploded 13->52, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -22.7%, and defensives (-6.7%) beat cyclicals (-18.5%) in a slowdown-scare quad. Macro de-risking plus AI-disruption fears for legacy SaaS drove the de-rating (SMH -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%).","drivers":["risk-off flush","DeepSeek","reciprocal tariffs","AI-disruption fear"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险回撤","body_zh":"经历DeepSeek恐慌和4月对等关税崩盘,在剧烈避险中下跌34%:VIX暴涨13->52,高贝塔相对低波重挫-22.7%,放缓恐慌象限中防御板块(-6.7%)跑赢周期股(-18.5%)。宏观去风险叠加传统SaaS被AI颠覆的担忧驱动估值下杀(SMH -27.3% 对 SPY -17.8%)。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","DeepSeek","对等关税","AI颠覆担忧"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Post-tariff relief rally, lagging the leaders","body":"A +32% bounce off the April low as tariff fears eased and a risk-on regime returned: VIX collapsed 52->15, high-beta beat low-vol by +47.8, the dollar fell -4.2% and growth>value +18.6 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -6.1%); gains lagged the AI leaders (SMH +61.9% vs the basket's softer SPY +28.7% tape) as software still faced an AI-disruption overhang.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","tariff relief","rate stabilization"],"title_zh":"关税后缓解反弹,落后龙头","body_zh":"关税担忧消退、风险偏好行情卷土重来,从4月低点反弹+32%:VIX崩落52->15,高贝塔跑赢低波+47.8,美元下跌-4.2%,成长跑赢价值+18.6,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -6.1%);由于软件仍面临AI颠覆阴影,涨幅落后于AI龙头(SMH +61.9% 对 篮子较温和的SPY +28.7%行情)。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","关税缓解","利率企稳"]},"2025-07-28":{"title":"Reflation-rotation drag out of growth","body":"A 47% slide as the early-2026 Hormuz oil shock (oil +44.8%, CPI 4.2%) drove a reflation/growth-up quad that punished long-duration software. Tellingly this was rotation, not a rate squeeze: bonds actually rallied (TLT +4.1%, yields fell), yet growth lagged value hard (-12.0) as capital fled high-multiple SaaS for energy and value while the index barely moved (SPY +7.6%) — a drag deepened by persistent AI-cannibalization fears into April 2026.","drivers":["growth-to-value rotation","reflation/oil shock","Hormuz CPI spike","AI cannibalization"],"title_zh":"再通胀轮动拖累,资金撤离成长","body_zh":"2026年初霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+44.8%,CPI 4.2%)催生再通胀/增长向上象限,重创长久期软件,下滑47%。值得注意的是这是轮动而非利率挤压:债券实际上上涨(TLT +4.1%,收益率下行),但成长大幅跑输价值(-12.0),资金从高估值SaaS撤向能源与价值股,而指数几乎未动(SPY +7.6%)——这一拖累被持续的AI蚕食担忧加深,直至2026年4月。","drivers_zh":["成长向价值轮动","再通胀/石油冲击","霍尔木兹CPI跳升","AI蚕食"]},"2026-04-10":{"title":"Ceasefire-relief recovery","body":"A +54% recovery as the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire eased the oil/inflation shock and a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up resumed: VIX fell 19->16, high-beta beat low-vol by +26.7 and growth>value +8.6 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -5.4%); oversold long-duration software re-rated (SMH +39.1%) as macro fear faded and budgets stabilized.","drivers":["risk-on melt-up","Hormuz ceasefire","yields ease","oversold rebound"],"title_zh":"停火缓解复苏","body_zh":"6月中旬霍尔木兹停火缓和石油/通胀冲击、科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升重启,回升+54%:VIX回落19->16,高贝塔跑赢低波+26.7,成长跑赢价值+8.6,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -5.4%);宏观恐慌消退、预算企稳,超卖的长久期软件估值重估(SMH +39.1%)。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好飙升","霍尔木兹停火","收益率回落","超卖反弹"]},"2026-06-01":{"title":"Hawkish-bias June pullback as breadth broadens","body":"A -27% pullback as the post-ceasefire Fed retained a hiking bias and tech leadership narrowed. The regime was a defensive rotation: VIX firmed 16->19, defensives (+5.3%) beat cyclicals (-0.1%), growth lagged value hard (-11.5) and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.6%) in a slowdown-scare quad, so rate-sensitive software gave back gains alongside the broad late-cycle de-risking.","drivers":["defensive rotation","Fed hiking bias","narrowing breadth","de-risking"],"title_zh":"鹰派倾向6月回调,广度扩散","body_zh":"停火后美联储维持加息倾向、科技领导力收窄,回调27%。当时是防御性轮动:VIX走强16->19,防御板块(+5.3%)跑赢周期股(-0.1%),成长大幅跑输价值(-11.5),市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +4.6%),处于放缓恐慌象限,利率敏感的软件随着广泛的周期末去风险一同回吐涨幅。","drivers_zh":["防御性轮动","美联储加息倾向","广度收窄","去风险"]}}},"b-cybersecurity":{"now":"Topping at the 87th percentile. Cyber (CRWD/PANW/ZS) compounded on secular spend and breach catalysts, but as a high-beta growth-software basket it amplified the 2026 risk-on melt-up — and now breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%), the dollar is firming (+3.4% DXY) and the broad tech-leadership rollover argues for consolidation off a stretched rally.","now_zh":"在87百分位见顶。网络安全(CRWD/PANW/ZS)受益于长期支出和数据泄露催化而复利增长,但作为高贝塔成长软件篮子,它放大了2026年的风险偏好飙升——如今市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、美元走强(DXY +3.4%),广泛的科技领导力回落令过度拉伸的涨势指向盘整。","legs":{"2021-11-09":{"title":"Growth-multiple compression in a rate-shock bear","body":"Cyber fell 36% as the Fed pivot de-rated high-multiple security-software growth names: yields surged (TLT -12.3%) and the dollar firmed +5.4% in a stagflation-ish, risk-off regime (VIX 18->32, defensives +1.3% vs cyclicals -5.1%). Rising rates outweighed strong secular bookings in the broad SaaS sell-off, and the basket's high beta amplified the de-rating (SMH -20.6% vs SPY -10.5%).","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","Fed hiking","multiple compression","SaaS sell-off"],"title_zh":"成长估值压缩,处于利率冲击熊市","body_zh":"美联储转向令高估值的安全软件成长股估值下杀,网络安全下跌36%:收益率飙升(TLT -12.3%)、美元走强+5.4%,处于类滞胀、避险行情(VIX 18->32,防御板块+1.3% 对 周期股-5.1%)。在广泛的SaaS抛售中,利率上升盖过了强劲的长期订单,篮子的高贝塔放大了估值下杀(SMH -20.6% 对 SPY -10.5%)。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","美联储加息","估值压缩","SaaS抛售"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Oversold relief bounce","body":"A +28% bounce as rate volatility briefly cooled (VIX 32->19) in a reflation/growth-up quad, with breadth narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.0%). The geopolitical backdrop kept a structural cyber-spend bid even as macro pressure lingered, but the move was an oversold reflex rather than a regime turn.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","oversold rebound","cyber-spend bid"],"title_zh":"超卖缓解反弹","body_zh":"利率波动短暂降温(VIX 32->19),反弹+28%,处于再通胀/增长向上象限,市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)。即便宏观压力犹存,地缘政治背景维持了结构性的网络安全支出买盘,但此波是超卖反射而非行情转向。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","超卖反弹","网络安全支出买盘"]},"2022-04-04":{"title":"Rate-shock new lows","body":"A 36% slide as surging real yields (TLT -10.1%) and a stronger dollar (+4.9%) hit growth software again in a slowdown-scare flight-to-safety (VIX 19->33, defensives -4.5% vs cyclicals -11.9%). Budget-scrutiny worries layered onto the macro de-rating, and the high-beta basket fell well past the index (SMH -18.6% vs SPY -14.0%).","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","real yields","budget scrutiny","de-rating"],"title_zh":"利率冲击新低","body_zh":"实际收益率飙升(TLT -10.1%)、美元走强(+4.9%)再度冲击成长软件,处于放缓恐慌的避险行情(VIX 19->33,防御板块-4.5% 对 周期股-11.9%),下滑36%。预算审视担忧叠加于宏观估值下杀之上,高贝塔篮子跌幅远超指数(SMH -18.6% 对 SPY -14.0%)。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","实际收益率","预算审视","估值下杀"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Peak-inflation relief rally","body":"A +33% rebound on peak-inflation hopes as VIX eased 33->20 in a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +8.2% vs defensives +5.9%), even as the dollar firmed +2.6% and bonds stayed soft (TLT -1.6%). Resilient security budgets supported the bounce relative to broader software, but it tracked the broad high-beta risk-on squeeze rather than a fundamental inflection.","drivers":["risk-on bounce","peak-inflation hope","resilient budgets"],"title_zh":"通胀见顶反弹","body_zh":"受通胀见顶预期提振,VIX回落33->20,处于类金发姑娘象限(周期股+8.2% 对 防御板块+5.9%),反弹+33%,尽管美元走强+2.6%、债券依旧偏弱(TLT -1.6%)。有韧性的安全预算使其反弹强于大盘软件,但此波跟随广泛的高贝塔风险偏好挤压而非基本面拐点。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","通胀见顶预期","韧性预算"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Hawkish, rate-driven leg down","body":"A 30% drop into January 2023 as Jackson Hole pushed yields higher (TLT -9.5%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Notably breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.9%) and growth lagged value hard (-14.2), a rotation away from long-duration growth in which lengthening sales cycles and macro caution pressured cyber (SMH -16.8% vs SPY -10.8%).","drivers":["rate-driven rotation","Jackson Hole","sales-cycle lengthening","yields up"],"title_zh":"鹰派利率驱动下跌","body_zh":"杰克逊霍尔推高收益率(TLT -9.5%),跌至2023年1月,下挫30%,处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。值得注意的是市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +4.9%),成长大幅跑输价值(-14.2),是远离长久期成长的轮动,拉长的销售周期和宏观谨慎压制网络安全(SMH -16.8% 对 SPY -10.8%)。","drivers_zh":["利率驱动轮动","杰克逊霍尔","销售周期拉长","收益率上升"]},"2023-01-05":{"title":"Secular-spend compounding on a narrow melt-up","body":"A +136% run as disinflation, the genAI rally and relentless secular security demand compounded — riding a goldilocks risk-on melt-up where VIX fell 22->15, growth crushed value by +67.4 and breadth was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -33.1%), a mega-cap-led tape. Breach catalysts and platform-consolidation wins at CrowdStrike and Palo Alto sustained the bid through the 2024 cut cycle even as yields drifted up (TLT -7.2%).","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","secular spend","platform consolidation","breach catalysts"],"title_zh":"长期支出复利,搭乘窄幅飙升","body_zh":"去通胀、生成式AI上涨和不断增长的长期安全需求叠加,上涨+136%——搭乘金发姑娘式风险偏好飙升,VIX回落22->15,成长大幅跑赢价值+67.4,市场广度极度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -33.1%),是大盘股主导的行情。数据泄露催化和CrowdStrike、Palo Alto的平台整合胜利,在2024年降息周期前维持买盘,即便收益率上行(TLT -7.2%)。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","长期支出","平台整合","数据泄露催化"]},"2025-02-13":{"title":"DeepSeek & tariff risk-off dip","body":"A -23% pullback through the DeepSeek scare and April's reciprocal-tariff crash, in a violent flight-to-safety: VIX exploded 15->52, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -20.9%, and defensives (-7.3%) beat cyclicals (-18.0%) in a slowdown-scare quad. Macro de-risking hit growth software despite resilient cyber fundamentals, with the basket amplifying the move (SMH -28.6% vs SPY -18.3%).","drivers":["risk-off flush","DeepSeek","reciprocal tariffs","de-risking"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险回调","body_zh":"经历DeepSeek恐慌和4月对等关税崩盘,在剧烈避险中回调23%:VIX暴涨15->52,高贝塔相对低波重挫-20.9%,放缓恐慌象限中防御板块(-7.3%)跑赢周期股(-18.0%)。尽管网络安全基本面稳健,宏观去风险仍冲击成长软件,篮子放大了跌幅(SMH -28.6% 对 SPY -18.3%)。","drivers_zh":["避险抛售","DeepSeek","对等关税","去风险"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery on breach catalysts and a risk-on melt-up","body":"A +44% recovery off the April low as tariff fears eased and a goldilocks risk-on regime returned: VIX collapsed 52->17, high-beta beat low-vol by +61.7, growth>value +25.0 and the dollar fell -3.4%. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -13.2%); high-profile breaches plus AI-security and identity demand kept this high-beta group bid (SMH +95.1%) into November.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","breach catalysts","AI security","tariff relief"],"title_zh":"数据泄露催化复苏,搭乘风险偏好飙升","body_zh":"关税担忧消退、金发姑娘式风险偏好行情卷土重来,从4月低点回升+44%:VIX崩落52->17,高贝塔跑赢低波+61.7,成长跑赢价值+25.0,美元下跌-3.4%。市场广度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -13.2%);备受关注的数据泄露叠加AI安全和身份认证需求,维持这只高贝塔板块的买盘(SMH +95.1%)至11月。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","数据泄露催化","AI安全","关税缓解"]},"2025-11-11":{"title":"Hawkish-reset consolidation as leadership broadens","body":"A 29% drop as the late-2025 hawkish reset and the early-2026 Hormuz oil/CPI shock pressured growth multiples. This was a rotation more than a crash: SPY was flat (+0.2%) while breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY +6.6%) and growth lagged value (-14.9) in a stagflation-ish quad. Stretched valuations made cyber vulnerable as capital left over-owned high-beta growth for the rest of the tape.","drivers":["leadership rotation","hawkish reset","Hormuz shock","valuation"],"title_zh":"鹰派重置盘整,领导力扩散","body_zh":"2025年末鹰派重置和2026年初霍尔木兹石油/CPI冲击压制成长估值,下跌29%。这更多是轮动而非崩盘:SPY持平(+0.2%),市场广度急剧扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%),成长跑输价值(-14.9),处于类滞胀象限。过高的估值使网络安全脆弱,资金从被过度持有的高贝塔成长流向其余板块。","drivers_zh":["领导力轮动","鹰派重置","霍尔木兹冲击","估值"]},"2026-02-23":{"title":"Ceasefire-relief rally to top","body":"A +64% rally as the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire eased macro fear and a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up resumed: VIX fell 21->16, high-beta beat low-vol by +30.6 and growth>value +8.5 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -7.5%); durable security spend reasserted leadership and this high-beta group ran to topping levels (SMH +47.2%) before the broad tech-leadership rollover began.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","Hormuz ceasefire","secular spend","risk-on rebound"],"title_zh":"停火缓解反弹至顶","body_zh":"6月中旬霍尔木兹停火缓和宏观恐慌、科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升重启,反弹+64%:VIX回落21->16,高贝塔跑赢低波+30.6,成长跑赢价值+8.5,处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度保持狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -7.5%);稳健的安全支出重申领导力,这只高贝塔板块涨至见顶水平(SMH +47.2%),随后广泛的科技领导力回落开始。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","霍尔木兹停火","长期支出","风险偏好反弹"]}}},"b-quantum_computing":{"now":"Trending with strong relative strength but speculative by nature. As a high-beta, retail-driven theme it amplifies the regime in both directions — and the current tape is risk-on but cooling: SMH +67.9% yet breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and the dollar is firming (+3.4% DXY) in a reflation/growth-up quad. With only two long legs of history, quantum remains prone to violent spikes, still riding the 2023-25 AI-adjacency narrative.","now_zh":"处于上升趋势且相对强度强,但本质投机。作为高贝塔、散户驱动的主题,它在两个方向都放大行情——当前行情风险偏好但正在降温:SMH +67.9%,但市场广度扩散(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)、美元走强(DXY +3.4%),处于再通胀/增长向上象限。仅有两条长腿的历史,量子计算仍易发生剧烈飙升,继续搭乘2023-25年的AI邻接叙事。","legs":{"2021-11-17":{"title":"SPAC-era speculative washout in a rate-shock bear","body":"Quantum names fell 61% over 15 months as a rate-shock bear crushed profitless, pre-revenue speculative tech: yields surged (TLT -25.2%) and the dollar ripped +9.2% in a risk-off, slowdown-scare regime (VIX 17->26, defensives +1.1% vs cyclicals -7.2%). As the highest-beta, most speculative cohort, the pre-revenue de-SPAC names saw the deepest multiple compression of the rate shock — far worse than the index (SPY -15.2%).","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","de-SPAC washout","no revenue","speculative de-rating"],"title_zh":"SPAC时代投机洗盘,处于利率冲击熊市","body_zh":"利率冲击熊市重创未盈利、零营收的投机科技,量子计算股15个月内下跌61%:收益率飙升(TLT -25.2%)、美元大涨+9.2%,处于避险、放缓恐慌行情(VIX 17->26,防御板块+1.1% 对 周期股-7.2%)。作为贝塔最高、最投机的群体,零营收的de-SPAC名字在利率冲击中遭遇最深的估值压缩——远逊于指数(SPY -15.2%)。","drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","de-SPAC洗盘","零营收","投机估值下杀"]},"2023-03-15":{"title":"AI-adjacency moonshot in a risk-on melt-up","body":"An explosive +1,773% run as the genAI boom and headline milestones (Google/IBM/Nvidia quantum signals) drew retail into the highest-beta frontier-tech theme — supercharged by a goldilocks risk-on tape: the dollar fell -5.4%, growth crushed value +59.6 and breadth was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -34.1%), a mega-cap-led melt-up (yields drifted up over the span, TLT -5.2%, but a weaker dollar and crushed-vol risk appetite did the lifting). As leveraged speculative longs, quantum names amplified that risk-on regime violently and largely detached from near-term revenue, peaking in October 2025.","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","AI-adjacency narrative","quantum milestones","retail momentum"],"title_zh":"AI邻接登月,处于风险偏好飙升","body_zh":"生成式AI热潮和标志性里程碑(谷歌/IBM/英伟达的量子信号)将散户引入贝塔最高的前沿科技主题,爆发性上涨+1,773%——被金发姑娘式风险偏好行情助燃:美元下跌-5.4%,成长大幅跑赢价值+59.6,市场广度极度狭窄(RSP跑输SPY -34.1%),是大盘股主导的飙升(该期间收益率实为上行,TLT -5.2%,真正的推力来自走弱的美元和波动率崩塌后的风险偏好)。作为带杠杆的投机多头,量子计算名字剧烈放大了这一风险偏好行情,且基本脱离近期营收,在2025年10月见顶。","drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","AI邻接叙事","量子里程碑","散户动能"]}}},"b-data_center_power":{"now":"Power & cooling kit for AI datacenters (GE Vernova, Vertiv, Eaton) — the electricity super-cycle re-rated this group from late 2023 as AI compute exploded demand for generation, transformers and thermal management. It just ran +287% off the April-2025 tariff low inside a semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +68%, VIX 14-18), but the regime is now broadening (equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%) and a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) plus a reflation/growth-up quad have leadership rotating toward Energy and Industrials — the basket is rolling over as the AI-capex pace gets re-examined.","now_zh":"为AI数据中心供电与散热的设备龙头（GE Vernova、Vertiv、Eaton）——电力超级周期自2023年底起重估这一组别，因AI算力激增推高了发电、变压器与热管理需求。它刚在半导体领涨的风险偏好行情中（半导体SMH +68%、VIX 14-18）自4月关税低点上涨287%，但当前象限转为再通胀/增长向上、市场广度正在扩散（等权跑赢市值权+2.9%）、美元走强（DXY +3.4%），领涨向能源与工业轮动——随着市场重新审视AI资本开支节奏，该篮子正在见顶回落。","legs":{"2021-11-08":{"title":"Rate-driven 2022 bear de-rates the group","body":"Power-infrastructure names fell -28% with the broad 2022 bear as the Fed pivoted to aggressive hiking: this was a rate-regime move, with the 10Y surging (TLT -21.3%) and a soaring dollar (DXY +11.8%) crushing long-duration capex stories. This pre-dated the AI-power thesis, so the group traded as ordinary rate-sensitive industrial/utility cyclicals into a stagflation-ish quad where defensives (+4.0%) led cyclicals (-13.3%) amid flight-to-safety (VIX 17->27).","drivers":["rate-regime de-rate (TLT -21.3%)","Fed hiking","flight-to-safety","pre-AI-thesis"],"title_zh":"利率驱动的2022年熊市压估值","body_zh":"电力基础设施类股随2022年大熊市下跌28%，原因是美联储转向激进加息：这是一轮利率主导行情，10年期收益率飙升（TLT -21.3%）、美元暴涨（DXY +11.8%），长久期资本开支题材遭压垮。此时尚无AI电力主线，该组别只是按利率敏感的工业／公用事业周期股交易，进入类滞胀象限，避险情绪下防御股（+4.0%）跑赢周期股（-13.3%）（VIX 17->27）。","drivers_zh":["利率主导下杀(TLT -21.3%)","美联储加息","避险","AI主线未现"]},"2022-07-01":{"title":"AI super-cycle re-rates into a semis-led melt-up","body":"From the 2022 low this basket compounded +319% as the AI-datacenter electricity thesis took hold through 2023-24 — power, transformers, switchgear and liquid cooling became the bottleneck on the AI buildout. As a high-beta capex play it amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +153.6%, growth>value +33.7, VIX collapsing 27->12) that pulled flows out of defensives; breadth was narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight -16.8%), a mega-cap-led tape that rewarded Vertiv, GE Vernova and Eaton as they re-rated from sleepy industrials into AI-power core holdings.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up","AI datacenter power","narrow breadth (-16.8%)","cooling bottleneck"],"title_zh":"AI超级周期在半导体领涨的暴涨中重估","body_zh":"自2022年低点起，该篮子累计上涨319%，因AI数据中心电力主线在2023–24年确立——电力、变压器、开关设备与液冷成为AI建设的瓶颈环节。作为高贝塔资本开支标的，它放大了一轮金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +153.6%、成长跑赢价值+33.7、VIX由27跌至12），资金流出防御股；市场广度偏窄（等权跑输市值权-16.8%），这种巨头领涨的行情奖励了从沉闷工业股重估为AI电力核心持仓的Vertiv、GE Vernova与Eaton。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨风险偏好暴涨","数据中心电力","窄广度(-16.8%)","散热瓶颈"]},"2024-05-24":{"title":"Aug-2024 deflation-scare flight-to-safety","body":"A shallow -20% pullback as megacap-tech and AI-adjacent names wobbled into the August 2024 volatility scare and yen-carry unwind — a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with VIX exploding 12->28, yields falling (TLT +6.0%) and defensives (+2.4%) beating cyclicals (-3.4%) in a classic risk-off rotation into safety. As a high-beta group it overshot the broad tape (SMH -13.4%), but the power thesis stayed intact; this was froth coming off an extended name on a vol spike, not a thesis break.","drivers":["risk-off flight-to-safety","Aug-2024 vol (VIX 12->28)","deflation-scare quad","carry unwind"],"title_zh":"2024年8月通缩惊魂避险回调","body_zh":"浅幅回调20%，在2024年8月波动惊魂与日元套利平仓前，巨型科技与AI相关股震荡——这是放缓/通缩惊魂象限，VIX由12飙至28、收益率下行（TLT +6.0%）、防御股（+2.4%）跑赢周期股（-3.4%），典型的避险轮动。作为高贝塔组别它超调于大盘（半导体SMH -13.4%），但电力主线依旧完好；这是涨幅过大标的在波动飙升时的泡沫挤出，并非逻辑破裂。","drivers_zh":["避险","8月波动(VIX 12->28)","通缩惊魂象限","套利平仓"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Fed cuts spark a narrow goldilocks risk-on bid","body":"A +60% leg as the Fed began cutting in September 2024 and hyperscaler capex guidance plus nuclear/grid power deals validated the AI electricity demand story. The macro backdrop was a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +26.9%, growth>value +13.9, VIX falling 28->15) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -5.7%) and a firmer dollar (DXY +4.8%) — a regime that rewards high-beta AI proxies. Datacenter power-purchase agreements and surging load forecasts kept the bid firm.","drivers":["goldilocks risk-on (SMH +26.9%)","Fed cuts","narrow breadth (-5.7%)","load growth"],"title_zh":"美联储降息点燃窄幅金发女郎风险偏好","body_zh":"上涨60%，因美联储于2024年9月开始降息，叠加超大规模厂商资本开支指引与核电／电网供电协议验证了AI电力需求逻辑。宏观背景是金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好行情（半导体SMH +26.9%、成长跑赢价值+13.9、VIX由28降至15），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-5.7%）、美元走强（DXY +4.8%）——奖励高贝塔AI代理标的的环境。数据中心购电协议与飙升的负荷预测使买盘稳固。","drivers_zh":["金发女郎风险偏好(SMH +26.9%)","美联储降息","窄广度(-5.7%)","负荷增长"]},"2025-01-22":{"title":"DeepSeek shock detonates a risk-off flush","body":"A -37% drawdown triggered by DeepSeek's late-January efficiency shock — which briefly questioned whether AI would need as much electricity — that deepened into the April tariff crash. As a high-beta AI proxy the basket amplified a violent risk-off flush: VIX tripled 15->45, semis cratered (SMH -32.3%) and defensives (-2.2%) outran cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The most directly power-levered names were hit hardest on the demand-destruction fear even as yields fell (TLT +7.2%).","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15->45)","DeepSeek shock","high-beta amplification","tariff crash"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击引爆避险急挫","body_zh":"回撤37%，由DeepSeek 1月底效率冲击触发——市场一度质疑AI是否仍需如此大量电力——随后在4月关税崩盘中加深。作为高贝塔AI代理，该篮子放大了一轮剧烈的避险急挫：VIX翻三倍由15升至45、半导体崩跌（半导体SMH -32.3%）、防御股（-2.2%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%），处于放缓/通缩惊魂象限。即便收益率下行（TLT +7.2%），电力杠杆最直接的标的在需求毁灭担忧下跌幅最大。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15->45)","DeepSeek冲击","高贝塔放大","关税崩盘"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Tariff-low moonshot in a semis-led risk-on tape","body":"A +287% recovery off the April-2025 tariff low as the DeepSeek scare faded and hyperscaler capex re-accelerated — power, cooling and grid kit reclaimed AI-leadership status. The basket rode a once-in-a-cycle semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +271.1%, VIX collapsing 45->17) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -13.4%), amplifying the regime as a high-beta capex proxy. It ran hard into mid-2026 before rolling over as the AI-capex pace was re-examined.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +271%)","capex re-accel","narrow breadth (-13.4%)","AI leadership"],"title_zh":"关税低点暴涨于半导体领涨的风险偏好行情","body_zh":"自2025年4月初关税低点上涨287%，DeepSeek惊魂消退、超大厂商资本开支重新加速——电力、散热与电网设备重夺AI领涨地位。该篮子搭乘周期一遇的半导体领涨风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +271.1%、VIX由45崩至17），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-13.4%），作为高贝塔资本开支代理放大了该象限。它一路猛涨至2026年中，随后因AI资本开支节奏被重新审视而见顶回落。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +271%)","资本开支再加速","窄广度(-13.4%)","AI领涨"]}}},"b-nuclear_power":{"now":"Nuclear utilities + SMR developers (Constellation, Vistra, Oklo, SMR) — the highest-beta way to play AI baseload power demand, reactor restarts and new-build optionality. After a ~205% surge into October 2025 the group corrected hard; now in prime-entry territory after a fresh leg lower into mid-2026. The current tape is a broadening reflation/growth-up quad (equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +17.6) with a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) and calm VIX (14-18) — leadership has rotated toward Energy/Industrials, leaving these speculative pure-plays out of the immediate bid.","now_zh":"核电公用事业＋小型模块化反应堆(SMR)开发商（Constellation、Vistra、Oklo、SMR）——押注AI基荷电力需求、反应堆重启与新建产能期权的最高弹性方式。在2025年10月飙升约205%后大幅回调；经2026年中又一轮下跌后，目前处于优选入场区间。当前行情是广度扩散的再通胀/增长向上象限（等权跑赢市值权+2.9%、油价+19.2%、铜金比+17.6），美元走强（DXY +3.4%）、VIX平静（14-18）——领涨已向能源／工业轮动，使这些投机性纯标的暂未获得买盘。","legs":{"2024-07-12":{"title":"Aug-2024 vol scare clips high-beta leaders","body":"A sharp -26% pullback into the August 2024 volatility spike and yen-carry unwind, as the newly hot nuclear-for-AI names gave back froth. The macro was a slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off (VIX exploding 12->39, defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals -6.6%, broadening +4.2%); as a high-beta cohort the group overshot the broad tape (SMH -22.3%). The restart/baseload thesis stayed intact — this was a positioning flush in a vol shock, not a fundamental break.","drivers":["risk-off vol shock (VIX 12->39)","high-beta overshoot","profit-taking","carry unwind"],"title_zh":"2024年8月波动惊魂回吐高贝塔涨幅","body_zh":"在2024年8月波动飙升与日元套利平仓前急跌26%，新晋火热的核电AI概念股吐出泡沫。宏观是放缓/通缩惊魂的避险（VIX由12飙至39、防御股+0.3%对周期股-6.6%、广度扩散+4.2%）；作为高贝塔组别它超调于大盘（半导体SMH -22.3%）。重启／基荷逻辑完好——此为波动冲击中的仓位急挫，而非基本面破裂。","drivers_zh":["避险波动冲击(VIX 12->39)","高贝塔超调","获利了结","套利平仓"]},"2024-08-05":{"title":"Datacenter-nuclear deals ignite a goldilocks re-rate","body":"A +202% rocket leg as marquee datacenter-nuclear deals — Constellation's Three Mile Island restart for Microsoft, Amazon/Google SMR commitments — validated nuclear as the AI baseload answer. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +23.1%, growth>value +12.9, VIX collapsing 39->15) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -5.5%) and a firmer dollar (DXY +4.6%); Fed cuts and reactor-restart headlines compounded the buying frenzy in the highest-beta corner of AI power.","drivers":["goldilocks risk-on (SMH +23.1%)","TMI restart","narrow breadth (-5.5%)","AI baseload"],"title_zh":"数据中心核电协议在金发女郎行情中点燃重估","body_zh":"上涨202%的火箭行情，标志性数据中心核电协议——Constellation为微软重启三哩岛、亚马逊／谷歌的SMR承诺——确立核电为AI基荷答案。该篮子放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好行情（半导体SMH +23.1%、成长跑赢价值+12.9、VIX由39崩至15），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-5.5%）、美元走强（DXY +4.6%）；美联储降息与反应堆重启新闻在AI电力中弹性最高的角落叠加放大买盘狂热。","drivers_zh":["金发女郎风险偏好(SMH +23.1%)","三哩岛重启","窄广度(-5.5%)","AI基荷"]},"2025-01-24":{"title":"DeepSeek demand-shock high-beta flush","body":"A two-session -22% flush as DeepSeek's efficiency claims hit late January 2025, hammering the AI-power-demand premium hardest in the high-beta nuclear/SMR cohort. It was a sharp risk-off jolt (VIX 15->18, defensives +0.9% vs cyclicals -0.9%, slowdown/deflation-scare quad) in which pre-revenue SMR developers — speculative leveraged longs — were the most exposed to the demand-destruction narrative.","drivers":["risk-off demand shock","DeepSeek shock","high-beta unwind","demand fear"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek需求冲击的高贝塔急挫","body_zh":"两个交易日内急挫22%，2025年1月底DeepSeek效率说法冲击AI电力需求溢价，对高弹性核电／SMR组别打击最重。这是一次急促的避险冲击（VIX 15->18、防御股+0.9%对周期股-0.9%、放缓/通缩惊魂象限），尚无营收的SMR开发商——投机性杠杆多头——最受需求毁灭叙事拖累。","drivers_zh":["避险需求冲击","DeepSeek冲击","高贝塔平仓","需求担忧"]},"2025-01-27":{"title":"Snap-back bargain bid as risk steadies","body":"A quick +22% bounce as dip-buyers concluded the DeepSeek demand-destruction read was overdone — efficiency gains arguably expand AI deployment and total power draw (the Jevons rebuttal). The tape was flat-to-stagflation-ish (VIX 18->16, cyclicals and defensives both +0.2%, copper-gold +5.4), so this was idiosyncratic, headline-driven mean-reversion in a thin high-beta pure-play group rather than a regime-driven rally.","drivers":["headline mean-reversion","dip-buying","Jevons rebuttal","calm tape"],"title_zh":"风险企稳下超跌反弹捡漏买盘","body_zh":"迅速反弹22%，抄底资金认为DeepSeek需求毁灭解读过度——效率提升反而可能扩大AI部署与总用电量（杰文斯反驳）。行情近乎走平、略偏类滞胀（VIX 18->16、周期股与防御股均+0.2%、铜金比+5.4），因此这是薄盘高贝塔纯概念组别中由个股新闻驱动的均值回归，而非象限驱动的反弹。","drivers_zh":["新闻均值回归","抄底","杰文斯反驳","行情平静"]},"2025-02-10":{"title":"Pre-tariff risk-off drains the speculative premium","body":"A -34% slide as the broad risk-off into the spring 2025 tariff scare drained the speculative premium from high-multiple nuclear/SMR names. The quad turned slowdown/deflation-scare with VIX rising 16->28, defensives (+1.1%) beating cyclicals (-6.8%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%); rate-sensitive utilities and pre-revenue developers both leaked as the high-beta cohort led the AI-power complex into the April low.","drivers":["risk-off de-rate (VIX 16->28)","tariff fear","high-beta multiple compression","deflation-scare quad"],"title_zh":"关税前避险抽走投机溢价","body_zh":"下跌34%，2025年春关税惊魂前的广泛避险抽走了高估值核电／SMR标的的投机溢价。象限转为放缓/通缩惊魂，VIX由16升至28、防御股（+1.1%）跑赢周期股（-6.8%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%）；利率敏感的公用事业与尚无营收的开发商均承压，高贝塔组别领跌AI电力板块至4月低点。","drivers_zh":["避险下杀(VIX 16->28)","关税担忧","高贝塔估值压缩","通缩惊魂象限"]},"2025-03-10":{"title":"Choppy relief rally on policy hopes","body":"A +24% bounce on nuclear-friendly policy signals and bargain-hunting before the final pre-tariff leg lower. The macro briefly stabilized into a mild goldilocks/growth-up quad (VIX easing 28->17, cyclicals +3.6% vs defensives -0.9%, oil +4.7%), but breadth was unimpressive and the market struggled to price the tariff overhang — a two-way, headline-sensitive tape against a still-intact AI-baseload story.","drivers":["mild risk-on stabilization","policy tailwind","dip-buying","choppy tape"],"title_zh":"政策预期带来震荡反弹","body_zh":"反弹24%，受利好核电的政策信号与逢低买盘推动，随后在关税前最后一轮下跌。宏观短暂企稳为温和的金发女郎/增长向上象限（VIX由28回落至17、周期股+3.6%对防御股-0.9%、油价+4.7%），但广度乏力，市场难以为关税阴影定价——这是依旧完好的AI基荷逻辑下、对新闻敏感的双向震荡行情。","drivers_zh":["温和风险偏好企稳","政策顺风","抄底","震荡行情"]},"2025-03-24":{"title":"Final pre-tariff capitulation flush","body":"A -26% drop into the early-April 2025 tariff-crash low, completing the deep correction from the January peak. This was a full risk-off capitulation (VIX exploding 17->45, defensives -4.6% vs cyclicals -12.7%, slowdown/deflation-scare quad) in which the high-beta nuclear group overshot the broad selloff (SMH -21.6%) alongside the whole AI complex before the recovery began.","drivers":["risk-off capitulation (VIX 17->45)","tariff crash","high-beta overshoot","broad de-risk"],"title_zh":"关税前最后投降性急挫","body_zh":"下跌26%至2025年4月初关税崩盘低点，完成自2025年1月高点的深度回调。这是一次彻底的避险投降（VIX由17飙至45、防御股-4.6%对周期股-12.7%、放缓/通缩惊魂象限），高弹性核电组别随整个AI板块超调于大盘抛售（半导体SMH -21.6%），随后反弹启动。","drivers_zh":["避险投降(VIX 17->45)","关税崩盘","高贝塔超调","广泛去风险"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Tariff-low moonshot in a semis-led risk-on tape","body":"A +205% surge off the April-2025 tariff low as AI-power demand reasserted, hyperscaler capex re-accelerated and the reactor-restart/SMR newsflow returned. As the highest-beta AI-power proxy the group amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89%, growth>value +23.0, VIX collapsing 45->21) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -11.2%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%), running to a fresh peak by mid-October 2025 on relentless AI-baseload buying.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89%)","AI power demand","narrow breadth (-11.2%)","capex re-accel"],"title_zh":"关税低点暴涨于半导体领涨的风险偏好行情","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点飙升205%，AI电力需求重新确立、超大厂商资本开支再加速、反应堆重启／SMR新闻流回归。作为弹性最高的AI电力代理，该组别放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +89%、成长跑赢价值+23.0、VIX由45崩至21），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-11.2%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%），在持续的AI基荷买盘下于2025年10月中创出新高。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +89%)","AI电力需求","窄广度(-11.2%)","资本开支再加速"]},"2025-10-15":{"title":"Blow-off top unwinds as breadth broadens","body":"A -39% drawdown from the October-2025 blow-off top as the most stretched AI-power trade unwound — AI-capex digestion fears and froth in pre-revenue SMR names drove the de-rate. The regime had quietly rotated to a broadening reflation/growth-up quad (equal-weight beating cap-weight +4.9%, Energy +45.7% on a 76.6% oil rip) that drained flows from narrow high-multiple AI proxies even as VIX only rose modestly (21->31); the fundamental restart thesis stayed intact through the price reset.","drivers":["broadening rotation out of AI","blow-off unwind","capex digestion","froth purge"],"title_zh":"喷发顶部在广度扩散中平仓","body_zh":"自2025年10月喷发顶部回撤39%，最被拉伸的AI电力交易平仓——AI资本开支消化担忧与尚无营收SMR标的的泡沫推动估值下杀。行情已悄然轮动至广度扩散的再通胀/增长向上象限（等权跑赢市值权+4.9%、油价大涨76.6%带动能源+45.7%），即便VIX仅小幅上行（21->31），资金仍从狭窄的高估值AI代理流出；价格重置过程中重启基本面逻辑依旧完好。","drivers_zh":["广度扩散使资金流出AI","喷发平仓","资本开支消化","泡沫挤出"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Oversold bounce as semis-led risk-on resumes","body":"A +30% recovery as bargain-hunting met fresh reactor-restart and SMR-licensing milestones in early 2026, riding a semis-led risk-on rebound (SMH +51.6%, VIX collapsing 31->17, narrow breadth -7.2%) in a reflation/growth-up quad. As a high-beta proxy the basket leveraged the up-tape; house view: a relief rally within a still-volatile group rather than a confirmed new uptrend.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on rebound (SMH +51.6%)","restart milestones","narrow breadth (-7.2%)","relief rally"],"title_zh":"半导体领涨风险偏好重启下的超跌反弹","body_zh":"反弹30%，2026年初逢低买盘遇上新的反应堆重启与SMR许可里程碑，搭乘半导体领涨的风险偏好反弹（半导体SMH +51.6%、VIX由31崩至17、窄广度-7.2%），处于再通胀/增长向上象限。作为高贝塔代理，该篮子放大了上涨行情；本观点：这是仍然波动的组别内的修复性反弹，而非确认的新上升趋势。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨风险偏好反弹(SMH +51.6%)","重启里程碑","窄广度(-7.2%)","修复反弹"]},"2026-05-06":{"title":"Stagflation-ish pullback into prime entry","body":"A -22% give-back into mid-June 2026 on a mild stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 17->22, defensives +0.4% vs cyclicals -1.7%, firmer dollar DXY +2.0%, copper-gold +14.1), leaving the basket deeply washed out and screening as prime-entry on our framework. House view: positioning is light and the AI-baseload thesis is durable, but confirmation of a trend turn is still pending in this high-beta group.","drivers":["stagflation-ish risk-off","washout","high-beta de-rate","prime entry"],"title_zh":"类滞胀回落至优选入场区","body_zh":"至2026年6月中回吐22%，受温和类滞胀避险影响（VIX 17->22、防御股+0.4%对周期股-1.7%、美元走强DXY +2.0%、铜金比+14.1），使篮子深度超跌，在我们框架中显示为优选入场。本观点：仓位轻、AI基荷逻辑持久，但这一高贝塔组别趋势反转的确认仍待出现。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀避险","超跌","高贝塔下杀","优选入场"]}}},"b-power_grid":{"now":"Grid & transmission buildout — transformers, switchgear, utility-adjacent capex riding the same AI-load + electrification wave. The group ran ~249% off the 2022 low but now sits in bottoming territory after a 2025-26 consolidation; the tape is a broadening reflation/growth-up quad (equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +17.6) with a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) and calm VIX (14-18). Positioning is washed out while the multi-year grid-capex story stays intact.","now_zh":"电网与输配电建设——变压器、开关设备、公用事业相关资本开支，搭乘同一波AI负荷＋电气化浪潮。该组别自2022年低点上涨约249%，但经2025–26年盘整后目前处于筑底区间；行情为广度扩散的再通胀/增长向上象限（等权跑赢市值权+2.9%、油价+19.2%、铜金比+17.6），美元走强（DXY +3.4%）、VIX平静（14-18）。仓位已超跌，而多年期电网资本开支逻辑依旧完好。","legs":{"2022-09-12":{"title":"Rate-driven 2022 bear-market low","body":"A -15% slide into the October 2022 cycle low as peak-hawkish Fed pricing hit rate-sensitive utilities and capital-goods names — a rate-regime move with the 10Y surging (TLT -8.0%) and a stronger dollar (DXY +4.6%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (defensives -11.2% and cyclicals -11.7% both deep red, VIX 24->32). Grid/electrification was not yet a market theme, so this traded as ordinary rate-sensitive defensive-cyclical weakness.","drivers":["rate-regime de-rate (TLT -8.0%)","Fed hiking","deflation-scare quad","pre-theme"],"title_zh":"利率驱动的2022年末熊市低点","body_zh":"下跌15%至2022年10月周期低点，美联储鹰派定价见顶打击利率敏感的公用事业与资本品标的——这是利率主导行情，10年期收益率飙升（TLT -8.0%）、美元走强（DXY +4.6%），处于放缓/通缩惊魂象限（防御股-11.2%、周期股-11.7%皆深跌，VIX 24->32）。电网／电气化尚未成为市场主线，故此为普通的利率敏感防御周期股走弱。","drivers_zh":["利率主导下杀(TLT -8.0%)","美联储加息","通缩惊魂象限","主线未现"]},"2022-10-14":{"title":"Grid super-cycle re-rates into a semis-led melt-up","body":"A +249% multi-year run as AI-datacenter load surge, electrification and aging-grid replacement turned transmission and transformer suppliers into a structural-growth story through 2023-24. It rode a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +208.7%, growth>value +56.6, VIX collapsing 32->15) and a weaker dollar (DXY -5.2%), with extremely narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight a striking -28.1%) — power-grid capex went from defensive to one of the market's best secular themes.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +209%)","grid capex","very narrow breadth (-28.1%)","electrification"],"title_zh":"电网超级周期在半导体领涨暴涨中重估","body_zh":"多年期上涨249%，AI数据中心负荷激增、电气化与老化电网更换使输配电与变压器供应商在2023–24年成为结构性成长故事。它搭乘金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +208.7%、成长跑赢价值+56.6、VIX由32崩至15）与美元走弱（DXY -5.2%），市场广度极窄、巨头领涨（等权大幅跑输市值权达-28.1%）——电网资本开支从防御性变为市场最佳长期主线之一。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +209%)","电网资本开支","极窄广度(-28.1%)","电气化"]},"2025-01-24":{"title":"DeepSeek + tariff risk-off de-rate","body":"A -29% correction triggered by DeepSeek's late-January efficiency shock — which questioned AI power demand — and deepened by the April tariff crash. The macro was a violent risk-off: VIX tripled 15->45, semis cratered (SMH -30.9%), defensives (-3.4%) beat cyclicals (-16.3%) and yields fell (TLT +7.6%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Grid names sold off on demand-doubt even though their order books reflected multi-year backlogs; breadth broadened (+3.3%) as the mega-cap AI tape unwound.","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15->45)","DeepSeek shock","demand doubt","tariff crash"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek＋关税避险压估值","body_zh":"回调29%，由DeepSeek 1月底效率冲击（质疑AI电力需求）触发，并在4月关税崩盘中加深。宏观是剧烈避险：VIX翻三倍由15升至45、半导体崩跌（半导体SMH -30.9%）、防御股（-3.4%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%）、收益率下行（TLT +7.6%），处于放缓/通缩惊魂象限。尽管订单簿反映多年积压，电网股仍因需求疑虑而下跌；随着巨头领涨的AI行情瓦解，广度扩散（+3.3%）。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15->45)","DeepSeek冲击","需求疑虑","关税崩盘"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Tariff-low recovery in a semis-led risk-on tape","body":"A +115% recovery off the April-2025 tariff low as AI-load forecasts and grid-interconnection backlogs reasserted the structural bid. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +103.9%, growth>value +30.0, VIX collapsing 45->17) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -16.0%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%); utility capex guidance and transformer-supply tightness kept the bid firm through October 2025.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +104%)","capex re-accel","narrow breadth (-16.0%)","transformer tightness"],"title_zh":"关税低点反弹于半导体领涨的风险偏好行情","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点上涨115%，AI负荷预测与电网并网积压重新确立结构性买盘。该篮子放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +103.9%、成长跑赢价值+30.0、VIX由45崩至17），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-16.0%）、美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）；公用事业资本开支指引与变压器供应紧张使买盘稳固至2025年10月。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +104%)","资本开支再加速","窄广度(-16.0%)","变压器紧缺"]},"2025-10-29":{"title":"Autumn AI-capex digestion dip","body":"A -17% pullback as the broad AI-capex complex digested its run into late 2025 — a mild slowdown/deflation-scare consolidation (VIX flat 17->18, defensives +1.9% vs cyclicals +0.3%, breadth broadening +4.2%) rather than a true risk-off. A garden-variety pause in an extended group as flows rotated, not a thesis break.","drivers":["mild risk-off consolidation","capex digestion","breadth broadening (+4.2%)","rotation"],"title_zh":"秋季AI资本开支消化回调","body_zh":"回调17%，整个AI资本开支板块在2025年底消化涨幅——这是温和的放缓/通缩惊魂盘整（VIX走平17->18、防御股+1.9%对周期股+0.3%、广度扩散+4.2%），而非真正的避险。这是涨幅过大组别在资金轮动时的常规歇脚，而非逻辑破裂。","drivers_zh":["温和避险盘整","资本开支消化","广度扩散(+4.2%)","板块轮动"]},"2025-12-17":{"title":"Grinds back as reflation rotation builds","body":"A +36% recovery into May 2026 in a reflation/growth-up quad (oil ripping +70.0%, cyclicals +13.4% vs defensives +3.7%, SMH +62.6%, VIX calm 18->17) that nonetheless leaves the group screening as bottoming with low positioning after the choppy 2025-26 range. House view: the multi-year grid/transmission-capex backlog is durable; a fresh trending breakout is still unconfirmed.","drivers":["reflation/growth-up rotation","grind-up","backlog durability","low positioning"],"title_zh":"再通胀轮动中缓步回升，目前筑底","body_zh":"至2026年5月回升36%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限（油价大涨+70.0%、周期股+13.4%对防御股+3.7%、半导体SMH +62.6%、VIX平静18->17），但经2025–26年震荡区间后该组别仍显示为筑底、仓位偏低。本观点：多年期电网／输配电资本开支积压持久；新的趋势突破仍未确认。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上轮动","缓步回升","积压持久","低仓位"]}}},"b-energy_complex":{"now":"Broad US oil & gas — integrateds, E&P, services and midstream that track crude (XLE). The basket round-tripped the 2022 Russia spike and 2025 tariff crash, spiked again on the 2026 Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz oil shock, then rolled over as the mid-June 2026 ceasefire unwound the war premium. The current tape is favorable on paper — a reflation/growth-up quad with oil +19.2% and copper-gold +17.6, Energy a top sector leader (+21.5%) — but a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a direct headwind for the commodity complex.","now_zh":"广义美国油气——综合油企、勘探开采、油服与中游，跟随原油走势(XLE)。该篮子经历了2022年俄乌飙升与2025年关税崩盘的往返，又在2026年伊朗／霍尔木兹海峡石油冲击中再度飙升，随后随2026年6月中停火、战争溢价消退而见顶回落。当前行情账面上有利——再通胀/增长向上象限、油价+19.2%、铜金比+17.6，能源为领涨板块之一（+21.5%）——但美元走强（DXY +3.4%）对大宗商品板块构成直接逆风。","legs":{"2020-10-28":{"title":"Reflation super-spike, Energy leads the bear","body":"A +331% rocket from the 2020 COVID trough through June 2022, as reopening demand collided with OPEC+ discipline and Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent crude soaring (oil +219.4%). This was a textbook reflation/growth-up quad — the 10Y surged (TLT -26.5%), the dollar strengthened (DXY +9.5%), cyclicals (+70.6%) crushed defensives (+26.6%) and breadth broadened (equal-weight beat cap-weight +13.8%) — and Energy (+255.8%) was the best-performing sector even as the rest of the market fell into a rate-driven bear.","drivers":["reflation/growth-up quad","Russia-Ukraine oil shock (+219%)","broadening (+13.8%)","OPEC+"],"title_zh":"再通胀超级飙升，能源领涨于熊市","body_zh":"自2020年疫情谷底至2022年6月火箭式上涨331%，复工需求碰上OPEC+限产，叠加2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰将原油推升（油价+219.4%）。这是教科书式的再通胀/增长向上象限——10年期收益率飙升（TLT -26.5%）、美元走强（DXY +9.5%）、周期股（+70.6%）碾压防御股（+26.6%）、广度扩散（等权跑赢市值权+13.8%）——在大盘陷入利率驱动的熊市之际，能源（+255.8%）是表现最佳的板块。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上象限","俄乌石油冲击(+219%)","广度扩散(+13.8%)","OPEC+"]},"2022-06-07":{"title":"Recession-fear crude pullback","body":"A -27% drop as demand-destruction and recession fear from aggressive Fed hiking pulled crude sharply off its June 2022 peak (oil -19.8%, copper-gold -19.9). The quad flipped to slowdown/deflation-scare with a surging dollar (DXY +6.1%), defensives (-3.6%) beating cyclicals (-14.0%) and Energy the worst sector (-25.9%) — the fastest leg of the broad commodity de-rate as growth expectations rolled over.","drivers":["slowdown/deflation-scare quad","demand destruction","Fed hiking, dollar +6.1%","recession fear"],"title_zh":"衰退担忧引发原油回调","body_zh":"下跌27%，美联储激进加息带来的需求毁灭与衰退担忧使原油从2022年6月峰值急挫（油价-19.8%、铜金比-19.9）。象限翻转为放缓/通缩惊魂，美元飙升（DXY +6.1%）、防御股（-3.6%）跑赢周期股（-14.0%）、能源为最差板块（-25.9%）——在增长预期回落之际，这是广义大宗商品估值下杀中最快的一段。","drivers_zh":["放缓/通缩惊魂象限","需求毁灭","美联储加息、美元+6.1%","衰退担忧"]},"2022-07-14":{"title":"Range-bound grind under a semis-led melt-up","body":"A +78% grind into late November 2024 as crude chopped in a wide range while disciplined buybacks, dividends and strong free cash flow rewarded integrateds and E&P. Notably this ran against the regime tide: the macro was a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +137.6%, growth>value +35.1, oil actually -25.6%) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -18.3%) where defensives/cyclicals favored tech — so Energy's slow, fundamentals-driven climb on capital discipline was a value-factor outlier, not a crude-price moonshot.","drivers":["counter-trend vs semis-led risk-on","capital discipline","narrow breadth (-18.3%)","range-bound crude"],"title_zh":"半导体领涨暴涨下的区间缓步上涨","body_zh":"至2024年11月底缓步上涨78%，原油宽幅震荡，而有纪律的回购、分红与强劲自由现金流回报综合油企与勘探开采商。值得注意的是这逆势而行：宏观为金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +137.6%、成长跑赢价值+35.1、油价实际-25.6%），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-18.3%），偏向科技——因此能源凭资本纪律缓慢的基本面驱动攀升是价值因子的异类，而非油价暴涨。","drivers_zh":["逆半导体领涨风险偏好","资本纪律","窄广度(-18.3%)","原油区间"]},"2024-11-22":{"title":"Tariff-crash risk-off + oversupply de-rate","body":"A -23% slide into the early-April 2025 tariff crash as global-growth fear and OPEC+ supply-add plans pressured crude (oil -16.4%). This was a slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off — VIX exploded 15->52, defensives (-7.1%) beat cyclicals (-18.7%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.2%) couldn't offset recession-demand worries. Energy underperformed badly (-20.1%) as a softening oil balance layered onto the broad de-risk.","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15->52)","tariff crash","OPEC+ supply","growth fear"],"title_zh":"关税崩盘避险＋供给过剩压估值","body_zh":"下跌23%至2025年4月初关税崩盘，全球增长担忧与OPEC+增产计划压制原油（油价-16.4%）。这是放缓/通缩惊魂的避险——VIX由15飙至52、防御股（-7.1%）跑赢周期股（-18.7%），即便美元走弱（DXY -4.2%）也无法抵消衰退需求担忧。在趋松的油市平衡叠加广泛去风险之际，能源大幅跑输（-20.1%）。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15->52)","关税崩盘","OPEC+增产","增长担忧"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Iran/Hormuz reflation oil-shock spike","body":"A +81% recovery off the tariff low, powered by the 2026 Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz crisis that spiked crude (oil +80.9%) and pushed CPI to 4.2% (house view). The backdrop turned to a reflation/growth-up quad with a broad semis-led risk-on tape underneath (SMH +203.2%, VIX collapsing 52->18) and a weaker dollar (DXY -3.6%) aiding the commodity bid; the war premium peaked into mid-May 2026 before the ceasefire, with Energy (+65.5%) a top leader on the supply-disruption bid.","drivers":["reflation oil shock (oil +80.9%)","Iran/Hormuz crisis","risk-on recovery (VIX 52->18)","weaker dollar tailwind"],"title_zh":"伊朗／霍尔木兹再通胀石油冲击飙升","body_zh":"自关税低点反弹81%，由2026年伊朗／霍尔木兹海峡危机驱动，将原油推升（油价+80.9%）、CPI升至4.2%（本观点）。背景转为再通胀/增长向上象限，底下是广泛的半导体领涨风险偏好行情（半导体SMH +203.2%、VIX由52崩至18），美元走弱（DXY -3.6%）助推大宗商品买盘；战争溢价于2026年5月中、停火前见顶，供应中断买盘下能源（+65.5%）为领涨之一。","drivers_zh":["再通胀石油冲击(油价+80.9%)","伊朗／霍尔木兹危机","风险偏好修复(VIX 52->18)","美元走弱顺风"]}}},"b-uranium_miners":{"now":"Uranium miners + fuel cycle (Cameco, Sprott physical) — the high-beta, supply-driven fuel side of the nuclear revival, geared to uranium spot price and reactor restarts. After a ~292% run into October 2025 the group sold off hard; it now sits deeply washed out in bottoming territory amid a 2026 spot-price consolidation. The tape is a broadening reflation/growth-up quad (oil +19.2%, copper-gold +17.6, equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%) which favors commodity/cyclical themes, but a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a headwind for the materials complex.","now_zh":"铀矿商＋燃料循环（Cameco、Sprott实物）——核电复兴中高弹性、供给驱动的燃料侧，紧贴铀现货价格与反应堆重启。在2025年10月飙升约292%后大幅下跌；目前在2026年现货价盘整中深度超跌、处于筑底区间。行情为广度扩散的再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+19.2%、铜金比+17.6、等权跑赢市值权+2.9%），有利于大宗商品/周期主题，但美元走强（DXY +3.4%）对材料板块构成逆风。","legs":{"2021-11-08":{"title":"Sprott-squeeze froth unwinds in risk-off","body":"A -45% drop into late January 2022 as the 2021 Sprott Physical Trust-driven spot squeeze faded and the broad risk-off into Fed hiking hit speculative miners. The macro was a stagflation-ish flight-to-safety (VIX 17->30, defensives +0.7% vs cyclicals -5.1%, dollar +3.4%) and as a high-beta name the group overshot the broad tape (SMH -14.5%). Pure spot/supply dynamics, ahead of the AI-power demand era.","drivers":["risk-off flight-to-safety","Sprott squeeze fade","high-beta overshoot","Fed hiking"],"title_zh":"Sprott逼空泡沫在避险中消退","body_zh":"下跌45%至2022年1月底，2021年由Sprott实物信托驱动的现货逼空消退，叠加美联储加息前的广泛避险打击投机性矿商。宏观为类滞胀避险（VIX 17->30、防御股+0.7%对周期股-5.1%、美元+3.4%），作为高贝塔标的它超调于大盘（半导体SMH -14.5%）。纯现货／供给动态，早于AI电力需求时代。","drivers_zh":["避险","Sprott逼空消退","高贝塔超调","美联储加息"]},"2022-01-27":{"title":"Russia supply-fear spot bid amid stagflation","body":"A +66% spike as Russia's invasion of Ukraine raised fears over Russian enrichment and conversion supply, lifting uranium spot and the high-beta miners. This was a stagflation-ish reflation episode — oil +20.4%, defensives (+9.7%) and cyclicals (+5.5%) both green, yields surging (TLT -13.5%) and a firmer dollar (DXY +2.7%) — a geopolitics-on-supply leg that bucked the broad de-risk (SMH -4.3%), characteristic of this group.","drivers":["stagflation-ish reflation","Russia supply fear","rate-regime move (TLT -13.5%)","geopolitics"],"title_zh":"类滞胀中俄罗斯供应担忧推升现货","body_zh":"飙升66%，俄罗斯入侵乌克兰引发对俄铀浓缩与转化供应的担忧，推高铀现货与高弹性矿商。这是类滞胀的再通胀片段——油价+20.4%、防御股（+9.7%）与周期股（+5.5%）皆涨、收益率飙升（TLT -13.5%）、美元走强（DXY +2.7%）——这是地缘政治冲击供给的一段，逆大盘去风险而行（半导体SMH -4.3%），为该组别的典型特征。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀再通胀","俄罗斯供应担忧","利率主导(TLT -13.5%)","地缘政治"]},"2022-04-13":{"title":"Hawkish-Fed risk-off flush","body":"A -44% flush as peak-hawkish Fed pricing and a broad commodity/risk-asset de-rate hit the volatile miners. A slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off (VIX 22->32, defensives -6.6% beating cyclicals -10.3%, surging dollar DXY +5.0%) in which high-beta uranium gave back its geopolitical spike on macro de-risking, overshooting the broad selloff (SMH -10.2%).","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 22->32)","Fed hiking, dollar +5.0%","high-beta unwind","deflation-scare quad"],"title_zh":"鹰派美联储避险急挫","body_zh":"急挫44%，美联储鹰派定价见顶与广义大宗商品／风险资产估值下杀打击波动剧烈的矿商。这是放缓/通缩惊魂的避险（VIX 22->32、防御股-6.6%跑赢周期股-10.3%、美元飙升DXY +5.0%），高弹性铀股在宏观去风险下回吐地缘政治飙升，超调于大盘抛售（半导体SMH -10.2%）。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 22->32)","美联储加息、美元+5.0%","高贝塔平仓","通缩惊魂象限"]},"2022-05-12":{"title":"Supply-deficit thesis re-bids as vol eases","body":"A +52% bounce as the structural supply-deficit story — underinvested mines versus reactor restarts and life-extensions — drew buyers back. The tape steadied into a goldilocks/growth-up quad (VIX easing 32->23, cyclicals +4.5% vs defensives +3.9%, high-beta minus low-vol +7.1) even as oil fell (-18.2%) and the dollar firmed (DXY +4.0%); spot uranium firmed on utility contracting and term-market activity, an idiosyncratic supply story riding a calmer risk backdrop.","drivers":["risk-on stabilization","supply deficit","utility contracting","spot firming"],"title_zh":"波动缓和下供给短缺逻辑重获买盘","body_zh":"反弹52%，结构性供给短缺故事——投资不足的矿山对比反应堆重启与延寿——吸引买盘回归。行情企稳为金发女郎/增长向上象限（VIX由32回落至23、周期股+4.5%对防御股+3.9%、高贝塔减低波动+7.1），即便油价下跌（-18.2%）、美元走强（DXY +4.0%）；公用事业签约与长协市场活跃使铀现货走强，这是在更平静风险背景下的个股供给故事。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好企稳","供给短缺","公用事业签约","现货走强"]},"2022-09-09":{"title":"Recession-demand de-rate vs a tech-led tape","body":"A -41% drawdown into May 2023 as global recession fear weighed on the cyclical miners. Notably the broad tape was a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on recovery (SMH +38.1%, growth>value +10.4, VIX falling 23->17, weaker dollar DXY -4.4%) with narrow breadth (-6.7%) — but uranium was a value/commodity laggard that diverged lower as spot consolidated, despite the durable long-term deficit narrative.","drivers":["value laggard vs tech-led risk-on","recession fear","narrow breadth (-6.7%)","spot consolidation"],"title_zh":"科技领涨行情下的衰退需求下杀","body_zh":"回撤41%至2023年5月，全球衰退担忧拖累周期性矿商。值得注意的是大盘为金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好修复（半导体SMH +38.1%、成长跑赢价值+10.4、VIX由23降至17、美元走弱DXY -4.4%），广度狭窄（-6.7%）——但铀作为价值/大宗落后者背离下行，现货盘整，尽管长期短缺叙事持久。","drivers_zh":["价值落后于科技领涨风险偏好","衰退担忧","窄广度(-6.7%)","现货盘整"]},"2023-05-30":{"title":"Spot breakout to $100 in a reflation risk-on tape","body":"A +164% surge into May 2024 as uranium spot broke out toward $100/lb on supply tightness, Kazatomprom production warnings, Sprott physical buying and the dawning AI-power/reactor-restart narrative. It rode a semis-led, reflation/growth-up risk-on tape (SMH +59.7%, growth>value +11.7, VIX collapsing 17->12, oil +14.9, copper-gold +14.8) with narrow breadth (-6.8%) and yields rising (TLT -7.4%) — the high-beta miners amplified the up-regime into the group's biggest clean trend in years.","drivers":["reflation/risk-on melt-up","spot to $100","supply tightness","AI-power narrative"],"title_zh":"再通胀风险偏好行情中现货突破奔向100美元","body_zh":"至2024年5月飙升164%，铀现货因供应紧张、Kazatomprom减产预警、Sprott实物买入与初现的AI电力／反应堆重启叙事而突破奔向每磅100美元。它搭乘半导体领涨、再通胀/增长向上的风险偏好行情（半导体SMH +59.7%、成长跑赢价值+11.7、VIX由17崩至12、油价+14.9、铜金比+14.8），广度狭窄（-6.8%）、收益率上行（TLT -7.4%）——高弹性矿商放大上行象限，交出多年来最干净的趋势。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/风险偏好暴涨","现货奔向100美元","供应紧张","AI电力叙事"]},"2024-05-20":{"title":"Spot rolls over into the Aug-2024 vol flush","body":"A -38% drop into September 2024 as uranium spot retreated from the $100 high on thin-volume term-market softness, capped by the August 2024 volatility scare. The macro turned slowdown/deflation-scare with VIX spiking 12->22, yields falling (TLT +10.7%) and defensives (+6.5%) beating cyclicals (-0.9%); the high-beta miners overshot the spot pullback and the broad de-risk.","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 12->22)","spot rollover","high-beta overshoot","deflation-scare quad"],"title_zh":"现货回落进入2024年8月波动急挫","body_zh":"下跌38%至2024年9月，铀现货因长协市场成交清淡转弱从100美元高位回落，并被2024年8月波动惊魂封顶。宏观转为放缓/通缩惊魂，VIX由12飙至22、收益率下行（TLT +10.7%）、防御股（+6.5%）跑赢周期股（-0.9%）；高弹性矿商超调于现货回调与大盘去风险。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 12->22)","现货回落","高贝塔超调","通缩惊魂象限"]},"2024-09-06":{"title":"Restart headlines re-ignite the bid in reflation","body":"A +82% rocket as datacenter-nuclear deals (Three Mile Island restart) and Fed cuts re-ignited the nuclear-fuel bid. The backdrop was a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +13.7% vs defensives +0.4%, oil +5.3) with yields surging (TLT -8.6%) and a strong dollar (DXY +6.2%); the high-beta miners were pulled up with the reactor-restart wave and the cyclical bid into late November 2024.","drivers":["reflation/growth-up quad","restart deals","rate-regime move (TLT -8.6%)","fuel-demand bid"],"title_zh":"再通胀中重启新闻重燃买盘","body_zh":"火箭式上涨82%，数据中心核电协议（三哩岛重启）与美联储降息重燃核燃料买盘。背景为再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+13.7%对防御股+0.4%、油价+5.3），收益率飙升（TLT -8.6%）、美元走强（DXY +6.2%）；高弹性矿商随反应堆重启浪潮与周期买盘被推升至2024年11月底。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上象限","重启协议","利率主导(TLT -8.6%)","燃料需求买盘"]},"2024-11-22":{"title":"DeepSeek + tariff deep risk-off de-rate","body":"A -49% drawdown into the April-2025 tariff low, hit first by DeepSeek's late-January AI-power-demand shock and then the tariff crash. This was a violent slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off — VIX exploded 15->52, defensives (-7.1%) beat cyclicals (-18.7%), semis cratered (SMH -26.1%) — in which the high-beta miners led the AI-nuclear complex lower on demand-doubt and broad de-risk, even as a weaker dollar (DXY -4.2%) offered no support.","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15->52)","DeepSeek shock","high-beta unwind","tariff crash"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek＋关税深度避险下杀","body_zh":"回撤49%至2025年4月关税低点，先受DeepSeek 1月底AI电力需求冲击，再遭关税崩盘。这是剧烈的放缓/通缩惊魂避险——VIX由15飙至52、防御股（-7.1%）跑赢周期股（-18.7%）、半导体崩跌（半导体SMH -26.1%）——高弹性矿商在需求疑虑与广泛去风险下领跌整个AI核电板块，即便美元走弱（DXY -4.2%）也未能提供支撑。","drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15->52)","DeepSeek冲击","高贝塔平仓","关税崩盘"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Tariff-low to spot moonshot in a semis-led melt-up","body":"A +292% surge off the April-2025 tariff low as uranium spot broke higher on reactor restarts, government nuclear support and supply-deficit buying, while the AI-baseload story re-accelerated. As the highest-beta fuel proxy it amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89.9%, growth>value +22.7, VIX collapsing 52->21) with narrow breadth (-10.2%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%) aiding the commodity bid — the miners delivered the group's largest run into October 2025.","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +90%)","spot breakout","narrow breadth (-10.2%)","supply deficit"],"title_zh":"关税低点至现货暴涨于半导体领涨行情","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点飙升292%，铀现货因反应堆重启、政府核能支持与供给短缺买盘而上行，AI基荷故事同步再加速。作为弹性最高的燃料代理，它放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +89.9%、成长跑赢价值+22.7、VIX由52崩至21），广度狭窄（-10.2%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%）助推大宗商品买盘——矿商交出该组别至2025年10月的最大一波涨幅。","drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +90%)","现货突破","窄广度(-10.2%)","供给短缺"]},"2025-10-15":{"title":"Blow-off top, 36% reset as flows rotate","body":"A -36% pullback from the October-2025 spot/equity peak as the most stretched fuel-cycle trade unwound on profit-taking and a spot-price stall. The macro was only a mild slowdown/deflation-scare (VIX 21->23, defensives +0.6% vs cyclicals -2.0%) — not a broad flush — so this was largely an idiosyncratic froth purge in a high-beta group as flows rotated off the AI-fuel trade, not a break of the supply-deficit thesis.","drivers":["mild risk-off rotation","spot stall","high-beta froth purge","profit-taking"],"title_zh":"喷发顶部，资金轮动中回调36%","body_zh":"自2025年10月现货／股价峰值回调36%，最被拉伸的燃料循环交易因获利了结与现货价停滞而平仓。宏观仅为温和的放缓/通缩惊魂（VIX 21->23、防御股+0.6%对周期股-2.0%）——并非广泛急挫——因此这主要是高弹性组别在资金撤离AI燃料交易时的个股泡沫挤出，而非供给短缺逻辑破裂。","drivers_zh":["温和避险轮动","现货停滞","高贝塔泡沫挤出","获利了结"]},"2025-11-21":{"title":"Restart-driven relief bounce in reflation","body":"A +71% rebound into late January 2026 on renewed reactor-restart and utility-contracting headlines that firmed uranium spot. The tape was a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +10.0% vs defensives +1.9%, oil +8.9, VIX easing 23->16) with a weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%) supporting commodities; volatile, headline-sensitive trade characteristic of the high-beta miners as they leveraged the up-regime.","drivers":["reflation/growth-up rebound","restart headlines","weaker dollar tailwind","spot firming"],"title_zh":"再通胀中重启驱动修复反弹","body_zh":"至2026年1月底反弹71%，新一轮反应堆重启与公用事业签约新闻使铀现货走强。行情为再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+10.0%对防御股+1.9%、油价+8.9、VIX由23回落至16），美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）支撑大宗商品；这是高弹性矿商典型的、对新闻敏感的剧烈交易，放大了上行象限。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上反弹","重启新闻","美元走弱顺风","现货走强"]},"2026-01-28":{"title":"Spot consolidates into a deep washout","body":"A -42% slide into mid-June 2026 as uranium spot consolidated and the high-beta miners de-rated, leaving the group deeply washed out in bottoming territory. The macro was a mixed reflation/growth-up quad (oil +42.4, copper-gold +28.6 but a stronger dollar DXY +3.6% and rising VIX 16->22) where the commodity tailwind couldn't hold up the stretched fuel trade. House view: the multi-year supply-deficit and restart thesis is durable, but a confirmed spot-price turn is still pending.","drivers":["stronger dollar headwind (+3.6%)","spot consolidation","high-beta de-rate","washout"],"title_zh":"现货盘整进入深度超跌","body_zh":"下跌42%至2026年6月中，铀现货盘整、高弹性矿商估值下杀，使该组别深度超跌、处于筑底区间。宏观为混合的再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+42.4、铜金比+28.6，但美元走强DXY +3.6%、VIX上行16->22），大宗商品顺风未能托住被拉伸的燃料交易。本观点：多年期供给短缺与重启逻辑持久，但现货价反转的确认仍待出现。","drivers_zh":["美元走强逆风(+3.6%)","现货盘整","高贝塔下杀","超跌"]}}},"b-defense":{"now":"Defense & Aerospace (RTX/LMT/GD/Boeing, ITA proxy) sits in the doghouse despite a world built for it — and the current tape explains the laggard read better than geopolitics does. The melt-up off the April-2025 low has been a narrow, tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +67.9%, growth-led, mega-cap breadth) that pulls flows toward AI beta and away from a steady cyclical-defensive name; a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is an added headwind for the exporting primes. Two hot wars and NATO rearmament should be a tailwind, yet the basket ranks #32 in relative strength, tagged 'Bottoming' near its range floor (pos 9.0). The real tell is policy, not the regime: Trump-era DOGE efficiency cuts (~8%/yr reprioritization) threaten legacy programs (F-35, armored vehicles) the primes lean on. After cresting in January 2026 (+111% off the April-2025 low), defense rolled over -18% and has only limped back — a value-coiled spring waiting on order flow, not a momentum leader the risk-on tape rewards.","now_zh":"国防与航空航天（RTX/LMT/GD/波音，ITA 为代理）所处的世界看似为其量身定做，却深陷冷宫——而当前的市场状态比地缘更能解释其落后表现。自 2025 年 4 月低点的融涨一直是狭窄、由科技/半导体引领的风险偏好（risk-on）regime（半导体 SMH +67.9%、成长引领、大盘股市场广度），把资金拉向 AI 高贝塔、远离稳健的周期防御品种；走强的美元（DXY +3.4%）对出口型主承包商又是逆风。两场热战与北约重整军备本应是顺风，然而该篮子相对强度排名第 32 位，被标记为'筑底'，接近区间底部（pos 9.0）。真正的关键在政策而非 regime：特朗普时代 DOGE 效率削减（每年约 8% 重新排序）威胁到主承包商赖以为生的传统项目（F-35、装甲车）。在 2026 年 1 月见顶后（较 2025 年 4 月低点 +111%），国防下挫 -18% 至今仅勉强回血——一根估值蓄势的弹簧，等待订单流，而非风险偏好行情奖励的动量领头羊。","legs":{"2020-07-09":{"title":"Post-COVID grind into the Ukraine bid, riding a reflation melt-up (+70%)","body":"Defense climbed off the 2020 COVID trough into a broad reflation/growth-up regime (SPY +47.6%, cyclicals +73% vs defensives +35.5%, breadth wide at RSP-SPY +14%) that lifted the whole risk complex even as yields surged (TLT -21.1%). The February 2022 Russian invasion then turned a cyclical recovery into a hard geopolitical re-rating — LMT/RTX bid as Europe woke to a multi-decade rearmament cycle. The leg topped in March 2022 at the invasion's emotional peak, just as the high-beta regime (SPHB-SPLV +67.5%) began to crack.","drivers":["Broad reflation/growth-up melt-up (cyclicals +73%, breadth wide) amplifies the rally","Russia-Ukraine invasion (Feb 2022) ignites a European rearmament re-rate","Multi-decade NATO defense-budget upcycle narrative","Rate-regime: yields surged (TLT -21.1%) but risk-on dominated"],"title_zh":"新冠后缓步走高迎俄乌买盘，搭乘再通胀融涨（+70%）","body_zh":"国防自 2020 年新冠低谷爬升，进入广泛的再通胀/增长上行 regime（SPY +47.6%、周期股 +73% 对防御 +35.5%、市场广度宽 RSP-SPY +14%），即便收益率飙升（TLT -21.1%）也抬升了整个风险资产群。2022 年 2 月俄罗斯入侵把周期复苏变成强烈的地缘重估——随着欧洲意识到数十年重整军备周期，LMT/RTX 获买盘。该腿段于 2022 年 3 月入侵情绪高峰见顶，恰逢高贝塔 regime（SPHB-SPLV +67.5%）开始破裂。","drivers_zh":["广泛再通胀/增长上行融涨（周期股 +73%、广度宽）放大涨幅","俄乌战争爆发（2022 年 2 月）点燃欧洲重整军备重估","数十年北约国防预算上行周期叙事","利率 regime：收益率飙升（TLT -21.1%）但风险偏好主导"]},"2022-03-25":{"title":"Hiking-bear, rate-driven pullback off the war spike (-21%)","body":"Even a war bid couldn't resist the 2022 Fed-hiking bear: a rate-driven slowdown/deflation-scare regime (yields surged, TLT -12.7%; DXY +4.9%; VIX 21->33) compressed every multiple into the June low. Defensives outperformed cyclicals (-10% vs -17.5%) in a flight-to-safety, but defense de-rated with the cyclical-cyclical crowd. The de-rate was pure macro — order books were swelling even as the strong dollar and surging yields hit the primes.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -12.7%) compress all multiples","Risk-off slowdown scare (VIX 21->33), flight-to-safety rotation","Strong dollar (DXY +4.9%) pressures the exporting primes","Profit-taking after the sharp invasion-week spike"],"title_zh":"加息熊市利率驱动从战争尖峰回落（-21%）","body_zh":"即便有战争买盘也难抵 2022 年美联储加息熊市：一个利率驱动的放缓/通缩恐慌 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -12.7%；DXY +4.9%；VIX 21->33）把每个倍数压缩至 6 月低点。避险（risk-off）中防御跑赢周期（-10% 对 -17.5%），但国防随周期股去估值。这是纯宏观去估值——订单簿仍在膨胀，强势美元与飙升收益率却冲击主承包商。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -12.7%）压缩所有倍数","避险放缓恐慌（VIX 21->33）、避险轮动","强势美元（DXY +4.9%）施压出口型主承包商","入侵当周急升后的获利了结"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Summer relief bounce in a tech-led risk-on window (+23%)","body":"Defense rode the broad mid-2022 relief rally as a tech/semis-led risk-on regime took hold (SMH +19.5%, growth>value +8.8, VIX 33->20) on hopes of a Fed pause that never came. A fast, multiple-driven bounce off oversold — defense participated but lagged the high-beta growth that leads these windows, with a strong dollar (DXY +2.8%) still a mild drag.","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on bounce (SMH +19.5%, growth>value), VIX 33->20","Premature 'Fed pivot' hopes lift the whole complex","Strong order backlog as a floor under the group","Dollar (DXY +2.8%) a mild headwind for the primes"],"title_zh":"夏季纾困反弹于科技引领的风险偏好窗口（+23%）","body_zh":"国防搭上 2022 年年中大盘纾困反弹，一个科技/半导体引领的风险偏好 regime（半导体 +19.5%、成长>价值 +8.8、VIX 33->20）因美联储暂停预期（最终未现）而成形。这是从超卖出发、倍数驱动的快速反弹——国防参与但落后于领涨这类窗口的高贝塔成长，强势美元（DXY +2.8%）仍是轻微拖累。","drivers_zh":["科技/半导体引领风险偏好反弹（半导体 +19.5%、成长>价值），VIX 33->20","过早的'美联储转向'预期抬升整个群组","强劲订单积压为板块托底","美元（DXY +2.8%）对主承包商轻微逆风"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole hawkish, rate-driven flush (-19%)","body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole reset killed the summer rally and triggered a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -11.4%; DXY +5.3%; VIX 20->32) into the September-2022 capitulation low. Defense fell with everything — semis -24%, cyclicals -15.3% — a macro de-risk rather than a defense-specific problem, with the dollar spike adding pressure on the exporting primes.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -11.4%) on hawkish Jackson Hole","Broad risk-off capitulation (VIX 20->32, semis -24%) into the autumn low","Dollar surge (DXY +5.3%) pressuring the multinational primes","Hawkish terminal-rate repricing"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派、利率驱动冲刷（-19%）","body_zh":"鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置终结夏季反弹，触发利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -11.4%；DXY +5.3%；VIX 20->32），跌至 2022 年 9 月投降低点。国防随一切下跌——半导体 -24%、周期股 -15.3%——这是宏观去风险而非国防特有问题，美元飙升对出口型主承包商再添压力。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -11.4%），杰克逊霍尔鹰派","广泛避险投降（VIX 20->32、半导体 -24%）至秋季低点","美元飙升（DXY +5.3%）施压跨国主承包商","鹰派终端利率重新定价"]},"2022-09-30":{"title":"The long war-and-budget bull inside a goldilocks AI melt-up (+150%)","body":"From the autumn-2022 low defense ran two-plus years — its best stretch of the cycle — and the regime amplified it: a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (SMH +189.7%, growth>value +48.4, VIX 32->15, weaker dollar -3.6%) lifted the whole risk complex. The tape was narrow and mega-cap-led (RSP-SPY -25.9%), so defense leaned on its own fuel — Ukraine resupply, the Oct-2023 Mideast escalation, surging NATO budgets — to keep pace into a January-2025 top. War demand met record spending met a risk-on backdrop.","drivers":["Goldilocks AI melt-up regime (SMH +189.7%, growth>value, VIX 32->15) lifts risk","Sustained Russia-Ukraine resupply and replenishment orders","Oct-2023 Mideast war adds a second conflict bid","NATO members ratcheting toward and above 2% of GDP; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -25.9%)"],"title_zh":"漫长战争与预算牛市，置于 goldilocks AI 融涨之中（+150%）","body_zh":"从 2022 年秋季低点起国防连涨两年多——本周期最强一段——而 regime 放大了它：一个 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀融涨（半导体 +189.7%、成长>价值 +48.4、VIX 32->15、美元走弱 -3.6%）抬升整个风险资产群。市场狭窄、大盘股引领（RSP-SPY -25.9%），故国防靠自身燃料——乌克兰补给、2023 年 10 月中东升级、激增的北约预算——保持步调至 2025 年 1 月高点。战争需求遇上创纪录开支遇上风险偏好背景。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI 融涨 regime（半导体 +189.7%、成长>价值、VIX 32->15）抬升风险","持续的俄乌补给与补充订单","2023 年 10 月中东战争增添第二处冲突买盘","北约成员国预算迈向并超过 GDP 2%；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -25.9%）"]},"2025-01-21":{"title":"Trump-trade unwind & DOGE-cut fears into a risk-off flush (-15%)","body":"Policy flipped the script just as the regime turned violently risk-off: a slowdown/deflation-scare flush (VIX 15->45, SMH -31.1%, SPHB-SPLV -25.4%) hit high-beta hardest, and the DeepSeek AI scare plus April-tariff fears compounded it. On top of that came defense-specific damage — talk of halving spending, ~8%/yr DOGE reprioritization, threats to legacy programs (F-35, armored vehicles) — that hit LMT/RTX even as defensives outperformed (-3.1% vs cyclicals -16.5%). The 'Trump = more defense' assumption broke into a falling tape.","drivers":["Risk-off flush regime (VIX 15->45, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -25.4%) leads lower","DOGE Pentagon-efficiency drive targets ~8%/yr cuts","Threats to legacy programs the primes depend on","DeepSeek shock + broad late-Jan de-risk; defensives led (-3.1% vs -16.5%)"],"title_zh":"特朗普交易平仓与 DOGE 削减恐慌，置于避险冲刷（-15%）","body_zh":"政策扭转剧本，恰逢 regime 剧烈转向避险：一次放缓/通缩恐慌冲刷（VIX 15->45、半导体 -31.1%、SPHB-SPLV -25.4%）对高贝塔打击最重，DeepSeek AI 恐慌加 4 月关税担忧雪上加霜。在此之上是国防特有的损伤——开支减半之议、每年约 8% DOGE 重新排序、对传统项目（F-35、装甲车）的威胁——冲击 LMT/RTX，即便防御跑赢（-3.1% 对周期 -16.5%）。'特朗普=更多国防'的假设在下跌行情中破裂。","drivers_zh":["避险冲刷 regime（VIX 15->45、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -25.4%）领跌","DOGE 五角大楼效率行动瞄准每年约 8% 削减","威胁主承包商赖以为生的传统项目","DeepSeek 冲击+1 月底普遍去风险；防御领先（-3.1% 对 -16.5%）"]},"2025-04-04":{"title":"Recovery off the tariff-crash low in a high-beta risk-on rip (+111%)","body":"Defense bottomed with the whole market at the April-8 reciprocal-tariff crash and then staged its sharpest run of the cycle, amplified by an explosive high-beta risk-on regime (VIX 45->16, SMH +122.1%, SPHB-SPLV +74.9%, weaker dollar -3.5%). A re-escalating geopolitical backdrop, allied rearmament and a re-think of the cut narrative drove it +111% into a January-2026 peak — the basket's most explosive leg, where a snap-back from deeply oversold met a market begging for beta.","drivers":["Explosive high-beta risk-on regime (VIX 45->16, SPHB-SPLV +74.9%, SMH +122.1%) amplifies the snap-back","Snap-back off the April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash low","Allied rearmament and Ukraine/Mideast escalation re-bid","Weaker dollar (DXY -3.5%); reassessment of worst-case budget cuts"],"title_zh":"从关税崩盘低点回升，置于高贝塔风险偏好暴涨（+111%）","body_zh":"国防随整个市场在 4 月 8 日对等关税崩盘触底，随后上演本周期最陡一段，被爆发性的高贝塔风险偏好 regime（VIX 45->16、半导体 +122.1%、SPHB-SPLV +74.9%、美元走弱 -3.5%）放大。地缘背景再升级、盟友重整军备、对削减叙事的重新思考，推升 +111% 至 2026 年 1 月高点——该篮子最具爆发力的腿，深度超卖的弹回遇上一个渴求贝塔的市场。","drivers_zh":["爆发性高贝塔风险偏好 regime（VIX 45->16、SPHB-SPLV +74.9%、半导体 +122.1%）放大弹回","从 2025 年 4 月对等关税崩盘低点弹回","盟友重整军备与乌克兰/中东升级再买入","美元走弱（DXY -3.5%）；对最坏情形预算削减的重新评估"]},"2026-01-16":{"title":"Top rolls over on budget reality in a stagflation-ish tape (-18%)","body":"The January-2026 high faded as budget reality reasserted itself into a stagflation-ish regime (VIX 16->31, oil +73.1% on the Hormuz shock, energy the lone leader +30.8%). Risk-off but shallow (SPY -8.4%), with the dollar firming (DXY +1.1%) — a headwind for exporters. The headline DOGE reprioritization plus rotation out of the leg's parabolic run gave back -18% into late March, setting up the current bottoming, lagging posture.","drivers":["Stagflation-ish regime (VIX 16->31, oil +73.1% Hormuz shock) caps risk","Budget-cut and program-rationalization reality re-priced","Firming dollar (DXY +1.1%) headwind for exporters","Rotation/profit-taking after a parabolic +111% leg"],"title_zh":"见顶后因预算现实回落，置于类滞胀行情（-18%）","body_zh":"随预算现实重新主导，2026 年 1 月高点回落，进入类滞胀 regime（VIX 16->31、油价 +73.1% 因霍尔木兹冲击、能源是唯一领头 +30.8%）。避险但浅（SPY -8.4%），美元转强（DXY +1.1%）——对出口商逆风。DOGE 重新排序加上从抛物线行情中的轮动，下挫 -18% 至 3 月底，奠定当前筑底、落后姿态。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀 regime（VIX 16->31、油价 +73.1% 霍尔木兹冲击）压制风险","预算削减与项目合理化现实重新定价","美元转强（DXY +1.1%）对出口商构成逆风","抛物线 +111% 腿段后的轮动/获利了结"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Tentative bounce, but lagging the narrow risk-on tape (+16%)","body":"A shallow recovery off the March low into a renewed tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +65.5%, growth>value +10.3, VIX 31->16) — but defense lacked the relative-strength leadership to confirm a new uptrend and still ranks #32, the basket's chronic problem in a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP-SPY -8.8%). The June-2026 Mideast flare and ceasefire kept defense demand topical, but in a market rewarding AI beta the group needs order flow, not headlines, to re-rate.","drivers":["Narrow tech/semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +65.5%, RSP-SPY -8.8%) leaves defense behind","Oversold bounce off the March-2026 low","June-2026 Iran/Hormuz flare keeps defense demand topical","Awaiting order-book confirmation; RS still lagging at #32"],"title_zh":"试探性反弹，却落后于狭窄的风险偏好行情（+16%）","body_zh":"从 3 月低点出发的浅幅回升，进入重燃的科技/半导体引领风险偏好 regime（半导体 +65.5%、成长>价值 +10.3、VIX 31->16）——但国防缺乏相对强度领导力确认新上升趋势，仍排第 32 位，这是它在狭窄、大盘股引领行情（RSP-SPY -8.8%）中的痼疾。2026 年 6 月中东突发与停火让国防需求保持热度，但在奖励 AI 贝塔的市场里，板块重估需要订单流而非头条。","drivers_zh":["狭窄科技/半导体引领风险偏好行情（半导体 +65.5%、RSP-SPY -8.8%）把国防甩在身后","从 2026 年 3 月低点超卖反弹","2026 年 6 月伊朗/霍尔木兹突发使国防需求保持热度","等待订单簿确认；相对强度仍落后于第 32 位"]}}},"b-reshoring":{"now":"Reshoring & Industrial Capex (XLI proxy) is the policy-tailwind trade with the receipts, and the current regime suits it: a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, equal-weight beating cap-weight by +2.9%, oil +19.2%) favors capex-cyclicals over pure AI beta. CHIPS/IRA/IIJA drove a real factory-construction boom — manufacturing construction spend roughly tripled from ~$80B/yr (2019) to ~$224B/yr by late 2025, $630B+ across 140 semiconductor projects. The 2024 Trump election layered an explicit reshoring/tariff lever on top. The basket is 'Trending', mid-pack at RS-rank #16 (pos 60.4), up +89% since the April-2025 low — a durable secondary leader, though a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a mild headwind for its industrial multinationals. Not a parabolic momentum name like the chip-equipment complex, but a broadening tape is exactly its kind of regime.","now_zh":"制造业回流与工业资本开支（XLI 为代理）是有实据支撑的政策顺风交易，当前 regime 也对它有利：一个广度扩张的再通胀/增长上行行情（周期股 +11.2% 对防御 +6.9%、等权跑赢市值权重 +2.9%、油价 +19.2%）偏好资本开支周期股而非纯 AI 高贝塔。CHIPS/IRA/IIJA 驱动了真实的工厂建设热潮——制造业建设开支从 2019 年约 800 亿美元/年大致翻三倍至 2025 年底约 2240 亿美元/年，140 个半导体项目逾 6300 亿美元。2024 年特朗普当选叠加了明确的回流/关税杠杆。该篮子'趋势中'，相对强度排名居中（第 16 位，pos 60.4），自 2025 年 4 月低点 +89%——一个耐久的次级领头羊，尽管走强的美元（DXY +3.4%）对其工业跨国企业是轻微逆风。它不像芯片设备群那样是抛物线动量品种，但市场广度（breadth）扩张恰是它的 regime。","legs":{"2021-11-16":{"title":"Hiking-bear, rate-and-dollar de-rate (-25%)","body":"Industrials de-rated through H1 2022 in a stagflation-ish regime — yields surged (TLT -19.4%), the dollar ripped (DXY +13.2%, a brutal headwind for industrial multinationals) and VIX ran 16->26 — as the Fed-hiking bear and China's COVID lockdowns crushed cyclical sentiment. Defensives held (+1.4%) while cyclicals fell -15.7% in a flight-to-safety. The reshoring thesis was nascent (CHIPS Act passed Aug 2022), so the group traded as plain rate-sensitive cyclicals into the June low.","drivers":["Rate-regime + dollar shock (TLT -19.4%, DXY +13.2%) compress cyclical multiples","Stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 16->26), flight-to-safety","China COVID lockdowns disrupt supply chains","Reshoring policy not yet a catalyst (pre-CHIPS Act)"],"title_zh":"加息熊市、利率与美元去估值（-25%）","body_zh":"工业在 2022 年上半年于类滞胀 regime 去估值——收益率飙升（TLT -19.4%）、美元暴涨（DXY +13.2%，对工业跨国企业是残酷逆风）、VIX 16->26——美联储加息熊市和中国新冠封控压垮周期情绪。避险（risk-off）中防御守住（+1.4%），周期股跌 -15.7%。回流主题尚处萌芽（CHIPS 法案 2022 年 8 月通过），故板块作为普通利率敏感周期股交易至 6 月低点。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime+美元冲击（TLT -19.4%、DXY +13.2%）压缩周期股倍数","类滞胀避险（VIX 16->26）、避险","中国新冠封控扰乱供应链","回流政策尚未成为催化剂（CHIPS 法案前）"]},"2022-07-14":{"title":"Summer pause-hope bounce in a reflation risk-on window (+23%)","body":"A broad relief rally off the June low as the regime turned reflation/growth-up risk-on (cyclicals +16.7% vs defensives +7.6%, SMH +16.3%, growth>value, VIX 26->20, dollar easing -1.9%) on premature Fed-pause hopes. Industrials — geared to the cyclical, weaker-dollar trade — participated well; the CHIPS Act passing in August seeded an emerging structural narrative under the cyclical bounce.","drivers":["Reflation/growth-up risk-on bounce (cyclicals +16.7%, VIX 26->20)","Easing dollar (DXY -1.9%) tailwind for industrial multinationals","CHIPS Act passage (Aug 2022) seeds the reshoring thesis","Premature 'Fed pause' positioning"],"title_zh":"夏季暂停预期反弹于再通胀风险偏好窗口（+23%）","body_zh":"从 6 月低点出发的大盘纾困反弹，regime 转向再通胀/增长上行风险偏好（周期股 +16.7% 对防御 +7.6%、半导体 +16.3%、成长>价值、VIX 26->20、美元走弱 -1.9%），因过早的美联储暂停预期。工业——偏向周期、弱美元交易——参与良好；8 月 CHIPS 法案通过在周期反弹之下播下新兴结构性叙事。","drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长上行风险偏好反弹（周期股 +16.7%、VIX 26->20）","美元走弱（DXY -1.9%）对工业跨国企业顺风","CHIPS 法案通过（2022 年 8 月）播下回流主题种子","过早的'美联储暂停'仓位"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole rate-driven flush (-18%)","body":"Powell's hawkish reset triggered a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -12.7%; DXY +7.1%; VIX 20->33) into the autumn-2022 capitulation low. Macro, not fundamental — factory-construction commitments kept building underneath, but the surging dollar and yields hit the industrial multinationals (cyclicals -15.0% vs defensives -10.3%) regardless.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -12.7%) on hawkish Jackson Hole","Broad risk-off capitulation (VIX 20->33) into the autumn low","Dollar strength (DXY +7.1%) pressuring industrial multinationals","Hawkish terminal-rate repricing"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔利率驱动冲刷（-18%）","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派重置触发利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -12.7%；DXY +7.1%；VIX 20->33），跌至 2022 年秋季投降低点。这是宏观而非基本面——工厂建设承诺仍在累积，但飙升的美元与收益率不分青红皂白地冲击工业跨国企业（周期股 -15.0% 对防御 -10.3%）。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -12.7%），杰克逊霍尔鹰派","广泛避险投降（VIX 20->33）至秋季低点","美元走强（DXY +7.1%）施压工业跨国企业","鹰派终端利率重新定价"]},"2022-09-27":{"title":"The reshoring bull inside a goldilocks AI melt-up (+103%)","body":"From the autumn-2022 low industrials more than doubled over two-plus years — the cleanest expression of the reshoring/capex super-cycle, supercharged by a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (SMH +156.4%, growth>value +35.6, VIX 33->14, weaker dollar -6.2%). CHIPS/IRA/IIJA money flowed into shovels-in-the-ground projects; the 2023 AI rally and 2024 Fed cuts lifted risk; the Nov-2024 'Trump reshoring trade' compounded the bid into a November-2024 top. The tape was narrow/mega-cap-led (RSP-SPY -19.1%), but the weaker dollar was a clean tailwind for the multinationals.","drivers":["Goldilocks AI melt-up regime (SMH +156.4%, growth>value, VIX 33->14) lifts risk","Weaker dollar (DXY -6.2%) tailwind; CHIPS/IRA/IIJA funding hits real spend","Nov-2024 election crystallizes the 'reshoring/Trump trade'","Electrification and AI-power capex emerging; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -19.1%)"],"title_zh":"回流牛市，置于 goldilocks AI 融涨之中（+103%）","body_zh":"从 2022 年秋季低点起工业翻倍有余——回流/资本开支超级周期最清晰的表达，被 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀融涨（半导体 +156.4%、成长>价值 +35.6、VIX 33->14、美元走弱 -6.2%）大幅增强。CHIPS/IRA/IIJA 资金流入破土项目；2023 年 AI 反弹与 2024 年降息抬升风险；2024 年 11 月'特朗普回流交易'把买盘叠加至 2024 年 11 月高点。市场狭窄、大盘股引领（RSP-SPY -19.1%），但走弱美元对跨国企业是干净顺风。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI 融涨 regime（半导体 +156.4%、成长>价值、VIX 33->14）抬升风险","美元走弱（DXY -6.2%）顺风；CHIPS/IRA/IIJA 资金落地为实际开支","2024 年 11 月大选确立'回流/特朗普交易'","电气化与 AI 电力资本开支兴起；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -19.1%）"]},"2024-11-26":{"title":"Tariff-crash selloff in a risk-off flush (-28%)","body":"The 'Trump trade' euphoria gave way to its dark side as the regime flipped violently risk-off (VIX 14->52, SMH -25.1%, SPHB-SPLV -19.7%) into the April-8 reciprocal-tariff crash. Globalized industrial supply chains were hit hardest — input costs, retaliation risk and demand fears at once — and defensives led (-8.4% vs cyclicals -19.0%). Reshoring beneficiaries sold off with the broad market despite being the structural policy winners.","drivers":["Risk-off flush regime (VIX 14->52, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -19.7%) leads lower","April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash hits supply chains","Tariff input-cost and retaliation fears","Rotation out of a parabolic two-year industrial run; defensives led (-8.4% vs -19.0%)"],"title_zh":"关税崩盘抛售，置于避险冲刷（-28%）","body_zh":"'特朗普交易'狂热让位于其阴暗面，regime 剧烈转向避险（VIX 14->52、半导体 -25.1%、SPHB-SPLV -19.7%），跌入 4 月 8 日对等关税崩盘。全球化工业供应链打击最重——投入成本、报复风险、需求担忧同时袭来——防御领先（-8.4% 对周期 -19.0%）。回流受益者虽是政策的结构性赢家，却随大盘抛售。","drivers_zh":["避险冲刷 regime（VIX 14->52、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -19.7%）领跌","2025 年 4 月对等关税崩盘冲击供应链","关税投入成本与报复担忧","从抛物线式两年工业行情中轮动出场；防御领先（-8.4% 对 -19.0%）"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery & AI-power capex leg, lifted by a high-beta risk-on rip (+89%)","body":"Off the April-8 low reshoring recovered strongly inside an explosive risk-on regime (VIX 52->19, SMH +255%, SPHB-SPLV +118.3%, weaker dollar -1.5%) that lifted everything cyclical. The tariff regime that caused the crash also hardens the long-run onshoring case, while electrification and AI-datacenter-power capex became a second engine. Up +89% into June 2026, the basket is a steady secondary leader (RS #16) — durable and policy-backed, lagging the parabolic semis but riding the broad cyclical recovery rather than narrow mega-cap (RSP-SPY -8.8%).","drivers":["Explosive risk-on regime (VIX 52->19, SMH +255%, SPHB-SPLV +118.3%) lifts cyclicals","Tariff regime reinforces structural onshoring incentive","Electrification + AI-datacenter-power capex as a fresh demand engine","Record manufacturing-construction spend (~$224B/yr); narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -8.8%)"],"title_zh":"回升与 AI 电力资本开支腿段，被高贝塔风险偏好暴涨抬升（+89%）","body_zh":"从 4 月 8 日低点起，回流强势回升于爆发性风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->19、半导体 +255%、SPHB-SPLV +118.3%、美元走弱 -1.5%），抬升一切周期品种。引发崩盘的关税体制也强化了长期本土化逻辑，而电气化与 AI 数据中心电力资本开支成为第二引擎。至 2026 年 6 月 +89%，该篮子是稳健的次级领头羊（相对强度第 16 位）——耐久、有政策支撑，落后于抛物线半导体，但搭乘广泛周期复苏而非狭窄大盘股（RSP-SPY -8.8%）。","drivers_zh":["爆发性风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->19、半导体 +255%、SPHB-SPLV +118.3%）抬升周期股","关税体制强化结构性本土化激励","电气化+AI 数据中心电力资本开支成为新需求引擎","创纪录的制造业建设开支（约 2240 亿美元/年）；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -8.8%）"]}}},"b-robotics_automation":{"now":"Robotics & Automation (ABB/ROK/industrial controls, machine vision, surgical robotics; BOTZ proxy) is a quality industrial-tech theme caught mid-correction — a high-beta name whose moves amplify the regime in both directions. It's 'Rolling over' at RS-rank #20 (pos 35.9): the basket nearly doubled (+90%) off the April-2025 tariff-crash low into a May-2026 high, then began consolidating as the tape shifted from explosive risk-on toward a broadening reflation regime (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, growth lagging value -15.2%) that no longer rewards long-duration industrial-tech. The thesis fuses classic factory-automation capex (overlapping reshoring) with the newer 'physical AI / humanoid' narrative. Near-term it digests a parabolic run against a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) and sticky-CPI 2026 backdrop that pressure the industrial-multinational and capital-equipment buyers at its core.","now_zh":"机器人与自动化（ABB/ROK/工业控制、机器视觉、手术机器人；BOTZ 为代理）是一个处于回调中段的优质工业科技主题——一个高贝塔品种，其运动在两个方向都放大 regime。它'见顶回落'，相对强度排名第 20 位（pos 35.9）：该篮子从 2025 年 4 月关税崩盘低点近乎翻倍（+90%）至 2026 年 5 月高点，随后开始盘整，因行情从爆发性风险偏好转向广度扩张的再通胀 regime（周期股 +11.2% 对防御 +6.9%、成长落后价值 -15.2%），不再奖励长久期工业科技。其逻辑融合经典工厂自动化资本开支（与回流重叠）和较新的'实体 AI/人形机器人'叙事。短期内它消化一段抛物线行情，背景是走强的美元（DXY +3.4%）和粘性 CPI 的 2026 年，这压制了位于核心的工业跨国企业和资本设备买家。","legs":{"2021-12-27":{"title":"Hiking-bear, rate-driven growth de-rate (-29%)","body":"High-multiple automation/robotics names led the 2022 growth-stock de-rate in a stagflation-ish, rate-driven regime — yields surged (TLT -20.3%), the dollar ripped (DXY +8.1%) and VIX ran 18->33. As long-duration industrial-tech, the group got hit harder than plain cyclicals (growth-value -18.1%) into the May-2022 low, even as breadth held (RSP-SPY +4.5%).","drivers":["Rate-regime + dollar shock (TLT -20.3%, DXY +8.1%) crush long-duration multiples","Stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 18->33), growth de-rate (growth-value -18.1%)","Supply-chain/component shortages hit hardware","High-beta rotation out of industrial tech"],"title_zh":"加息熊市、利率驱动成长去估值（-29%）","body_zh":"高倍数自动化/机器人个股领跌 2022 年成长股去估值，处于类滞胀、利率驱动 regime——收益率飙升（TLT -20.3%）、美元暴涨（DXY +8.1%）、VIX 18->33。作为长久期工业科技，该板块所受冲击重于普通周期股（成长-价值 -18.1%），跌至 2022 年 5 月低点，尽管市场广度守住（RSP-SPY +4.5%）。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime+美元冲击（TLT -20.3%、DXY +8.1%）压垮长久期倍数","类滞胀避险（VIX 18->33）、成长去估值（成长-价值 -18.1%）","供应链/元件短缺冲击硬件","从工业科技中高贝塔轮动"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Summer relief bounce in a growth-led risk-on window (+26%)","body":"Caught the broad mid-2022 relief rally off oversold as the regime briefly turned goldilocks/growth-up (growth>value +7.8, SMH +11.7%, VIX 33->20) on premature Fed-pause hopes. A multiple-driven bounce where high-beta automation amplified the upside (SPHB-SPLV +12.6%) — not a fundamental turn.","drivers":["Growth-led risk-on bounce (growth>value +7.8, VIX 33->20) amplifies high-beta","Premature 'Fed pivot' hopes","Component-shortage easing optimism","Oversold mean-reversion"],"title_zh":"夏季纾困反弹于成长引领的风险偏好窗口（+26%）","body_zh":"从超卖中搭上 2022 年年中大盘纾困反弹，因过早的美联储暂停预期，regime 短暂转向 goldilocks/增长上行（成长>价值 +7.8、半导体 +11.7%、VIX 33->20）。倍数驱动的反弹，高贝塔自动化放大上行（SPHB-SPLV +12.6%）——而非基本面转折。","drivers_zh":["成长引领风险偏好反弹（成长>价值 +7.8、VIX 33->20）放大高贝塔","过早的'美联储转向'预期","元件短缺缓解的乐观情绪","超卖均值回归"]},"2022-08-12":{"title":"Jackson Hole rate-driven flush (-21%)","body":"Powell's hawkish reset ended the bounce in a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -12.5%; DXY +8.0%; VIX 20->33) into the autumn-2022 capitulation low. Pure macro de-risking of long-duration tech — the strong dollar an extra weight on the industrial multinationals (cyclicals -14.7%).","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -12.5%) on hawkish Jackson Hole","Risk-off capitulation (VIX 20->33) across equities","Dollar surge (DXY +8.0%) pressuring industrial multinationals","Long-duration de-rate"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔利率驱动冲刷（-21%）","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派重置在利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -12.5%；DXY +8.0%；VIX 20->33）中终结反弹，跌至 2022 年秋季投降低点。纯粹是对长久期科技的宏观去风险——强势美元对工业跨国企业再添重压（周期股 -14.7%）。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -12.5%），杰克逊霍尔鹰派","股市避险投降（VIX 20->33）","美元飙升（DXY +8.0%）施压工业跨国企业","长久期去估值"]},"2022-09-27":{"title":"AI-rally recovery in a goldilocks, weaker-dollar tape (+63%)","body":"From the autumn-2022 low the group rode the 2023 AI rally in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime (SMH +69.6%, growth>value +11.6, VIX 33->14, dollar collapsing -10.7%) — a weaker-dollar tailwind for the industrial multinationals. Automation re-rated as a near-AI industrial-tech beneficiary in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP-SPY -5.0%), topping in July 2023 as early-AI enthusiasm cooled.","drivers":["Goldilocks AI risk-on regime (SMH +69.6%, growth>value, VIX 33->14)","Dollar collapse (DXY -10.7%) tailwind for multinationals","Reshoring-capex narrative supports order books","Near-AI re-rating; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -5.0%)"],"title_zh":"AI 反弹回升于 goldilocks、弱美元行情（+63%）","body_zh":"从 2022 年秋季低点起，该板块在 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀 regime（半导体 +69.6%、成长>价值 +11.6、VIX 33->14、美元崩跌 -10.7%）中搭乘 2023 年 AI 反弹——弱美元对工业跨国企业是顺风。自动化作为近 AI 工业科技受益者在狭窄大盘股行情（RSP-SPY -5.0%）中获重估，随早期 AI 热情降温于 2023 年 7 月见顶。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI 风险偏好 regime（半导体 +69.6%、成长>价值、VIX 33->14）","美元崩跌（DXY -10.7%）对跨国企业顺风","回流资本开支叙事支撑订单簿","近 AI 重估；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -5.0%）"]},"2023-07-31":{"title":"Rate-scare, yield-driven pullback (-22%)","body":"The autumn-2023 bond-yield spike (10Y toward 5%, TLT -13.9%) defined the regime and hit rate-sensitive growth and industrial-tech hardest (SPHB-SPLV -13.6%), with a firming dollar (DXY +4.9%). A clean rates-driven correction into the late-October low — even with growth>value holding (+3.1), the duration hit dominated.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: 10Y spike toward 5% (TLT -13.9%) hits duration","Higher-for-longer repricing crushes growth multiples (SPHB-SPLV -13.6%)","Firming dollar (DXY +4.9%) headwind","Profit-taking after the AI-rally leg"],"title_zh":"利率恐慌、收益率驱动回落（-22%）","body_zh":"2023 年秋季债券收益率飙升（10 年期逼近 5%、TLT -13.9%）定义了 regime，对利率敏感的成长与工业科技打击最重（SPHB-SPLV -13.6%），伴随美元转强（DXY +4.9%）。一次干净的利率驱动回调至 10 月底低点——即便成长>价值守住（+3.1），久期冲击仍主导。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：10 年期逼近 5%（TLT -13.9%）冲击久期","更高更久重新定价压垮成长倍数（SPHB-SPLV -13.6%）","美元转强（DXY +4.9%）逆风","AI 反弹腿段后的获利了结"]},"2023-11-01":{"title":"Soft-landing rally on a falling-yield, risk-on regime (+48%)","body":"The late-2023 dovish pivot drove a goldilocks regime where yields fell (TLT +13.6%), VIX dropped 17->13, semis ripped (+93.4%) and growth>value (+16.7) — the duration tailwind that had been a headwind. Automation rode broad risk into a July-2024 top in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP-SPY -7.5%), with reshoring capex and early physical-AI optimism adding a thematic bid.","drivers":["Goldilocks risk-on regime: yields fell (TLT +13.6%), VIX 17->13, SMH +93.4%","Late-2023 Fed dovish pivot, 2024 cut cycle","Reshoring capex + early 'physical AI' narrative","Narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP-SPY -7.5%)"],"title_zh":"软着陆反弹于收益率下行、风险偏好 regime（+48%）","body_zh":"2023 年底鸽派转向驱动一个 goldilocks regime，收益率下行（TLT +13.6%）、VIX 17->13、半导体暴涨（+93.4%）、成长>价值（+16.7）——曾经的久期逆风转为顺风。自动化搭乘大盘风险至 2024 年 7 月高点，处于狭窄大盘股行情（RSP-SPY -7.5%），回流资本开支与早期实体 AI 乐观增添主题买盘。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 风险偏好 regime：收益率下行（TLT +13.6%）、VIX 17->13、半导体 +93.4%","2023 年底美联储鸽派转向、2024 年降息周期","回流资本开支+早期'实体 AI'叙事","狭窄大盘股市场广度（RSP-SPY -7.5%）"]},"2024-07-16":{"title":"Yen-carry unwind, high-beta flush (-16%)","body":"The early-August 2024 yen-carry-trade unwind triggered a sharp risk-off flush (VIX 13->28, SMH -22.7%, SPHB-SPLV -14.6%); high-beta automation amplified the move into the August low while defensives held (+0.9% vs cyclicals -8.1%). Sharp and brief — a positioning shock, not a fundamental change.","drivers":["Risk-off flush regime (VIX 13->28, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -14.6%) hits hardest","Aug-2024 yen-carry-trade unwind","Global high-beta de-risking; defensives led (+0.9% vs -8.1%)","Rotation after a multi-month rally"],"title_zh":"日元套利平仓、高贝塔冲刷（-16%）","body_zh":"2024 年 8 月初日元套利交易平仓触发急剧避险冲刷（VIX 13->28、半导体 -22.7%、SPHB-SPLV -14.6%）；高贝塔自动化放大跌势至 8 月低点，防御守住（+0.9% 对周期 -8.1%）。急促而短暂——是仓位冲击而非基本面变化。","drivers_zh":["避险冲刷 regime（VIX 13->28、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -14.6%）打击最重","2024 年 8 月日元套利交易平仓","全球高贝塔去风险；防御领先（+0.9% 对 -8.1%）","多月反弹后的轮动"]},"2024-08-07":{"title":"Election & physical-AI bid in a goldilocks risk-on tape (+26%)","body":"Recovered off the August low into a November-2024 high as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up risk-on (cyclicals +18.3% vs defensives +5.9%, SMH +15.2%, VIX 28->15). The 'Trump reshoring trade' and intensifying physical-AI/humanoid enthusiasm met capex optimism — though a firming dollar (DXY +3.5%) was a mild headwind for the multinationals.","drivers":["Goldilocks risk-on regime (cyclicals +18.3%, VIX 28->15) lifts the group","Nov-2024 election 'reshoring/Trump trade'","Physical-AI / humanoid-robot narrative intensifies","Firming dollar (DXY +3.5%) a mild headwind"],"title_zh":"大选与实体 AI 买盘于 goldilocks 风险偏好行情（+26%）","body_zh":"从 8 月低点回升至 2024 年 11 月高点，regime 转向 goldilocks/增长上行风险偏好（周期股 +18.3% 对防御 +5.9%、半导体 +15.2%、VIX 28->15）。'特朗普回流交易'与日益高涨的实体 AI/人形机器人热情遇上资本开支乐观——尽管美元转强（DXY +3.5%）对跨国企业是轻微逆风。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 风险偏好 regime（周期股 +18.3%、VIX 28->15）抬升板块","2024 年 11 月大选'回流/特朗普交易'","实体 AI/人形机器人叙事升温","美元转强（DXY +3.5%）轻微逆风"]},"2024-11-25":{"title":"Tariff-crash selloff, high-beta amplifies the flush (-33%)","body":"Robotics took a deep hit into the April-8 reciprocal-tariff crash as the regime collapsed to violent risk-off (VIX 15->52, SMH -25.8%, SPHB-SPLV -21.0%). Its globalized hardware supply chains sit squarely in the tariff blast radius, and high beta meant it fell harder than the market (-33% vs SPY -16.4%) — the basket's harshest drawdown of the cycle — with the DeepSeek-led tech de-rate compounding it.","drivers":["Violent risk-off regime (VIX 15->52, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -21.0%) amplifies the drop","April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash hits hardware supply chains","Capital-equipment demand fears","DeepSeek-led tech de-rate (Jan 2025) compounds it"],"title_zh":"关税崩盘抛售，高贝塔放大冲刷（-33%）","body_zh":"机器人在 4 月 8 日对等关税崩盘中深度受挫，regime 崩塌为剧烈避险（VIX 15->52、半导体 -25.8%、SPHB-SPLV -21.0%）。其全球化硬件供应链正处关税冲击半径，高贝塔意味着跌幅大于大盘（-33% 对 SPY -16.4%）——该篮子本周期最严酷回撤——DeepSeek 引领的科技去估值雪上加霜。","drivers_zh":["剧烈避险 regime（VIX 15->52、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -21.0%）放大跌幅","2025 年 4 月对等关税崩盘冲击硬件供应链","资本设备需求担忧","DeepSeek 引领的科技去估值（2025 年 1 月）加剧跌势"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery & physical-AI re-rate, riding the high-beta risk-on rip (+90%)","body":"Off the April-8 low robotics nearly doubled (+90%) into a May-2026 high, supercharged by an explosive risk-on regime (VIX 52->17, SMH +235.7%, SPHB-SPLV +107.2%, weaker dollar -3.7%) where high beta led. The physical-AI/humanoid narrative re-accelerated and reshoring capex underpinned orders. The leg is now rolling over as the basket digests a parabolic run against a stronger dollar and sticky-CPI 2026 backdrop that pressures capital-equipment buyers.","drivers":["Explosive high-beta risk-on regime (VIX 52->17, SPHB-SPLV +107.2%, SMH +235.7%) leads the run","Physical-AI / humanoid re-rate re-accelerates","Reshoring-capex order support; weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%) tailwind","2026 strong dollar / sticky CPI now pressures capital-equipment buyers"],"title_zh":"回升与实体 AI 重估，搭乘高贝塔风险偏好暴涨（+90%）","body_zh":"从 4 月 8 日低点起机器人近乎翻倍（+90%）至 2026 年 5 月高点，被爆发性风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->17、半导体 +235.7%、SPHB-SPLV +107.2%、美元走弱 -3.7%）大幅增强，高贝塔领涨。实体 AI/人形机器人叙事再加速、回流资本开支支撑订单。该腿段如今见顶回落，篮子在走强美元、粘性 CPI 的 2026 年背景下消化抛物线行情，这压制资本设备买家。","drivers_zh":["爆发性高贝塔风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->17、SPHB-SPLV +107.2%、半导体 +235.7%）领跑","实体 AI/人形机器人重估再加速","回流资本开支订单支撑；美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）顺风","2026 年强势美元/粘性 CPI 如今压制资本设备买家"]}}},"b-space_economy":{"now":"Space Economy (RKLB/launch/satcom/Earth-obs, ARKX proxy) is the high-beta speculative end of the industrials complex — a leveraged long on the regime that swings 30-40% in both directions and amplifies whatever the tape is doing. It's 'Rolling over' at RS-rank #26 (pos 43.9), having dumped -42% off a late-May-2026 high. The 2023-25 era turned space from a SPAC graveyard into a credible build-out (launch cadence, direct-to-device satcom, Earth observation, a defense-space bid), but RKLB-style names trade like long-duration call options: when risk appetite is on they melt up vertically, and when VIX spikes or a milestone slips they crater. The late-2025/2026 Neutron-rocket delays triggered exactly the 35%+ drawdown this group is prone to, even with backlogs intact, and it's now in a risk-off phase against a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%). High torque, low quality of trend; size accordingly.","now_zh":"太空经济（RKLB/发射/卫星通信/对地观测，ARKX 为代理）是工业群组中高贝塔的投机端——一个对 regime 的杠杆多头，在两个方向都以 30-40% 摆动，放大行情的任何走向。它'见顶回落'，相对强度排名第 26 位（pos 43.9），刚从 2026 年 5 月底高点暴跌 -42%。2023-25 年间太空从 SPAC 坟场变成可信的建设浪潮（发射节奏、直连设备卫星通信、对地观测、国防航天买盘），但 RKLB 这类个股交易起来像长久期看涨期权：风险偏好（risk-on）时垂直融涨，VIX 飙升或里程碑滑期时暴跌。2025 年底/2026 年的 Neutron 火箭延期，恰恰触发了该板块易发的 35%+ 回撤（即便积压完好），如今处于避险阶段，背景是走强的美元（DXY +3.4%）。高扭矩、低趋势质量；据此控制仓位。","legs":{"2021-02-19":{"title":"SPAC-bubble unwind, speculation de-rates first (-44%)","body":"Space de-SPACs led the 2021-22 unwind well before the broad bear — the regime hadn't even turned risk-off yet (SPY still +9.6%, cyclicals +16.7%), but as liquidity tightened and the Fed pivoted hawkish, the most speculative, profitless corner of growth got hit first and hardest into the February-2022 low. High beta cuts both ways: it led down even while the index was up.","drivers":["Speculation de-rates ahead of the regime (SPY still +9.6% as space crashed)","SPAC/de-SPAC speculative bubble deflates","Fed-hiking pivot punishes profitless growth first","Long-duration story-stock risk-off"],"title_zh":"SPAC 泡沫破裂，投机最先去估值（-44%）","body_zh":"太空 de-SPAC 早在大盘熊市之前就领跌 2021-22 年破裂——彼时 regime 甚至尚未转向避险（SPY 仍 +9.6%、周期股 +16.7%），但随流动性收紧、美联储转鹰，最具投机性、无盈利的成长角落最先、最重受挫至 2022 年 2 月低点。高贝塔双向切割：即便指数上涨它也领跌。","drivers_zh":["投机领先 regime 去估值（太空崩盘时 SPY 仍 +9.6%）","SPAC/de-SPAC 投机泡沫消退","美联储加息转向最先惩罚无盈利成长","长久期故事股避险"]},"2022-02-23":{"title":"Sharp dead-cat bounce off a stagflation tape (+28%)","body":"A high-beta oversold snap-back typical of this group's violent two-way moves, in a choppy stagflation-ish regime (VIX 31->19, dollar firming +2.9%) where the index barely moved (SPY +8.6%, breadth narrow). No fundamental turn — just speculative torque off a deep low.","drivers":["High-beta oversold bounce in a flat, stagflation-ish tape (SPY +8.6%)","Brief risk-on window (VIX 31->19)","Speculative dip-buying","Firming dollar (DXY +2.9%) a backdrop drag"],"title_zh":"急促死猫反弹于类滞胀行情（+28%）","body_zh":"高贝塔超卖弹回，是该板块剧烈双向运动的典型，处于震荡的类滞胀 regime（VIX 31->19、美元转强 +2.9%），指数几乎不动（SPY +8.6%、广度狭窄）。无基本面转折——只是从深低点的投机扭矩。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔超卖反弹于平淡、类滞胀行情（SPY +8.6%）","短暂风险偏好窗口（VIX 31->19）","投机性逢低买入","美元转强（DXY +2.9%）背景拖累"]},"2022-04-04":{"title":"Hiking-bear, rate-driven flush (-33%)","body":"Resumed the broad 2022 decline as the Fed-hiking bear intensified into a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -10.1%; DXY +4.9%; VIX 19->33) into the June low. Speculative space got no shelter — high beta meant it fell harder than the index (-33% vs SPY -14.0%, SPHB-SPLV -15.1%).","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -10.1%) into a risk-off slowdown","Profitless-growth flush (VIX 19->33, SPHB-SPLV -15.1%)","Liquidity withdrawal hits speculation hardest","Strong dollar (DXY +4.9%) headwind"],"title_zh":"加息熊市、利率驱动冲刷（-33%）","body_zh":"随美联储加息熊市加剧进入利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -10.1%；DXY +4.9%；VIX 19->33），恢复 2022 年大盘下跌至 6 月低点。投机性太空毫无庇护——高贝塔意味着跌幅大于指数（-33% 对 SPY -14.0%、SPHB-SPLV -15.1%）。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -10.1%）进入避险放缓","无盈利成长冲刷（VIX 19->33、SPHB-SPLV -15.1%）","流动性撤出对投机打击最重","强势美元（DXY +4.9%）逆风"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Summer relief bounce, high-beta upside mirror (+42%)","body":"A big high-beta bounce off the spring low as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up (growth>value +7.9, SMH +10.9%, VIX 33->20) on premature Fed-pause hopes — the upside mirror of this group's outsized drawdowns, with SPHB-SPLV +11.5% amplifying a modest +9.9% index move.","drivers":["Growth-led risk-on bounce (growth>value +7.9, VIX 33->20)","High-beta upside torque off oversold (SPHB-SPLV +11.5%)","Premature 'Fed pause' relief rally","Brief speculative risk-on"],"title_zh":"夏季纾困反弹、高贝塔上行镜像（+42%）","body_zh":"从春季低点的高贝塔大反弹，regime 转向 goldilocks/增长上行（成长>价值 +7.9、半导体 +10.9%、VIX 33->20），因过早的美联储暂停预期——是该板块超大回撤的上行镜像，SPHB-SPLV +11.5% 放大了温和的 +9.9% 指数涨幅。","drivers_zh":["成长引领风险偏好反弹（成长>价值 +7.9、VIX 33->20）","从超卖出发的高贝塔上行扭矩（SPHB-SPLV +11.5%）","过早的'美联储暂停'纾困反弹","短暂投机性风险偏好"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole rate-driven flush (-34%)","body":"Powell's hawkish reset sent speculative space into the December-2022 low in a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -12.6%; SPHB-SPLV -11.8%). High-beta names lagged the broad late-2022 recovery as liquidity stayed tight — when the cost of carry is rising, the longest-duration speculation gets no bid.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -12.6%) on hawkish Jackson Hole","Tight-liquidity penalty on high-beta speculation (SPHB-SPLV -11.8%)","Tax-loss selling into year-end","Risk-off de-rate"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔利率驱动冲刷（-34%）","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派重置把投机性太空送入 2022 年 12 月低点，处于利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -12.6%；SPHB-SPLV -11.8%）。流动性持续偏紧，高贝塔个股落后于 2022 年底大盘复苏——持有成本上升时，最长久期的投机得不到买盘。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -12.6%），杰克逊霍尔鹰派","紧流动性对高贝塔投机的惩罚（SPHB-SPLV -11.8%）","年末税务亏损抛售","避险去估值"]},"2022-12-27":{"title":"January high-beta squeeze on a risk-on flip (+83%)","body":"A ferocious early-2023 high-beta rally as the regime flipped reflation/growth-up risk-on (SPHB-SPLV +18.3%, SMH +17.2%, VIX flat 22) and the most-shorted, most-oversold speculation ripped on the 'soft landing' re-risk. Pure high-beta torque — the basket +83% against a +4.5% index — topped fast in February 2023.","drivers":["Risk-on flip (SPHB-SPLV +18.3%, SMH +17.2%) ignites the squeeze","Early-2023 high-beta short squeeze","Soft-landing re-risk","Speculative mean-reversion off deep lows (basket +83% vs SPY +4.5%)"],"title_zh":"1 月高贝塔逼空于风险偏好翻转（+83%）","body_zh":"2023 年初凶猛的高贝塔反弹，regime 翻转为再通胀/增长上行风险偏好（SPHB-SPLV +18.3%、半导体 +17.2%、VIX 持平 22），最被做空、最超卖的投机在'软着陆'再担风险中暴涨。纯高贝塔扭矩——篮子 +83% 对 +4.5% 指数——于 2023 年 2 月快速见顶。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好翻转（SPHB-SPLV +18.3%、半导体 +17.2%）点燃逼空","2023 年初高贝塔逼空","软着陆再担风险","从深低点的投机均值回归（篮子 +83% 对 SPY +4.5%）"]},"2023-02-22":{"title":"Rate-scare grind lower under higher-for-longer (-44%)","body":"Space gave most of the squeeze back through 2023 as the SVB scare and then the autumn yield spike (TLT -14.9%) hammered speculation in a regime where breadth was punishingly narrow (RSP-SPY -12.4%) and high beta lagged badly (SPHB-SPLV -3.6% even as growth>value +18.3). A long, grinding -44% into the October-2023 low — the index actually rose (+4.2%) while space bled.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: autumn 10Y spike toward 5% (TLT -14.9%) de-rates duration","SVB regional-bank scare (Mar 2023)","Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -12.4%) starves speculation while SPY +4.2%","Higher-for-longer punishes the longest-duration names"],"title_zh":"利率恐慌于更高更久缓步下行（-44%）","body_zh":"随 SVB 恐慌、继而秋季收益率飙升（TLT -14.9%）重击投机，太空在 2023 年间回吐大部分逼空涨幅，处于市场广度极度狭窄（RSP-SPY -12.4%）、高贝塔严重落后（SPHB-SPLV -3.6%，即便成长>价值 +18.3）的 regime。一段漫长缓慢的 -44% 至 2023 年 10 月低点——指数实际上涨（+4.2%）而太空流血。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：秋季 10 年期逼近 5%（TLT -14.9%）使久期去估值","SVB 区域银行恐慌（2023 年 3 月）","市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -12.4%）饿死投机，而 SPY +4.2%","更高更久惩罚最长久期个股"]},"2023-10-27":{"title":"The space build-out bull on a goldilocks AI melt-up (+381%)","body":"The defining leg: +381% over 16 months as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (SMH +82.4%, growth>value +23.1, VIX 21->16, yields falling TLT +11.3%) — falling yields and risk-on are rocket fuel for the longest-duration speculation. A genuine fundamental shift (launch cadence, direct-to-device satcom, Earth-obs, defense-space) turned the SPAC graveyard into a credible build-out, and high beta turned that into a 381% melt-up in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP-SPY -11.9%). RKLB-type names led into the February-2025 top.","drivers":["Goldilocks AI melt-up (SMH +82.4%, falling yields TLT +11.3%, VIX 21->16) is rocket fuel","Real fundamentals: launch cadence, satcom, Earth-obs, defense-space","High-beta amplifies risk-on into a +381% run; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -11.9%)","SPAC-era survivors mature into investable businesses"],"title_zh":"太空建设牛市于 goldilocks AI 融涨（+381%）","body_zh":"决定性的一段：16 个月内 +381%，regime 转向 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀（半导体 +82.4%、成长>价值 +23.1、VIX 21->16、收益率下行 TLT +11.3%）——收益率下行加风险偏好是最长久期投机的火箭燃料。一次真实基本面转变（发射节奏、直连设备卫星通信、对地观测、国防航天）把 SPAC 坟场变成可信建设浪潮，高贝塔把它变成狭窄大盘股行情（RSP-SPY -11.9%）中的 381% 融涨。RKLB 这类个股领涨至 2025 年 2 月高点。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI 融涨（半导体 +82.4%、收益率下行 TLT +11.3%、VIX 21->16）是火箭燃料","真实基本面：发射节奏、卫星通信、对地观测、国防航天","高贝塔放大风险偏好至 +381% 行情；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -11.9%）","SPAC 时代幸存者成长为可投资企业"]},"2025-02-10":{"title":"DeepSeek & tariff de-risk, high-beta leads down (-40%)","body":"Speculative space led the early-2025 de-risk: the DeepSeek AI scare then the April-8 tariff crash flipped the regime violently risk-off (VIX 16->52, SMH -27.9%, SPHB-SPLV -21.9%). The highest-beta theme on the board flushed hardest into the April low while defensives held (-6.5% vs cyclicals -17.7%).","drivers":["Violent risk-off regime (VIX 16->52, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -21.9%) leads space down","DeepSeek AI scare (Jan 2025) hits speculation","April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash","Defensives led (-6.5% vs -17.7%) as high beta flushed"],"title_zh":"DeepSeek 与关税去风险、高贝塔领跌（-40%）","body_zh":"投机性太空领跌 2025 年初去风险：DeepSeek AI 恐慌继而 4 月 8 日关税崩盘把 regime 剧烈翻转为避险（VIX 16->52、半导体 -27.9%、SPHB-SPLV -21.9%）。面板上扭矩最高的主题在 4 月低点冲刷最重，防御守住（-6.5% 对周期 -17.7%）。","drivers_zh":["剧烈避险 regime（VIX 16->52、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -21.9%）领跌太空","DeepSeek AI 恐慌（2025 年 1 月）冲击投机","2025 年 4 月对等关税崩盘","防御领先（-6.5% 对 -17.7%），高贝塔冲刷"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Tariff-low moonshot on a high-beta risk-on rip (+154%)","body":"Classic high-beta torque off the April-8 low: +154% into an October-2025 high as the regime snapped to risk-on (VIX 52->21, SPHB-SPLV +59.4%, growth>value +22.7, weaker dollar -4.1%) and the build-out narrative re-engaged. Speculative space does this — vertical rallies that amplify a +34.7% index into a triple-digit basket move and demand respect for both directions.","drivers":["High-beta risk-on rip (VIX 52->21, SPHB-SPLV +59.4%, growth>value +22.7) amplifies the snap-back","Snap-back off the April-2025 crash low","Build-out narrative re-engages (launch, satcom, defense-space)","Weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%); basket +154% vs SPY +34.7%"],"title_zh":"关税低点登月于高贝塔风险偏好暴涨（+154%）","body_zh":"从 4 月 8 日低点的经典高贝塔扭矩：+154% 至 2025 年 10 月高点，regime 切换为风险偏好（VIX 52->21、SPHB-SPLV +59.4%、成长>价值 +22.7、美元走弱 -4.1%），建设叙事重新发力。投机性太空就是如此——垂直拉升，把 +34.7% 指数放大为三位数篮子涨幅，要求对两个方向都心存敬畏。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔风险偏好暴涨（VIX 52->21、SPHB-SPLV +59.4%、成长>价值 +22.7）放大弹回","从 2025 年 4 月崩盘低点弹回","建设叙事重新发力（发射、卫星通信、国防航天）","美元走弱（DXY -4.1%）；篮子 +154% 对 SPY +34.7%"]},"2025-10-15":{"title":"Autumn high-beta flush front-runs a risk wobble (-39%)","body":"A sharp high-beta correction off the October high — the regime only wobbled mildly (VIX 21->26, SPY -1.9%), but speculative space front-ran it with its usual outsized drawdown (-39% on a -1.9% index, SPHB-SPLV -5.3%). This is the group's signature: it de-risks first and hardest at the first hint of a turn.","drivers":["High beta front-runs a mild risk wobble (-39% vs SPY -1.9%, VIX 21->26)","Late-2025 broad risk wobble","Profit-taking after a +154% run","Speculation de-risks fastest"],"title_zh":"秋季高贝塔冲刷抢跑风险动摇（-39%）","body_zh":"从 10 月高点的急剧高贝塔回调——regime 仅轻微动摇（VIX 21->26、SPY -1.9%），但投机性太空以惯常的超大回撤抢跑（-39% 对 -1.9% 指数、SPHB-SPLV -5.3%）。这是该板块的标志：一有转向迹象就最先、最重地去风险。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔抢跑轻微风险动摇（-39% 对 SPY -1.9%、VIX 21->26）","2025 年底大盘风险动摇","+154% 行情后的获利了结","投机最快去风险"]},"2025-11-20":{"title":"Year-end rip on a reflation risk-on flip (+120%)","body":"Another vertical high-beta rally — +120% into late January 2026 — as the regime flipped reflation/growth-up risk-on (VIX 26->16, SPHB-SPLV +16.0%, broadening RSP-SPY +2.4%, weaker dollar -3.7%) on renewed risk appetite and launch/contract milestones. Pure speculative torque off an oversold low, the basket +120% against a +6.9% index.","drivers":["Reflation risk-on flip (VIX 26->16, SPHB-SPLV +16.0%) fuels the rip","Renewed risk-on into year-end/new-year","Launch and contract milestones","High-beta torque off oversold (basket +120% vs SPY +6.9%)"],"title_zh":"年末暴涨于再通胀风险偏好翻转（+120%）","body_zh":"又一次垂直高贝塔反弹——+120% 至 2026 年 1 月底——regime 翻转为再通胀/增长上行风险偏好（VIX 26->16、SPHB-SPLV +16.0%、广度扩张 RSP-SPY +2.4%、美元走弱 -3.7%），受风险偏好重燃与发射/合同里程碑驱动。从超卖低点的纯投机扭矩，篮子 +120% 对 +6.9% 指数。","drivers_zh":["再通胀风险偏好翻转（VIX 26->16、SPHB-SPLV +16.0%）助燃暴涨","年末/新年风险偏好重燃","发射与合同里程碑","从超卖的高贝塔扭矩（篮子 +120% 对 SPY +6.9%）"]},"2026-01-28":{"title":"Quick correction as defensives bid (-26%)","body":"A fast pullback off the January high as the regime tilted mildly risk-off/stagflation-ish (VIX 16->21, defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals +0.8%, growth-value -6.5%). Routine volatility for a basket that swings 25%+ on sentiment and single-name news — notably emerging Neutron-rocket timeline worries — with high beta giving back fast (-26% on a -2.0% index).","drivers":["Mild risk-off/stagflation tilt (VIX 16->21, defensives +4.6% vs +0.8%)","Routine high-beta pullback after a +120% run (-26% vs SPY -2.0%)","Early Neutron-rocket timeline concerns (RKLB)","Sentiment-driven two-way volatility"],"title_zh":"快速回调，防御获买盘（-26%）","body_zh":"从 1 月高点的快速回落，regime 轻微转向避险/类滞胀（VIX 16->21、防御 +4.6% 对周期 +0.8%、成长-价值 -6.5%）。对一个因情绪和单一个股新闻（尤其新兴的 Neutron 火箭时间线担忧）就摆动 25%+ 的篮子而言是常规波动，高贝塔回吐迅速（-26% 对 -2.0% 指数）。","drivers_zh":["轻微避险/类滞胀倾斜（VIX 16->21、防御 +4.6% 对 +0.8%）","+120% 行情后的常规高贝塔回落（-26% 对 SPY -2.0%）","早期 Neutron 火箭时间线担忧（RKLB）","情绪驱动的双向波动"]},"2026-02-12":{"title":"Spring melt-up on a tech-led risk-on regime (+115%)","body":"Yet another +115% high-beta surge into a late-May-2026 peak as the regime turned tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +47.7%, growth>value +6.1, VIX 21->16). The build-out story stayed intact and risk appetite carried the highest-torque theme to a new high — the basket +115% against a +10.8% index in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP-SPY -7.0%).","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +47.7%, VIX 21->16) carries the melt-up","Build-out fundamentals (launch cadence, satcom, defense-space)","High-beta torque to a new cycle high (basket +115% vs SPY +10.8%)","Narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP-SPY -7.0%)"],"title_zh":"春季融涨于科技引领的风险偏好 regime（+115%）","body_zh":"又一次 +115% 高贝塔飙升至 2026 年 5 月底高点，regime 转向科技/半导体引领风险偏好（半导体 +47.7%、成长>价值 +6.1、VIX 21->16）。建设故事完好，风险偏好把扭矩最高的主题推向新高——篮子 +115% 对 +10.8% 指数，处于狭窄大盘股行情（RSP-SPY -7.0%）。","drivers_zh":["科技/半导体引领风险偏好 regime（半导体 +47.7%、VIX 21->16）推动融涨","建设基本面（发射节奏、卫星通信、国防航天）","高贝塔扭矩创周期新高（篮子 +115% 对 SPY +10.8%）","狭窄大盘股市场广度（RSP-SPY -7.0%）"]},"2026-05-28":{"title":"Neutron-delay drawdown into a risk-off, strong-dollar tape (-42%)","body":"The current selloff. RKLB-style names dumped as Neutron-rocket qualification setbacks and a delayed maiden flight (slipping toward mid-2026) collided with profit-taking off a parabolic high — exactly the 35%+ drawdown this group is structurally prone to. The regime turned risk-off/stagflation-ish (VIX 16->19, oil -19.1%, growth-value -10.0%, dollar firming +2.4%, defensives bid), and high beta meant the basket fell -42% against a -2.4% index. Backlogs stayed intact ($1B+), but space trades on milestones and torque, not backlog. Now 'Rolling over' (RS #26) — a high-volatility theme back in its risk-off phase.","drivers":["Risk-off/stagflation tilt (VIX 16->19, growth-value -10.0%, dollar +2.4%) caps the high-beta theme","Neutron-rocket qualification setback / maiden-flight delay (RKLB)","Profit-taking off a parabolic late-May high (-42% vs SPY -2.4%)","Milestone-driven selloff despite intact $1B+ backlog"],"title_zh":"Neutron 延期回撤进入避险、强美元行情（-42%）","body_zh":"当前的抛售。RKLB 这类个股因 Neutron 火箭资格测试受挫、首飞延期（滑向 2026 年年中）与抛物线高点获利了结叠加而暴跌——正是该板块结构性易发的 35%+ 回撤。regime 转向避险/类滞胀（VIX 16->19、油价 -19.1%、成长-价值 -10.0%、美元转强 +2.4%、防御获买盘），高贝塔意味着篮子跌 -42% 对 -2.4% 指数。积压完好（逾 10 亿美元），但太空靠里程碑和扭矩，而非积压。如今'见顶回落'（相对强度第 26 位）——高波动主题重回避险阶段。","drivers_zh":["避险/类滞胀倾斜（VIX 16->19、成长-价值 -10.0%、美元 +2.4%）压制高贝塔主题","Neutron 火箭资格测试受挫/首飞延期（RKLB）","5 月底抛物线高点的获利了结（-42% 对 SPY -2.4%）","里程碑驱动的抛售，尽管逾 10 亿美元积压完好"]}}},"b-industrial_distribution":{"now":"Industrial Distribution & Capital Goods (Grainger/Fastenal-type MRO distributors, equipment rental, short-cycle tooling; XLI proxy) is the late-cycle workhorse — the boring-but-effective, lower-beta end of industrials. It's 'Trending' at RS-rank #15 (pos 67.2), up +58% off the April-2025 tariff-crash low, and the current regime suits it: a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%, oil +19.2%) rewards capex-cyclicals over pure AI beta. The thesis is restock + nonresidential construction + pricing power — distributors sell the picks-and-shovels (fasteners, tools, MRO) to everyone building factories and grids. Quality, steady, lower-beta compounders rather than a torque trade — precisely why they hold up better than the speculative themes when the tape gets choppy, and why a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) only mildly dents the multinationals here.","now_zh":"工业分销与资本货物（Grainger/Fastenal 这类 MRO 分销商、设备租赁、短周期工具；XLI 为代理）是后周期主力——工业群组中乏味却有效、低贝塔的一端。它'趋势中'，相对强度排名第 15 位（pos 67.2），自 2025 年 4 月关税崩盘低点 +58%，当前 regime 也对它有利：一个广度扩张的再通胀/增长上行行情（周期股 +11.2% 对防御 +6.9%、等权跑赢市值权重 +2.9%、油价 +19.2%）奖励资本开支周期股而非纯 AI 高贝塔。其逻辑是补库+非住宅建设+定价权——分销商向所有建工厂、建电网的人出售'镐与铲'（紧固件、工具、MRO）。它们是优质、稳健、低贝塔的复利机器，而非扭矩交易——这恰是它们在行情震荡时比投机主题更抗跌的原因，也是走强美元（DXY +3.4%）在此仅轻微影响跨国企业的原因。","legs":{"2021-11-16":{"title":"Hiking-bear, rate-and-dollar de-rate (-25%)","body":"Distributors de-rated through H1 2022 with the broad cyclical complex in a stagflation-ish regime — yields surged (TLT -22.0%), the dollar ripped (DXY +9.2%) and VIX ran 16->31 — as the Fed-hiking bear and recession fears mounted. A multiple compression, not an earnings break: short-cycle demand stayed firm under the price weakness, but the surging dollar and yields hit the rate-sensitive cyclical (cyclicals -14.6% vs defensives -5.3%).","drivers":["Rate-regime + dollar shock (TLT -22.0%, DXY +9.2%) compress cyclical multiples","Stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 16->31) as recession fears mount","China lockdowns / supply-chain noise","Defensives led (-5.3% vs -14.6%) in the flight-to-safety"],"title_zh":"加息熊市、利率与美元去估值（-25%）","body_zh":"分销商连同大盘周期群组在 2022 年上半年于类滞胀 regime 去估值——收益率飙升（TLT -22.0%）、美元暴涨（DXY +9.2%）、VIX 16->31——美联储加息熊市和衰退担忧加剧。这是倍数压缩而非盈利断裂：价格疲软下短周期需求保持稳健，但飙升的美元与收益率冲击利率敏感的周期股（周期股 -14.6% 对防御 -5.3%）。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime+美元冲击（TLT -22.0%、DXY +9.2%）压缩周期股倍数","类滞胀避险（VIX 16->31），衰退担忧加剧","中国封控/供应链噪音","避险中防御领先（-5.3% 对 -14.6%）"]},"2022-06-17":{"title":"Summer relief bounce in a goldilocks risk-on window (+26%)","body":"Caught the broad mid-2022 relief rally as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up (SMH +18.5%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 31->20) on premature Fed-pause hopes. Multiple-driven, with resilient distributor fundamentals as a floor — cyclicals and defensives moved together (+16.4% vs +15.2%) in a broad, lower-conviction bounce.","drivers":["Goldilocks risk-on bounce (SMH +18.5%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 31->20)","Premature 'Fed pause' hopes lift the complex","Resilient MRO/short-cycle demand as a floor","Broad participation (cyclicals +16.4% vs defensives +15.2%)"],"title_zh":"夏季纾困反弹于 goldilocks 风险偏好窗口（+26%）","body_zh":"搭上 2022 年年中大盘纾困反弹，regime 转向 goldilocks/增长上行（半导体 +18.5%、成长>价值 +7.2、VIX 31->20），因过早的美联储暂停预期。倍数驱动，分销商稳健基本面提供托底——周期与防御同步（+16.4% 对 +15.2%），是一次广泛、低信念的反弹。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 风险偏好反弹（半导体 +18.5%、成长>价值 +7.2、VIX 31->20）","过早的'美联储暂停'预期抬升群组","稳健的 MRO/短周期需求托底","广泛参与（周期股 +16.4% 对防御 +15.2%）"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole rate-driven flush (-18%)","body":"Powell's hawkish reset triggered a rate-driven slowdown regime (yields surged, TLT -10.4%; DXY +7.1%; VIX 20->32) into a late-September low. Macro de-risking briefly overrode the group's defensive-cyclical quality — but its lower beta showed, falling -17.9% peak-to-trough versus far deeper drawdowns in the speculative themes.","drivers":["Rate-regime move: yields surged (TLT -10.4%) on hawkish Jackson Hole","Risk-off slowdown (VIX 20->32) across equities","Dollar strength (DXY +7.1%) pressure","Lower beta cushions vs speculative peers"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔利率驱动冲刷（-18%）","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派重置触发利率驱动的放缓 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -10.4%；DXY +7.1%；VIX 20->32），跌至 9 月底低点。宏观去风险短暂压过该板块防御性周期的优质属性——但其低贝塔得以显现，相对投机主题远浅的回撤。","drivers_zh":["利率 regime 移动：收益率飙升（TLT -10.4%），杰克逊霍尔鹰派","股市避险放缓（VIX 20->32）","美元走强（DXY +7.1%）压力","低贝塔相对投机同行提供缓冲"]},"2022-09-26":{"title":"The late-cycle compounder bull inside a goldilocks melt-up (+100%)","body":"From the autumn-2022 low distributors doubled over two-plus years — a steady, quality-led advance riding a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime (SMH +160.8%, growth>value +34.6, VIX 32->15, weaker dollar -6.4%). Pricing power held through disinflation, the reshoring/electrification build-out fed nonres-construction demand, and the Nov-2024 'reshoring trade' carried it to a top. As a lower-beta name it didn't lead the narrow mega-cap tape (RSP-SPY -18.3%), but the weaker dollar was a clean tailwind — the late-cycle compounder thesis working cleanly.","drivers":["Goldilocks melt-up regime (SMH +160.8%, growth>value, VIX 32->15) lifts cyclicals","Weaker dollar (DXY -6.4%) tailwind; pricing power through disinflation","Reshoring/electrification build-out drives nonres-construction demand","2024 soft landing + Nov-2024 'reshoring trade'; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -18.3%)"],"title_zh":"后周期复利机器牛市，置于 goldilocks 融涨之中（+100%）","body_zh":"从 2022 年秋季低点起分销商翻倍——一段稳健、由优质引领的上涨，搭乘 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀 regime（半导体 +160.8%、成长>价值 +34.6、VIX 32->15、美元走弱 -6.4%）。定价权在去通胀中保持，回流/电气化建设浪潮喂养非住宅建设需求，2024 年 11 月'回流交易'把它带至高点。作为低贝塔品种，它未领涨狭窄大盘股行情（RSP-SPY -18.3%），但走弱美元是干净顺风——后周期复利机器逻辑干净运行。","drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 融涨 regime（半导体 +160.8%、成长>价值、VIX 32->15）抬升周期股","美元走弱（DXY -6.4%）顺风；定价权穿越去通胀","回流/电气化建设浪潮驱动非住宅建设需求","2024 年软着陆+2024 年 11 月'回流交易'；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -18.3%）"]},"2024-11-25":{"title":"Tariff-crash selloff, but lower beta cushions (-27%)","body":"Sold off into the April-8 tariff crash as the regime flipped violently risk-off (VIX 15->52, SMH -25.8%, SPHB-SPLV -21.0%) on input-cost, demand and supply-chain fears. The drawdown was real but shallower than the higher-beta industrial themes — defensives led (-7.6% vs cyclicals -18.9%) and the group's lower-beta quality showed in a -27% vs the speculative names' -33%+.","drivers":["Violent risk-off regime (VIX 15->52, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -21.0%) drives the selloff","April-2025 reciprocal-tariff crash","Input-cost and short-cycle demand fears","Lower beta cushions vs higher-beta peers; defensives led (-7.6% vs -18.9%)"],"title_zh":"关税崩盘抛售，但低贝塔提供缓冲（-27%）","body_zh":"抛售至 4 月 8 日关税崩盘，regime 剧烈翻转为避险（VIX 15->52、半导体 -25.8%、SPHB-SPLV -21.0%），因投入成本、需求和供应链担忧。回撤真实但浅于高贝塔工业主题——防御领先（-7.6% 对周期 -18.9%），板块低贝塔优质属性显现于 -27% 对投机品种的 -33%+。","drivers_zh":["剧烈避险 regime（VIX 15->52、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -21.0%）驱动抛售","2025 年 4 月对等关税崩盘","投入成本与短周期需求担忧","低贝塔相对高贝塔同行提供缓冲；防御领先（-7.6% 对 -18.9%）"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Recovery & build-out leg, broad cyclical bid (+58%)","body":"Off the April-8 low distributors recovered +58% into June 2026 in an explosive risk-on regime (VIX 52->19, SMH +255%, weaker dollar -1.5%) — though as a lower-beta name it advanced less than the parabolic semis (+58% vs the high-beta themes' +90%). Pricing power held and the reshoring/electrification/AI-power construction wave fed steady demand. The basket is 'Trending' (RS #15), a quality late-cycle leader that compounds rather than spikes, holding up even as 2026's strong dollar and sticky CPI pressure the broader capital-goods buyer.","drivers":["Explosive risk-on regime (VIX 52->19, SMH +255%) lifts cyclicals; lower beta = steadier +58%","Reshoring / electrification / AI-power construction demand","Pricing power and restock support margins","Late-cycle quality holds up vs. higher-beta peers; narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -8.8%)"],"title_zh":"回升与建设腿段，广泛周期买盘（+58%）","body_zh":"从 4 月 8 日低点起分销商回升 +58% 至 2026 年 6 月，处于爆发性风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->19、半导体 +255%、美元走弱 -1.5%）——但作为低贝塔品种，涨幅小于抛物线半导体（+58% 对高贝塔主题的 +90%）。定价权保持，回流/电气化/AI 电力建设浪潮喂养稳定需求。该篮子'趋势中'（相对强度第 15 位），一个复利而非尖峰的优质后周期领头羊，即便 2026 年强势美元和粘性 CPI 压制更广泛资本货物买家仍表现抗跌。","drivers_zh":["爆发性风险偏好 regime（VIX 52->19、半导体 +255%）抬升周期股；低贝塔=更稳的 +58%","回流/电气化/AI 电力建设需求","定价权与补库支撑利润率","后周期优质属性相对高贝塔同行更抗跌；市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -8.8%）"]}}},"b-critical_minerals":{"now":"Critical Minerals & Rare Earths (MP Materials/lithium/allied ex-China supply; REMX proxy) is the most policy-driven, most violent basket here — and right now the most beaten-down, tagged 'Bottoming' at pos 1.6 (range floor), RS-rank #27. It's idiosyncratic: a supply-policy story, not a demand story, so it marches to China export-control headlines more than to the macro regime. But it is still high-beta, and the current backdrop is no help — a broadening reflation tape that nonetheless carries a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%, a headwind for materials). China controls rare-earth processing and weaponizes it (the strict April-2025 regime, then a June-2026 escalation sanctioning MP/USA Rare Earth and barring 46 US firms incl. LMT/RTX/Boeing/GD). The US response is state-backed: a ~15% Pentagon stake in MP, a $110/kg NdPr floor, a 10-year magnet offtake, a $725M metallization loan. The result is a complex that gapped +715% (2024-25), then whipsawed 30-43% as the trade war escalated and de-escalated. Whippy, headline-hostage, asymmetric — a strategic theme trading like an option on geopolitics.","now_zh":"关键矿产与稀土（MP Materials/锂/盟友去中国化供应；REMX 为代理）是此处最受政策驱动、最剧烈的篮子——眼下也最被打压，标记为'筑底'，pos 1.6（区间底部），相对强度排名第 27 位。它特立独行：是供应政策故事而非需求故事，故更随中国出口管制头条而非宏观 regime 起舞。但它仍是高贝塔，当前背景也无助——一个广度扩张的再通胀行情却携带走强的美元（DXY +3.4%，对材料是逆风）。中国掌控稀土加工并以之为武器（2025 年 4 月严格体制，继而 2026 年 6 月升级，制裁 MP/USA Rare Earth 并排除 46 家美国企业含 LMT/RTX/波音/GD）。美国回应是国家背书：五角大楼约 15% MP 股权、110 美元/公斤镨钕下限、10 年磁体包销、7.25 亿美元金属化贷款。结果是一个群组跳涨 +715%（2024-25），随后在贸易战升级与缓和中以 30-43% 来回鞭打。鞭打剧烈、被头条挟持、不对称——一个交易起来像地缘政治期权的战略主题。","legs":{"2021-11-12":{"title":"Hiking-bear, high-beta commodity de-rate (-28%)","body":"Rare-earth and lithium names de-rated through early 2022 in a stagflation-ish, risk-off regime (VIX 16->30, defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals -4.5%) as the Fed-hiking bear and China lockdowns hit commodity-linked equities. Speculative, high-beta materials sold off ahead of the broad market — the basket fell -28% while SPY was only -7.4%.","drivers":["Stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 16->30) hits high-beta commodity equities","Fed-hiking bear; basket -28% vs SPY -7.4%","China lockdowns dampen materials demand","Flight-to-safety (defensives +0.3% vs -4.5%)"],"title_zh":"加息熊市、高贝塔大宗去估值（-28%）","body_zh":"稀土和锂个股在 2022 年初于类滞胀、避险 regime（VIX 16->30、防御 +0.3% 对周期 -4.5%）去估值，美联储加息熊市和中国封控冲击大宗相关股票。投机性、高贝塔材料领先大盘抛售——篮子跌 -28%，而 SPY 仅 -7.4%。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀避险（VIX 16->30）冲击高贝塔大宗股票","美联储加息熊市；篮子 -28% 对 SPY -7.4%","中国封控抑制材料需求","避险（防御 +0.3% 对 -4.5%）"]},"2022-01-27":{"title":"Commodity-supercycle bounce against a yield surge (+46%)","body":"Rallied with the 2022 commodity/inflation spike even as the rate regime savaged the index — yields surged (TLT -22.3%, SPY -1.8%) and the dollar firmed (DXY +4.6%), but the Russia-Ukraine supply shock lifted the whole materials complex into early 2023. A commodity-driven move decoupled from the equity tape: breadth was broad (RSP-SPY +6.5%) and lithium prices ran hot.","drivers":["Commodity-supercycle bid decoupled from the rate regime (TLT -22.3%, SPY -1.8%)","Russia-Ukraine supply-shock bid for materials","Lithium price spike on EV demand","Broad breadth (RSP-SPY +6.5%) despite a firming dollar (DXY +4.6%)"],"title_zh":"大宗超级周期反弹，逆收益率飙升（+46%）","body_zh":"随 2022 年大宗/通胀飙升上涨，即便利率 regime 重创指数——收益率飙升（TLT -22.3%、SPY -1.8%）、美元转强（DXY +4.6%），但俄乌供应冲击抬升整个材料群组至 2023 年初。一次与股市行情脱钩的大宗驱动行情：市场广度宽（RSP-SPY +6.5%），锂价火热。","drivers_zh":["大宗超级周期买盘与利率 regime 脱钩（TLT -22.3%、SPY -1.8%）","俄乌供应冲击对材料的买盘","EV 需求推动锂价飙升","市场广度宽（RSP-SPY +6.5%），尽管美元转强（DXY +4.6%）"]},"2023-02-02":{"title":"Lithium/rare-earth price collapse while the index melted up (-39%)","body":"A long, brutal bear as the 2022 commodity spike fully unwound — lithium prices crashed on oversupply and slowing EV growth, dragging the basket -39% for a full year into the February-2024 low. The regime was the opposite of helpful for this group: a goldilocks AI melt-up (SMH +56.9%, growth>value +27.8, narrow RSP-SPY -16.1%) where SPY rose +21% while commodities and these names bled — capital was chasing semis, not rare earths.","drivers":["Commodity bust vs a goldilocks AI melt-up (SPY +21% while basket -39%)","Lithium oversupply and price crash","Slowing EV-demand growth","Narrow tech-led breadth (RSP-SPY -16.1%) starves materials"],"title_zh":"锂/稀土价格崩盘，而指数融涨（-39%）","body_zh":"一段漫长残酷的熊市，2022 年大宗飙升彻底回吐——锂价因供过于求和 EV 增长放缓崩盘，把篮子拖累 -39% 整整一年至 2024 年 2 月低点。regime 对该板块恰恰相反地不利：一个 goldilocks AI 融涨（半导体 +56.9%、成长>价值 +27.8、狭窄 RSP-SPY -16.1%），SPY 涨 +21% 而大宗与这些个股流血——资金追逐半导体而非稀土。","drivers_zh":["大宗崩盘对 goldilocks AI 融涨（SPY +21% 而篮子 -39%）","锂供过于求与价格崩盘","EV 需求增长放缓","狭窄科技引领市场广度（RSP-SPY -16.1%）饿死材料"]},"2024-02-20":{"title":"The policy-driven moonshot, regime-agnostic (+715%)","body":"The defining leg — a staggering +715% over 20 months that ran almost entirely on policy, not the macro tape. As China tightened rare-earth export controls and the US/allied response crystallized (the 2025 Pentagon stake in MP, the $110/kg NdPr floor, magnet offtake), the ex-China supply chain re-rated from value trap to strategic must-own. The backdrop was a benign goldilocks regime (SMH +69.4%, VIX 15->21, weaker dollar -4.8%) that didn't hurt, but this was a national-security re-rating: government backing turned a commodity story into a must-own, and the stocks gapped into an October-2025 top.","drivers":["Policy re-rating dominates the regime (+715% as SPY +36%, weaker dollar -4.8%)","China tightens rare-earth export controls (the strict 2025 regime)","US/allied ex-China supply policy (Pentagon stake in MP, $110/kg NdPr floor, 10-yr offtake)","Rare earths re-rated as a national-security imperative"],"title_zh":"政策驱动的登月，与 regime 无关（+715%）","body_zh":"决定性的一段——20 个月内惊人的 +715%，几乎全凭政策而非宏观行情。随中国收紧稀土出口管制、美国/盟友回应成型（2025 年五角大楼入股 MP、110 美元/公斤镨钕下限、磁体包销），去中国化供应链从价值陷阱重估为战略必持。背景是良性的 goldilocks regime（半导体 +69.4%、VIX 15->21、美元走弱 -4.8%），无害但非主因：这是国家安全重估，政府背书把大宗故事变成必持，股票跳涨至 2025 年 10 月高点。","drivers_zh":["政策重估主导 regime（+715% 而 SPY +36%、美元走弱 -4.8%）","中国收紧稀土出口管制（严格的 2025 年体制）","美国/盟友去中国化供应政策（五角大楼入股 MP、110 美元/公斤镨钕下限、10 年包销）","稀土被重估为国家安全要务"]},"2025-10-14":{"title":"Parabolic-top flush on a mild risk wobble (-43%)","body":"A sharp -43% reset off the October-2025 high — a parabolic +715% run does not unwind gently. The regime barely moved (SPY +1.2%, VIX 21->20, breadth flat), but high beta plus extreme extension meant the most-stretched theme on the board flushed -43% on a basically flat tape, on profit-taking alone.","drivers":["High beta + extreme extension flush on a flat tape (-43% vs SPY +1.2%)","Profit-taking off a parabolic +715% run","Late-2025 broad risk wobble (VIX 21->20)","Over-extended theme de-risks first"],"title_zh":"抛物线顶部冲刷于轻微风险动摇（-43%）","body_zh":"从 2025 年 10 月高点的急剧 -43% 重置——抛物线 +715% 行情不会温和回吐。regime 几乎不动（SPY +1.2%、VIX 21->20、广度持平），但高贝塔加极度延伸意味着面板上最拉伸的主题在基本持平的行情中仅凭获利了结就冲刷 -43%。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔+极度延伸于平淡行情冲刷（-43% 对 SPY +1.2%）","抛物线 +715% 行情后的获利了结","2025 年底大盘风险动摇（VIX 21->20）","过度延伸主题最先去风险"]},"2025-11-06":{"title":"Policy-escalation rip on a broadening tape (+80%)","body":"Snapped back +80% into late January 2026 as trade-war escalation re-ignited the supply-security bid — paradoxically, every fresh export-control headline is bullish for the ex-China names that benefit from scarcity. The regime helped at the margin (broadening RSP-SPY +4.2%, VIX 20->16, weaker dollar -2.1%, materials-led leadership), but the driver was policy: the basket +80% against a +3.1% index.","drivers":["Policy escalation drives the rip (basket +80% vs SPY +3.1%)","Trade-war / export-control re-escalation re-ignites the supply-security bid","Broadening tape (RSP-SPY +4.2%, weaker dollar -2.1%) a tailwind","Materials-led leadership; scarcity premium re-prices"],"title_zh":"政策升级暴涨于广度扩张行情（+80%）","body_zh":"弹回 +80% 至 2026 年 1 月底，因贸易战升级重新点燃供应安全买盘——悖论地，每条新出口管制头条对受益于稀缺的去中国化个股是利好。regime 边际有利（广度扩张 RSP-SPY +4.2%、VIX 20->16、美元走弱 -2.1%、材料引领），但驱动是政策：篮子 +80% 对 +3.1% 指数。","drivers_zh":["政策升级驱动暴涨（篮子 +80% 对 SPY +3.1%）","贸易战/出口管制再升级重新点燃供应安全买盘","广度扩张行情（RSP-SPY +4.2%、美元走弱 -2.1%）顺风","材料引领；稀缺溢价重新定价"]},"2026-01-23":{"title":"De-escalation pullback into a stagflation, strong-dollar tape (-30%)","body":"Gave back -30% into late March as the trade war cooled (a partial export-control suspension was negotiated, to Nov-10-2026). Easing tensions remove the scarcity premium — the inverse of the escalation rip — and the regime turned against it: a stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 16->31, oil +68.5% on the Hormuz shock) with a firming dollar (DXY +3.0%, a direct materials headwind). The basket -30% on a -8.1% index.","drivers":["Stagflation-ish risk-off + strong dollar (VIX 16->31, DXY +3.0%) compound the de-rate","Partial export-control suspension negotiated (to Nov-2026)","Scarcity premium unwinds on de-escalation","Basket -30% vs SPY -8.1%"],"title_zh":"降级回落进入类滞胀、强美元行情（-30%）","body_zh":"随贸易战降温（谈成部分出口管制暂停，至 2026 年 11 月 10 日），回吐 -30% 至 3 月底。紧张缓和移除稀缺溢价——升级暴涨的反面——而 regime 转为不利：一个类滞胀避险（VIX 16->31、油价 +68.5% 因霍尔木兹冲击）伴随美元转强（DXY +3.0%，对材料的直接逆风）。篮子 -30% 对 -8.1% 指数。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀避险+强美元（VIX 16->31、DXY +3.0%）加重去估值","谈成部分出口管制暂停（至 2026 年 11 月）","降级使稀缺溢价回吐","篮子 -30% 对 SPY -8.1%"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"Re-escalation bounce on a high-beta risk-on flip (+61%)","body":"Another +61% whip higher into early May as supply-security headlines flared again, amplified by a regime flip to tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +51.6%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 31->17, weaker dollar -2.5%). The pattern is unmistakable: this basket is an option on US-China trade tension, ripping on escalation and fading on detente — and high beta turns a +16% index into a +61% basket move.","drivers":["High-beta risk-on flip (SMH +51.6%, VIX 31->17) amplifies the bounce (+61% vs SPY +16%)","Renewed supply-security / trade-tension headlines","Scarcity-premium re-pricing; weaker dollar (DXY -2.5%) tailwind","Option-like sensitivity to US-China tension"],"title_zh":"再升级反弹于高贝塔风险偏好翻转（+61%）","body_zh":"随供应安全头条再度爆发，又一次 +61% 鞭打走高至 5 月初，被 regime 翻转为科技/半导体引领风险偏好（半导体 +51.6%、成长>价值 +7.2、VIX 31->17、美元走弱 -2.5%）放大。模式明白无误：该篮子是中美贸易紧张的期权，升级则暴涨、缓和则消退——高贝塔把 +16% 指数变成 +61% 篮子涨幅。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔风险偏好翻转（半导体 +51.6%、VIX 31->17）放大反弹（+61% 对 SPY +16%）","供应安全/贸易紧张头条重燃","稀缺溢价重新定价；美元走弱（DXY -2.5%）顺风","对中美紧张的期权式敏感性"]},"2026-05-06":{"title":"Current de-risk to the lows, policy-supported washout (-32%)","body":"The current selloff — down -32% to pos 1.6 (range floor), tagged 'Bottoming'. The June-2026 escalation (China sanctioning MP/USA Rare Earth and barring 46 US firms) is a double-edged headline: bullish for the long-run scarcity thesis, but it landed in a stagflation-ish, strong-dollar tape (VIX 17->18, DXY +3.4%, oil -27.2%, defensives bid) that drained the high-beta materials complex. With the Pentagon backstop ($110/kg floor, $725M metallization loan) under the leaders, this reads as a policy-supported washout in an unhelpful regime rather than a structural break.","drivers":["Stagflation-ish, strong-dollar tape (DXY +3.4%, defensives bid) flushes high-beta materials","June-2026 China sanctions on MP/USA Rare Earth + 46 US-firm procurement ban","Pentagon backstop ($110/kg floor, $725M metallization loan) under the leaders","Bottoming at the range floor (pos 1.6) on a policy-supported washout"],"title_zh":"当前去风险至低位，政策支持的洗盘（-32%）","body_zh":"当前的抛售——下跌 -32% 至 pos 1.6（区间底部），标记为'筑底'。2026 年 6 月升级（中国制裁 MP/USA Rare Earth 并排除 46 家美国企业）是双刃头条：对长期稀缺逻辑利好，但它落在类滞胀、强美元行情（VIX 17->18、DXY +3.4%、油价 -27.2%、防御获买盘）中，抽干了高贝塔材料群组。在五角大楼后盾（110 美元/公斤下限、7.25 亿美元金属化贷款）支撑龙头之下，这读作不利 regime 中政策支持的洗盘，而非结构性断裂。","drivers_zh":["类滞胀、强美元行情（DXY +3.4%、防御获买盘）冲刷高贝塔材料","2026 年 6 月中国制裁 MP/USA Rare Earth+46 家美国企业采购禁令","五角大楼后盾（110 美元/公斤下限、7.25 亿美元金属化贷款）支撑龙头","在区间底部（pos 1.6）于政策支持的洗盘中筑底"]}}},"b-insurance":{"now":"Insurance & brokers (KIE) keep grinding higher in a low-drama uptrend — the quietest compounder in Financials and a low-beta anchor in a reflation/growth-up tape where Tech leads (+24.3%) and Financials lag (−2.7%). The whole story since mid-2022 is one long rally: a hard property/casualty pricing cycle (rate-on-line still firm), and a rate tailwind that turned every dollar of insurance float into real investment income once the Fed left policy restrictive. Brokers (Marsh, Aon, Gallagher) compound fees regardless of the rate path; P&C names (Progressive, Chubb, Travelers) earn the underwriting margin. With the dollar firm (+3.4% DXY), breadth broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and VIX a calm 14→18, this is a hold-and-collect, not a chase. The 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock and a Fed back in hiking bias are mild positives here (more investment income, no credit blow-up), which is exactly why this low-beta group is where you hide when the high-beta AI trade wobbles.","now_zh":"保险与经纪（KIE）在低波动上行趋势中继续稳步走高——金融板块中最安静的复利机器，也是再通胀/增长向上行情里的低贝塔锚（科技领涨+24.3%、金融落后−2.7%）。自2022年中以来就是一段长牛：财产险（P&C）定价处于硬周期（rate-on-line 仍坚挺），加上利率顺风——美联储维持限制性政策后，每一美元保险浮存金都转化为真实的投资收益。经纪商（Marsh、Aon、Gallagher）无论利率如何都靠手续费复利增长；P&C 巨头（Progressive、Chubb、Travelers）赚承保利润。美元坚挺（+3.4% DXY）、市场广度转宽（RSP 跑赢 SPY +2.9%）、VIX 平稳于14→18，本组属于持有收息、而非追涨的标的。2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击叠加美联储重回加息倾向，对这一低贝塔组温和利好（投资收益更多、无信用爆雷），这正是高贝塔 AI 交易动摇时资金避险的去处。","legs":{"2022-04-20":{"title":"2022 rate-shock dip (−16% in a −18% tape)","title_zh":"2022年利率冲击回调（大盘−18%中跌−16%）","body":"Insurance sold off with the broad 2022 Fed-hiking bear (SPY −18%, VIX 20→33), but as a low-beta defensive it fell far more shallowly than tech — a −16% drawdown versus 30%+ in growth, in a rate-regime move where the 10Y surged (TLT −7.8%). Higher discount rates hit every equity, yet for insurers the same rising rates were a long-term gift: bond reinvestment yields were climbing, and a hard P&C pricing cycle was already underway after years of catastrophe losses. This was a macro/rates drawdown, not a business-model crack.","body_zh":"保险随2022年美联储加息熊市回调（SPY −18%、VIX 20→33），但作为低贝塔防御品，跌幅远浅于科技——回撤仅约−16%，而成长股跌逾30%；这是一次利率主导的下跌，10Y 飙升（TLT −7.8%）。更高的贴现率压制所有股票，但对保险公司而言，同样的利率上行是长期礼物：债券再投资收益率正在攀升，且在多年巨灾损失之后，P&C 硬定价周期已经启动。这是宏观/利率回撤，而非商业模式破裂。","drivers":["Rate-regime move: 10Y surged (TLT −7.8%) compressed all equity multiples","Low-beta defensive: −16% vs 30%+ in growth in a −18% tape","Hard P&C pricing cycle already lifting rate-on-line","Rising reinvestment yields = future float income"],"drivers_zh":["利率主导下跌：10Y 飙升（TLT −7.8%）压缩全市场估值","低贝塔防御：大盘−18%中跌−16%，远浅于成长股逾30%","P&C 硬定价周期已在抬升 rate-on-line","再投资收益率上升＝未来浮存金收益"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"The quiet +96% compounder rode the goldilocks tape (Jun '22 → Apr '25)","title_zh":"安静的+96%复利行情乘 goldilocks 顺风（2022年6月→2025年4月）","body":"From the June 2022 low, insurance rallied ~96% in an almost straight line through a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime — SPY +61%, VIX 33→22, semis +114.5% — yet as a low-beta name it didn't need the melt-up: it ignored every macro storm (SVB Mar '23, the 2024 Fed cuts and election, the April 2025 tariff crash). The engine is structural — a multi-year hard pricing cycle (insurers raising premiums faster than claims inflation) layered on a rate tailwind (the 10Y stayed elevated, TLT −9.5% over the leg) that made insurance float genuinely profitable for the first time in a decade. Brokers compounded fees; P&C names compounded underwriting margin. In a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY −20.1%), this was the textbook steady compounder — the place capital rotates to when the speculative trade gets scary. The leg's end near April 2025 marks where the basket cooled off its peak, not where the thesis broke.","body_zh":"自2022年6月低点起，保险在 goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的环境中近乎直线上涨约96%——SPY +61%、VIX 33→22、半导体 +114.5%——但作为低贝塔标的，它并不依赖这场融涨：它无视一切宏观风暴（2023年3月 SVB、2024年美联储降息与大选、2025年4月关税崩盘）。引擎是结构性的——多年期硬定价周期（保险公司提价快于理赔通胀）叠加利率顺风（10Y 维持高位，整段 TLT −9.5%），使保险浮存金十年来首次真正盈利。经纪商靠手续费复利，P&C 巨头靠承保利润复利。在狭窄、由大型股主导的行情中（RSP 落后 SPY −20.1%），这是教科书式的稳健复利——正是投机交易令人恐惧时资金轮动的去处。该行情在2025年4月附近见顶，标志篮子从高点回落，而非论点破裂。","drivers":["Goldilocks/growth-up regime (SPY +61%, VIX 33→22) — but low-beta KIE didn't need the melt-up","Multi-year hard P&C pricing cycle (premiums > claims inflation)","Rate tailwind (TLT −9.5%) turned float into real investment income","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP −20.1% vs SPY); shrugged off SVB + tariff crash"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks/增长向上环境（SPY +61%、VIX 33→22）——但低贝塔 KIE 不依赖融涨","多年期 P&C 硬定价周期（保费涨幅＞理赔通胀）","利率顺风（TLT −9.5%）使浮存金转为真实投资收益","狭窄大型股行情（RSP 落后 SPY −20.1%）；无视 SVB 与关税崩盘"]}}},"b-payments_fintech":{"now":"Payments & fintech (proxied by XLF) is at Prime entry — pos 15.1, washed out near the bottom of its range after a sharp ~29% drawdown from the August 2025 peak into early 2026. This is the rate-sensitive, consumer-spend-levered corner of Financials, and it splits into two betas: the networks (Visa, Mastercard) are toll-roads on transaction volume, while the disruptors (PayPal, Block/Square) trade like long-duration high-beta growth and get whipsawed by every move in rates and recession odds. The current tape is reflation/growth-up (Tech leads +24.3%), but Financials lag (−2.7%) and growth>value has reversed hard (growth−value −15.2%) with the dollar firm (+3.4% DXY) — a mixed setup. The 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock (CPI 4.2%) and a Fed back in hiking bias are the proximate weight: higher rates compress fintech multiples and a squeezed consumer threatens spend volume. But the low absolute position and the strong V/MA secular volume story are why this scores as a setup, not a sell — the cash-flow networks anchor the basket; the speculative fintech tail is the high-beta risk.","now_zh":"支付与金融科技（以 XLF 代理）处于黄金入场——pos 15.1，自2025年8月高点经历约−29%的急跌至2026年初后，已在区间底部附近被洗盘。这是金融板块中对利率敏感、与消费支出高度挂钩的角落，且分为两种贝塔：支付网络（Visa、Mastercard）是交易量上的收费公路，而颠覆者（PayPal、Block/Square）则像长久期高贝塔成长股，随利率与衰退概率的每次波动剧烈摇摆。当前行情为再通胀/增长向上（科技领涨+24.3%），但金融板块落后（−2.7%）、成长跑赢价值大幅反转（成长−价值 −15.2%）、美元坚挺（+3.4% DXY）——格局喜忧参半。2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击（CPI 4.2%）叠加美联储重回加息倾向，是当前压力的近因：高利率压缩金融科技估值，受挤压的消费者威胁支付量。但绝对位置偏低、加上 V/MA 强劲的长期交易量故事，正是本组被评为入场而非卖出的原因——现金流网络巨头锚定篮子；投机性金融科技尾部才是高贝塔风险所在。","legs":{"2021-09-23":{"title":"2021-22 duration purge — rate/dollar shock ground zero (−45%)","title_zh":"2021–22久期出清——利率/美元冲击震中（−45%）","body":"Fintech was ground zero for the 2022 Fed-hiking bear. As the most rate-sensitive, longest-duration, highest-beta corner of Financials, the basket fell ~45% while the broad market barely cracked (SPY −5.6%) — an outsized break driven by the rate/dollar shock (10Y surged, TLT −10.5%; DXY +6.4%) that obliterated growth-at-any-price names (PayPal off its pandemic highs, Block, Affirm) as discount rates rose and the work-from-home spend bubble deflated. Even the durable networks (V/MA) de-rated. This leg is the classic warning that fintech bundles two very different betas: toll-road networks and speculative long-duration growth.","body_zh":"金融科技是2022年美联储加息熊市的震中。作为金融板块中对利率最敏感、久期最长、贝塔最高的角落，篮子下跌约45%，而大盘几乎没破裂（SPY −5.6%）——这是由利率/美元冲击驱动的超额破裂（10Y 飙升 TLT −10.5%、DXY +6.4%），随贴现率上升、居家办公支付泡沫消退，不计价格的成长群（PayPal 从疫情高点滑落、Block、Affirm）被摧毁。即便耐用的网络巨头（V/MA）也估值下修。这段行情是经典警示：金融科技捆绑了两类截然不同的贝塔——收费公路网络与投机性长久期成长。","drivers":["Rate/dollar shock (TLT −10.5%, DXY +6.4%) → highest-duration multiple compression","Outsized break: −45% while SPY only −5.6%","Pandemic-stimulus spend bubble deflated; PYPL/SQ/AFRM crushed worst","Even durable networks (V/MA) de-rated"],"drivers_zh":["利率/美元冲击（TLT −10.5%、DXY +6.4%）→最长久期估值压缩","超额破裂：−45% 而 SPY 仅−5.6%","疫情刺激支付泡沫消退；PYPL/SQ/AFRM 跌幅最深","即便耐用网络（V/MA）也估值下修"]},"2022-03-14":{"title":"Oversold relief bounce on a tech-led rip (+27%)","title_zh":"超卖喘息反弹乘科技领涨急升（+27%）","body":"A sharp two-week snapback from the March 2022 low as the market priced the first Fed hike as 'known' and a tech/semis-led risk-on rip (SPY +11.0%, semis +18.8%, growth−value +8.7, VIX 32→19) lifted bombed-out long-duration growth. The high-beta fintech disruptors led the reflex bounce — but it was a counter-trend move inside the larger 2022 bear, in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY −2.4%), not a turn.","body_zh":"自2022年3月低点起为期两周的急速回升，市场把首次美联储加息视为已知，科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好急升（SPY +11.0%、半导体 +18.8%、成长−价值 +8.7、VIX 32→19）提振了被打入谷底的长久期成长。高 beta 金融科技颠覆者领涨反射性反弹——但这是更大2022年熊市中的逆势波动，处于狭窄的大型股行情（RSP 落后 SPY −2.4%），而非转折。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on rip (semis +18.8%, growth−value +8.7, VIX 32→19)","First Fed hike priced as 'known' → reflex bounce in long-duration growth","High-beta fintech disruptors led; narrow tape (RSP −2.4%)","Counter-trend move inside the 2022 bear"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨风险偏好急升（半导体 +18.8%、成长−价值 +8.7、VIX 32→19）","首次美联储加息被视为已知→长久期成长反射性反弹","高 beta 金融科技颠覆者领涨；狭窄行情（RSP −2.4%）","2022年熊市中的逆势波动"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Hawkish-repricing leg down — rate shock + slowdown scare (−32%)","title_zh":"鹰派重定价下行段——利率冲击＋放缓恐慌（−32%）","body":"The relief bounce reversed hard into May 2022 as the Fed signaled a faster, larger hiking path: the 10Y surged again (TLT −9.5%), the dollar ripped (DXY +5.5%), VIX 19→33, and the regime tipped to a slowdown/deflation-scare with high-beta crushed (high-beta minus low-vol −16.7%) and the whole market dropping (SPY −14.9%). Rate-sensitive fintech was hit worst — every upward revision in the terminal-rate path re-compressed the long-duration multiples. The networks held up far better than the speculative high-beta tail.","body_zh":"随美联储释放更快、更大的加息路径信号，喘息反弹急转直下至2022年5月：10Y 再度飙升（TLT −9.5%）、美元大涨（DXY +5.5%）、VIX 19→33，环境转向放缓/通缩恐慌，高贝塔被碾压（高贝塔减低波 −16.7%），全市场下跌（SPY −14.9%）。对利率敏感的金融科技受创最重——终端利率路径的每次上修都再次压缩长久期估值。网络巨头远比投机性高贝塔尾部抗跌。","drivers":["Rate shock (TLT −9.5%, DXY +5.5%) re-compressed long-duration multiples","Slowdown/deflation-scare regime; high-beta crushed (high-beta−low-vol −16.7%)","Fed signaled faster/larger hiking path; recession fear built","Networks held up better than the speculative high-beta tail"],"drivers_zh":["利率冲击（TLT −9.5%、DXY +5.5%）再压缩长久期估值","放缓/通缩恐慌环境；高贝塔被碾压（高贝塔−低波 −16.7%）","美联储释放更快/更大加息路径信号；衰退担忧累积","网络巨头比投机性高贝塔尾部抗跌"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Short-squeeze bounce in a hated group (+24%)","title_zh":"被嫌弃组别的空头回补反弹（+24%）","body":"A brief two-week bounce off the May 2022 low — an oversold, short-covering rally in a deeply hated group as the dollar softened (DXY −2.1%) and VIX eased 33→26. No fundamental catalyst; with the broad market only modestly up (SPY +5.7%) and risk appetite still fragile, the high-beta fintech tail caught a reflex bid that fizzled within weeks as the market resumed its slide toward the mid-2022 low.","body_zh":"自2022年5月低点起为期两周的短暂反弹——深度被嫌弃组别中的超卖、空头回补行情，美元走软（DXY −2.1%）、VIX 回落33→26。无基本面催化剂；大盘仅温和上涨（SPY +5.7%）、风险偏好仍脆弱之际，高贝塔金融科技尾部抓住反射性买盘，数周内即熄火，随后大盘恢复向2022年中低点的下滑。","drivers":["Oversold, short-covering rally in a deeply hated high-beta group","Dollar softened (DXY −2.1%), VIX eased 33→26","No fundamental catalyst; broad tape only +5.7%","Fizzled within weeks"],"drivers_zh":["深度被嫌弃高贝塔组别的超卖、空头回补行情","美元走软（DXY −2.1%）、VIX 回落33→26","无基本面催化剂；大盘仅+5.7%","数周内熄火"]},"2022-05-27":{"title":"Final 2022-bear leg down — rate shock + slowdown (−21%)","title_zh":"2022年熊市最后下行段——利率冲击＋放缓（−21%）","body":"The last leg of the first-half 2022 selloff into the mid-June low, as a hot CPI print forced the Fed into a 75bp hike and recession pricing peaked. The regime was slowdown/deflation-scare (SPY −11.7%, VIX 26→33, cyclicals −12.5% vs defensives −10.5%) with another rate jolt (TLT −6.0%); rate-sensitive fintech bottomed here with the broad market before the summer relief rally.","body_zh":"上半年2022年抛售的最后一段，至6月中旬低点，火热的 CPI 数据迫使美联储加息75个基点、衰退定价见顶。环境为放缓/通缩恐慌（SPY −11.7%、VIX 26→33、周期股 −12.5% 对防御股 −10.5%），伴随又一次利率震荡（TLT −6.0%）；对利率敏感的金融科技在此随大盘见底，随后迎来夏季喘息反弹。","drivers":["Slowdown/deflation-scare flush (SPY −11.7%, VIX 26→33)","Rate jolt (TLT −6.0%); hot CPI forced a 75bp Fed hike","Recession pricing peaked; bottomed with broad market at mid-June low","Set up the summer relief rally"],"drivers_zh":["放缓/通缩恐慌冲洗（SPY −11.7%、VIX 26→33）","利率震荡（TLT −6.0%）；火热 CPI 迫使美联储加息75个基点","衰退定价见顶；随大盘于6月中旬低点见底","为夏季喘息反弹铺路"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Summer relief rally on a tech-led risk-on melt-up (+34%)","title_zh":"夏季喘息反弹乘科技领涨风险偏好融涨（+34%）","body":"A strong +34% summer rally into mid-August 2022 on a tech/semis-led, goldilocks-leaning risk-on bounce (SPY +17.7%, semis +19.5%, growth−value +8.8, VIX 33→20, oil collapsing −26.4%) and hopes that inflation had peaked and the Fed might pivot. Long-duration fintech, the most beaten-down high-beta cohort, led the bounce — but it was a classic bear-market rally that reversed once Jackson Hole reaffirmed the hawkish stance.","body_zh":"随科技/半导体领涨、偏 goldilocks 的风险偏好反弹（SPY +17.7%、半导体 +19.5%、成长−价值 +8.8、VIX 33→20、油价暴跌−26.4%），加上通胀见顶、美联储或将转向的预期，出现强劲的+34%夏季反弹至2022年8月中旬。跌得最惨的高贝塔长久期金融科技领涨——但这是经典的熊市反弹，在杰克逊霍尔重申鹰派立场后即反转。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (semis +19.5%, growth−value +8.8, VIX 33→20)","Hopes inflation had peaked / Fed pivot; oil collapsed −26.4%","Most beaten-down long-duration high-beta fintech led","Classic bear-market rally; reversed after Jackson Hole"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨风险偏好融涨（半导体 +19.5%、成长−价值 +8.8、VIX 33→20）","通胀见顶/美联储转向预期；油价暴跌−26.4%","跌得最惨的长久期高贝塔金融科技领涨","经典熊市反弹；杰克逊霍尔后反转"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole give-back — the worst rate jolt of 2022 (−24%)","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔回吐——2022年最猛利率震荡（−24%）","body":"The summer rally unwound into November 2022 after Jackson Hole crushed pivot hopes and rates pushed to new cycle highs — the leg's TLT −17.8% is the most violent rate jolt of the whole 2022 saga, alongside DXY +3.8% and SPY −12.6%. Rate-sensitive fintech gave back most of the bounce as the long-duration discount-rate squeeze re-intensified; the basket made a higher low here as the broad market neared its October 2022 bottom.","body_zh":"夏季反弹在杰克逊霍尔粉碎转向预期、利率推升至新周期高点后回吐至2022年11月——本段 TLT −17.8% 是整个2022年剧本中最猛烈的利率震荡，伴随 DXY +3.8% 与 SPY −12.6%。对利率敏感的金融科技回吐大部分涨幅，长久期贴现率挤压重新加剧；篮子在此筑出更高的低点，恰逢大盘逼近2022年10月底部。","drivers":["Most violent rate jolt of 2022 (TLT −17.8%, DXY +3.8%)","Jackson Hole crushed pivot hopes; rates to new cycle highs","Long-duration discount-rate squeeze re-intensified","Higher low as broad market neared October bottom"],"drivers_zh":["2022年最猛烈利率震荡（TLT −17.8%、DXY +3.8%）","杰克逊霍尔粉碎转向预期；利率至新周期高点","长久期贴现率挤压重新加剧","大盘逼近10月底部时筑更高低点"]},"2022-11-09":{"title":"First bounce off the lows — rates fall, dollar breaks (+32%)","title_zh":"自低点的首次反弹——利率回落、美元破位（+32%）","body":"A sharp recovery into February 2023 as the regime flipped goldilocks: yields finally fell (TLT +15.3%), the dollar broke (DXY −8.0%), semis ripped +32.2% and high-beta led (high-beta minus low-vol +22.2%, VIX 26→19). The networks led on volume — Visa and Mastercard kept posting double-digit growth regardless of macro — while the bombed-out fintech disruptors got the high-beta oversold bounce. The move stalled by February 2023, just before the SVB regional-bank crisis re-introduced fear into anything Financials-coded.","body_zh":"随环境翻转为 goldilocks，出现急速反弹至2023年2月：收益率终于回落（TLT +15.3%）、美元破位（DXY −8.0%）、半导体急升+32.2%、高贝塔领涨（高贝塔减低波 +22.2%、VIX 26→19）。网络巨头凭交易量领涨——无论宏观如何，Visa 与 Mastercard 持续录得两位数增长——同时被打入谷底的金融科技颠覆者迎来高贝塔超卖反弹。该行情在2023年2月停滞，恰在 SVB 区域银行危机给一切带金融标签的资产重新注入恐惧之前。","drivers":["Goldilocks flip: yields fell (TLT +15.3%), dollar broke (DXY −8.0%)","High-beta led (semis +32.2%, high-beta−low-vol +22.2%, VIX 26→19)","Networks led on double-digit volume; disruptors got oversold bounce","Stalled into the Feb-2023 SVB scare"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 翻转：收益率回落（TLT +15.3%）、美元破位（DXY −8.0%）","高贝塔领涨（半导体 +32.2%、高贝塔−低波 +22.2%、VIX 26→19）","网络巨头凭两位数交易量领涨；颠覆者超卖反弹","行情停滞于2023年2月 SVB 恐慌前夕"]},"2023-02-02":{"title":"SVB-scare pullback — guilt by sector association (−22%)","title_zh":"SVB恐慌回调——板块关联的连坐（−22%）","body":"A −22% drop into May 2023 as the SVB regional-bank crisis hit anything Financials-coded — and notably this was an idiosyncratic Financials de-risk, not a market event (SPY −1.0%, VIX 19→18 barely moved), but breadth narrowed hard (RSP lagged SPY −6.3%). Payments got caught in the cross-asset de-risking even though the networks had no banking-deposit exposure — guilt by sector association. The basket bottomed in early May with the regional-bank low.","body_zh":"回落−22%至2023年5月，SVB 区域银行危机冲击一切带金融标签的资产——值得注意，这是个体化的金融板块去风险，而非市场事件（SPY −1.0%、VIX 19→18 几乎没动），但广度大幅收窄（RSP 落后 SPY −6.3%）。支付被卷入跨资产去风险，尽管网络巨头并无银行存款敞口——板块关联的连坐。篮子于5月初随区域银行低点见底。","drivers":["Idiosyncratic Financials de-risk: −22% while SPY only −1.0%, VIX flat 19→18","SVB crisis hit anything Financials-coded; breadth narrowed (RSP −6.3%)","Guilt by sector association (networks have no deposit risk)","Bottomed early May with regional-bank low"],"drivers_zh":["个体化金融去风险：−22% 而 SPY 仅−1.0%、VIX 持平19→18","SVB 危机冲击一切带金融标签资产；广度收窄（RSP −6.3%）","板块关联的连坐（网络无存款风险）","5月初随区域银行低点见底"]},"2023-05-02":{"title":"Post-SVB recovery on the genAI risk-on (+41%)","title_zh":"SVB后复苏乘生成式AI风险偏好（+41%）","body":"A strong +41% rebound into August 2023 as the SVB panic faded and the early genAI rally broadened into a tech/semis-led risk-on (SPY +11.5%, semis +30.0%, growth−value +8.8, VIX 18→14). The durable networks led on resilient consumer spend while the fintech disruptors caught the high-beta tailwind — even with the 10Y still rising (TLT −6.4%), the risk-on impulse and falling VIX dominated. A real recovery leg, not just a bounce.","body_zh":"强劲反弹+41%至2023年8月，SVB 恐慌消退、早期生成式 AI 行情扩散为科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好（SPY +11.5%、半导体 +30.0%、成长−价值 +8.8、VIX 18→14）。耐用的网络巨头凭借坚韧的消费支出领涨，金融科技颠覆者抓住高贝塔顺风——即便10Y 仍在上行（TLT −6.4%），风险偏好脉冲与回落的 VIX 占主导。这是真正的复苏行情，而非仅是反弹。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led genAI risk-on (semis +30.0%, growth−value +8.8, VIX 18→14)","SVB panic faded; Fed near end of hiking cycle","Durable networks led on resilient consumer spend; disruptors caught high-beta upside","Risk-on dominated despite the 10Y still rising (TLT −6.4%)"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨生成式 AI 风险偏好（半导体 +30.0%、成长−价值 +8.8、VIX 18→14）","SVB 恐慌消退；美联储接近加息尾声","耐用网络凭坚韧消费支出领涨；颠覆者抓住高贝塔上行","尽管10Y 仍上行（TLT −6.4%），风险偏好占主导"]},"2023-08-01":{"title":"Higher-for-longer dip — yield toward 5% (−23%)","title_zh":"更高更久回调——收益率逼近5%（−23%）","body":"A −23% pullback into late October 2023 as the 10-year yield spiked toward 5% on a 'higher-for-longer' Fed — a stagflation-ish, rate-driven selloff (TLT −13.5%, DXY +4.2%, VIX 14→21, SPY −9.7%) that hit all long-duration assets. Rate-sensitive fintech sold off with them, but this October 2023 low became the launchpad for the +117% bull run that followed.","body_zh":"回调−23%至2023年10月底，10年期收益率在美联储更高更久立场下飙向5%——一场偏滞胀、由利率驱动的抛售（TLT −13.5%、DXY +4.2%、VIX 14→21、SPY −9.7%）冲击所有长久期资产。对利率敏感的金融科技随之抛售，但这个2023年10月低点成为随后+117%牛市的发射台。","drivers":["Rate-driven stagflation-ish selloff (TLT −13.5%, DXY +4.2%, VIX 14→21)","10-year yield spiked toward 5% on 'higher-for-longer'","Rate-sensitive fintech sold with all long-duration assets","Oct-2023 low became launchpad for the +117% run"],"drivers_zh":["利率驱动的偏滞胀抛售（TLT −13.5%、DXY +4.2%、VIX 14→21）","10年期收益率在更高更久立场下飙向5%","对利率敏感金融科技随长久期资产抛售","2023年10月低点成为+117%行情发射台"]},"2023-10-27":{"title":"The +117% post-SVB-to-peak bull rode the goldilocks melt-up","title_zh":"SVB之后至高点的+117%牛市乘 goldilocks 融涨","body":"The big leg: from the October 2023 low, payments & fintech more than doubled (+117%) into February 2025 — 2.3x the broad market (SPY +51.4%) — riding a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (semis +87.2%, growth−value +23.3%, yields falling TLT +10.2%, VIX 21→15). Falling-rate expectations, a resilient US consumer, and the September 2024 Fed cuts re-rated the long-duration fintech names, while the networks compounded steadily on cross-border travel and ecommerce volume. The November 2024 election added a deregulation/M&A tailwind to the whole financial complex. In a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY −12.2%), the speculative high-beta tail (Block, Affirm, the BNPL cohort) earned its biggest returns alongside the durable V/MA core.","body_zh":"主升浪：自2023年10月低点起，支付与金融科技翻倍有余（+117%），一路涨至2025年2月——是大盘的2.3倍（SPY +51.4%），乘 goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的融涨（半导体 +87.2%、成长−价值 +23.3%、收益率回落 TLT +10.2%、VIX 21→15）。降息预期、坚韧的美国消费者、加上2024年9月美联储降息，使长久期金融科技股重估；同时网络巨头靠跨境旅行与电商交易量稳步复利。2024年11月大选为整个金融板块叠加放松监管/并购的顺风。在狭窄的大型股行情中（RSP 落后 SPY −12.2%），投机性高贝塔尾部（Block、Affirm、先买后付群）取得最大涨幅，与耐用的 V/MA 核心并肩。","drivers":["Goldilocks/growth-up melt-up (semis +87.2%, growth−value +23.3%, TLT +10.2%, VIX 21→15)","+117% vs SPY +51.4%; Sep-2024 Fed cuts re-rated long-duration fintech","Resilient US consumer + Nov-2024 deregulation/M&A tailwind","Narrow tape (RSP −12.2%); high-beta tail (BLOCK/AFRM/BNPL) led, V/MA core compounded"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks/增长向上融涨（半导体 +87.2%、成长−价值 +23.3%、TLT +10.2%、VIX 21→15）","+117% 对 SPY +51.4%；2024年9月美联储降息使长久期金融科技重估","坚韧的美国消费者＋2024年11月放松监管/并购顺风","狭窄行情（RSP −12.2%）；高贝塔尾部（Block/Affirm/BNPL）领涨、V/MA 核心复利"]},"2025-02-18":{"title":"DeepSeek-to-tariff air pocket — the VIX-15-to-52 flush (−30%)","title_zh":"DeepSeek至关税的真空区——VIX 15到52冲洗（−30%）","body":"Payments rolled over with the broad market in the early-2025 risk-off: the DeepSeek shock dented growth multiples, then the April 8 tariff crash hit the most cyclical, consumer-exposed names hardest. This was a violent flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15→52, high-beta minus low-vol −23.3%, defensives −6.9% vs cyclicals −18.7%, SPY −18.6%) — and as a high-beta consumer-cyclical group, fintech amplified it. A squeezed consumer means lower spend volume (the direct fear for payments) and higher recession odds compress fintech multiples. The basket bottomed with the broad market on April 8.","body_zh":"支付随2025年初的避险情绪与大盘一同回落：DeepSeek 冲击削弱成长估值，随后4月8日关税崩盘对最具周期性、消费暴露最高的标的打击最重。这是一次猛烈的避险冲洗（VIX 15→52、高贝塔减低波 −23.3%、防御股 −6.9% 对周期股 −18.7%、SPY −18.6%）——作为高贝塔消费周期组别，金融科技将其放大。受挤压的消费者意味着更低的支付量（支付板块最直接的担忧），更高的衰退概率压缩金融科技估值。篮子于4月8日随大盘见底。","drivers":["Violent flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15→52, high-beta−low-vol −23.3%)","High-beta consumer-cyclical amplified it: −30% with SPY −18.6%","DeepSeek shock + April-8 tariff crash hit consumer-cyclical names hardest","Squeezed-consumer fear → lower spend volume; recession-odds compressed multiples"],"drivers_zh":["猛烈避险冲洗（VIX 15→52、高贝塔−低波 −23.3%）","高贝塔消费周期股放大：−30%、SPY −18.6%","DeepSeek 冲击＋4月8日关税崩盘对消费周期股打击最重","消费受挤压担忧→支付量下降；衰退概率压缩估值"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Tariff-low recovery rode the high-beta V-bounce (+57%)","title_zh":"关税低点修复乘高贝塔 V 型反弹（+57%）","body":"A strong +57% V-bounce off the April 2025 tariff low as the market recovered into a tech/semis-led risk-on (SPY +30.3%, semis +61.3%, growth−value +17.8, VIX 52→15, high-beta minus low-vol +47.4%, dollar weak DXY −5.0%). A capital-markets revival, easing recession fear, and renewed deal/IPO activity favored the whole financial complex; the networks resumed compounding and the high-beta fintech disruptors caught the outsized upside. In a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY −6.5%), the leg ran into late August 2025 before the next macro reset.","body_zh":"随大盘修复进入科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好（SPY +30.3%、半导体 +61.3%、成长−价值 +17.8、VIX 52→15、高贝塔减低波 +47.4%、美元走弱 DXY −5.0%），自2025年4月关税低点出现强劲的+57% V 型反弹。资本市场复苏、衰退担忧缓解、并购/IPO 活动重启，利好整个金融板块；网络巨头恢复复利，高贝塔金融科技颠覆者抓住超额上行。在狭窄行情中（RSP 落后 SPY −6.5%），该行情持续至2025年8月底，随后迎来下一轮宏观重置。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led high-beta V-bounce (semis +61.3%, high-beta−low-vol +47.4%, VIX 52→15)","Dollar weak (DXY −5.0%); capital-markets revival (deals/IPOs)","Easing recession fear lifted high-beta fintech; networks resumed compounding","Narrow tape (RSP −6.5%); ran into late-Aug 2025 reset"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨高贝塔 V 型反弹（半导体 +61.3%、高贝塔−低波 +47.4%、VIX 52→15）","美元走弱（DXY −5.0%）；资本市场复苏（并购/IPO）","衰退担忧缓解提振高贝塔金融科技；网络巨头恢复复利","狭窄行情（RSP −6.5%）；持续至2025年8月底重置"]},"2025-08-29":{"title":"Oil-shock / hawkish-Fed drawdown — the stagflation squeeze (−29%)","title_zh":"油价冲击/鹰派美联储回撤——滞胀挤压（−29%）","body":"The basket sold off ~29% from its August 2025 peak into March 2026, leading into the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock — a stagflation-ish regime where oil exploded +55.7%, VIX 15→31, and growth>value reversed hard (growth−value −12.6%) even as the broad index barely moved (SPY −0.9%). Notably this was an idiosyncratic Financials drawdown (Financials −10.4% one of the worst sectors) within a flat tape. CPI running 4.2% and a Fed shifting back to a hiking bias is the worst macro mix for rate-sensitive fintech: higher discount rates compress the long-duration names, and an oil-driven squeeze on the consumer threatens transaction volume. This reset the basket to its current Prime-entry washout near pos 15.","body_zh":"篮子自2025年8月高点下跌约−29%至2026年3月，领先于2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击——一个偏滞胀的环境，油价暴涨+55.7%、VIX 15→31、成长跑赢价值大幅反转（成长−价值 −12.6%），而大盘几乎没动（SPY −0.9%）。值得注意，这是平淡行情中的个体化金融回撤（金融板块 −10.4% 为最差板块之一）。CPI 高达4.2%、美联储重回加息倾向，是对利率敏感金融科技最糟糕的宏观组合：更高的贴现率压缩长久期标的，油价驱动的消费挤压威胁交易量。正是这轮回撤把篮子重置到当前 pos 15 附近的黄金入场洗盘状态。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish squeeze (oil +55.7%, VIX 15→31, growth−value −12.6%)","Idiosyncratic Financials drawdown (Financials −10.4%) in a flat tape (SPY −0.9%)","2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock, CPI 4.2%, Fed back to hiking bias","Higher rates compressed long-duration fintech; oil-driven consumer squeeze hit volume"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀挤压（油价 +55.7%、VIX 15→31、成长−价值 −12.6%）","平淡行情（SPY −0.9%）中的个体化金融回撤（金融板块 −10.4%）","2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击，CPI 4.2%，美联储重回加息倾向","高利率压缩长久期金融科技；油价驱动的消费挤压打击交易量"]},"2026-03-27":{"title":"Mid-June-ceasefire bounce on the risk-on flip (+19%)","title_zh":"6月中旬停火反弹乘风险偏好翻转（+19%）","body":"A reflex rally off the March 2026 low as the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire took the worst-case oil/inflation tail off the table and the regime flipped goldilocks (oil −10.1%, semis +24.0%, growth−value +6.8, VIX 31→19). Lower oil eases the consumer squeeze and softens the Fed's hawkish bias — both directly positive for spend volume and fintech multiples. The bounce is modest (+19%, lagging SPY +11.8% only slightly) and the basket sits low, which is the constructive read: most of the damage is done, and the durable V/MA core gives the setup a real floor.","body_zh":"随6月中旬霍尔木兹停火消除最坏情形的油价/通胀尾部风险、环境翻转为 goldilocks（油价 −10.1%、半导体 +24.0%、成长−价值 +6.8、VIX 31→19），自2026年3月低点出现反射性反弹。油价回落缓解消费挤压、软化美联储鹰派倾向——两者都直接利好支付量与金融科技估值。反弹幅度温和（+19%，略逊于 SPY +11.8%）、篮子位置偏低，这正是建设性的解读：大部分损伤已消化，耐用的 V/MA 核心为这一入场提供了真实底部。","drivers":["Goldilocks flip (oil −10.1%, semis +24.0%, growth−value +6.8, VIX 31→19)","Mid-June Hormuz ceasefire removed worst-case oil/inflation tail","Lower oil eased consumer squeeze + softer Fed bias helped multiples","Durable V/MA core anchors the low-position setup"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 翻转（油价 −10.1%、半导体 +24.0%、成长−价值 +6.8、VIX 31→19）","6月中旬霍尔木兹停火消除最坏油价/通胀尾部","油价回落缓解消费挤压＋美联储倾向软化利好估值","耐用 V/MA 核心锚定低位入场"]}}},"b-regional_banks":{"now":"Regional banks (KRE) are Trending at pos 56.3 — fully healed from the trauma that defines this basket's modern history, and a high-beta, economically-sensitive corner of Financials that amplifies the cycle in both directions. KRE was the epicenter of the March 2023 crisis: Silicon Valley Bank's collapse over a duration-mismatched bond book triggered a deposit run that took down Signature and First Republic and gutted the whole group. What rebuilt it from the May 2023 low is the same thing that broke it, in reverse — net interest margin (NIM) stabilizing as the rate panic faded, deposits stickier, and from the November 2024 election a powerful deregulation/M&A Trump trade. The current tape is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +17.6) which is normally a bank tailwind, yet Financials lag (−2.7%) — and the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock with a Fed in hiking bias cuts both ways: steeper rates can help NIM but stress commercial real estate and credit. At RS #14 and mid-range positioning, this is a participate-but-watch-credit basket.","now_zh":"区域银行（KRE）处于趋势中，pos 56.3——已从定义本篮子现代史的创伤中完全康复；它是金融板块中高贝塔、对经济高度敏感的角落，在两个方向上都放大周期。KRE 是2023年3月危机的震中：硅谷银行（SVB）因久期错配的债券账户崩溃，引发存款挤兑，拖垮了 Signature 与 First Republic 并重创整组。自2023年5月低点将其重建的，正是当初摧毁它的因素的反向运行——随利率恐慌消退，净息差（NIM）企稳、存款黏性增强；以及自2024年11月大选起强劲的放松监管/并购特朗普交易。当前行情为再通胀/增长向上（周期股 +11.2% 对防御股 +6.9%、油价 +19.2%、铜金比 +17.6），通常是银行顺风，但金融板块却落后（−2.7%）——而2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击叠加美联储加息倾向双向作用：更陡的利率可助 NIM，但会压力商业地产与信用。RS 第14位、位置居中，这是一个参与但需盯紧信用的篮子。","legs":{"2020-07-09":{"title":"Reopening rate-steepening boom amplified the reflation melt-up (+152%)","title_zh":"复工/曲线趋陡繁荣放大再通胀融涨（+152%）","body":"From the COVID lows, regional banks ripped +152% into January 2022 — nearly 3x the broad market (SPY +51%) — as a high-beta cyclical levered into the classic early-cycle bank trade. The regime did the heavy lifting: a roaring reflation/growth-up melt-up (cyclicals +69.0% vs defensives +33.2%, oil +111.6%, copper-gold +55.0, high-beta minus low-vol +75.6%, broadening RSP beat SPY +13.5%) with a steepening curve (TLT −13.1% as yields rose) and reopening loan demand. Rising rates promised to finally widen net interest margins after years of zero-rate compression. In hindsight this leg planted the seed of the 2023 crisis — banks loaded up on long-dated bonds at peak prices, an unhedged duration bet that would detonate when rates spiked.","body_zh":"自新冠低点起，区域银行飙升+152%至2022年1月——是大盘的近三倍（SPY +51%），作为高贝塔周期股放大了经典的周期早段银行交易。环境功不可没：轰鸣的再通胀/增长向上融涨（周期股 +69.0% 对防御股 +33.2%、油价 +111.6%、铜金比 +55.0、高贝塔减低波 +75.6%、广度转宽 RSP 跑赢 SPY +13.5%），曲线趋陡（收益率上行 TLT −13.1%），复工贷款需求。加息承诺在多年零利率压缩后终于拓宽净息差。事后看，正是这段行情埋下了2023年危机的种子——银行在价格高点囤积了长久期债券，一笔未对冲的久期押注，将在利率飙升时引爆。","drivers":["Reflation/growth-up melt-up (cyclicals +69.0%, oil +111.6%, broadening RSP +13.5%)","High-beta cyclical amplified the regime: +152% vs SPY +51%","Steepening curve (TLT −13.1%) + reopening loan demand promised wider NIM","Banks loaded long-dated bonds at peak — the unhedged duration bet"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上融涨（周期股 +69.0%、油价 +111.6%、广度 RSP +13.5%）","高贝塔周期股放大行情：+152% 对 SPY +51%","曲线趋陡（TLT −13.1%）＋复工贷款需求承诺更宽 NIM","银行在价格高点囤积长久期债券——未对冲久期押注"]},"2022-01-14":{"title":"2022 Fed-hiking drawdown — rate/dollar shock loads the powder (−27%)","title_zh":"2022年美联储加息回撤——利率/美元冲击铺设火药（−27%）","body":"Banks fell −27% with the broad 2022 bear (SPY −20.9%) in a stagflation-ish rate-and-dollar shock — the 10Y surged hard (TLT −20.8%), DXY ripped +8.9%, VIX 19→33 — and as a high-beta cyclical KRE tracked the cyclical wreckage (cyclicals −15.5% vs defensives −8.4%). The headline worry was recession-and-credit, but the deeper, under-appreciated damage was on the balance sheet: every rate hike marked those peak-priced bond portfolios further underwater. The market couldn't yet see it — held-to-maturity accounting masked the unrealized losses — but the same rate move powering the macro selloff was laying the powder for 2023.","body_zh":"随2022年大熊市（SPY −20.9%），银行在偏滞胀的利率与美元冲击中下跌−27%——10Y 猛烈飙升（TLT −20.8%）、DXY 大涨+8.9%、VIX 19→33——作为高贝塔周期股，KRE 跟随周期股残局（周期股 −15.5% 对防御股 −8.4%）。表面担忧是衰退与信用，但更深、被低估的损伤在资产负债表上：每一次加息都让那些高价买入的债券组合浮亏更深。市场当时还看不到——持有至到期会计掩盖了未实现损失——但驱动宏观抛售的同一波利率走势，正在为2023年铺设火药。","drivers":["Rate/dollar shock (TLT −20.8%, DXY +8.9%, VIX 19→33) drove the −27%","High-beta cyclical tracked the wreckage (cyclicals −15.5% vs defensives −8.4%)","Peak-priced bond books marked further underwater each hike","Held-to-maturity accounting masked the powder being laid for 2023"],"drivers_zh":["利率/美元冲击（TLT −20.8%、DXY +8.9%、VIX 19→33）驱动−27%","高贝塔周期股跟随残局（周期股 −15.5% 对防御股 −8.4%）","每次加息让高价债券账户浮亏加深","持有至到期会计掩盖为2023年铺设的火药"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Pre-crisis relief rally on the goldilocks bounce (+20%)","title_zh":"危机前喘息反弹乘 goldilocks 反弹（+20%）","body":"A modest +20% recovery into February 2023, riding a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation bounce (SPY +14.7%, VIX 33→19, oil −34.4% as the inflation scare eased, broadening RSP beat SPY +4.2%) on peak-rate hopes and the early-2023 genAI risk-on. It looked like a normal cyclical bank bounce — but it ended abruptly in early February, mere weeks before the deposit run began. In hindsight this is the calm before the storm: the unrealized bond losses were still buried, and the catalyst was about to arrive.","body_zh":"随 goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的反弹（SPY +14.7%、VIX 33→19、通胀恐慌缓解油价 −34.4%、广度转宽 RSP 跑赢 SPY +4.2%），借利率见顶预期与2023年初生成式 AI 风险偏好，温和复苏+20%至2023年2月。看似一次普通的周期银行股反弹——但在2月初戛然而止，距存款挤兑开始仅数周。事后看这是暴风雨前的平静：未实现的债券损失仍被掩埋，而催化剂即将到来。","drivers":["Goldilocks bounce (SPY +14.7%, VIX 33→19, oil −34.4%, RSP +4.2%)","Peak-rate hopes + early-2023 genAI risk-on","Normal-looking cyclical bank bounce","Unrealized bond losses still buried — calm before the SVB storm"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks 反弹（SPY +14.7%、VIX 33→19、油价 −34.4%、RSP +4.2%）","利率见顶预期＋2023年初生成式 AI 风险偏好","看似普通的周期银行股反弹","未实现债券损失仍被掩埋——SVB 暴风雨前的平静"]},"2023-02-07":{"title":"The SVB crisis collapse — an idiosyncratic break (−38%)","title_zh":"SVB危机崩溃——个体化破裂（−38%）","body":"The defining event, and a rare idiosyncratic crash: in March 2023, Silicon Valley Bank's forced bond-portfolio sale revealed the unrealized losses the whole group was sitting on, triggering a digital-age deposit run that collapsed SVB, Signature, and First Republic within days. KRE crashed −38% while the broad market barely moved (SPY −2.1%, VIX 19→20) — this was not a macro de-risk but a sector-specific solvency panic, with capital fleeing anything regional for money-market funds and too-big-to-fail banks (narrow tape, RSP lagged SPY −5.8%). The Fed's emergency BTFP facility eventually stemmed the panic, but the basket bottomed in early May 2023 a shadow of itself — the crisis epicenter.","body_zh":"决定性事件，且是罕见的个体化崩盘：2023年3月，硅谷银行（SVB）被迫抛售债券组合，暴露了全组所共有的未实现损失，引发数字时代的存款挤兑，数日内令 SVB、Signature 与 First Republic 相继崩溃。KRE 暴跌−38%，而大盘几乎没动（SPY −2.1%、VIX 19→20）——这不是宏观去风险，而是板块特异的偿付能力恐慌，资金逃离一切区域银行、奔向货币市场基金与大到不能倒银行（狭窄行情，RSP 落后 SPY −5.8%）。美联储紧急的 BTFP 工具最终遏制了恐慌，但篮子于2023年5月初触底时已大幅缩水——危机的震中。","drivers":["Idiosyncratic break: −38% while SPY only −2.1% (sector solvency panic, not macro)","SVB forced bond sale exposed unrealized losses; digital-age deposit run","Took down SVB/Signature/First Republic; flight to MMFs and TBTF banks","Fed emergency BTFP facility eventually stemmed the panic"],"drivers_zh":["个体化破裂：−38% 而 SPY 仅−2.1%（板块偿付恐慌、非宏观）","SVB 被迫抛售债券暴露未实现损失；数字时代存款挤兑","拖垮 SVB/Signature/First Republic；资金逃向货币基金与大到不能倒银行","美联储紧急 BTFP 工具最终遏制恐慌"]},"2023-05-04":{"title":"The +128% deregulation recovery rode the goldilocks melt-up","title_zh":"+128%放松监管复苏乘 goldilocks 融涨","body":"From the May 2023 crisis low, KRE more than doubled (+128%) into November 2024 — 2.5x the broad market (SPY +50.6%) — one of the great recovery trades, and a high-beta cyclical amplifying a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (semis +101.2%, growth−value +27.1%, VIX 20→15, credit firm HYG−LQD +10.0). The healing was mechanical at first: deposits stabilized, NIM bottomed as the rate panic faded, and survivors proved their books money-good. Then the November 2024 election added rocket fuel — a deregulation/M&A Trump trade promising lighter capital rules and a wave of consolidation. The September 2024 Fed cuts eased deposit-cost pressure. From epicenter to leader in eighteen months, even in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY −14.2%).","body_zh":"自2023年5月危机低点起，KRE 翻倍有余（+128%）至2024年11月——是大盘的2.5倍（SPY +50.6%），堪称伟大的复苏交易之一；作为高贝塔周期股，它放大了 goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的融涨（半导体 +101.2%、成长−价值 +27.1%、VIX 20→15、信用坚挺 HYG−LQD +10.0）。康复起初是机械式的：存款企稳，随利率恐慌消退 NIM 见底，幸存者证明其账户资产成色十足。随后2024年11月大选注入火箭燃料——放松监管/并购的特朗普交易，承诺更宽松的资本规则与整合潮。2024年9月美联储降息缓解了存款成本压力。十八个月内，从震中到领涨，即便处于狭窄的大型股行情（RSP 落后 SPY −14.2%）。","drivers":["Goldilocks/growth-up melt-up (semis +101.2%, growth−value +27.1%, VIX 20→15)","High-beta cyclical amplified it: +128% vs SPY +50.6%","Deposits/NIM healed; Nov-2024 deregulation/M&A Trump trade added rocket fuel","Sep-2024 Fed cuts eased deposit costs; narrow tape (RSP −14.2%)"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks/增长向上融涨（半导体 +101.2%、成长−价值 +27.1%、VIX 20→15）","高贝塔周期股放大：+128% 对 SPY +50.6%","存款/NIM 康复；2024年11月放松监管/并购特朗普交易注入火箭燃料","2024年9月美联储降息缓解存款成本；狭窄行情（RSP −14.2%）"]},"2024-11-25":{"title":"Tariff-crash give-back — high-beta hit hardest (−30%)","title_zh":"关税崩盘回吐——高贝塔受创最重（−30%）","body":"Banks gave back −30% of the post-election rally into the April 2025 tariff crash — deeper than the broad market (SPY −16.4%) in a flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15→52, high-beta minus low-vol −21.0%, defensives −7.6% vs cyclicals −18.9%). The Trump-trade optimism that had powered them since November ran into a tariff-driven growth scare, and recession-odds spiking is the direct enemy of bank credit — so this high-beta, economically-sensitive group sold off hardest. The basket bottomed with the broad market on April 8, 2025.","body_zh":"随2025年4月关税崩盘，银行回吐了大选后涨幅−30%——在避险冲洗中（VIX 15→52、高贝塔减低波 −21.0%、防御股 −7.6% 对周期股 −18.9%）跌幅深于大盘（SPY −16.4%）。自11月以来推动它们的特朗普交易乐观情绪，撞上了关税驱动的增长恐慌，衰退概率飙升是银行信用的直接敌人——故这一高贝塔、对经济敏感的组别跌幅最深。篮子于2025年4月8日随大盘见底。","drivers":["Flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15→52, high-beta−low-vol −21.0%) — sold harder than tape","−30% vs SPY −16.4%: high-beta economically-sensitive group hit hardest","Tariff growth scare; recession-odds spike is the enemy of bank credit","Bottomed with broad market April 8, 2025"],"drivers_zh":["避险冲洗（VIX 15→52、高贝塔−低波 −21.0%）——抛售比大盘更猛","−30% 对 SPY −16.4%：高贝塔、经济敏感组别受创最重","关税增长恐慌；衰退概率飙升是银行信用的敌人","于2025年4月8日随大盘见底"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"The +68% tariff-low rally rode the risk-on V-bounce","title_zh":"+68%关税低点行情乘风险偏好 V 型反弹","body":"From the April 2025 tariff low, KRE rallied +68% into mid-2026, restoring its Trending status by riding a powerful reflation/growth-up V-bounce (SPY +49.6%, semis a blistering +255.0%, VIX 52→19, high-beta minus low-vol +118.3%, cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +20.4%). The recovery rode the market-wide rebound, a renewed deregulation/M&A thrust, and stabilizing NIM. The 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock and Fed hiking bias cut both ways — steeper rates can widen margins, but the inflation/rates combo stresses commercial real estate and credit quality, the perennial regional-bank vulnerability. The mid-June ceasefire took the worst-case tail off. The basket is healthy and mid-range; in a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY −8.8%) the thing to watch from here is credit, not deposits.","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点起，KRE 上涨+68%至2026年中，借一场强劲的再通胀/增长向上 V 型反弹（SPY +49.6%、半导体狂飙+255.0%、VIX 52→19、高贝塔减低波 +118.3%、周期股 +51.4% 对防御股 +20.4%）重回趋势中状态。复苏借力全市场反弹、放松监管/并购的再度发力、以及企稳的 NIM。2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击与美联储加息倾向双向作用——更陡的利率可拓宽利差，但通胀/利率组合会压力商业地产与信用质量，这是区域银行长期的软肋。6月中旬停火消除了最坏尾部。篮子健康、位置居中；在狭窄行情中（RSP 落后 SPY −8.8%），从此往后要盯的是信用，而非存款。","drivers":["Risk-on V-bounce (SPY +49.6%, semis +255.0%, high-beta−low-vol +118.3%, VIX 52→19)","+68% restored Trending; renewed deregulation/M&A thrust + stabilizing NIM","2026 oil shock/hiking bias cuts both ways for banks (NIM vs CRE/credit)","Narrow tape (RSP −8.8%); watch credit/CRE, not deposits, from here"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好 V 型反弹（SPY +49.6%、半导体 +255.0%、高贝塔−低波 +118.3%、VIX 52→19）","+68% 重回趋势中；放松监管/并购再发力＋NIM 企稳","2026年油价冲击/加息倾向对银行双向（NIM 对商业地产/信用）","狭窄行情（RSP −8.8%）；从此往后盯信用/商业地产，而非存款"]}}},"b-big_pharma":{"now":"Big pharma (PPH) is Rolling over at pos 32.4 with weak RS (#31) — the policy-overhang laggard of Healthcare, and a low-beta defensive that the current reflation/growth-up tape has left behind: Tech leads +24.3%, Energy +21.5%, while this group sits in the back. This basket (Merck, Pfizer, Bristol, AbbVie, J&J; GLP-1 leaders sit in their own obesity basket) carries the heaviest political tax in the market: the May 2025 Most-Favored-Nation (MFN) drug-pricing executive order, which threatens to peg US drug prices to lower foreign benchmarks, plus RFK Jr. at HHS injecting genuine uncertainty into FDA, vaccines, and approval pathways. On top of that sits the structural patent-cliff problem — several mega-blockbusters losing exclusivity this decade — which keeps the group leaning on M&A to refill pipelines. The macro doesn't help: with growth>value reversing (growth−value −15.2%), defensives are not the leadership here, and after a long drug-pricing-driven slide into May 2025, the group's late-2025 defensive bid (cheap, dividend-paying, recession-resistant) has rolled back over. It's a value/yield hold with a policy sword hanging over it, not a momentum name.","now_zh":"大型药企（PPH）处于见顶回落，pos 32.4、RS 疲弱（第31位）——医疗板块中受政策压制的落后者，也是被当前再通胀/增长向上行情抛在身后的低贝塔防御品：科技领涨+24.3%、能源+21.5%，本组居后。该篮子（Merck、Pfizer、Bristol、AbbVie、J&J；GLP-1 龙头另列减肥药篮子）承担着市场上最重的政治税：2025年5月的最惠国（MFN）药品定价行政令，威胁将美国药价锚定至更低的海外基准；加上小肯尼迪（RFK Jr.）执掌 HHS，为 FDA、疫苗与审批路径注入真实的不确定性。叠加结构性专利悬崖问题——数款超级重磅药本十年将失去独占权——使该组别持续依赖并购来补充管线。宏观也不帮忙：随成长跑赢价值反转（成长−价值 −15.2%），防御股并非此处的领导者；在因药品定价拖累、长期下滑至2025年5月后，该组别2025年末的防御性买盘（低估值、派息、抗衰退）已再度回落。这是一个头顶政策利剑的价值/收益持有标的，而非动量品种。","legs":{"2024-09-16":{"title":"Idiosyncratic drug-pricing slide in a rising tape (−20%)","title_zh":"上涨大盘中的个体化药品定价下滑（−20%）","body":"From September 2024, big pharma ground down −20% into May 2025 even though the broad market was up (SPY +5.4%) — a glaring idiosyncratic underperformance under a thickening policy cloud, not a macro drawdown. The tape was a narrow, goldilocks-leaning, rate-driven one (10Y surged, TLT −13.4%; RSP lagged SPY −4.0%; defensives −6.2% vs cyclicals +6.1%) that punished low-beta defensive yield names — and pharma's drag stacked policy on top: the November 2024 election and the incoming drug-pricing agenda, RFK Jr.'s nomination to HHS, the looming MFN threat (culminating in the May 2025 executive order), and the structural patent-cliff worry with several blockbusters facing loss of exclusivity. Even through the April 2025 tariff episode, pharma fell for its own reasons.","body_zh":"自2024年9月起，尽管大盘上涨（SPY +5.4%），大型药企却在日益浓重的政策阴云下震荡下行−20%至2025年5月——这是刺眼的个体化跑输，而非宏观回撤。当时的行情狭窄、偏 goldilocks、由利率驱动（10Y 飙升，TLT −13.4%；RSP 落后 SPY −4.0%；防御股 −6.2% 对周期股 +6.1%），惩罚低贝塔防御收益股——而药企的拖累在此之上叠加了政策：2024年11月大选与新政府的药品定价议程、RFK Jr. 获提名执掌 HHS、逼近的 MFN 威胁（以2025年5月行政令收尾）、以及数款重磅药面临独占权到期的结构性专利悬崖担忧。即便穿越2025年4月关税事件，药企也因自身原因下跌。","drivers":["Idiosyncratic: fell −20% while SPY rose +5.4% (policy, not macro)","Rate-driven low-beta tape (TLT −13.4%, defensives −6.2%) hurt yield names","Nov-2024 election + MFN drug-pricing overhang + RFK Jr. to HHS","Structural patent-cliff loss-of-exclusivity worry"],"drivers_zh":["个体化：SPY 涨+5.4% 时本组跌−20%（政策而非宏观）","利率驱动的低贝塔行情（TLT −13.4%、防御股 −6.2%）压制收益股","2024年11月大选＋MFN 药品定价压制＋RFK Jr. 执掌 HHS","结构性专利悬崖独占权到期担忧"]},"2025-05-14":{"title":"Defensive bid / policy-fatigue rally — the stagflation hiding place (+42%)","title_zh":"防御性买盘/政策疲劳反弹——滞胀期的避风港（+42%）","body":"From the May 2025 low, big pharma rallied +42% into February 2026 — a recovery built less on growth than on defensiveness and policy fatigue, and one that suited the regime: a stagflation-ish, falling-rate window (TLT +10.1%, DXY −3.4%, copper-gold −34.2%) where defensives (+21.6%) finally matched cyclicals (+19.8%) and low-beta yield came back into favor. With the MFN order's actual bite proving slower and more negotiable than feared, the market stopped pricing the worst case, and the group caught a genuine defensive bid — cheap, fat dividends, recession-resistant cash flows, exactly the profile investors want when the AI/high-beta trade gets wobbly and the 2026 oil shock raises macro risk. The Rolling-over phase and weak RS say the rally has since stalled — the policy sword still hangs, and without pipeline catalysts pharma reverts to a value/yield holding pattern.","body_zh":"自2025年5月低点起，大型药企上涨+42%至2026年2月——这是一场建立在防御性与政策疲劳、而非增长之上的复苏，且契合当时的环境：偏滞胀、利率下行的窗口（TLT +10.1%、DXY −3.4%、铜金比 −34.2%），防御股（+21.6%）终于追平周期股（+19.8%），低贝塔收益重获青睐。随着 MFN 行政令的实际杀伤力被证明比担忧的更慢、更可谈判，市场停止定价最坏情形，该组别获得真正的防御性买盘——低估值、丰厚股息、抗衰退现金流，正是 AI/高贝塔交易动摇、2026年油价冲击抬高宏观风险时投资者想要的画像。见顶回落阶段与疲弱 RS 表明该涨势此后停滞——政策利剑仍悬，缺乏管线催化剂时，药企回归价值/收益的横盘格局。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish/falling-rate window (TLT +10.1%, DXY −3.4%) favored low-beta defensives","Defensives (+21.6%) finally matched cyclicals (+19.8%)","MFN bite proved slower/more negotiable; cheap, dividend, recession-resistant bid","Hiding place as AI/high-beta wobbled + 2026 oil shock; stalled since"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀/利率下行窗口（TLT +10.1%、DXY −3.4%）利好低贝塔防御","防御股（+21.6%）终于追平周期股（+19.8%）","MFN 杀伤力更慢、更可谈判；低估值、派息、抗衰退买盘","AI/高贝塔动摇＋2026年油价冲击时的避险去处；此后停滞"]}}},"b-obesity_glp1":{"now":"GLP-1 & obesity is Trending at pos 44.1 with strong RS (#13) — the secular super-cycle, now maturing into a competitive war, and a basket whose growth-y, high-conviction names ride risk-on tape harder than ordinary pharma. This is the Eli Lilly / Novo Nordisk story: incretin drugs (Mounjaro/Zepbound, Ozempic/Wegovy) that reshaped metabolic medicine and created one of the largest TAMs in pharma history. The 2025-26 chapter is the pivot from monopoly to oligopoly and from injectable to oral. By late 2025 / early 2026 both giants brought oral pills to market — Novo's oral Wegovy approved first, but Lilly's orforglipron (no food/timing restrictions) is the Street's projected long-run winner. Critically, both agreed to White House pricing deals capping starter-dose orals near $149/month — a pricing reset that trades margin per script for vastly larger volume. The basket also holds the supply chain and the names the drugs hurt (food, dialysis, medical devices). Strong RS holding up even as the broad tape goes reflation/growth-up with Tech (+24.3%) leading says the market still rewards the volume story; the risk is pricing compression and a crowded late-stage pipeline.","now_zh":"GLP-1 与减肥药处于趋势中，pos 44.1、RS 强劲（第13位）——长期超级周期，如今正成熟为一场竞争战争；这是一个成长属性、高信念的篮子，比普通药企更能放大风险偏好行情。这是礼来（Eli Lilly）/诺和诺德（Novo Nordisk）的故事：肠促胰素类药物（Mounjaro/Zepbound、Ozempic/Wegovy）重塑了代谢医学，缔造了制药史上最大的潜在市场（TAM）之一。2025–26 篇章是从垄断到寡头、从注射剂到口服剂的转折。到2025年末/2026年初，两巨头均推出口服丸剂——诺和诺德的口服 Wegovy 率先获批，但礼来的 orforglipron（无饮食/服用时间限制）被华尔街预期为长期赢家。关键是，两家均与白宫达成定价协议，将口服起始剂量封顶在约149美元/月——这是一次以单方处方利润换取远大销量的定价重置。篮子还纳入供应链与被该类药物伤害的标的（食品、透析、医疗器械）。即便大盘转入由科技领涨（+24.3%）的再通胀/增长向上行情，强劲 RS 依旧坚挺，表明市场仍奖励销量故事；风险在于定价压缩与拥挤的后期管线。","legs":{"2021-09-02":{"title":"Pre-super-cycle bear — just-pharma in the rate/dollar storm (−36%)","title_zh":"超级周期前的熊市——利率/美元风暴中的普通药企（−36%）","body":"Before the obesity narrative exploded, these names traded as ordinary large pharma/biotech and fell ~36% into May 2022 — a deeper drawdown than the broad market (SPY −12.5%) in a stagflation-ish, rate-and-dollar-shock regime (TLT −20.3%, DXY +12.6%, VIX 16→33) that punished long-duration healthcare. Lilly and Novo were known quantities (diabetes, established franchises) — the market had not yet grasped that semaglutide and tirzepatide were about to redefine the entire metabolic category. This is the basket as just-pharma, swept along by the macro before the re-rating.","body_zh":"在减肥叙事爆发之前，这些标的作为普通大型药企/生物科技交易，随2022年美联储加息熊市下跌约−36%至2022年5月——在偏滞胀、利率与美元双冲击的环境中（TLT −20.3%、DXY +12.6%、VIX 16→33），跌幅深于大盘（SPY −12.5%），长久期医疗受到惩罚。礼来与诺和诺德是已知量（糖尿病、成熟特许经营）——市场尚未领悟司美格鲁肽与替尔泊肽即将重新定义整个代谢领域。这是重估之前、被宏观裹挟、作为普通药企的篮子。","drivers":["Rate/dollar shock regime (TLT −20.3%, DXY +12.6%) hit long-duration healthcare","Fell −36% vs SPY −12.5% — traded as ordinary pharma, swept by macro","Market had not yet grasped the GLP-1 TAM","Pre-re-rating: just-pharma"],"drivers_zh":["利率/美元冲击环境（TLT −20.3%、DXY +12.6%）打击长久期医疗","跌−36% 对 SPY −12.5%——作为普通药企被宏观裹挟","市场尚未领悟 GLP-1 潜在市场","重估前：仅是普通药企"]},"2022-05-11":{"title":"Tirzepatide approval spark, against the grain (+43%)","title_zh":"替尔泊肽获批火花，逆势而上（+43%）","body":"The first leg of recognition: Lilly's tirzepatide (Mounjaro) won FDA approval for diabetes in mid-2022 and the weight-loss data was stunning — the market began to see the metabolic super-cycle coming. The +43% rally vastly outran the modest goldilocks-leaning summer bounce in the broad market (SPY +9.7%, VIX 33→20), a stock-specific re-rating that fired even though the 2022 bear was still in force. This is the basket decoupling from macro on a genuine catalyst — the obesity TAM thesis taking hold.","body_zh":"认知的第一段：礼来的替尔泊肽（Mounjaro）于2022年中获 FDA 批准用于糖尿病，且减重数据惊人——市场开始预见代谢超级周期的到来。+43%的上涨远超大盘温和的偏 goldilocks 夏季反弹（SPY +9.7%、VIX 33→20），这是个股特异性重估，尽管2022年熊市仍在持续依然点燃。这是篮子凭借真实催化剂与宏观脱钩——减肥潜在市场论点确立。","drivers":["Stock-specific catalyst: Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) FDA approval, stunning data","+43% vastly outran the modest summer tape (SPY +9.7%, VIX 33→20)","Decoupled from the still-active 2022 bear on the TAM thesis","First leg of metabolic re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["个股催化剂：替尔泊肽（Mounjaro）获 FDA 批准、数据惊人","+43% 远超温和的夏季行情（SPY +9.7%、VIX 33→20）","凭潜在市场论点与仍在持续的2022年熊市脱钩","代谢重估的第一段"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Brief macro pullback in the risk-off flush (−19%)","title_zh":"避险冲洗中的短暂宏观回调（−19%）","body":"A short, shallow give-back into late September 2022 as the broad market made its 2022 bear-market low in a flight-to-safety flush (SPY −14.7%, VIX 20→32, defensives −8.8% vs cyclicals −14.8%, TLT −10.0%, DXY +7.1%). Nothing thesis-specific — the GLP-1 names were simply pulled along by the last leg of the macro selloff before the December 2022 bottom set up the real bull run. The basket fell less than the cyclical wreckage, but its growth tilt meant it couldn't fully dodge the rate-and-dollar risk-off.","body_zh":"随大盘在避险冲洗中于2022年9月底创下2022年熊市低点（SPY −14.7%、VIX 20→32、防御股 −8.8% 对周期股 −14.8%、TLT −10.0%、DXY +7.1%），出现短暂而浅的回吐。无关论点本身——GLP-1 标的只是被宏观抛售的最后一段拖累，随后2022年12月触底为真正的牛市铺路。篮子跌幅小于周期股残局，但其成长倾向意味着无法完全躲过利率与美元的避险。","drivers":["Flight-to-safety flush (VIX 20→32, defensives > cyclicals) dragged the group","Rate/dollar risk-off (TLT −10.0%, DXY +7.1%) hit growth tilt","No thesis-specific catalyst — pulled by macro","Set up the real bull run off the Dec-2022 bottom"],"drivers_zh":["避险冲洗（VIX 20→32、防御股跑赢周期股）拖累本组","利率/美元避险（TLT −10.0%、DXY +7.1%）打击成长倾向","无关论点的催化剂——被宏观拖累","为2022年12月底部后的真正牛市铺路"]},"2022-09-26":{"title":"The +224% super-cycle amplified the goldilocks melt-up","title_zh":"+224%超级周期放大 goldilocks 融涨","body":"The defining leg: from September 2022, the basket exploded +224% into December 2024 — more than 3x the broad market (SPY +70.9%) — as GLP-1 went from clinical promise to cultural and commercial phenomenon. The backdrop was a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (semis +163.4%, growth−value +45.4%, VIX 32→14, DXY −7.0%) that rewarded high-conviction growth, and this high-beta secular winner amplified it: Zepbound's obesity approval, Wegovy's cardiovascular-benefit data, chronic global supply shortages (demand vastly outran manufacturing), and ever-expanding labels turned Lilly and Novo into two of the most valuable companies on earth. In a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY −22.5%), this is exactly the kind of name a risk-on regime concentrates flows into — one of the great secular growth stories of the decade.","body_zh":"决定性行情：自2022年9月起，篮子爆发式上涨+224%至2024年12月——是大盘的三倍多（SPY +70.9%），GLP-1 从临床前景跃升为文化与商业现象。背景是 goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的融涨（半导体 +163.4%、成长−价值 +45.4%、VIX 32→14、DXY −7.0%），奖励高信念成长，而这一高贝塔长期赢家将其放大：Zepbound 获批用于肥胖、Wegovy 的心血管获益数据、长期的全球供应短缺（需求远超产能）、不断扩展的适应症标签，把礼来与诺和诺德推上全球市值最高公司之列。在狭窄的大型股行情中（RSP 落后 SPY −22.5%），这正是风险偏好环境集中资金流入的那类标的——本十年伟大的长期成长故事之一。","drivers":["Goldilocks/growth-up melt-up (semis +163.4%, growth−value +45.4%, VIX 32→14)","High-beta secular winner amplified the regime: +224% vs SPY +70.9%","Zepbound obesity approval + Wegovy CV data + chronic supply shortages","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP −22.5%) concentrated flows into the winner"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks/增长向上融涨（半导体 +163.4%、成长−价值 +45.4%、VIX 32→14）","高贝塔长期赢家放大行情：+224% 对 SPY +70.9%","Zepbound 获批肥胖＋Wegovy 心血管数据＋长期供应短缺","狭窄大型股行情（RSP −22.5%）将资金集中流入赢家"]},"2024-12-09":{"title":"Policy + tariff drawdown — high-beta de-risk (−28%)","title_zh":"政策＋关税回撤——高贝塔去风险（−28%）","body":"The super-cycle met its first real correction into April 2025 — a −28% drop steeper than the broad market (SPY −17.4%) in a flight-to-safety flush (VIX 14→52, high-beta minus low-vol −23.4%, defensives −6.3% vs cyclicals −18.0%). As a heavily-owned, richly-valued high-beta name it de-risked harder than the tape: the November 2024 election and incoming MFN agenda, RFK Jr. at HHS, and disappointing next-gen trial data introduced doubt, then the April 8 tariff crash finished the job. The valuation premium that powered the super-cycle on the way up also made it the first to get sold when the risk-off hit.","body_zh":"超级周期迎来首次真正调整，至2025年4月——跌幅−28%深于大盘（SPY −17.4%），处于避险冲洗中（VIX 14→52、高贝塔减低波 −23.4%、防御股 −6.3% 对周期股 −18.0%）。作为持仓集中、估值高企的高贝塔标的，它去风险比大盘更猛：2024年11月大选与新政府 MFN 议程、RFK Jr. 执掌 HHS、下一代试验数据令人失望注入怀疑，随后4月8日关税崩盘完成最后一击。使超级周期在上行时如此强劲的估值溢价，也使其在避险来袭时最先被抛售。","drivers":["Flight-to-safety flush (VIX 14→52, high-beta−low-vol −23.4%) — sold harder than tape","High-beta de-risk: −28% vs SPY −17.4%","Nov-2024 election + MFN overhang + RFK Jr. + weak next-gen trial data","April-8 tariff crash finished the de-risking"],"drivers_zh":["避险冲洗（VIX 14→52、高贝塔−低波 −23.4%）——抛售比大盘更猛","高贝塔去风险：−28% 对 SPY −17.4%","2024年11月大选＋MFN 压制＋RFK Jr.＋疲弱下一代试验数据","4月8日关税崩盘完成去风险"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"The +77% oral-era recovery led the risk-on V-bounce","title_zh":"+77%口服时代复苏领跑风险偏好 V 型反弹","body":"From the April 2025 tariff low, the basket rallied +77% into mid-2026, outrunning a powerful risk-on V-bounce (SPY +48.5%, semis +240.9%, VIX 52→18, high-beta minus low-vol +111.3%) as the story matured from injectable monopoly to oral oligopoly. The regime — high-beta crushing low-vol, growth back in favor — rewarded this exact profile, and the fundamentals delivered: by late 2025 / early 2026 both giants commercialized obesity pills (Novo's oral Wegovy first, Lilly's orforglipron fast-tracked with the convenience edge and the Street's projected ~60% long-run share), and both signed White House deals capping starter-dose orals near $149/month — a deliberate margin-for-volume reset that gets ahead of the MFN threat. Strong RS held through the 2026 oil shock; the watch-items are pricing compression and an increasingly crowded next-gen pipeline.","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点起，篮子上涨+77%至2026年中，跑赢一场强劲的风险偏好 V 型反弹（SPY +48.5%、半导体 +240.9%、VIX 52→18、高贝塔减低波 +111.3%），随故事从注射剂垄断成熟为口服剂寡头。当时的环境——高贝塔碾压低波、成长重获青睐——恰恰奖励这种画像，基本面也兑现：到2025年末/2026年初，两巨头均将减肥丸剂商业化（诺和诺德口服 Wegovy 率先，礼来 orforglipron 快速审批、凭便利优势与华尔街预期的约60%长期份额），并均签署白宫定价协议将口服起始剂量封顶约149美元/月——一次有意的以利润换销量重置，抢先化解 MFN 威胁。强劲 RS 穿越2026年油价冲击；需盯的是定价压缩与日益拥挤的下一代管线。","drivers":["Risk-on V-bounce (semis +240.9%, high-beta−low-vol +111.3%, VIX 52→18) rewarded the profile","Outran the tape: +77% led the rebound; strong RS held through 2026 oil shock","Late-2025/early-2026 oral pills: Novo first, Lilly orforglipron leads long-run","White House deals cap starter-dose orals ~$149/month; watch pricing compression"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好 V 型反弹（半导体 +240.9%、高贝塔−低波 +111.3%、VIX 52→18）奖励该画像","跑赢大盘：+77% 领跑反弹；强劲 RS 穿越2026年油价冲击","2025末/2026初口服丸剂：诺和诺德率先，礼来 orforglipron 长期领先","白宫协议将口服起始剂量封顶约149美元/月；需盯定价压缩"]}}},"b-managed_care":{"now":"Managed care (UNH, Elevance, Cigna, Humana) is the standout of the entire screen — Topping at pos 99.7 (pinned to the top of its range) with RS rank #4 — and notably it is LEADING from the low-beta/defensive side while the tape is reflation/growth-up with Tech (+24.3%) and high-beta out front (high-beta minus low-vol +20.7%). That is a violent, idiosyncratic recovery from a genuine industry crisis, not a macro beta trade. Through 2025 the medical loss ratio blew out: seniors used outpatient surgery and high-cost GLP-1 drugs far above actuarial assumptions while Medicare Advantage funding was cut, pushing UNH's medical care ratio to ~88.9% and 2025 net profit down ~16%. The turn came when 2026 economics stabilized — Q1 2026 MCR improved to ~83.9%, UNH raised guidance, and CMS finalized favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%), with the Street modeling a sharp MA-EBIT rebound off pricing resets. The result is the +73% rally into mid-2026 that left the basket pinned at the top. The honest read: the recovery is real and stock-specific, but pos 99.7 + Topping is exactly where you respect the move and watch for exhaustion — the easy repricing is done, and utilization/policy risk never fully leaves this group.","now_zh":"管理式医疗（UNH、Elevance、Cigna、Humana）是整张筛选表的标杆——见顶，pos 99.7（贴在区间顶部）、RS 第4位——值得注意，它是从低贝塔/防御一侧领跑，而当前行情为再通胀/增长向上、科技领涨（+24.3%）、高贝塔在前（高贝塔减低波 +20.7%）。这是从一场真正行业危机中的暴力、个体化复苏，而非宏观贝塔交易。2025年全年医疗损失率（MLR）失控：老年人使用门诊手术与高价 GLP-1 药物的频率远超精算假设，同时 Medicare Advantage（MA）资金被削减，使 UNH 的医疗成本率升至约88.9%、2025年净利润下降约16%。转折出现在2026年经济性企稳时——2026年一季度 MCR 改善至约83.9%、UNH 上调指引、CMS 敲定有利的2027年 MA 费率（约2.48%），华尔街据定价重置建模出 MA-EBIT 的急剧反弹。结果是涨至2026年中的+73%行情，使篮子贴在顶部。诚实的解读：复苏真实且个股驱动，但 pos 99.7＋见顶恰恰是应当尊重涨势、警惕衰竭的位置——容易的重估已经完成，而利用率/政策风险从未真正离开这一组别。","legs":{"2021-05-28":{"title":"2021-22 defensive de-rate held up in the dollar shock (−21%)","title_zh":"2021–22防御性估值下修，美元冲击中抗跌（−21%）","body":"Managed care drifted −21% into January 2022 — a relatively mild drawdown that actually held up against a flat tape (SPY +3.7%) through a stagflation-ish dollar shock (DXY +8.0%, oil +30.6%, VIX 17→30). Health insurers are low-beta, defensive, recession-resistant cash machines, so they fared better than the high-beta names (high-beta minus low-vol −12.2%) as the Fed turned hawkish. The MCO model (collect premiums, manage the medical-loss ratio, keep the spread) is countercyclical-ish, and that defensiveness is the through-line of the whole basket's history.","body_zh":"管理式医疗震荡下行−21%至2022年1月——相对温和的回撤，实际上在偏滞胀的美元冲击中（DXY +8.0%、油价 +30.6%、VIX 17→30）相对平淡的大盘（SPY +3.7%）抗住了。健康保险公司是低贝塔、防御性、抗衰退的现金机器，因此在美联储转鹰时比高贝塔标的（高贝塔减低波 −12.2%）表现更好。MCO 模式（收保费、管理医疗损失率、赚取价差）略带逆周期性，而这种防御性是整个篮子历史的主线。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish dollar shock (DXY +8.0%, oil +30.6%, VIX 17→30)","Low-beta defensive held up: −21% vs a flat SPY +3.7%, beat high-beta (−12.2%)","MCO premium-minus-MLR spread is countercyclical-ish","Defensiveness is the basket's through-line"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀美元冲击（DXY +8.0%、油价 +30.6%、VIX 17→30）","低贝塔防御抗跌：−21% 对平淡的 SPY +3.7%，跑赢高贝塔（−12.2%）","MCO 的保费减 MLR 价差略带逆周期","防御性是篮子的主线"]},"2022-01-27":{"title":"Inflation-bear defensive bid — the first safe-haven episode (+28%)","title_zh":"通胀熊市防御性买盘——首次避风港行情（+28%）","body":"A +28% rally into April 2022 as capital rotated into defensives during the early 2022 inflation/rate scare — a rate-driven, defensives-led tape (TLT −14.6% as yields surged, defensives +11.1% vs cyclicals +6.6%, VIX 30→20) where Utilities and Real Estate led with managed care. With growth stocks unraveling (growth−value −4.7%) and high-beta still soft, the steady, dividend-paying, recession-resistant MCOs were exactly where investors hid — the first of several times this basket plays the safe-haven role.","body_zh":"随2022年初通胀/利率恐慌期间资金轮入防御股，出现+28%上涨至2022年4月——一个由利率驱动、防御股领涨的行情（收益率飙升 TLT −14.6%、防御股 +11.1% 对周期股 +6.6%、VIX 30→20），公用与地产与管理式医疗一同领涨。在成长股瓦解（成长−价值 −4.7%）、高贝塔仍疲软之际，稳健、派息、抗衰退的 MCO 正是投资者的避险去处——这是本篮子多次扮演避风港角色中的第一次。","drivers":["Rate-driven, defensives-led tape (TLT −14.6%, defensives +11.1% vs cyclicals +6.6%)","Capital rotated into defensives during inflation scare; growth unraveled (growth−value −4.7%)","Steady, dividend-paying, recession-resistant safe-haven bid","First of several safe-haven episodes"],"drivers_zh":["利率驱动、防御股领涨行情（TLT −14.6%、防御股 +11.1% 对周期股 +6.6%）","通胀恐慌期间资金轮入防御股；成长瓦解（成长−价值 −4.7%）","稳健、派息、抗衰退的避险买盘","多次避风港行情中的第一次"]},"2022-04-20":{"title":"Macro pullback — even defensives caught in the rate flush (−18%)","title_zh":"宏观回调——利率冲洗中连防御股也被卷入（−18%）","body":"A shallow −18% give-back into June 2022 alongside the broad market's mid-2022 leg lower (SPY −17.6%, VIX 20→33) in a stagflation-ish rate move (TLT −7.8%, DXY +3.2%). No MCO-specific catalyst — even defensives (−14.5%) got pulled into the general selloff, though they still beat cyclicals (−16.4%) before resuming their relative outperformance. A reminder that in a wholesale risk-off flush, low beta cushions but doesn't immunize.","body_zh":"随大盘2022年中段下行（SPY −17.6%、VIX 20→33）、在偏滞胀的利率走势中（TLT −7.8%、DXY +3.2%），出现浅幅−18%回吐至2022年6月。无关 MCO 本身的催化剂——即便防御股（−14.5%）也被卷入整体抛售，但仍跑赢周期股（−16.4%），随后恢复相对超额表现。这提醒：在全面避险冲洗中，低贝塔提供缓冲但无法免疫。","drivers":["Rate-driven flush (TLT −7.8%, DXY +3.2%, VIX 20→33)","Even defensives caught: −18% with SPY −17.6%, but beat cyclicals (−16.4%)","No MCO-specific catalyst — pulled into general risk-off","Resumed relative outperformance after"],"drivers_zh":["利率驱动冲洗（TLT −7.8%、DXY +3.2%、VIX 20→33）","连防御股也被卷入：−18%、SPY −17.6%，但跑赢周期股（−16.4%）","无关 MCO 本身的催化剂——被卷入整体避险","之后恢复相对超额表现"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Defensive leadership rally through the bear (+31%)","title_zh":"穿越熊市的防御性领导反弹（+31%）","body":"A +31% surge into August 2022 as managed care led the defensive trade through the heart of the 2022 bear. The tape was a goldilocks-leaning summer bounce (SPY +17.5%, semis +20.8%, VIX 33→20, oil −24.0%), and notably this defensive group kept pace with the high-beta rip (defensives +14.2% nearly matched cyclicals +15.4%) — printing steady earnings while tech bled and the safe-haven premium widened. The group's relative strength peaked around here before a long 2022-23 consolidation set in.","body_zh":"随管理式医疗在2022年熊市核心阶段领跑防御交易，出现+31%飙升至2022年8月。当时是偏 goldilocks 的夏季反弹（SPY +17.5%、半导体 +20.8%、VIX 33→20、油价 −24.0%），值得注意，这一防御组别跟上了高贝塔急升（防御股 +14.2% 几乎追平周期股 +15.4%）——科技流血之际录得稳定盈利、避险溢价扩大。该组别的相对强度在此附近见顶，随后进入漫长的2022–23盘整。","drivers":["Goldilocks-leaning summer bounce (semis +20.8%, VIX 33→20, oil −24.0%)","Defensive group kept pace (defensives +14.2% ~ cyclicals +15.4%)","Led the defensive trade; steady earnings while tech bled","Relative strength peaked before long consolidation"],"drivers_zh":["偏 goldilocks 夏季反弹（半导体 +20.8%、VIX 33→20、油价 −24.0%）","防御组别跟上（防御股 +14.2% ~ 周期股 +15.4%）","领跑防御交易；科技流血时录得稳定盈利","相对强度见顶后进入长盘整"]},"2022-08-15":{"title":"Defensives unwind into genAI risk-on — source of funds (−27%)","title_zh":"防御股向生成式AI风险偏好的解仓——资金来源（−27%）","body":"Managed care fell −27% into March 2023 — the mirror image of its 2022 strength, and a striking divergence: the broad market barely fell (SPY −7.2%, semis actually +6.2%) but defensives were sold (−8.4% vs cyclicals −5.6%, DXY −3.8%). As the December 2022 low gave way to the early-2023 genAI risk-on, capital rotated OUT of defensives and INTO growth and tech. When the market wants beta, the safe-haven MCOs become a source of funds. The bottom in March 2023 coincided with the SVB crisis peak-fear moment.","body_zh":"管理式医疗下跌−27%至2023年3月——其2022年强势的镜像，且是惊人的背离：大盘几乎没跌（SPY −7.2%、半导体反而 +6.2%），但防御股被抛售（−8.4% 对周期股 −5.6%、DXY −3.8%）。随2022年12月低点让位于2023年初的生成式 AI 风险偏好，资金从防御股轮出、流入成长与科技。当市场追逐 beta 时，避险型 MCO 成为资金来源。2023年3月的底部恰逢 SVB 危机的恐慌峰值时刻。","drivers":["Divergence: −27% while SPY only −7.2% and semis +6.2%","Risk-on rotation OUT of defensives (−8.4%) INTO genAI growth","Safe-haven MCOs became a source of funds for the beta trade","Bottomed at the March-2023 SVB peak-fear"],"drivers_zh":["背离：−27% 而 SPY 仅−7.2%、半导体 +6.2%","风险偏好轮动：从防御股（−8.4%）流出、流入生成式 AI 成长","避险型 MCO 成为 beta 交易的资金来源","于2023年3月 SVB 恐慌峰值见底"]},"2023-03-23":{"title":"The +57% pre-crisis bull lagged the AI melt-up (Mar '23 → Sep '24)","title_zh":"+57%危机前牛市跑输 AI 融涨（2023年3月→2024年9月）","body":"A long, steady +57% climb into September 2024 — solid in absolute terms but a laggard versus a roaring goldilocks/growth-up melt-up (SPY +45.5%, semis +84.3%, growth−value +25.4%, VIX 23→17) where the market chased AI and low-beta defensives trailed (defensives +25.6% vs cyclicals +35.7%, narrow tape RSP lagged SPY −15.4%). Strong enrollment, disciplined medical-cost management, and Medicare Advantage growth drove durable earnings regardless. This is the last normal uptrend before the 2025 crisis — the calm that preceded the medical-loss-ratio blowout, ending right at the September 2024 peak as the first cracks in MA economics appeared.","body_zh":"稳健的长升浪，+57%至2024年9月——绝对意义上扎实，但相对一场轰鸣的 goldilocks/增长向上融涨（SPY +45.5%、半导体 +84.3%、成长−价值 +25.4%、VIX 23→17）属于落后者，市场追逐 AI、低贝塔防御股拖后（防御股 +25.6% 对周期股 +35.7%、狭窄行情 RSP 落后 SPY −15.4%）。强劲的参保人数、严格的医疗成本管理、以及 Medicare Advantage 增长仍驱动了持久盈利。这是2025年危机前最后一段正常上行趋势——医疗损失率失控前的平静，在2024年9月高点结束，恰逢 MA 经济性首批裂缝显现之际。","drivers":["Goldilocks/growth-up AI melt-up (semis +84.3%, growth−value +25.4%) — defensives lagged","+57% trailed SPY +45.5% leadership; narrow tape (RSP −15.4%)","Strong enrollment + disciplined medical-cost management + MA growth","Last normal uptrend; ended at Sep-2024 peak as first MA cracks appeared"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks/增长向上 AI 融涨（半导体 +84.3%、成长−价值 +25.4%）——防御股落后","+57% 跑输 SPY +45.5% 的领导；狭窄行情（RSP −15.4%）","强劲参保＋严格医疗成本管理＋MA 增长","最后一段正常上行；于2024年9月高点结束，MA 首批裂缝显现"]},"2024-09-13":{"title":"First MA-cost crack — idiosyncratic, against a rising tape (−23%)","title_zh":"首批MA成本裂缝——个体化，逆上涨大盘（−23%）","body":"The first leg down of the crisis, and a glaring idiosyncratic break: −23% into December 2024 even though the broad market rose (SPY +7.9%) in a goldilocks tape (VIX 17→16, growth−value +11.5%, DXY +5.8%). This was company/sector-specific, not macro — Medicare Advantage cost trends started running hot and a near-flat preliminary MA rate proposal landed. The market began to grasp that utilization (outpatient procedures, and increasingly expensive GLP-1 prescriptions) was overrunning the actuarial assumptions baked into premiums. The defensive armor was cracking.","body_zh":"危机的第一段下跌，且是刺眼的个体化破裂：−23%至2024年12月，尽管大盘上涨（SPY +7.9%）、处于 goldilocks 行情（VIX 17→16、成长−价值 +11.5%、DXY +5.8%）。这是公司/板块特异，而非宏观——Medicare Advantage 成本趋势开始升温、近乎持平的初步 MA 费率提案落地。市场开始领悟，利用率（门诊手术、以及日益昂贵的 GLP-1 处方）正在压垮内置于保费中的精算假设。防御铠甲正在开裂。","drivers":["Idiosyncratic: −23% while SPY rose +7.9% in a goldilocks tape (VIX 17→16)","Medicare Advantage cost trends ran hot; near-flat preliminary MA rate proposal","Utilization (outpatient + GLP-1) overran actuarial assumptions","Company/sector-specific, not macro; defensive armor began cracking"],"drivers_zh":["个体化：SPY 涨+7.9%、goldilocks 行情（VIX 17→16）时本组跌−23%","Medicare Advantage 成本趋势升温；近乎持平的初步 MA 费率提案","利用率（门诊＋GLP-1）压垮精算假设","公司/板块特异、非宏观；防御铠甲开始开裂"]},"2024-12-17":{"title":"Pre-tariff relief bounce — defensive bid in the VIX-16-to-38 flush (+29%)","title_zh":"关税前喘息反弹——VIX 16到38冲洗中的防御性买盘（+29%）","body":"A +29% bounce into April 2025 as the market hoped the cost trend was a one-off and the final MA rate would beat the flat proposal. Helpfully, the regime turned flight-to-safety (SPY −11.1%, VIX 16→38, defensives flat 0.0% vs cyclicals −10.6%, DXY −6.7%), so as a defensive the group actually attracted a relative bid even as the broad market fell. The optimism was premature — the leg ended right at the April 2025 tariff-crash window, just before UNH's guidance cut revealed the cost problem was far worse and structural, not transitory.","body_zh":"随市场期望成本趋势只是一次性、且最终 MA 费率会好于持平提案，出现+29%反弹至2025年4月。有利的是，环境转向避险（SPY −11.1%、VIX 16→38、防御股持平0.0% 对周期股 −10.6%、DXY −6.7%），故作为防御品，该组别在大盘下跌时反而吸引到相对买盘。这份乐观为时过早——该行情恰在2025年4月关税崩盘窗口结束，就在 UNH 的指引下调揭示成本问题远更严重且为结构性、而非暂时性之前。","drivers":["Flight-to-safety regime (VIX 16→38, defensives 0.0% vs cyclicals −10.6%)","Defensive bid as SPY fell −11.1%; hope cost trend was one-off","Hope final MA rate beats the flat proposal — premature optimism","Ended at April-2025 tariff window, before UNH guidance cut"],"drivers_zh":["避险环境（VIX 16→38、防御股 0.0% 对周期股 −10.6%）","SPY 跌−11.1% 时的防御性买盘；期望成本趋势是一次性","期望最终 MA 费率优于持平提案——为时过早的乐观","于2025年4月关税窗口结束，UNH 指引下调之前"]},"2025-04-11":{"title":"The crisis capitulation — idiosyncratic, against a roaring rally (−33%)","title_zh":"危机投降——个体化，逆狂飙行情（−33%）","body":"The deepest leg of the crisis, and a stunning divergence: −33% into August 2025 while the broad market roared back (SPY +16.8%, semis +41.1%, high-beta minus low-vol +36.3%, VIX 38→20). This was pure company-specific carnage in the face of a risk-on melt-up — UNH cut guidance and the market finally priced the full severity: the medical care ratio blowing out toward ~88.9%, full-year 2025 net profit down ~16%, the cost overrun confirmed as industry-wide. GLP-1 utilization (the obesity-drug super-cycle, ironically) was itself a major cost driver. Berkshire's later stake exit and a leadership/regulatory cloud over UNH deepened the gloom. Genuine capitulation in what had been Healthcare's safest group — and the safe-haven character offered no cushion because the problem was fundamental, not macro.","body_zh":"危机最深的一段，且是惊人的背离：−33%至2025年8月，而大盘狂飙回升（SPY +16.8%、半导体 +41.1%、高贝塔减低波 +36.3%、VIX 38→20）。这是面对风险偏好融涨时纯粹的公司特异屠杀——UNH 下调指引，市场终于定价完整严重程度：医疗成本率向约88.9%失控、2025全年净利润下降约16%、成本超支被确认为全行业。具讽刺意味的是，GLP-1 利用率（减肥药超级周期本身）正是主要成本驱动因素之一。伯克希尔后来退出持股、加上 UNH 的领导层/监管阴云加深了悲观。曾经医疗板块最安全组别中真正的投降——避险属性毫无缓冲，因为问题是基本面的、而非宏观的。","drivers":["Stunning divergence: −33% while SPY roared +16.8% (risk-on melt-up)","Company-specific: UNH guidance cut; MCR blew out toward ~88.9%","FY2025 net profit −16%, cost overrun industry-wide; GLP-1 utilization a cost driver","Berkshire stake exit + UNH leadership/regulatory cloud; safe-haven offered no cushion"],"drivers_zh":["惊人背离：−33% 而 SPY 狂飙+16.8%（风险偏好融涨）","公司特异：UNH 下调指引；MCR 向约88.9%失控","2025全年净利润 −16%，成本超支全行业；GLP-1 利用率为成本驱动","伯克希尔退出持股＋UNH 领导层/监管阴云；避险属性毫无缓冲"]},"2025-08-01":{"title":"First recovery bounce — stock-specific, low-beta tape (+37%)","title_zh":"首次复苏反弹——个股驱动，低贝塔行情（+37%）","body":"A sharp +37% snapback into October 2025 — the first sign the worst was priced, and a stock-specific recovery in a quiet, near-trendless tape (SPY +8.6%, growth−value +3.3%, VIX 20→16, balanced cyclicals +6.8% vs defensives +5.0%). Bombed-out valuations, early evidence that 2026 repricing (insurers raising premiums and tightening benefits to restore margin) would fix the spread, and a sense that the capitulation had overshot drove an oversold rally in the most beaten-down group in Healthcare — fundamentals, not regime, did the work.","body_zh":"急速回升+37%至2025年10月——最坏情形已被定价的第一个迹象，是在平静、近乎无趋势的行情中（SPY +8.6%、成长−价值 +3.3%、VIX 20→16、周期股 +6.8% 与防御股 +5.0% 均衡）的个股驱动复苏。被打入谷底的估值、2026年重定价（保险公司提高保费、收紧福利以恢复利润）将修复价差的早期证据、以及投降已超调的感觉，共同驱动了医疗板块跌得最惨组别的超卖反弹——是基本面、而非环境，在发挥作用。","drivers":["Stock-specific recovery in a quiet, near-trendless tape (VIX 20→16, balanced)","First sign the worst was priced; bombed-out valuations","Early evidence 2026 repricing would restore the spread","Oversold rally in Healthcare's most beaten-down group — fundamentals, not regime"],"drivers_zh":["平静、近乎无趋势行情中的个股驱动复苏（VIX 20→16、均衡）","最坏已被定价的首个迹象；谷底估值","2026年重定价将恢复价差的早期证据","医疗板块跌得最惨组别的超卖反弹——是基本面、非环境"]},"2025-10-08":{"title":"Choppy bottoming dip in the risk-off retest (−18%)","title_zh":"避险回踩中的震荡筑底回调（−18%）","body":"A −18% pullback into November 2025 — a normal retest as the recovery digested, with the broad tape softening into a mild flight-to-safety (SPY −3.1%, VIX 16→26, defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals −4.7%). Notably the defensive group actually outperformed in the dip (Health a leader at +4.8%), consistent with its safe-haven character. The 2026 setup wasn't fully confirmed yet (rates, MCR trajectory, guidance all still in question), so the bounce gave back ground before the durable turn. Part of the bottoming process, not a new down-leg.","body_zh":"回调−18%至2025年11月——复苏消化期间的正常回踩，大盘转软进入温和的避险（SPY −3.1%、VIX 16→26、防御股 +0.3% 对周期股 −4.7%）。值得注意，防御组别在回调中反而跑赢（医疗以+4.8%领涨），与其避险属性一致。2026年的格局尚未完全确认（费率、MCR 轨迹、指引均存疑），故反弹在持久转折前回吐了部分涨幅。这是筑底过程的一部分，而非新的下跌段。","drivers":["Mild flight-to-safety retest (SPY −3.1%, VIX 16→26, defensives > cyclicals)","Defensive group outperformed (Health +4.8%) — safe-haven character","2026 setup not yet fully confirmed (rates/MCR/guidance)","Part of bottoming, not a new down-leg"],"drivers_zh":["温和避险回踩（SPY −3.1%、VIX 16→26、防御股跑赢周期股）","防御组别跑赢（医疗 +4.8%）——避险属性","2026年格局尚未完全确认（费率/MCR/指引）","筑底的一部分、非新下跌段"]},"2025-11-20":{"title":"Confirmation rally — defensive leadership returns (+25%)","title_zh":"确认反弹——防御领导回归（+25%）","body":"A +25% leg into January 2026 as the 2026-recovery thesis firmed up, in a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (SPY +6.4%, VIX 26→16, RSP beat SPY +3.6%) that supported a turn off the lows. Signs the medical-cost trend was peaking and that insurers' repricing would stick gave the market conviction the trough earnings were in. The group started reclaiming its defensive-leadership mantle as the broader market braced for the building 2026 oil-shock/inflation backdrop.","body_zh":"随2026年复苏论点夯实，出现+25%上涨至2026年1月，处于广度转宽的再通胀/增长向上行情（SPY +6.4%、VIX 26→16、RSP 跑赢 SPY +3.6%），支撑自低点的转折。医疗成本趋势见顶、保险公司重定价将站稳的迹象，给了市场盈利低点已现的信心。在大盘为正在累积的2026年油价冲击/通胀背景做准备之际，该组别开始重拾防御领导地位。","drivers":["Broadening reflation/growth-up tape (VIX 26→16, RSP beat SPY +3.6%)","2026-recovery thesis firmed; medical-cost trend peaking + repricing would stick","Conviction trough earnings were in","Reclaiming defensive leadership amid building oil-shock backdrop"],"drivers_zh":["广度转宽的再通胀/增长向上行情（VIX 26→16、RSP 跑赢 SPY +3.6%）","2026年复苏论点夯实；医疗成本趋势见顶＋重定价站稳","盈利低点已现的信心","在累积的油价冲击背景中重拾防御领导"]},"2026-01-15":{"title":"Oil-shock-window dip — even defensives caught in the stagflation flush (−26%)","title_zh":"油价冲击窗口回调——滞胀冲洗中连防御股也被卷入（−26%）","body":"A −26% drawdown into March 2026, overlapping the worst of the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock — a stagflation-ish flush where oil exploded +73.8%, VIX 16→31, and the whole market fell (SPY −8.5%, Financials −10.6%, Tech −12.2%). Even a defensive group gets caught in a broad risk-off when inflation spikes and the Fed turns hawkish, and after a big recovery run managed care was a profit-taking target — though it held up better than the cyclical leaders (defensives −0.7% vs cyclicals −1.7%). This proved to be the launchpad for the final, biggest leg up.","body_zh":"回撤−26%至2026年3月，与2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击最严重时期重叠——一个偏滞胀的冲洗，油价暴涨+73.8%、VIX 16→31，全市场下跌（SPY −8.5%、金融板块 −10.6%、科技 −12.2%）。即便防御组别，在通胀飙升、美联储转鹰的整体避险中也难以幸免，且在一轮大幅复苏之后，管理式医疗成为获利了结的目标——尽管它比周期领涨者更抗跌（防御股 −0.7% 对周期股 −1.7%）。这后来证明是最后、也是最大一段上行的发射台。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish flush (oil +73.8%, VIX 16→31, SPY −8.5%, Financials −10.6%)","Even defensives caught in inflation-spike risk-off (but held better, −0.7% vs cyclicals −1.7%)","Profit-taking after big recovery run; 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock (CPI 4.2%)","Launchpad for the final, biggest leg up"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀冲洗（油价 +73.8%、VIX 16→31、SPY −8.5%、金融板块 −10.6%）","通胀飙升避险中即便防御股也难幸免（但更抗跌，−0.7% 对周期股 −1.7%）","大幅复苏后的获利了结；2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击（CPI 4.2%）","最后、最大一段上行的发射台"]},"2026-03-30":{"title":"The +73% recovery blow-off — leading from the defensive side","title_zh":"+73%复苏喷发——从防御侧领跑","body":"The capstone: +73% from the March 2026 low into mid-2026, the stock-specific leg that pinned the basket at the top of its range (pos 99.7, RS #4) and saw a low-beta defensive LEAD even as the broad tape went reflation/growth-up with Tech (+42.0%) and high-beta (high-beta minus low-vol +30.7%) out front. The 2026 economics were now confirmed in the print — Q1 2026 MCR improving to ~83.9%, UNH raising 2026 EPS guidance, and CMS finalizing favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%) with the Street modeling a sharp MA-EBIT rebound off the pricing resets. The mid-June Hormuz ceasefire (oil −32.7%) removed the macro tail and let the recovery run clean. The honest caveat: Topping at pos 99.7 means the easy repricing is done — respect the move, but utilization and policy risk never fully leave this group, and this is exactly where you watch for exhaustion rather than chase.","body_zh":"收官之作：自2026年3月低点起+73%至2026年中，正是这段个股驱动的行情把篮子钉在区间顶部（pos 99.7、RS 第4位），且让一个低贝塔防御品领跑，即便大盘转入由科技（+42.0%）与高贝塔（高贝塔减低波 +30.7%）领跑的再通胀/增长向上。2026年的经济性如今已在财报中确认——一季度 MCR 改善至约83.9%、UNH 上调2026年 EPS 指引、CMS 敲定有利的2027年 MA 费率（约2.48%），华尔街据定价重置建模出 MA-EBIT 的急剧反弹。6月中旬霍尔木兹停火（油价 −32.7%）消除了宏观尾部，让复苏得以干净地推进。诚实的提醒：pos 99.7 处见顶意味着容易的重估已经完成——尊重涨势，但利用率与政策风险从未真正离开这一组别，这恰恰是该警惕衰竭、而非追涨的位置。","drivers":["Low-beta defensive LED even as tape went growth-up (Tech +42.0%, high-beta−low-vol +30.7%)","Q1-2026 MCR improved to ~83.9%, UNH raised guidance; CMS favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%)","Street modeled sharp MA-EBIT rebound off pricing resets","Mid-June Hormuz ceasefire (oil −32.7%) removed macro tail; watch exhaustion at pos 99.7"],"drivers_zh":["低贝塔防御领跑，即便大盘转增长向上（科技 +42.0%、高贝塔−低波 +30.7%）","2026一季度 MCR 改善至约83.9%、UNH 上调指引；CMS 有利的2027年 MA 费率（约2.48%）","华尔街据定价重置建模 MA-EBIT 急剧反弹","6月中旬霍尔木兹停火（油价 −32.7%）消除宏观尾部；pos 99.7 处警惕衰竭"]}}},"b-housing":{"now":"The housing chain (XHB-proxied builders DHI/LEN, Home Depot and building-products names) sits mid-pack (pos 40, RS rank 17) and is grinding higher again. Its whole story is one variable — mortgage rates — so the basket lives or dies on the rate regime, not the equity beta. The current reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, broad RSP-beat-SPY +2.9%) is friendly, but a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) and the earlier 2026 oil-shock CPI run to 4.2% had pushed long yields and the 30-year mortgage up, sinking builders ~25% into May. The mid-June Hormuz ceasefire let rates ease at the margin and the group bounced ~22% off the low. This is a rate-relief rally, not a demand boom — housing remains hostage to the next CPI print and the Fed's reaction.","now_zh":"住房产业链（以XHB为代理，包括房屋建筑商DHI/LEN、家得宝及建筑产品公司）处于中游（位置40，RS排名17），正再度震荡走高。它的全部故事系于一个变量——抵押贷款利率，因此该篮子的命运取决于利率/收益率环境，而非股票贝塔。当前再通胀/增长向上的市场环境（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，等权RSP跑赢SPY+2.9%、市场广度健康）是友好的，但更强的美元（DXY+3.4%）以及2026年初油价冲击将CPI推高至4.2%，曾把长端收益率与30年期抵押贷款利率推高，到5月把建筑商打下约25%。6月中旬霍尔木兹停火让利率边际回落，该板块从低点反弹约22%。这是利率减压反弹而非需求爆发——住房依然受制于下一个CPI数据及美联储反应。","legs":{"2021-12-31":{"title":"Rate-hike bear: mortgage shock cracks builders","body":"Builders fell ~38% in H1 2022 — far worse than the broad -22.6% SPY — as the Fed's most aggressive hiking cycle in decades sent the 30-year mortgage doubling toward 6%. This was a textbook rate-regime crush: TLT fell -24.0% and the dollar surged (DXY +8.3%), and the most rate-sensitive group on the board led Discretionary's -34% rout. With copper/gold rolling over into a stagflation-ish quad, demand froze and the whole chain from DHI/LEN to Home Depot de-rated on collapsing affordability.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME crush: TLT -24.0%, yields surge","Fed launches its most aggressive hiking cycle","30-year mortgage doubles toward 6%","Builders -38% vs SPY -22.6% on affordability shock"],"title_zh":"加息熊市：抵押贷款冲击击垮建筑商","body_zh":"建筑商在2022年上半年下跌约38%——远逊于大盘SPY的-22.6%——因美联储几十年来最激进的加息周期将30年期抵押贷款利率推高近一倍至6%。这是教科书式的利率/收益率压制：TLT下跌-24.0%、美元飙升（DXY+8.3%），这一全场最利率敏感的板块领跌、可选消费暴跌-34%。在铜金比走弱、类滞胀象限下，需求冻结，从DHI/LEN到家得宝的整个链条都因购房负担崩塌而估值下调。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率压制：TLT-24.0%、收益率飙升","美联储启动最激进加息周期","30年期抵押贷款利率翻倍冲向6%","建筑商-38% vs SPY-22.6%，负担能力冲击"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Summer bear-market bounce on a pivot that never came","body":"A ~26% relief rally from the June 2022 low into mid-August, riding the broad goldilocks/disinflation bounce (SPY +17.7%, SMH +19.5%, VIX 33->20, growth>value +8.8) as bond yields paused and the market priced a Fed pivot. As the most rate-sensitive group, housing amplified the move and led Discretionary's snap-back — until the Jackson Hole hawkish reset killed it.","drivers":["RISK-ON disinflation bounce: VIX 33->20, growth>value","Market prices a premature Fed pivot","Rate-sensitive housing amplifies the rebound","Oversold reflex ended by Jackson Hole"],"title_zh":"夏季熊市反弹：押注从未兑现的转向","body_zh":"从2022年6月低点到8月中旬约26%的减压反弹，搭乘大盘金发姑娘/去通胀反弹（SPY+17.7%、SMH+19.5%、VIX 33->20、成长跑赢价值+8.8），债券收益率暂停、市场押注美联储转向。作为最利率敏感的板块，住房放大了这一动作、领涨可选消费的反弹——直到杰克逊霍尔的鹰派重置终结它。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好去通胀反弹：VIX 33->20、成长跑赢价值","市场押注美联储提前转向","利率敏感的住房放大反弹","超卖反射被杰克逊霍尔终结"]},"2022-08-16":{"title":"Jackson Hole reset: second leg down","body":"A ~20% selloff into late October as Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech erased pivot hopes and another rate-regime leg hit: TLT -17.8%, DXY +6.0%, VIX 20->30, with mortgage rates pushing past 7%. Housing led the laggards alongside Real Estate -23.7% and printed its cycle low with the broad equity bottom.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME leg: TLT -17.8%, DXY +6.0%","Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech","Mortgage rates push past 7%","Housing prints its cycle low with the market"],"title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重置：第二段下跌","body_zh":"到10月下旬约20%的抛售，鲍威尔的鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话抹去转向预期，又一轮利率/收益率冲击来袭：TLT-17.8%、美元DXY+6.0%、VIX 20->30，抵押贷款利率突破7%。住房与房地产-23.7%一同领跌，并随大盘底部打出周期低点。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率冲击：TLT-17.8%、DXY+6.0%","鲍威尔鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话","抵押贷款利率突破7%","住房随大盘打出周期低点"]},"2022-10-20":{"title":"Peak-rates rally: builders front-run the cut","body":"A powerful ~78% surge from the October 2022 low through August 2023, riding a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +75.1%, SPY +24.8%, VIX 30->16, growth>value +14.2) and a falling dollar (DXY -9.6%). Because builders trade on the second derivative of rates, they front-ran the eventual easing even before mortgage rates fell — and as a high-beta cyclical, the group amplified the goldilocks tape (cyclicals +23.5% vs defensives +9.3%), helped by a frozen resale market funneling demand to new builds.","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +75.1%, VIX 30->16, DXY -9.6%","Fed nears the end of its hiking cycle","Builders trade on rate direction, not level","Frozen resale market funnels demand to new builds"],"title_zh":"利率见顶反弹：建筑商抢跑降息","body_zh":"从2022年10月低点到2023年8月约78%的强劲飙升，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+75.1%、SPY+24.8%、VIX 30->16、成长跑赢价值+14.2）与走弱的美元（DXY-9.6%）。由于建筑商交易的是利率的二阶导数，它们在抵押贷款利率下行之前就抢跑了最终的宽松——作为高贝塔周期股，该板块放大了金发姑娘环境（周期+23.5% vs 防御+9.3%），并受益于二手房市场冻结将需求导向新建房。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+75.1%、VIX 30->16、DXY-9.6%","美联储接近加息周期尾声","建筑商交易利率方向而非水平","二手房冻结将需求导向新建房"]},"2023-08-07":{"title":"Yield spike scare: 10Y toward 5%","body":"A ~20% pullback into late October 2023 as the 10-year ran toward 5% and the 30-year mortgage touched ~8%, the worst in two decades. This was a clean rate-regime hit — TLT -12.2%, DXY +4.4% — inside a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -3.8%). As the most rate-sensitive group, housing led the laggards (Real Estate -13.6%, Discretionary -13.1%) before the year-end pivot rally.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME hit: TLT -12.2%, DXY +4.4%","10-year toward 5%, mortgage ~8% (two-decade worst)","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -3.8% vs SPY)","Rate-sensitive housing leads the pullback"],"title_zh":"收益率飙升恐慌：10年期逼近5%","body_zh":"到2023年10月下旬约20%的回调，10年期收益率逼近5%、30年期抵押贷款利率触及约8%，为二十年来最差。这是一次干净的利率/收益率冲击——TLT-12.2%、DXY+4.4%——发生在狭窄的大盘股主导环境中（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.8%）。作为最利率敏感的板块，住房领跌（房地产-13.6%、可选消费-13.1%），随后才迎来年末转向反弹。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率冲击：TLT-12.2%、DXY+4.4%","10年期逼近5%、抵押贷款约8%（二十年最差）","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-3.8% vs SPY）","利率敏感的住房领跌"]},"2023-10-25":{"title":"Pivot rally to all-time highs","body":"A ~90% rip from the October 2023 low through October 2024 on the rare combination of a dovish Fed and a melt-up tape: TLT +17.0% (yields FELL), SMH +82.5%, VIX calm at ~18, growth>value +11.6. The Fed's December 2023 pivot and the actual September 2024 cut sent builders to records, with Financials/Industrials/Real Estate leading the cyclical surge and chronic existing-home under-supply keeping new-build order books full.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME tailwind: TLT +17.0%, yields fall","RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +82.5%, VIX calm","Dec-2023 pivot + actual Sept-2024 rate cut","Chronic existing-home undersupply props new builds"],"title_zh":"转向反弹至历史新高","body_zh":"从2023年10月低点到2024年10月约90%的飙升，源于鸽派美联储与融涨环境的罕见组合：TLT+17.0%（收益率下行）、SMH+82.5%、VIX平静约18、成长跑赢价值+11.6。美联储2023年12月转向与2024年9月实际降息把建筑商推至纪录高位，金融/工业/房地产领涨周期股，二手房长期供给不足让新建房订单饱满。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率顺风：TLT+17.0%、收益率下行","风险偏好融涨：SMH+82.5%、VIX平静","2023年12月转向+2024年9月实际降息","二手房长期供给不足支撑新建房"]},"2024-10-18":{"title":"Higher-for-longer plus tariff-shock flush","body":"A ~34% slide from the October 2024 peak into the April 8, 2025 low. Sticky inflation revived 'higher-for-longer' and pushed mortgage rates back toward 7%, then the April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash triggered a risk-off flush (VIX 18->52, SMH -28.1%, SPHB-SPLV -19.7) into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. As a high-beta cyclical with a direct input-cost hit from tariffs, builders amplified the drawdown — falling far more than the -14.5% SPY.","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 18->52, SPHB-SPLV -19.7","Sticky inflation revives higher-for-longer rates","April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash + input-cost hit","High-beta builders amplify a -34% drawdown"],"title_zh":"更高更久叠加关税冲击下泄","body_zh":"从2024年10月高点到2025年4月8日低点约34%的下滑。粘性通胀重燃“更高更久”、把抵押贷款利率推回7%附近，随后2025年4月对等关税崩盘引发避险下泄（VIX 18->52、SMH-28.1%、SPHB-SPLV-19.7），进入放缓/通缩恐慌象限。作为高贝塔周期股、且直接承受关税带来的投入成本冲击，建筑商放大了回撤——跌幅远超SPY的-14.5%。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 18->52、SPHB-SPLV-19.7","粘性通胀重燃更高更久利率","2025年4月对等关税崩盘+投入成本冲击","高贝塔建筑商放大-34%回撤"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Post-tariff recovery on a risk-on melt-up","body":"A ~37% rebound off the April 2025 tariff low into September as worst-case tariffs were dialed back and rate-cut hopes revived, lifting the group with a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +64.8%, SPY +31.1%, VIX 52->15, growth>value +19.8, DXY -5.4%). The tape was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%) so builders rode the cyclical recovery (cyclicals +28.8% vs defensives +8.1%) rather than leading it; affordability stayed the persistent ceiling.","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +64.8%, VIX 52->15, DXY -5.4%","Tariff de-escalation eases input-cost fears","Rate-cut hopes revive through summer 2025","Affordability stays the persistent ceiling"],"title_zh":"关税后复苏，搭乘风险偏好融涨","body_zh":"从2025年4月关税低点到9月约37%的反弹，最坏关税情形被回调、降息预期重燃，搭乘科技/半导体引领的融涨（SMH+64.8%、SPY+31.1%、VIX 52->15、成长跑赢价值+19.8、DXY-5.4%）。市场广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-7.4%），故建筑商是随周期复苏（周期+28.8% vs 防御+8.1%）而非引领；负担能力仍是持续上限。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+64.8%、VIX 52->15、DXY-5.4%","关税降级缓解投入成本担忧","2025年夏降息预期重燃","负担能力仍是持续上限"]},"2025-09-08":{"title":"Autumn fade as rate optimism stalls","body":"A ~20% pullback into late November 2025 as the rate-cut path stalled and the tape rotated risk-off (VIX 15->26, defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals -2.3%, DXY +2.8%) into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Long bonds went nowhere (TLT +0.1%), so this fade was driven by the risk-off rotation and a firmer dollar rather than a yield back-up; with money fleeing to safety, the most rate-sensitive group gave back its summer gains ahead of the 2026 inflation scare.","drivers":["RISK-OFF rotation: VIX 15->26, defensives lead, DXY +2.8%","Rate-cut hopes fade, long yields flat (TLT +0.1%)","Late-cycle demand softness","Rate-sensitive housing leads the fade"],"title_zh":"秋季回落：利率乐观停滞","body_zh":"到2025年11月下旬约20%的回调，降息路径停滞，市场转向避险（VIX 15->26、防御+4.6% vs 周期-2.3%、DXY+2.8%），进入放缓/通缩恐慌象限。长债基本持平（TLT+0.1%），故此次回落由避险轮动与更坚挺的美元驱动，而非收益率回升；资金奔向安全，这一最利率敏感的板块在2026年通胀恐慌前吐回夏季涨幅。","drivers_zh":["避险轮动：VIX 15->26、防御领涨、DXY+2.8%","降息预期消退、长端收益率持平（TLT+0.1%）","晚周期需求疲软","利率敏感的住房领跌"]},"2025-11-20":{"title":"Year-end seasonal bounce on a broadening tape","body":"A ~25% rally into February 2026 on a calmer rate backdrop and a broadening, reflationary tape (RSP beat SPY +5.8%, DXY -3.3%, cyclicals +14.4% vs defensives +7.1%, SMH +28.0%). Brief rate-cut optimism and the typical late-year recovery lifted the group — before the Iran/Hormuz oil shock reset the inflation picture and undid it.","drivers":["BROADENING reflation: RSP +5.8% vs SPY, DXY -3.3%","Calmer rate backdrop into year-end","Seasonal late-year bounce + rate-cut optimism","Rally cut short by the 2026 oil shock"],"title_zh":"年末季节性反弹，市场广度扩散","body_zh":"到2026年2月约25%的反弹，利率背景趋于平静、市场广度扩散并再通胀（等权RSP跑赢SPY+5.8%、DXY-3.3%、周期+14.4% vs 防御+7.1%、SMH+28.0%）。短暂的降息乐观与典型的年末复苏提振该板块——随后伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击重置通胀图景并终结它。","drivers_zh":["广度扩散再通胀：RSP+5.8% vs SPY、DXY-3.3%","年末利率背景趋稳","季节性年末反弹+降息乐观","反弹被2026年油价冲击终结"]},"2026-02-11":{"title":"Oil-shock inflation scare backs up mortgages","body":"A ~25% selloff into mid-May 2026 as the Iran/Hormuz oil shock sent crude +66.7% and CPI to 4.2%, pushing the Fed back into hiking and TLT down -4.7%. Even though the broad tape stayed firm (SPY +6.1%, SMH +31.1%) on a narrow mega-cap rally (RSP lagged SPY -6.5%), the 30-year mortgage backed up and housing — the front-line rate-sensitive group — sold off hard while the index held.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME hit: oil +66.7%, CPI 4.2%, TLT -4.7%","Fed shifts back into hiking mode","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -6.5% vs SPY)","Front-line rate-sensitivity drives the selloff"],"title_zh":"油价冲击通胀恐慌推高抵押利率","body_zh":"到2026年5月中旬约25%的抛售，伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击令原油+66.7%、CPI升至4.2%，迫使美联储重回加息、TLT下跌-4.7%。尽管大盘在狭窄的大盘股领涨下保持坚挺（SPY+6.1%、SMH+31.1%，等权RSP跑输SPY-6.5%），30年期抵押贷款利率回升，住房——一线利率敏感板块——在指数企稳之际大幅下跌。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率冲击：油+66.7%、CPI4.2%、TLT-4.7%","美联储重回加息","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-6.5% vs SPY）","一线利率敏感性驱动抛售"]},"2026-05-19":{"title":"Ceasefire rate-relief bounce","body":"A ~23% rebound off the May 2026 low. The mid-June Hormuz ceasefire and easing pump prices (oil -35.8%) took the tail risk out of inflation, letting yields and mortgage rates ease (TLT +5.6%) and giving the most beaten-down rate-sensitive group a sharp reflex on a broadening tape (RSP beat SPY +4.7%, even as SPY was flat). This is rate relief, not a demand boom — housing remains hostage to the next CPI print.","drivers":["RATE-RELIEF + broadening: TLT +5.6%, RSP +4.7% vs SPY","Mid-June Hormuz ceasefire, oil -35.8%","Mortgage rates ease at the margin","Sharp reflex off a deeply oversold low"],"title_zh":"停火带来利率减压反弹","body_zh":"从2026年5月低点约23%的反弹。6月中旬霍尔木兹停火与油价回落（油-35.8%）抽走了通胀的尾部风险，让收益率与抵押贷款利率回落（TLT+5.6%），在市场广度扩散下（即便SPY持平，等权RSP跑赢SPY+4.7%）给予这一最受打击的利率敏感板块一次急促反射。这是利率减压而非需求爆发——住房仍受制于下一个CPI数据。","drivers_zh":["利率减压+广度扩散：TLT+5.6%、RSP+4.7% vs SPY","6月中旬霍尔木兹停火、油-35.8%","抵押贷款利率边际回落","深度超卖低点的急促反射"]}}},"b-retail":{"now":"Retail (XLY-proxied big-box and off-price — Walmart, Costco, Target, plus discretionary) is the weakest theme on the board (pos 16, RS rank 30) and is trying to base. Its story is the health of the US consumer, and the regime is mixed: the tape is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, RSP beat SPY +2.9%), which should help, but the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock pushed gasoline and CPI to 4.2% and the dollar firmed (DXY +3.4%), squeezing real wages exactly where this basket lives. Import-heavy discount retail also wears the tariff cost from the April 2025 reciprocal tariffs, echoing the 2022 inventory/margin shock. Defensive staples like Walmart and Costco hold up better than discretionary; the basket is bottoming, not breaking out.","now_zh":"零售（以XLY为代理的大卖场与折扣零售——沃尔玛、Costco、塔吉特及可选消费）是全场最弱主题（位置16，RS排名30），正尝试筑底。其故事是美国消费者的健康状况，环境喜忧参半：市场是再通胀/增长向上（周期+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%、等权RSP跑赢SPY+2.9%），本应有助，但2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击把油价与CPI推至4.2%、美元走强（DXY+3.4%），恰好挤压了该篮子所处的实际工资。进口密集的折扣零售还承担2025年4月对等关税的成本，呼应2022年的库存/利润率冲击。防御性必需品如沃尔玛、Costco比可选消费更抗跌；该篮子在筑底而非突破。","legs":{"2021-11-18":{"title":"Early rate-hike de-rate","body":"Retail fell ~18% from the late-2021 peak as the Fed signaled the end of easy money. The tape was already rolling risk-off into a stagflation-ish quad (VIX 18->31, SMH -16.4%, growth>value -13.4) with money fleeing to safety, and Discretionary led the laggards at -19.6%. Multiples compressed as the market braced for higher rates and slowing discretionary spend.","drivers":["RISK-OFF de-rate: VIX 18->31, growth>value -13.4","Fed signals end of easy money","Discretionary leads laggards (-19.6%)","Multiples compress on higher-rate fears"],"title_zh":"加息初期估值下调","body_zh":"零售从2021年末高点下跌约18%，美联储释放结束宽松信号。市场已转向避险、进入类滞胀象限（VIX 18->31、SMH-16.4%、成长跑赢价值-13.4），资金奔向安全，可选消费领跌-19.6%。在市场为更高利率与可选消费放缓做准备时，估值压缩。","drivers_zh":["避险下调：VIX 18->31、成长跑赢价值-13.4","美联储释放结束宽松信号","可选消费领跌（-19.6%）","更高利率担忧下估值压缩"]},"2022-02-23":{"title":"Reopening-demand bounce","body":"A ~19% rally into April 2022 as still-strong consumer demand and reopening spending temporarily outweighed rate fears. The quad stayed stagflation-ish with energy leading (+20.4%) and a rate-regime move underneath (TLT -10.7%, DXY +4.4%) — defensives actually led cyclicals (+12.7% vs +7.9%), so this was a defensive-tilted relief, not a risk-on melt-up, before the margin shock arrived.","drivers":["STAGFLATION quad: energy leads, TLT -10.7%","Resilient consumer + reopening spending","Defensive-tilted relief (defensives > cyclicals)","Pre-margin-shock optimism"],"title_zh":"重启需求反弹","body_zh":"到2022年4月约19%的反弹，仍然强劲的消费者需求与重启支出暂时盖过利率担忧。象限维持类滞胀、能源领涨（+20.4%），底层是利率/收益率上行（TLT-10.7%、DXY+4.4%）——防御实际跑赢周期（+12.7% vs +7.9%），故这是偏防御的减压而非风险偏好融涨，随后便迎来利润率冲击。","drivers_zh":["滞胀象限：能源领涨、TLT-10.7%","消费者韧性+重启支出","偏防御的减压（防御>周期）","利润率冲击前的乐观"]},"2022-04-20":{"title":"The 2022 margin shock","body":"A brutal ~24% plunge in a month as Walmart and Target both missed badly — bloated post-COVID inventory, surging freight and labor costs and weakening discretionary demand crushed margins. The macro amplified it: a stagflation-ish risk-off tape (VIX 20->29, SPY -12.4%) sent Discretionary down -22.7%, the worst sector. It was the defining retail event of the cycle.","drivers":["RISK-OFF stagflation: VIX 20->29, Discretionary -22.7%","Walmart and Target miss earnings badly","Bloated post-COVID inventory + freight/labor costs","Discretionary demand weakens"],"title_zh":"2022年利润率冲击","body_zh":"一个月内约24%的暴跌，沃尔玛与塔吉特双双大幅不及预期——疫情后膨胀的库存、飙升的运费与人工成本、走弱的可选需求压垮利润率。宏观放大了它：类滞胀的避险环境（VIX 20->29、SPY-12.4%）令可选消费下跌-22.7%、为最差板块。这是本轮周期标志性的零售事件。","drivers_zh":["避险滞胀：VIX 20->29、可选消费-22.7%","沃尔玛与塔吉特大幅不及预期","疫情后库存膨胀+运费/人工成本","可选需求走弱"]},"2022-05-20":{"title":"Long grind off the margin low","body":"A ~42% recovery from the May 2022 low through April 2023 as a goldilocks/disinflation backdrop took hold (VIX 29->17, oil -30.4%, DXY -1.7%). After clearing excess inventory, retailers normalized margins and the consumer proved more resilient than feared; off-price and discount names led. The tape was mega-cap-narrow (RSP lagged SPY -2.9%), so this was a stock-specific grind more than a broad rip.","drivers":["DISINFLATION backdrop: VIX 29->17, oil -30.4%","Excess inventory cleared, margins normalize","Consumer more resilient than feared","Narrow tape (RSP -2.9% vs SPY)"],"title_zh":"利润率低点后的长期爬升","body_zh":"从2022年5月低点到2023年4月约42%的复苏，金发姑娘/去通胀背景确立（VIX 29->17、油-30.4%、DXY-1.7%）。在清理过剩库存后，零售商利润率回归正常、消费者比担忧的更有韧性；折扣与平价品牌领涨。市场由大盘股主导、广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-2.9%），故这更像个股驱动的爬升而非全面飙升。","drivers_zh":["去通胀背景：VIX 29->17、油-30.4%","清理过剩库存、利润率回归","消费者比担忧更有韧性","狭窄市场（RSP-2.9% vs SPY）"]},"2023-04-24":{"title":"Mid-cycle consumer wobble on a yield spike","body":"A ~15% pullback into late October 2023 as a sharp rate-regime move (TLT -18.6%, DXY +5.1%) plus restarting student-loan payments and 'higher-for-longer' fears hit consumer-spending sentiment. The tape was narrow and growth-led (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%, growth>value +11.9), so defensives and rate-sensitive retail were left behind even as Tech held up.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME hit: TLT -18.6%, DXY +5.1%","Student-loan payments restart","Narrow growth-led tape (RSP -7.4% vs SPY)","Consumer sentiment softens"],"title_zh":"周期中段消费者动摇，收益率飙升","body_zh":"到2023年10月下旬约15%的回调，剧烈的利率/收益率上行（TLT-18.6%、DXY+5.1%）叠加学生贷款还款重启与“更高更久”担忧，打击消费支出情绪。市场狭窄且由成长引领（等权RSP跑输SPY-7.4%、成长跑赢价值+11.9），故防御与利率敏感的零售被落下，即便科技坚挺。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率冲击：TLT-18.6%、DXY+5.1%","学生贷款还款重启","狭窄成长主导（RSP-7.4% vs SPY）","消费者情绪走软"]},"2023-10-27":{"title":"Soft-landing rally","body":"A ~42% advance from the October 2023 low into December 2024 on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +78.8%, VIX 21->14, growth>value +25.2) with yields falling (TLT +14.4%). The Fed pivot and the September 2024 cut powered a broad consumer rally — Discretionary surged +59.4% — though the tape was very narrow (RSP lagged SPY -10.4%); Walmart and Costco led on share gains and steady traffic.","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +78.8%, TLT +14.4%, VIX 21->14","Fed pivot and September 2024 rate cut","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -10.4% vs SPY)","Walmart and Costco gain share"],"title_zh":"软着陆反弹","body_zh":"从2023年10月低点到2024年12月约42%的上涨，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+78.8%、VIX 21->14、成长跑赢价值+25.2），收益率下行（TLT+14.4%）。美联储转向与2024年9月降息推动广泛的消费反弹——可选消费飙升+59.4%——尽管市场广度极窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-10.4%）；沃尔玛与Costco凭份额提升与稳定客流领涨。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+78.8%、TLT+14.4%、VIX 21->14","美联储转向与2024年9月降息","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-10.4% vs SPY）","沃尔玛与Costco抢占份额"]},"2024-12-11":{"title":"Tariff-shock selloff","body":"A ~16% slide into the April 8, 2025 low as a risk-off flush hit (VIX 14->52, SMH -26.5%, SPHB-SPLV -23.4) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Import-heavy discount retail sat squarely in the tariff crosshairs — the April 2025 reciprocal tariffs threatened landed costs on foreign-sourced goods, hitting margins and sentiment together. Defensives cushioned (-5.2%) while cyclicals/Discretionary led the laggards (-25.1%).","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 14->52, SPHB-SPLV -23.4","April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash","Import-heavy retail wears landed-cost hit","Defensives cushion vs Discretionary -25.1%"],"title_zh":"关税冲击抛售","body_zh":"到2025年4月8日低点约16%的下滑，避险下泄来袭（VIX 14->52、SMH-26.5%、SPHB-SPLV-23.4），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。进口密集的折扣零售正处关税靶心——2025年4月对等关税威胁海外采购商品的到岸成本，同时打击利润率与情绪。防御缓冲（-5.2%），而周期/可选消费领跌（-25.1%）。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 14->52、SPHB-SPLV-23.4","2025年4月对等关税崩盘","进口密集零售承受到岸成本冲击","防御缓冲 vs 可选消费-25.1%"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Post-tariff relief recovery","body":"A ~48% rebound off the April 2025 tariff low into February 2026 as tariff fears eased and the consumer held up better than feared, riding a reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +41.7% vs defensives +23.3%, SMH +127.3%, DXY -5.9%) — though the rally was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -4.2%). Walmart and Costco led on defensive resilience; the run then ran into the 2026 oil-shock inflation squeeze.","drivers":["REFLATION tape: SMH +127.3%, DXY -5.9%, cyclicals lead","Tariff de-escalation eases margin fears","Consumer holds up better than feared","Rally caps into the 2026 oil shock"],"title_zh":"关税后减压复苏","body_zh":"从2025年4月关税低点到2026年2月约48%的反弹，关税担忧缓解、消费者比预期更坚挺，搭乘再通胀/增长向上的环境（周期+41.7% vs 防御+23.3%、SMH+127.3%、DXY-5.9%）——尽管反弹广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-4.2%）。沃尔玛与Costco凭防御韧性领涨；随后撞上2026年油价冲击的通胀挤压。","drivers_zh":["再通胀环境：SMH+127.3%、DXY-5.9%、周期领涨","关税降级缓解利润率担忧","消费者比预期更坚挺","反弹撞上2026年油价冲击"]}}},"b-travel":{"now":"Travel & experiences (JETS-proxied airlines, cruises, lodging and gaming) is topping (pos 78, RS rank 11) after a long post-COVID run. From the April 2025 low it has rallied ~78% on resilient experiential spending — but it is now extended and consumer-cyclical, exactly the wrong profile if the 2026 oil-shock squeeze (oil +19.2% on the leg, CPI 4.2%, DXY +3.4%) erodes discretionary budgets and jet-fuel costs bite airline margins. The reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%) is still constructive, but as a high-beta cyclical the group amplifies both directions: the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire helps on fuel, yet the risk/reward has shifted from 'catch-up' to 'late-cycle.'","now_zh":"旅游与体验（以JETS为代理的航空、邮轮、住宿与博彩）在漫长的疫情后行情后进入顶部区（位置78，RS排名11）。自2025年4月低点已反弹约78%，得益于韧性十足的体验式消费——但它现已超买且属消费周期股，恰是2026年油价冲击挤压（本段油价+19.2%、CPI4.2%、DXY+3.4%）侵蚀可选预算、燃油成本压缩航司利润率时最不利的画像。再通胀/增长向上的环境（周期+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%）仍偏建设性，但作为高贝塔周期股，该板块双向放大：6月中旬霍尔木兹停火在燃油端有助，然而风险回报已从“补涨”转向“晚周期”。","legs":{"2020-06-26":{"title":"Reopening super-rally on a reflationary risk-on tape","body":"A ~116% surge from mid-2020 through March 2021 as vaccine news detonated the most COVID-crushed group. The regime was a textbook reflation melt-up that amplified high-beta cyclicals: SPHB-SPLV +72.0, copper/gold +57.6, oil +69.9%, DXY -5.8% and broadening breadth (RSP beat SPY +13.0%). Airlines, cruises and hotels led the 'return to normal' trade as the rate-regime turned (TLT -16.4%, yields surged on reflation).","drivers":["REFLATION melt-up: SPHB-SPLV +72.0, copper/gold +57.6","Vaccine breakthroughs spark reopening hopes","Most COVID-crushed group amplifies the rip","Broadening breadth (RSP +13.0% vs SPY)"],"title_zh":"重启超级反弹，搭乘再通胀风险偏好环境","body_zh":"从2020年中到2021年3月约116%的飙升，疫苗消息引爆这一最受疫情打击的板块。环境是教科书式再通胀融涨、放大高贝塔周期股：SPHB-SPLV+72.0、铜金比+57.6、油+69.9%、DXY-5.8%、广度扩散（等权RSP跑赢SPY+13.0%）。航空、邮轮、酒店领涨“回归常态”交易，利率/收益率转向（TLT-16.4%、收益率因再通胀飙升）。","drivers_zh":["再通胀融涨：SPHB-SPLV+72.0、铜金比+57.6","疫苗突破点燃重启预期","最受疫情打击的板块放大涨幅","广度扩散（RSP+13.0% vs SPY）"]},"2021-03-15":{"title":"Delta-variant pause into a deflation scare","body":"A ~22% pullback into July 2021 as the Delta variant raised reopening doubts and the tape rotated to a slowdown/deflation scare — yields FELL (TLT +11.3%), defensives led cyclicals (+7.9% vs +2.3%) and high-beta de-rated (SPHB-SPLV -15.8) on a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -4.5%). The most cyclical group gave back its easy first-leg gains as flight-to-safety took over.","drivers":["DEFLATION-SCARE rotation: TLT +11.3%, defensives lead","Delta variant raises reopening doubts","High-beta de-rates (SPHB-SPLV -15.8)","Narrow tape (RSP -4.5% vs SPY)"],"title_zh":"Delta变种暂停，转入通缩恐慌","body_zh":"到2021年7月约22%的回调，Delta变种引发重启疑虑，市场转向放缓/通缩恐慌——收益率下行（TLT+11.3%）、防御跑赢周期（+7.9% vs +2.3%）、高贝塔估值下调（SPHB-SPLV-15.8），且广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-4.5%）。在避险接管之际，这一最周期的板块吐回了第一段轻松涨幅。","drivers_zh":["通缩恐慌轮动：TLT+11.3%、防御领涨","Delta变种引发重启疑虑","高贝塔估值下调（SPHB-SPLV-15.8）","狭窄市场（RSP-4.5% vs SPY）"]},"2021-07-19":{"title":"Reopening trade resumes on a risk-on tape","body":"A ~23% recovery into November 2021 as Delta fears faded and risk-on returned: a tech/semis-led tape (SMH +20.2%, growth>value +3.9, calm VIX 22->16) inside a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +15.2% vs defensives +4.1%, oil +22.4%). As a high-beta cyclical, travel amplified the move with Discretionary +20.2% as bookings rebounded toward year-end.","drivers":["RISK-ON reflation: SMH +20.2%, VIX 22->16, oil +22.4%","Delta fears fade, bookings rebound","High-beta travel amplifies the cyclical leg","Risk appetite recovers into year-end"],"title_zh":"重启交易恢复，搭乘风险偏好环境","body_zh":"到2021年11月约23%的复苏，Delta担忧消退、风险偏好回归：科技/半导体引领（SMH+20.2%、成长跑赢价值+3.9、VIX平静22->16），处于再通胀/增长向上象限（周期+15.2% vs 防御+4.1%、油+22.4%）。作为高贝塔周期股，旅游放大了动作，可选消费+20.2%，预订量在年末前回升。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好再通胀：SMH+20.2%、VIX 22->16、油+22.4%","Delta担忧消退、预订回升","高贝塔旅游放大周期段","风险偏好向年末回升"]},"2021-11-05":{"title":"Omicron scare risk-off flush","body":"A sharp ~22% drop into early December 2021 as the Omicron variant emerged and travel bans returned. The tape flipped risk-off into a slowdown/deflation scare (VIX 16->31, oil -19.3%, RSP lagged SPY -2.1%); as the highest-beta consumer-cyclical, travel was hit far harder than the -3.8% SPY as bookings stalled.","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 16->31, oil -19.3%","Omicron variant emerges, travel bans return","High-beta travel sells off worse than SPY -3.8%","Bookings stall"],"title_zh":"Omicron恐慌避险下泄","body_zh":"到2021年12月初约22%的急跌，Omicron变种出现、旅行禁令重返。市场转向避险、进入放缓/通缩恐慌（VIX 16->31、油-19.3%、等权RSP跑输SPY-2.1%）；作为最高贝塔的消费周期股，旅游受创远超SPY的-3.8%，预订停滞。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 16->31、油-19.3%","Omicron变种出现、旅行禁令重返","高贝塔旅游跌幅超SPY-3.8%","预订停滞"]},"2021-12-01":{"title":"Omicron-mild relief bounce","body":"A ~23% rebound into mid-February 2022 as Omicron proved milder than feared. The tape was reflationary (oil +42.8%, broadening RSP beat SPY +4.3%, cyclicals +4.9% vs defensives +3.7%) even as a rate-regime move bit underneath (TLT -10.6%) — reopening confidence and pricing power let the cyclical group rebound while broad indices went sideways (SPY -0.5%).","drivers":["REFLATION + broadening: oil +42.8%, RSP +4.3% vs SPY","Omicron proves milder than feared","Rate-regime move underneath (TLT -10.6%)","Reopening confidence returns"],"title_zh":"Omicron温和减压反弹","body_zh":"到2022年2月中旬约23%的反弹，Omicron被证实比担忧温和。市场偏再通胀（油+42.8%、广度扩散等权RSP跑赢SPY+4.3%、周期+4.9% vs 防御+3.7%），尽管底层利率/收益率上行（TLT-10.6%）——重启信心与定价能力让周期板块反弹，而大盘横盘（SPY-0.5%）。","drivers_zh":["再通胀+广度扩散：油+42.8%、RSP+4.3% vs SPY","Omicron被证实更温和","底层利率/收益率上行（TLT-10.6%）","重启信心回归"]},"2022-02-16":{"title":"Ukraine and oil-spike risk-off","body":"A ~25% selloff into early March 2022 as Russia's invasion of Ukraine spiked oil (+27.5%) into a stagflation-ish quad, threatening jet-fuel costs. The tape went risk-off (VIX 24->36, DXY +3.8) with flight-to-safety — defensives led cyclicals (+2.3% vs -5.1%) — and high-beta travel amplified the drop with Discretionary -12.3%, the worst sector.","drivers":["STAGFLATION risk-off: VIX 24->36, oil +27.5%","Russia invades Ukraine, jet-fuel costs threatened","Flight-to-safety (defensives > cyclicals)","High-beta travel amplifies the drop"],"title_zh":"乌克兰与油价飙升避险","body_zh":"到2022年3月初约25%的抛售，俄罗斯入侵乌克兰令油价飙升（+27.5%）、进入类滞胀象限，威胁燃油成本。市场转向避险（VIX 24->36、DXY+3.8）、出现避险流——防御跑赢周期（+2.3% vs -5.1%）——高贝塔旅游放大跌幅，可选消费-12.3%为最差板块。","drivers_zh":["滞胀避险：VIX 24->36、油+27.5%","俄罗斯入侵乌克兰、燃油成本受威胁","避险流（防御>周期）","高贝塔旅游放大跌幅"]},"2022-03-07":{"title":"Oil-pullback bounce on a disinflation tape","body":"A ~24% rally into late March 2022 as oil pulled back (-12.7%) and the tape turned briefly goldilocks/disinflation (SMH +16.9%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 36->19). Pent-up spring/summer travel demand reasserted itself and the high-beta cyclical amplified the bounce (Discretionary +17.5%), even as a rate-regime move ran underneath (TLT -6.1%).","drivers":["DISINFLATION bounce: SMH +16.9%, VIX 36->19","Oil pulls back -12.7% from the spike","High-beta travel amplifies (Discretionary +17.5%)","Pent-up spring/summer demand"],"title_zh":"油价回落反弹，搭乘去通胀环境","body_zh":"到2022年3月下旬约24%的反弹，油价回落（-12.7%），市场短暂转向金发姑娘/去通胀（SMH+16.9%、成长跑赢价值+7.2、VIX 36->19）。被压抑的春夏旅游需求重现，高贝塔周期股放大了反弹（可选消费+17.5%），尽管底层利率/收益率上行（TLT-6.1%）。","drivers_zh":["去通胀反弹：SMH+16.9%、VIX 36->19","油价从飙升回落-12.7%","高贝塔旅游放大（可选消费+17.5%）","被压抑的春夏需求"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Rate-hike bear catches travel","body":"A ~35% slide into the June 2022 bear low as aggressive Fed hikes (TLT -14.1%, DXY +5.3%) and recession fears hit the consumer-cyclical group inside a stagflation-ish quad. The tape was a flight-to-safety risk-off (VIX 19->33, defensives -11.2% vs cyclicals -18.2%); high-beta travel amplified it with Discretionary -29.7%, deep underperforming the -20.6% SPY.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME bear: TLT -14.1%, DXY +5.3%","Aggressive Fed hikes + recession fears","Flight-to-safety (VIX 19->33)","High-beta travel -35% vs SPY -20.6%"],"title_zh":"加息熊市波及旅游","body_zh":"到2022年6月熊市低点约35%的下滑，激进的美联储加息（TLT-14.1%、DXY+5.3%）与衰退担忧在类滞胀象限打击消费周期板块。市场是避险流（VIX 19->33、防御-11.2% vs 周期-18.2%）；高贝塔旅游放大跌幅，可选消费-29.7%，深度跑输SPY的-20.6%。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率熊市：TLT-14.1%、DXY+5.3%","激进加息+衰退担忧","避险流（VIX 19->33）","高贝塔旅游-35% vs SPY-20.6%"]},"2022-06-16":{"title":"Revenge-travel boom on a disinflation melt-up","body":"A ~68% surge from the June 2022 low through July 2023. 'Revenge travel' ran full throttle even as the Fed kept hiking — but the macro tailwind was real: a tech/semis-led goldilocks melt-up (SMH +58.9%, VIX 33->13, growth>value +21.4, oil -35.6%, DXY -3.6%). As a high-beta cyclical, travel amplified the cyclical leg (cyclicals +25.6% vs defensives +9.0%); pricing power and full planes overwhelmed cost fears.","drivers":["DISINFLATION melt-up: SMH +58.9%, VIX 33->13, oil -35.6%","'Revenge travel' demand runs full throttle","High-beta travel amplifies cyclicals (+25.6%)","Pricing power and full planes"],"title_zh":"报复性旅游繁荣，搭乘去通胀融涨","body_zh":"从2022年6月低点到2023年7月约68%的飙升。即便美联储仍在加息，“报复性旅游”全速运行——但宏观顺风是真实的：科技/半导体引领的金发姑娘融涨（SMH+58.9%、VIX 33->13、成长跑赢价值+21.4、油-35.6%、DXY-3.6%）。作为高贝塔周期股，旅游放大了周期段（周期+25.6% vs 防御+9.0%）；定价能力与满舱压倒成本担忧。","drivers_zh":["去通胀融涨：SMH+58.9%、VIX 33->13、油-35.6%","“报复性旅游”需求全速运行","高贝塔旅游放大周期（+25.6%）","定价能力与满舱"]},"2023-07-18":{"title":"Yield-spike consumer scare","body":"A ~26% pullback into late October 2023 as the 10-year ran toward 5% in a sharp rate-regime move (TLT -16.4%, DXY +6.6%) inside a stagflation-ish quad. Fears grew that travel demand had peaked; the narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -3.2%) and high-beta profile sent the cyclical group down with Discretionary -15.0% leading the laggards.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME hit: TLT -16.4%, DXY +6.6%","10-year toward 5%, peak-demand fears","Narrow tape (RSP -3.2% vs SPY)","High-beta travel leads laggards (-15.0%)"],"title_zh":"收益率飙升消费者恐慌","body_zh":"到2023年10月下旬约26%的回调，10年期收益率逼近5%，构成剧烈的利率/收益率上行（TLT-16.4%、DXY+6.6%），处于类滞胀象限。市场担忧旅游需求见顶；狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.2%）与高贝塔画像令周期板块下跌，可选消费-15.0%领跌。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率冲击：TLT-16.4%、DXY+6.6%","10年期逼近5%、需求见顶担忧","狭窄市场（RSP-3.2% vs SPY）","高贝塔旅游领跌（-15.0%）"]},"2023-10-27":{"title":"Soft-landing reopening run","body":"A ~81% advance from the October 2023 low into February 2025 on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +88.0%, VIX 21->15, growth>value +22.9) with yields falling (TLT +10.3%). The Fed pivot and 2024 cut sustained the travel boom to new highs; Financials/Comm/Discretionary led the cyclical surge even as the tape was very narrow (RSP lagged SPY -12.3%).","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +88.0%, TLT +10.3%, VIX 21->15","Fed pivot and 2024 rate cut","Strong experiential spending persists","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -12.3% vs SPY)"],"title_zh":"软着陆重启行情","body_zh":"从2023年10月低点到2025年2月约81%的上涨，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+88.0%、VIX 21->15、成长跑赢价值+22.9），收益率下行（TLT+10.3%）。美联储转向与2024年降息把旅游繁荣推至新高；金融/通信/可选消费领涨周期股，尽管市场广度极窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-12.3%）。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+88.0%、TLT+10.3%、VIX 21->15","美联储转向与2024年降息","体验式消费持续强劲","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-12.3% vs SPY）"]},"2025-02-19":{"title":"Tariff-shock plunge","body":"A ~34% selloff into the April 8, 2025 low as the reciprocal-tariff crash triggered a risk-off flush (VIX 15->52, SMH -30.1%, SPHB-SPLV -22.8) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Travel is the first budget line cut when households brace for a downturn — and as the highest-beta consumer-cyclical, it amplified the move, with Discretionary -21.8% well below the -18.8% SPY.","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 15->52, SPHB-SPLV -22.8","April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash, recession fears","Travel is the first discretionary cut","High-beta travel amplifies the drop"],"title_zh":"关税冲击暴跌","body_zh":"到2025年4月8日低点约34%的抛售，对等关税崩盘引发避险下泄（VIX 15->52、SMH-30.1%、SPHB-SPLV-22.8），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。当家庭为衰退做准备时，旅游是第一个被砍的预算项——作为最高贝塔的消费周期股，它放大了动作，可选消费-21.8%远低于SPY的-18.8%。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 15->52、SPHB-SPLV-22.8","2025年4月对等关税崩盘、衰退担忧","旅游是第一个被砍的可选项","高贝塔旅游放大跌幅"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Reopening rally matures into a top","body":"A ~78% rebound off the April 2025 low into June 2026 as tariff fears eased and experiential demand stayed strong, riding a reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +50.3% vs defensives +22.3%, SMH +240.9%, oil +16.2%) — though narrow (RSP lagged SPY -8.7%). The basket is now extended and late-cycle: the 2026 oil shock lifted jet-fuel costs and pinched the consumer, and the mid-June ceasefire only partially offsets that. As a high-beta cyclical, its risk/reward has flipped from catch-up to caution.","drivers":["REFLATION tape: SMH +240.9%, cyclicals +50.3%, oil +16.2%","Tariff fears ease, demand stays strong","Basket reaches a topping/extended state","Late-cycle consumer pinch caps upside"],"title_zh":"重启行情成熟见顶","body_zh":"从2025年4月低点到2026年6月约78%的反弹，关税担忧缓解、体验需求保持强劲，搭乘再通胀/增长向上的环境（周期+50.3% vs 防御+22.3%、SMH+240.9%、油+16.2%）——尽管广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-8.7%）。该篮子现已超买且晚周期：2026年油价冲击抬升燃油成本、挤压消费者，6月中旬停火仅部分抵消。作为高贝塔周期股，其风险回报已从补涨翻转为审慎。","drivers_zh":["再通胀环境：SMH+240.9%、周期+50.3%、油+16.2%","关税担忧缓解、需求保持强劲","篮子进入顶部/超买状态","晚周期消费者挤压封顶上行"]}}},"b-defensives":{"now":"Defensives (XLP/XLU-proxied staples, utilities and low-vol cash-flows) sit mid-pack (pos 38, RS rank 24) in a slow uptrend. By design this is the low-beta safe-haven blend — it lags in risk-on melt-ups and shines when fear spikes, so it inversely tracks the regime. The 2026 backdrop is a tug-of-war: the Iran/Hormuz oil shock, hot 4.2% CPI and a hawkish Fed are the kind of stress that usually bids defensives, but the current reflation/growth-up tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, SMH +67.9%, SPHB-SPLV +20.7) keeps money chasing growth, and a firm dollar plus rising yields hurt the rate-sensitive utility leg. The result is a steady-but-unexciting grind — this basket is the portfolio's shock absorber, not its engine, and its relative strength improves precisely when the rest of the board cracks.","now_zh":"防御股（以XLP/XLU为代理的必需品、公用事业与低波动现金流）处于中游（位置38，RS排名24），处于缓慢上行趋势。按设计这是低贝塔的避险组合——在风险偏好融涨中落后、在恐慌飙升时发光，故与市场环境呈反向。2026年背景是一场拉锯：伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击、4.2%的高CPI与鹰派美联储是通常会买入防御股的那种压力，但当前再通胀/增长向上的环境（周期+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%、SMH+67.9%、SPHB-SPLV+20.7）让资金追逐成长，加上坚挺美元与上行收益率伤及利率敏感的公用事业一腿。结果是稳健却乏味的爬升——这个篮子是组合的减震器而非引擎，其相对强度恰在全场其余裂开时改善。","legs":{"2022-04-21":{"title":"Even defensives can't escape the 2022 bear","body":"A ~15% drawdown into October 2022 — defensives held up far better than growth, but the rate-hike bear hit everything inside a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with a violent rate-regime move (TLT -15.4%, a crushing DXY +12.1%, VIX 23->31). Rising yields particularly pressured the bond-proxy utility leg (-14.3%) even as staples cushioned; the low-beta blend lost less than the -16.5% SPY but couldn't avoid an absolute drawdown.","drivers":["RATE-REGIME bear: TLT -15.4%, DXY +12.1%","Rate-hike bear pressures all assets","Rising yields hit the utility leg (-14.3%)","Low-beta cushion (-15% vs SPY -16.5%)"],"title_zh":"连防御股也逃不过2022年熊市","body_zh":"到2022年10月约15%的回撤——防御股远比成长股抗跌，但加息熊市在放缓/通缩恐慌象限里波及一切，伴随剧烈的利率/收益率冲击（TLT-15.4%、压迫性的DXY+12.1%、VIX 23->31）。上行收益率尤其压制债券代理的公用事业一腿（-14.3%），即便必需品起到缓冲；低贝塔组合跌幅小于SPY的-16.5%，但仍难免绝对回撤。","drivers_zh":["利率/收益率熊市：TLT-15.4%、DXY+12.1%","加息熊市压制所有资产","上行收益率打击公用事业一腿（-14.3%）","低贝塔缓冲（-15% vs SPY-16.5%）"]},"2022-10-07":{"title":"Safe-haven bid into the bottom","body":"A ~21% rally from October 2022 into May 2023. As the bear ended and SVB's March 2023 collapse triggered a flight to safety, defensives caught a steady haven bid and a falling dollar (DXY -9.4%) with steadier yields (TLT +3.9%) helped utilities. The broad tape was goldilocks/disinflation (SMH +33.6%, VIX 31->16) and narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.1%), so this was a low-drama recovery rather than a high-beta rip — exactly the defensive profile.","drivers":["FLIGHT-TO-SAFETY bid: SVB collapse, DXY -9.4%","Bear-market bottom forms","Falling yields help utilities (TLT +3.9%)","Low-drama recovery vs narrow tape"],"title_zh":"避险买盘伴随见底","body_zh":"从2022年10月到2023年5月约21%的反弹。随着熊市结束、2023年3月硅谷银行（SVB）倒闭触发避险，防御股获得稳定的避险买盘，走弱的美元（DXY-9.4%）与趋稳的收益率（TLT+3.9%）助力公用事业。大盘是金发姑娘/去通胀（SMH+33.6%、VIX 31->16）且狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.1%），故这是低戏剧性的复苏而非高贝塔飙升——正是防御画像。","drivers_zh":["避险买盘：SVB倒闭、DXY-9.4%","熊市底部形成","收益率下行助公用事业（TLT+3.9%）","低戏剧性复苏 vs 狭窄市场"]},"2023-05-01":{"title":"Defensives lag the AI risk-on","body":"A ~15% drawdown into October 2023 — the textbook defensive curse. A tech/semis-led growth rally (SMH +22.2%, growth>value +13.6, VIX flat near its lows at 16->17) pulled money into growth and left low-vol staples and utilities behind, with defensives -10.0% while cyclicals were +5.3% in a reflation/growth-up quad. The autumn yield spike (TLT -15.3%, DXY +4.3%) compounded the pain on the bond-proxy leg (utilities -13.8%); the narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -7.3%) added to the underperformance.","drivers":["RISK-ON drag: SMH +22.2%, growth>value +13.6","AI rally pulls money into growth","Autumn yield spike hits utilities (TLT -15.3%)","Textbook low-vol underperformance"],"title_zh":"防御股落后于AI风险偏好","body_zh":"到2023年10月约15%的回撤——教科书式的防御诅咒。科技/半导体引领的成长行情（SMH+22.2%、成长跑赢价值+13.6、VIX在低位附近持平16->17）把资金拉向成长、把低波动必需品与公用事业落下，再通胀/增长向上象限里防御-10.0%而周期+5.3%。秋季收益率飙升（TLT-15.3%、DXY+4.3%）加重了债券代理一腿的痛苦（公用事业-13.8%）；狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-7.3%）加剧了跑输。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好拖累：SMH+22.2%、成长跑赢价值+13.6","AI行情把资金拉向成长","秋季收益率飙升打击公用事业（TLT-15.3%）","教科书式低波动跑输"]},"2023-10-12":{"title":"Long, steady defensive grind","body":"A ~43% advance from October 2023 into February 2026 — the basket's defining steady-compounder leg, even as the broad tape was a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +170.7%, growth>value +8.8, very narrow RSP lagged SPY -11.5%) that defensives structurally lag. Falling yields (TLT +16.3%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -8.4%) helped utilities, which also picked up an AI-power-demand tailwind. This low-drama uptrend through the soft landing and various risk scares ran right up to the 2026 oil-shock stress.","drivers":["RISK-ON backdrop defensives lag: SMH +170.7%, RSP -11.5% vs SPY","Falling yields + weak dollar aid utilities (TLT +16.3%)","AI-power-demand tailwind for utilities","Low-drama uptrend into the 2026 oil shock"],"title_zh":"漫长稳健的防御爬升","body_zh":"从2023年10月到2026年2月约43%的上涨——这是该篮子标志性的稳健复利段，尽管大盘是科技/半导体引领的融涨（SMH+170.7%、成长跑赢价值+8.8、极窄的等权RSP跑输SPY-11.5%）而防御股结构性落后。下行收益率（TLT+16.3%）与走弱美元（DXY-8.4%）助力公用事业，后者还获得AI电力需求的顺风。这条穿越软着陆与各种风险恐慌的低戏剧性上行趋势，一直延伸到2026年油价冲击的压力。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好背景下防御落后：SMH+170.7%、RSP-11.5% vs SPY","下行收益率+弱美元助公用事业（TLT+16.3%）","AI电力需求为公用事业提供顺风","低戏剧性上行延伸至2026年油价冲击"]}}},"b-crypto":{"now":"Crypto & digital assets (IBIT-proxied exchanges, miners and bitcoin-treasury names — COIN, MSTR and miners) is trending (pos 35, RS rank 10) and remains the highest-beta theme on the board — the purest risk-appetite barometer here, leading on the way up and on the way down. Everything is a leveraged bet on Bitcoin: COIN's volumes, MSTR's stack and miner economics all swing on the coin. After the late-2025 pullback the basket put in a ~86% rally into June 2026. The 2026 oil-shock/hawkish-Fed backdrop is a headwind — high-beta crypto hates rising real rates and a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) — but the current reflation/growth-up tape (SPHB-SPLV +20.7, SMH +67.9%) plus structural tailwinds (post-halving supply, the maturing spot-ETF complex, corporate treasury adoption) keep the floor higher than in past cycles.","now_zh":"加密与数字资产（以IBIT为代理的交易所、矿企与比特币储备公司——COIN、MSTR及矿企）处于趋势中（位置35，RS排名10），仍是全场最高贝塔的主题——这里最纯粹的风险偏好晴雨表，上涨领先、下跌也领先。一切都是对比特币的杠杆押注：COIN的成交量、MSTR的持币与矿企经济全随币价波动。在2025年末回调后，该篮子到2026年6月录得约86%的反弹。2026年油价冲击/鹰派美联储是逆风——高贝塔加密厌恶上行的实际利率与更坚挺的美元（DXY+3.4%）——但当前再通胀/增长向上的环境（SPHB-SPLV+20.7、SMH+67.9%）加上结构性顺风（减半后供给、成熟的现货ETF体系、企业储备采用）让其底部高于以往周期。","legs":{"2021-02-19":{"title":"First 2021 correction: high-beta unwind","body":"A ~53% drawdown into May 2021 as the first half of the 2021 bull cycle topped — China's mining crackdown and an overheated, over-leveraged market triggered a violent high-beta unwind. The macro tape was actually benign (SPY +6.7%, broadening RSP beat SPY +3.9%, reflation/growth-up), which underscores that this was a crypto-specific blow-off: the most leveraged basket on the board fell while the broad market rose.","drivers":["CRYPTO-SPECIFIC vs benign tape (SPY +6.7%)","China mining crackdown","Overheated, over-leveraged market","Violent high-beta unwind"],"title_zh":"2021年首次回调：高贝塔去杠杆","body_zh":"到2021年5月约53%的回撤，2021年牛市上半场见顶——中国矿业打击与过热、过度杠杆的市场触发剧烈的高贝塔去杠杆。宏观环境其实温和（SPY+6.7%、广度扩散等权RSP跑赢SPY+3.9%、再通胀/增长向上），这凸显这是加密自身的吹顶：全场最高杠杆的篮子下跌、而大盘上涨。","drivers_zh":["加密自身 vs 温和大盘（SPY+6.7%）","中国矿业打击","过热、过度杠杆的市场","剧烈高贝塔去杠杆"]},"2021-05-21":{"title":"Run to the November 2021 cycle top","body":"A ~119% surge into November 2021 as the bull cycle made its final blow-off high. The tape was risk-on (SMH +26.8%, growth>value +15.9, calm VIX 20->17, falling yields TLT +9.1) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto amplified it hard — ETF optimism, retail mania and peak risk appetite drove COIN and miners to records before the long winter. The narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -4.9%) flagged the late-cycle character.","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +26.8%, growth>value +15.9","Bull cycle's final blow-off high","Highest-beta basket amplifies the rip","Narrow late-cycle tape (RSP -4.9% vs SPY)"],"title_zh":"冲向2021年11月周期顶","body_zh":"到2021年11月约119%的飙升，牛市作出最后的吹顶高点。环境偏风险偏好（SMH+26.8%、成长跑赢价值+15.9、VIX平静20->17、收益率下行TLT+9.1），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密强力放大它——ETF乐观、散户狂热与峰值风险偏好把COIN与矿企推至纪录高位，随后进入漫长寒冬。狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-4.9%）已预示晚周期特征。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+26.8%、成长跑赢价值+15.9","牛市最后的吹顶高点","最高贝塔篮子放大涨幅","狭窄晚周期市场（RSP-4.9% vs SPY）"]},"2021-11-08":{"title":"Crypto winter begins on the Fed's hawkish pivot","body":"A ~66% plunge into January 2022 as the Fed's hawkish pivot and the start of the rate-hike cycle drained liquidity. The tape rotated risk-off into a stagflation-ish quad (VIX 17->30, SPHB-SPLV -13.8, growth>value -10.1) with flight-to-safety (defensives +0.7% vs cyclicals -5.1%); the highest-beta asset sold off first and far worse than the -7.7% SPY, kicking off the 2022 crypto winter.","drivers":["RISK-OFF rotation: VIX 17->30, SPHB-SPLV -13.8","Fed's hawkish pivot drains liquidity","Highest-beta asset sells off first","Crypto -66% vs SPY -7.7%"],"title_zh":"加密寒冬开启于美联储鹰派转向","body_zh":"到2022年1月约66%的暴跌，美联储鹰派转向与加息周期启动抽走流动性。市场转向避险、进入类滞胀象限（VIX 17->30、SPHB-SPLV-13.8、成长跑赢价值-10.1），伴随避险流（防御+0.7% vs 周期-5.1%）；最高贝塔资产最先且远更剧烈地抛售，跌幅超SPY的-7.7%，拉开2022年加密寒冬序幕。","drivers_zh":["避险轮动：VIX 17->30、SPHB-SPLV-13.8","美联储鹰派转向抽走流动性","最高贝塔资产最先抛售","加密-66% vs SPY-7.7%"]},"2022-01-27":{"title":"Bear-market relief bounce","body":"A ~57% rebound into late March 2022 — a sharp but doomed counter-trend rally typical of a high-beta bear. The tape gave a brief reflationary reprieve (SPY +7.4%, VIX 30->19, oil +20.4%) even as yields rose (TLT -8.4%), enough to spark an oversold high-beta bounce before the deeper leg down.","drivers":["BRIEF risk-on reprieve: VIX 30->19, SPY +7.4%","Counter-trend bear rally","Oversold high-beta bounce","Doomed before the deeper leg down"],"title_zh":"熊市减压反弹","body_zh":"到2022年3月下旬约57%的反弹——典型高贝塔熊市中急促却注定夭折的反趋势行情。市场给出短暂的再通胀喘息（SPY+7.4%、VIX 30->19、油+20.4%），即便收益率上行（TLT-8.4%），也足以点燃超卖的高贝塔反弹，随后是更深一段下跌。","drivers_zh":["短暂风险偏好喘息：VIX 30->19、SPY+7.4%","反趋势熊市行情","超卖高贝塔反弹","更深下跌前的夭折反弹"]},"2022-03-29":{"title":"Luna/Terra cascade amid a risk-off flush","body":"A ~74% collapse into June 2022 as the Terra/Luna implosion and the 3AC/Celsius leverage cascade vaporized crypto credit. The macro amplified the carnage: a flight-to-safety risk-off (VIX 19->29, SPHB-SPLV -18.1, DXY +6.4) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad sent the highest-beta basket down ~4x the -17.9% SPY — the worst stretch of the winter.","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 19->29, SPHB-SPLV -18.1, DXY +6.4","Terra/Luna stablecoin implosion","3AC and Celsius leverage cascade","Crypto -74% vs SPY -17.9%"],"title_zh":"Luna/Terra连环崩塌叠加避险下泄","body_zh":"到2022年6月约74%的崩溃，Terra/Luna内爆与3AC/Celsius杠杆连环爆破令加密信用蒸发。宏观放大了惨况：放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的避险下泄（VIX 19->29、SPHB-SPLV-18.1、DXY+6.4）把最高贝塔篮子打下约为SPY-17.9%的4倍——本轮寒冬最惨阶段。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 19->29、SPHB-SPLV-18.1、DXY+6.4","Terra/Luna稳定币内爆","3AC与Celsius杠杆连环爆","加密-74% vs SPY-17.9%"]},"2022-06-30":{"title":"Post-Luna dead-cat bounce","body":"A ~112% rebound into mid-August 2022 — a violent oversold bounce after the Luna cascade, amplified by a brief tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +20.4%, growth>value +6.5, VIX 29->20) in a goldilocks/disinflation quad. The highest-beta basket ripped on the summer risk appetite before the FTX collapse delivered the final blow.","drivers":["RISK-ON bounce: SMH +20.4%, VIX 29->20","Violent post-Luna oversold rebound","Highest-beta basket amplifies summer risk-on","Pre-FTX false dawn"],"title_zh":"Luna后的死猫跳","body_zh":"到2022年8月中旬约112%的反弹——Luna连环崩塌后的剧烈超卖反弹，被一段短暂的科技/半导体引领的风险偏好放大（SMH+20.4%、成长跑赢价值+6.5、VIX 29->20），处于金发姑娘/去通胀象限。最高贝塔篮子借夏季风险偏好飙升，随后FTX崩盘给出致命一击。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹：SMH+20.4%、VIX 29->20","Luna后剧烈超卖反弹","最高贝塔篮子放大夏季风险偏好","FTX前的虚假黎明"]},"2022-08-12":{"title":"FTX collapse: the winter low","body":"A ~68% plunge into late December 2022 as the November 2022 FTX collapse — the largest crypto fraud and exchange failure on record — destroyed confidence. The macro was a risk-off rate-regime move (TLT -12.8%, VIX 20->22, growth>value -12.1) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; the highest-beta basket marked the cycle's washout low.","drivers":["RISK-OFF rate move: TLT -12.8%, growth>value -12.1","November 2022 FTX collapse","Largest exchange failure on record","Cycle washout low"],"title_zh":"FTX崩盘：寒冬低点","body_zh":"到2022年12月下旬约68%的暴跌，2022年11月FTX崩盘——史上最大加密欺诈与交易所倒闭——摧毁了信心。宏观是放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的避险型利率/收益率冲击（TLT-12.8%、VIX 20->22、成长跑赢价值-12.1）；最高贝塔篮子打出本轮周期的洗盘低点。","drivers_zh":["避险利率冲击：TLT-12.8%、成长跑赢价值-12.1","2022年11月FTX崩盘","史上最大交易所倒闭","周期洗盘低点"]},"2022-12-28":{"title":"ETF super-cycle: 12x off the bottom","body":"A staggering ~1220% surge from the December 2022 FTX low through December 2024 on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +153.5%, growth>value +63.1, VIX 22->13). The spot-Bitcoin-ETF approval (January 2024), the April 2024 halving and Trump's pro-crypto November 2024 win drove the highest-beta basket to a generational run; the extremely narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -28.5%) was the perfect fuel for the most leveraged theme on the board.","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +153.5%, growth>value +63.1","January 2024 spot-Bitcoin-ETF approval + halving","Trump's pro-crypto November 2024 win","Narrow mega-cap tape fuels high-beta (RSP -28.5%)"],"title_zh":"ETF超级周期：自底部12倍","body_zh":"从2022年12月FTX低点到2024年12月约1220%的惊人飙升，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+153.5%、成长跑赢价值+63.1、VIX 22->13）。现货比特币ETF获批（2024年1月）、2024年4月减半与特朗普2024年11月亲加密的胜选把最高贝塔篮子推向一代人级别的行情；极窄、大盘股主导的市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-28.5%）正是全场最高杠杆主题的完美燃料。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+153.5%、成长跑赢价值+63.1","2024年1月现货比特币ETF获批+减半","特朗普2024年11月亲加密胜选","狭窄大盘股市场为高贝塔提供燃料（RSP-28.5%）"]},"2024-12-06":{"title":"Tariff-shock unwind","body":"A ~53% drawdown into the April 8, 2025 low as post-election euphoria faded, the DeepSeek AI scare hit sentiment, and the April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash drained risk appetite. The tape was a brutal risk-off flush (VIX 13->52, SMH -27.3%, SPHB-SPLV -22.7) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; the highest-beta basket fell hardest, ~3x the -17.8% SPY.","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 13->52, SPHB-SPLV -22.7","Post-election euphoria fades, DeepSeek scare","April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash","High-beta crypto -53% vs SPY -17.8%"],"title_zh":"关税冲击去杠杆","body_zh":"到2025年4月8日低点约53%的回撤，大选后欣快消退、DeepSeek的AI恐慌打击情绪、2025年4月对等关税崩盘抽走风险偏好。市场是放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的残酷避险下泄（VIX 13->52、SMH-27.3%、SPHB-SPLV-22.7）；最高贝塔篮子跌得最惨，约为SPY-17.8%的3倍。","drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 13->52、SPHB-SPLV-22.7","大选后欣快消退、DeepSeek恐慌","2025年4月对等关税崩盘","高贝塔加密-53% vs SPY-17.8%"]},"2025-04-08":{"title":"Post-tariff crypto surge","body":"A ~246% rally off the April 2025 tariff low into October 2025 as risk appetite roared back. The tape was a goldilocks melt-up (SMH +89.9%, growth>value +22.7, VIX 52->21, DXY -4.1%) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto amplified the cyclical leg (cyclicals +30.3% vs defensives +14.1%). ETF inflows resumed and corporate Bitcoin-treasury adoption (MSTR-style) accelerated, sending COIN and miners sharply higher on a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -10.2%).","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +89.9%, VIX 52->21, DXY -4.1%","Risk appetite roars back, ETF inflows resume","Highest-beta basket amplifies cyclicals (+30.3%)","Corporate Bitcoin-treasury adoption accelerates"],"title_zh":"关税后加密飙升","body_zh":"从2025年4月关税低点到2025年10月约246%的反弹，风险偏好强势回归。市场是金发姑娘融涨（SMH+89.9%、成长跑赢价值+22.7、VIX 52->21、DXY-4.1%），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密放大了周期段（周期+30.3% vs 防御+14.1%）。ETF资金流入恢复、企业比特币储备采用（MSTR式）加速，在狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-10.2%）中把COIN与矿企大幅推高。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+89.9%、VIX 52->21、DXY-4.1%","风险偏好强势回归、ETF流入恢复","最高贝塔篮子放大周期（+30.3%）","企业比特币储备采用加速"]},"2025-10-15":{"title":"Late-2025 correction","body":"A ~51% drawdown into February 2026 as the parabolic rally cooled and the building 2026 macro stress — rising rates and early oil-shock fears — hit the highest-beta basket first. Notably the broad tape barely moved (SPY +2.2%, VIX 21->22, broadening RSP beat SPY +3.4% on a reflation rotation into Energy/Materials), so this was a high-beta-specific unwind: crypto fell ~51% while the index held, the mirror image of its leveraged-on-the-way-up character.","drivers":["HIGH-BETA unwind vs flat tape (SPY +2.2%)","Parabolic rally cools, rising rates pressure high-beta","Reflation rotation into Energy/Materials","Highest-beta basket hit first"],"title_zh":"2025年末回调","body_zh":"到2026年2月约51%的回撤，抛物线行情降温、2026年累积的宏观压力——上行利率与早期油价冲击担忧——最先打击最高贝塔篮子。值得注意的是大盘几乎未动（SPY+2.2%、VIX 21->22、广度扩散等权RSP跑赢SPY+3.4%，资金再通胀轮动进能源/材料），故这是高贝塔自身的去杠杆：加密下跌约51%而指数企稳，正是其“上涨时加杠杆”特征的镜像。","drivers_zh":["高贝塔去杠杆 vs 平盘大盘（SPY+2.2%）","抛物线行情降温、上行利率压制高贝塔","再通胀轮动进能源/材料","最高贝塔篮子最先受击"]},"2026-02-05":{"title":"Structural-floor rebound","body":"A strong ~86% rebound off the February 2026 low into June. The tape turned risk-on again (SMH +59.5%, growth>value +7.9, VIX 22->16) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto snapped back hard off oversold levels — even against the hawkish oil-shock backdrop and a firmer dollar (DXY +1.4%). The maturing spot-ETF complex, post-halving supply scarcity and corporate-treasury demand provided a higher floor than past cycles, though the narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -6.6%) kept it a mega-cap-led, high-beta move.","drivers":["RISK-ON snapback: SMH +59.5%, VIX 22->16","Maturing spot-ETF complex provides a floor","Post-halving supply + corporate-treasury demand","Highest-beta basket amplifies off oversold lows"],"title_zh":"结构性底部反弹","body_zh":"从2026年2月低点到6月约86%的强劲反弹。市场再度转向风险偏好（SMH+59.5%、成长跑赢价值+7.9、VIX 22->16），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密自超卖水平强力反弹——即便面对鹰派油价冲击背景与更坚挺的美元（DXY+1.4%）。成熟的现货ETF体系、减半后供给稀缺与企业储备需求提供了高于以往周期的底部，尽管狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-6.6%）使其仍是大盘股主导的高贝塔行情。","drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹：SMH+59.5%、VIX 22->16","成熟现货ETF体系提供底部","减半后供给+企业储备需求","最高贝塔篮子自超卖低点放大"]}}}};
